PVD("bangladesh_ndp_2020-2025",{"docs":["","BGD NDP 2020 25"],"s":{"1":[[1,"63","3","Urban Water and Sanitation Expansion","In particular, the access to safe water and sanitation will be enhanced in both urban and rural areas to improve health and fight the COVID-19 infection.",""],[1,"63","3","Urban Housing Regulatory and Mortgage Finance Reform","Urban housing would be promoted through regulatory simplifications relating to land and property registration, reduction in registration fee, and strengthening of housing mortgage finance.",""],[1,"503","7","Urban Water Supply, Sewerage and Drainage Services","WASA in four city corporation areas made consistent progress with planning, development and maintenance of water supply, sewerage and drainage facilities.",""],[1,"503","7","Rural Safe Water and Arsenic Mitigation Measures","The government has taken a number of interventions, including awareness, arsenic test, providing",""],[1,"516","12","Safe Water Supply and Sanitation Facilities Provision","Ensure safe water supply and sanitation facilities in a sustainable manner",""],[1,"523","10","Piped Water Supply Initiative","A piped water supply has been targeted in the densely populated villages; the strategy will be different in villages where households are located sparsely.",""],[1,"523","12","Coastal Pond Digging for Safe Water Supply","Pond digging will be extended in coastal areas for safe water supply;",""],[1,"523","14","Rural Faecal Sludge Management Strategy","Suitable strategies will be undertaken for faecal sludge management in rural areas.",""]],"2":[[1,"784","3","Implementation of the National Social Security Strategy","The Seventh Plan emphasizes on the successful implementation of the National Social Security Strategy (NSSS) adopted in June 2015",""],[1,"784","3","Social Protection Reform Package","The Seventh plan opined that 'the Proposed reforms will be instrumental in eliminating leakages, improving targeting, increasing the average value of the transfers, lowering the risks faced by the poor and vulnerable population, reducing poverty, helping to reduce income inequality and build social capital'.",""],[1,"784","4","National Social Security Strategy Modernization","It seeks to modernize the Bangladesh social security by combining tax-funded safety net programmes with contributory social insurance and employment regulations to protect the workers.",""],[1,"784","4","Social Protection Administrative Reform Package","It also seeks to considerably improve the administrative arrangements for social protection programmes by consolidating complementary programmes, by strengthening staffing and institutions, by instituting a modern MIS system, by replacing food-based transfer payments with cash-based payments using the financial sector based G2P (government to people) system, by introducing a grievance redressaling mechanism and by installing proper results- based M&E system.",""],[1,"786","3","National Social Security Strategy Implementation and Reform Package","The successful implementation of the NSSS will provide a strong basis for Bangladesh to extend proper social protection to its poor and vulnerable population.",""],[1,"786","5","Inclusive Social Security System Expansion","Build an inclusive SSS for all deserving Bangladeshis",""],[1,"786","7","Social Security System Reform","Reform the SSS by ensuring more efficient and effective use of resources, strengthened delivery systems and progress towards a more inclusive form of Social Security that effectively tackles lifecycle risks, prioritizing the poorest and most vulnerable members of society.",""],[1,"792","2","Social Security Outreach and Grievance Redress Mechanism","This will involve sensitizing staff of Social Security agencies as well as relying on local government and NGOs for identifying potential beneficiaries.",""],[1,"792","3","Social Insurance Product Development","The 8FYP may focus on developing products which may attract a burgeoning affordable middle-income class in Bangladesh to buy various types of social insurance aiming at smoothing their consumption in times of need.",""],[1,"793","1","Affordable Unemployment Insurance Scheme","This may include access of affordable unemployment insurance schemes for both formal and informal workers; and care services (i.e. for both child and adult care) to ensure higher participation of female workforce in the labour market.",""],[1,"793","1","Child and Adult Care Services Expansion","This may include access of affordable unemployment insurance schemes for both formal and informal workers; and care services (i.e. for both child and adult care) to ensure higher participation of female workforce in the labour market.",""],[1,"793","3","Contributory Pension Scheme Introduction","Contributory pension schemes need to be introduced to complement the social pension schemes.",""],[1,"795","2","Cash-for-Work Conversion of Food-Based Work Programmes","conversion of all food- based work programmes into cash for work programmes would be a key reform.",""],[1,"795","3","Government-to-Person Social Protection Payment Pilot","Finance Division (FD) has been implementing pilot fund transfers through G2P.","Finance Division (FD)"],[1,"795","3","Scale-Up of Digital Government-to-Person Transfers","special attention should be given to scale it to 60 to 70 per cent of the total SP fund transfer via G2P within the 8FYP.",""],[1,"796","1","Social Protection Delivery Reform Package","The 8FYP will implement the following reforms: (i) properly consolidate the multitude of programmes into the core Life Cycle schemes; (ii); develop a proper list of beneficiaries to minimize exclusion and inclusion errors;(iii) develop an adequate MIS system; (iv) develop a proper M&E system; and (v) Further strengthen the Grievance Redressal System (GRS) with online filing of complaints and a time-based follow-up and resolution of complaints.",""],[1,"796","3","National Household Database and Proxy Means Test Targeting System","the government has undertaken a project to develop a comprehensive database of all households (known as the National Household Database - NHD) and use a selection method based on 'Proxy Means Test (PMT)' model to improve the selection of poor and thereby reduce the high level of exclusion and inclusion errors.",""],[1,"797","4","Continuous Result-Based Monitoring System","Continuous result based monitoring will be needed to improve delivery processes, document results, inform policymakers about the effectiveness of alternative approaches, and mobilise political support for sustainability and expansion of the programmes that comprise the strategy.",""],[1,"797","5","National Social Security Monitoring and Evaluation Framework","M&E activities will be divided into three components.","Implementing Ministries/Divisions | IMED | GED | Central Monitoring Committee (CMC) | Cabinet Secretary"],[1,"797","6","M&E Results Dissemination Mechanism for Social Security","It is therefore important that there are well- specified mechanisms for disseminating the findings of the M&E.","Planning Commission | GED | Cabinet Division"],[1,"798","1","Dedicated Social Protection System Survey","a dedicated survey of social protection system may be carried out under the aegis of the General Economics Division.",""],[1,"798","1","Review of Major Social Protection Scheme Administration","this should be supplemented by a comprehensive review of the administrative arrangements of the major 15 to 20 social protection schemes covering cash, CCT, food and livelihood programmes.",""],[1,"848","1","National Social Security Strategy Implementation","For the Eighth Plan, the top most priority is to implement the NSSS.",""],[1,"848","1","Poverty-Focused Social Protection Spending Increase","the Eighth Plan also projects to increase the average poverty-focused spending on social protection from 1.2% of GDP to 2.0 % during the Eighth Plan.",""]],"3":[[1,"341","1","Bandwidth Price Reduction for ICT Sector Expansion","The price of bandwidth needs to be reduced to facilitate increasing number of net users, enhancing demand for local content and applications and developing a connected Bangladesh.",""],[1,"341","1","Rural Telecommunications Network Development and Utilization Guideline Implementation","The Rural Telecommunications Network Development and Utilization Guideline 2010 will need to be implemented to make sure that the existing network infrastructures have been optimally utilized for commercial communication and key social services (e.g. education, health care, e-governance, etc.).",""],[1,"343","1","Rural Broadband Connectivity Expansion","Specifically, the Government will invite private sector and not-for-profit sector for rolling out broadband connectivity in rural area.",""],[1,"346","19","ICT Parks through PPP Initiative","Build ICT parks through PPP initiative,",""],[1,"346","20","Second Submarine Cable Installation","Install the second submarine cable connection for expanding high speed internet facilities.",""],[1,"346","21","Second Phase Broadband Internet Connectivity Implementation","Complete the Second Phase of implementation of broadband internet connectivity under the South Asia Sub-Regional Cooperation (SASEC) initiative.",""],[1,"346","23","Public-Private Partnership Facilitation for ICT-Enabled Services","Facilitate PPP for ICT enabled services in e-Governance, agriculture, health, education, fintech sectors.",""],[1,"479","4","Info-Sarkar Phase 3 High-Speed Internet Expansion Project","With the goal of expanding high speed internet service in marginal rural areas, Info-Sarkar (Phase- 3) project has been undertaken by the government.",""],[1,"479","4","Connected Bangladesh Remote Area Internet Connectivity Project","the project titled 'Establishment of ICT Network to Remote Areas (Connected Bangladesh)' is being implemented to provide internet connectivity in further 777 Unions.",""],[1,"479","5","Third Submarine Cable Connection Agreement","MoU has been already signed with SEA-ME-WE-6 Submarine Cable Consortium for connection with the third submarine cable to add additional 12 Tbps capacity which is expected to be operational by 2025.",""],[1,"479","6","Modernization of Telecommunication Network for Digital Connectivity","The \"Modernization of Telecommunication Network for Digital Connectivity\" project is being implemented by BTCL.",""],[1,"480","1","Nationwide Teletalk 3G and 4G Service Provision","Teletalk is providing 3G mobile services across the country through 4,936 2G BTS and 3,909 3G BTS (Node B) and 2,348 4G Node-B in all districts and 48 Upazilas.",""],[1,"480","1","Teletalk E-Services Delivery Platform","Teletalk is providing e-services to the citizens in the areas of public examination results, university admissions and publication of results, medical, education, disaster management, entertainment, utility bill payment etc.",""],[1,"481","2","Optical Fibre Cable Plant Capacity Expansion","Steps have been taken to install one new high speed sheathing line machine to increase the annual production capacity of the optical fibre cable plant to 9,000 km.",""],[1,"481","2","HDPE Silicon Duct Plant Upgradation","Up gradation of the duct plant is on-going to increase the annual production capacity to 3,500 km.",""],[1,"487","4","Third Submarine Cable Connectivity Expansion","Bangladesh has already taken steps to strengthen its international digital communication infrastructure by deciding to connect to the country's third submarine cable SEA-ME-WE-6.",""],[1,"487","5","Domestic Backhaul Expansion and 5G Transmission Upgrade","high speed and high capacity robust domestic backhaul throughout the country will be very critical in upcoming days.",""],[1,"493","7","Public Telecommunications Infrastructure Upgrade","Encouraging existing public telecommunication service providers to upgrade their infrastructure as per requirements of the future networks.",""],[1,"493","9","International Submarine and Terrestrial Cable Connectivity Expansion","Expanding the international submarine and/or terrestrial cable connectivity considering the present growth rate and expected development.",""],[1,"493","10","International Cable Interconnectivity Enhancement","Establishing interconnectivity within the international cables in order to provide seamless international connectivity.",""],[1,"493","11","International Cable Connectivity Capacity Expansion","Expanding the capacity of the existing international submarine/terrestrial cable connectivity by upgrading terminal equipment.",""],[1,"493","12","Optical Fibre Transmission Network Expansion","Expanding the optical fibre transmission network up-to all of the union levels of the country, wherever feasible.",""],[1,"493","13","Optical Fibre and Microwave Transmission Network Expansion","Establishing optical fibre/microwave-based transmission network in the remote/ riverine chars/ coastal areas/ islands/ hilly and hard to reach areas where satellite service is not technologically and economically viable.",""],[1,"493","14","Backhaul Transmission Capacity Expansion for International Cable Connections","Ensuring adequate backhaul transmission capacity at the places of connecting upcoming international cables.",""],[1,"493","15","Backhaul Transmission Capacity Assessment and Equipment Upgradation","Regular assessment of the capacity requirement of the backhaul transmission in different parts of the country and up gradation of transmission equipment accordingly.",""],[1,"493","16","Interagency Coordination for Network Cable Construction and Maintenance","Coordinating with state organizations like Roads and Highways department, Local :selected: Government Engineering department, Bangladesh Railway, Bangladesh Bridge Authority and Power Grid Company of Bangladesh Limited etc. to facilitate convenient construction, operation and maintenance of the network cables.",""],[1,"496","7","National Digital Connectivity Expansion","Expanding high speed and affordable digital connectivity throughout the country irrespective of urban and rural areas.",""]],"4":[[1,"491","4","National Digital Skills Training Center Expansion","A number of training centers and Institutes will have to be established throughout the country both under public and private sector initiatives.",""],[1,"491","4","Modernization of Existing Training Institutes","Alongside, it is needed to modernize the existing institutes with state of art facilities and appropriate pool of resource persons.",""],[1,"491","4","Industry-Academia Collaboration for Workforce Readiness","Industry-academia collaboration will be required to prepare the working forces ready to take challenges for the new order of the technology horizons.",""],[1,"491","4","Dedicated Digital Communications Research and Human Resource Development Organization","A dedicated organization is required for research and human Resource Development in digital communications and services and to guide the overall activities of human resource development.",""],[1,"507","7","ICT Capacity-Building Training Programme","The ministry continues to facilitate training on ICT to improve the technical capacity of educational institutions, journalists, and law-enforcing agencies.",""],[1,"507","7","Advanced Digital Skills Training for Unemployed Youth","It has provided the unemployed youths with advanced training on computer programming, internet, outsourcing and freelancing.",""],[1,"527","1","Rural IT Access Development","The rural area will be enabled to use the IT facilities so that the people can utilize it for communication, information, online services, ecommerce and other relevant services.",""],[1,"527","1","Village IT Centre Establishment","BRDB will establish some of its rural development societies as IT centre in the village in a participatory manner.",""],[1,"527","1","ICT Training for Rural Society Members","BRDB will train the eligible member of the selected societies on ICT and will coordinate them with UP and NBDs.",""],[1,"531","4","Rural Youth Awareness and Skills Development Initiative","During 8th plan period, PDBF will undertake activities on creation of small entrepreneurs, and self- employment programmes, awareness and skills development of rural youths with special focus on the poor and vulnerable groups in rural areas.",""],[1,"725","1","ICT Sector Human Resource Development Programme","Human resource development for the ICT sector is one of the key focuses of ICT Division.","ICT Division"],[1,"725","1","ICT Inclusion for Persons with Disabilities Project","BCC has initiated Empowerment of persons with disabilities including NDD through ICT Project.","BCC"],[1,"725","1","ICT Professionals' Professional Certification Capacity Building","BCC is also introducing and promoting the ICT Professionals' Professional Certification (ITEE) system in Bangladesh through Capacity Building on ITEE Management Project.","BCC"],[1,"725","1","Japanese Language and IT Skills Training for Students","Students are trained with the skillset such as Japanese Language, IT skills (including ITEE Level 2 Exam preparation) and Japanese business manner through this project.",""],[1,"725","3","She Power Project: Sustainable Development for Women through ICT","For empowering women through ICT, a project has already been started named, \"She Power Project: Sustainable Development for Women through ICT\".",""],[1,"725","4","ICT Career Camp Programme","This project has also conducted ICT Career camp in 64 districts and reached more than 80,000 students of Bangladesh.",""],[1,"738","8","Upskilling Needs Assessment and Female Worker Upskilling","Training need for up skilling should be assessed based on likely transformation of task content production.",""],[1,"738","8","Targeted Upskilling for Female Workers","Moreover, special emphasis should be given to up skilling female workers, as they are worse sufferer to automation.",""],[1,"744","2","Universal Employability Registry","ICT Division proposes five immediate short-term interventions: a) establish a universal employability registry;","ICT Division"],[1,"747","2","Digital Divide Reduction Initiative","The ICT Division proposes the following interventions: a) address the digital divide; b) launch digital online training program; c) link local manufacturers with global marketplaces; and, d) digitize workforce database.","ICT Division"],[1,"747","2","Digital Online Training Program","The ICT Division proposes the following interventions: a) address the digital divide; b) launch digital online training program; c) link local manufacturers with global marketplaces; and, d) digitize workforce database.","ICT Division"],[1,"747","2","Workforce Database Digitization Initiative","The ICT Division proposes the following interventions: a) address the digital divide; b) launch digital online training program; c) link local manufacturers with global marketplaces; and, d) digitize workforce database.","ICT Division"],[1,"748","18","National Skills Registry Policy","Introduction of National Skills Registry Policy",""],[1,"750","7","Digital Skills Gap Reduction and Capacity-Building Programme","It will aim to reduce the skills gap at multiple levels in agencies and among citizens.",""],[1,"755","3","Youth Development Investment","The government has been devoted to the development of youth and plans to continue investing in their future in the upcoming five years, so as to pave the way to for achieving the development goals and commitments at the national level and the international level such as Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs).",""]],"5":[[1,"55","4","Labour-Intensive Export-Oriented Manufacturing Growth Strategy","Promote labour-intensive, export-oriented manufacturing-led growth along with expansion of the domestic market;",""],[1,"55","8","Non-Factor Services Export Promotion","Push exports of non-factor services;",""],[1,"56","1","Non-RMG Manufacturing Export Diversification Strategy","the 8FYP growth strategy will put top priority to the production and exports of non-RMG manufacturing to diversify the production and export base in areas including processed food, leather and footwear, light engineering, and pharmaceuticals.",""],[1,"56","1","Trade Liberalization and Competitive Exchange Rate Reform","Trade policy bias against exports will be removed by reducing trade protection, the exchange rate will be made more flexible and competitive, and FDI and domestic investment in manufacturing will be promoted through reforms of the investment climate to implement this strategy.",""],[1,"56","2","Agricultural Export Promotion Initiative","Agriculture exports will be promoted to increase farm income and employment in non-crop activities especially fisheries, fruits, vegetables and dairy products.",""],[1,"56","4","Services Exports Expansion Strategy","A major growth and employment driver that will be supported is the expansion of services exports.",""],[1,"57","2","Export Base Diversification Strategy","The strong performance in the balance of payments will be preserved by promoting a strong and diversified export base, focused on both goods and non-factor services (NFS).",""],[1,"57","2","Non-Factor Services Export Promotion","The scope for increasing exports of NFS is huge, given the large world market, with special emphasis on shipping, tourism, and ICT services (the gig market).",""],[1,"96","2","Fiscal Stimulus Package for Manufacturing Sector Retention","Introducing fiscal stimulus package to retain workers in the manufacturing sector, to maintain competitiveness of the enterprises especially in the export-oriented manufacturing sector and to revitalize the economic activities and business environment.",""],[1,"96","2","Low-Interest Credit Facilities for Businesses and MSMEs","The major policy interventions in this regard are to provide several credit facilities at low interest rate from the banking system for the businesses including MSMEs.",""],[1,"96","7","Special Salary Support Fund for Export-Oriented Manufacturing Workers","Special Fund for salary support to export- oriented manufacturing industry workers",""],[1,"96","10","Export Development Fund Expansion","Expansion of Export Development Fund (EDF)",""],[1,"97","4","Special Salary Support Fund for Export-Oriented Manufacturing Workers","Special Fund for Salary support to export oriented manufacturing industry workers",""],[1,"97","7","Expansion of Export Development Fund Facility","Expansion of facility provided through Export Development Fund (EDF) by Bangladesh Bank","Bangladesh Bank"],[1,"98","10","Export Diversification and Manufacturing Base Expansion","Similarly, export diversification and expansion of a diversified manufacturing base are of utmost importance.",""],[1,"113","2","Labor-Intensive and Export-Oriented Manufacturing Growth Strategy","The critical areas of 8FYP will be to stimulate labor-intensive and export-oriented manufacturing-led growth",""],[1,"113","2","Non-Factor Services Promotion","promote non-factor services",""],[1,"113","2","Overseas Employment Strengthening","strengthen overseas employment.",""],[1,"114","2","Labour-Intensive Export-Oriented Manufacturing Growth Strategy","Promote labour-intensive, export-oriented manufacturing-led growth.",""],[1,"114","9","Non-RMG Manufacturing Export Diversification Strategy","the 8FYP growth strategy will put top priority to the production and exports of non-RMG manufacturing to diversify the production and export base in areas including processed food, leather and footwear, light engineering, and pharmaceuticals.",""],[1,"114","9","Trade Reform and Investment Climate Improvement Package","Trade policy bias against exports will be removed through trade reforms, the exchange rate will be made more flexible and competitive, and FDI and domestic investment in manufacturing will be promoted through reforms of the investment climate to implement this strategy.",""],[1,"125","1","Removal of Anti-export Bias and Export-oriented Manufacturing Incentives","policies must support the elimination of ant-export bias of trade policy and improve incentives for export- oriented manufacturing.",""],[1,"130","2","Diversified Export Growth Strategy","This needs to be tackled with a strong export growth strategy based on a diversified export base.",""],[1,"130","5","RMG-Led Export Growth Strategy","As in the past, RMG sector will continue to lead the export growth strategy under the 8FYP.",""],[1,"130","5","Export-Supporting Infrastructure Investment","This will require massive amounts of investment in this sector along with investment in growth supporting infrastructure like power/electricity, land for setting up industries, transport, port etc.",""],[1,"130","5","Trade Protection Reduction and Duty-Free Input Access","The government will address the anti-export bias of trade policy by reducing trade protection and will provide duty free access to industrial inputs and capital machineries along the lines offered to the RMG sector.",""],[1,"134","3","Flexible Exchange Rate Management","The 8FYP is committed to improving the exchange rare management to bring in greater flexibility to correct for the past appreciation of the real exchange rate and then make concerted efforts to avoid real exchange appreciation over the coming years.",""],[1,"146","1","Export Diversification and Labour Skills Upgrading","Bangladesh must also diversify its export base and improve labour skills and productivity to sustain growth momentum and provide good jobs",""],[1,"170","4","Manufacturing Export Diversification and Trade Policy Reform","The main elements of the policy framework to spur the growth of manufacturing value-added and employment is to promote the diversification of labour-intensive export-oriented manufacturing beyond RMG.",""],[1,"170","4","Competitive Exchange Rate and Trade Protection Reduction Measures","policy supports for other labour-intensive manufacturing exports include a competitive real exchange rate, reduction in trade protection to remove the anti-export bias of trade policy, improve infrastructure services, and reduce the cost of trade logistics through deregulation, automation and transport links between the ports and the factory-gate.",""]],"6":[[1,"361","2","Development of Stress-Tolerant High-Yield Crop Varieties","The Bangladesh Agricultural Research Institute (BARI), BINA, BJRI, Bangladesh Sugar crop Research Institute (BSRI) and Bangladesh Wheat and Maize Research Institute (BWMRI) and Bangladesh Rice Research Institute (BRRI) has been working to develop new verities of stress tolerant HYV products through innovation.",""],[1,"361","3","National Agricultural Technology Programme Phase 2","with the financial help from the World Bank, the government initiated the National Agricultural Technology Prgramme-Phase 2 Project (NATP2) to disseminate different rice yield gap minimization technologies.",""],[1,"365","5","Agricultural Research and Innovation Modernization","Develop agricultural research for promoting export of products through coordination with local and international partner organizations; modernize agricultural research, education, extension, input management and develop skilled manpower for sustainable technology innovation.",""],[1,"365","11","Science-Led Climate-Smart Agriculture Technology Promotion","Introduce nanotechnology in agriculture promote science-led agriculture technology systems and encourage research and adoption of modern agricultural practices for development of drought, submergence and saline prone agriculture considering water and time economy, adaptation to climate change, proper use of genetically modified technology in agriculture, and promote adoption of modern agricultural practices in dry land, wetland, hills and coastal areas including use of environment friendly green technologies (e.g. IPM, INM, AWD, etc.) and climate-smart/resilient technologies; introduce salinity, submergence and other stress tolerant varieties specially in the Southern regions.",""],[1,"366","7","Crop Variety Development Programme","To develop crop varieties for rice (25 varieties) and non-rice (2000 genetic resources, 100 climate resilient varieties).",""],[1,"366","9","Agricultural Technology and Input Management Development","To develop seed production, soil and fertilizer management, crop management, pest management and location specific technologies.",""],[1,"368","3","Area-Specific Modern Variety Research and Development","The strategy requires research for area specific modern variety development and increasing productivity.",""],[1,"368","3","New Agricultural Technology Innovation by NARS and Universities","The National Agricultural Research System (NARS) institutes and agricultural universities need to play critical role in inventing relevant new technologies.",""],[1,"368","3","Farm-Level Dissemination of New Agricultural Technologies","The DAE will be responsible for farm level dissemination of the new technologies.",""],[1,"368","3","Agricultural Ministry Coordination Mechanism","The MoA has to play the leading role for proper coordination among different ministries.","MoA"],[1,"368","3","Short-Duration Aus Rice Variety Development","In the case of rice, a short duration variety of Aus rice to avoid climatic uncertainty during the late summer is of upmost importance.",""],[1,"368","3","Yield Gap Reduction through Modern Farm Technologies","Strategies are also needed for minimizing yield gap through increasing productivity and using modern and appropriate technologies at the farm level.",""],[1,"371","2","Regenerative Agriculture Promotion Initiative","During the implementation of the 8th Plan efforts will be made to promote and popularize regenerative agriculture among the farmers ...",""],[1,"371","3","Post-Harvest Technology Research for Agro-Processing","Agricultural research institutes like BARI and BRRI will carry out research on technology development for post-harvest management e.g. packaging and agro-processing.",""],[1,"372","2","Agricultural Research Promotion and Innovation Programme","In the 8FYP, emphasis will be given on agricultural research promotion, focusing on developing and refining technologies that will bridge yield gaps and promote diversification and intensification, community farming, sustainable natural resources management (e.g., rain water and river water harvesting for agricultural production), disease and pest management, development of varieties/species with postharvest technology of high value agricultural commodities, frontier researches like genomics and phenomics, physiologial mechanisms regulating photosynthetic efficiency, polyshed and nutrient dense culture, vertical farming, mechanization, etc.",""],[1,"372","2","Climate-Resilient Crop Breeding and Post-Harvest Technology Development","It will also address climate change effects by breeding and introducing saline and drought tolerant, short duration varieties, high value commodities, and low-cost, high-impact post-harvest technologies.",""],[1,"372","2","Agricultural Research and Extension Budget Expansion","For this purpose, budgetary allocation for research and extension should be expanded to at least 5 per cent of Agricultural GDP as against 1.5 per cent of current allocation.",""],[1,"372","11","Agricultural Technology Demonstration and Outreach Activities","Organizing technology demonstration, field days, agricultural exhibition, etc.",""]],"7":[[1,"350","3","Sector-Oriented Adaptation Strategy Development","Advance a sector-oriented approach to experimentation and adaptation: Sector strategies for adaptation, involving the key industry bodies, and combining support for adoption of new technologies, new business methods and models, and new skills.",""],[1,"350","3","Stakeholder Incentive Model Experimentation","Encourage experimentation, particularly with incentive models for different stakeholders, to arrive at the right strategies.",""],[1,"350","4","National Adaptive Collective Intelligence System","National adaptive collective intelligence system: Pool different sources of knowledge to help Bangladesh build labour market resilience.",""],[1,"549","4","Climate Change Trust Fund","To finance BCCTF, the government allocated 3,652 crore Taka so far.",""],[1,"549","5","Pro-Poor Climate Change Management Strategy","A pro-poor Climate Change Management strategy has been implemented emphasizing on adaptation, resilience building, disaster risk reduction, low carbon development, green technology and R&D.",""],[1,"549","6","Disaster and Climate Change Mainstreaming in National Planning","Government has been active in establishing various policies and institutional initiatives to integrate disaster and climate change into its national planning.",""],[1,"550","1","Climate Change Mainstreaming in Union Parishad Planning","Local Government Division also mainstreamed climate change into 72 most climate vulnerable Union Parishad's planning process and supported 300,000 people to build their adaptive capacity against salinity, cyclone, flash flood and floods in coastal, haor and Charlands.","Local Government Division"],[1,"550","1","Revision of the Standing Order on Disaster","the Standing Order on Disaster is revised to address new risks including earthquake, urban disasters following the same principle of whole of society approach.",""],[1,"550","1","Ex-Ante Disaster Impact Assessment Development","development of 'ex-ante' Disaster Impact Assessment (DIA), which is a tool for integrating knowledge and information on potential disasters in the process of 'Risk-informed planning', is underway, pursued by Ministry of Planning.","Ministry of Planning"],[1,"550","1","Digital Risk Information Platform Establishment","the Planning Commission is establishing Digital Risk Information Platform (DRIP) connecting existing initiatives for digital Bangladesh, with an aim to provide necessary disaster and climate risk data and information to carry out Disaster Impact Assessment (DIA) of development projects.","Planning Commission"],[1,"559","4","Climate and Environment Plan Harmonization and Coordination","Coordinating NAP, BCCSAP, CIP and NDC with BDP 2100: Mainstreaming environment and climate change into planning process involves improved governance and coordination and linkage among various plan documents.","GED | MoEFCC | sectoral ministries | ERD | NDA | MoEFCC and DoE"],[1,"562","9","ERD Team for SDG Financing Mobilization","The Government will also form a team with ERD to pursue the US$100 billion to LDCs for achieving SDGs, particularly for climate change adaptation.","ERD"],[1,"568","5","Climate Change Trust Fund Strengthening and Resource Mobilization","The Government will remain committed to strengthening the Climate Change Trust Fund (CCTF) and will mobilize more than Taka 8000crore under the 8FYP to strengthen the Fund further as an instrument support programmes for adaptation and mitigation.",""],[1,"568","5","International Partnership for Climate Adaptation and Mitigation Projects","The Bangladesh Climate Change Trust (BCCT), which is the Government body that overlooks the utilization of the CCTF, will also develop an international partnership with the leading organizations undertaking climate change adaptation and mitigation activities to draw lessons from the international experience, so that innovative projects are funded to support effective measures against climate change.",""],[1,"568","6","Green Climate Fund Access and National Readiness Arrangement","Now, in order to access to the GCF the recipient countries have to ready themselves by meeting certain criteria and standards.",""],[1,"568","6","National Designated Authority for Green Climate Fund Access","the member countries have to assign a National Designated Authority (NDA) to operate the Fund and support the National Implementation Entity (NIE)/Multilateral Implementation Entity (MIE) to access the Fund.",""],[1,"569","1","Accelerate Accreditation of Additional National Implementing Entities","Hence, under the 8FYP, the Government will take more measures to accelerate the accreditation of more NIES.",""],[1,"569","2","Third-Party Monitoring of the Climate Change Trust Fund","The Government will ensure third party monitoring of the Climate Change Trust Fund (CCTF), so that the funds are not misused by any actors undertaking unproductive projects.",""],[1,"569","3","National Adaptation Plan Formulation and Advancement","Bangladesh is formulating the NAP process that is expected to be completed by 2022 with financial and technical support from the GCF and UNDP.",""],[1,"569","3","Climate Adaptation Integration into Policies and Planning","The NAP will facilitate the integration of climate change adaptation into relevant new and existing policies, programmes and activities in a coherent manner, in particular development planning processes and strategies, within all relevant sectors and at different levels, as appropriate.",""],[1,"569","3","Nature-Based Solutions and Ecosystem-Based Adaptation Prioritization","The NAP will give priorities in Nature Based Solution (NBS) and Ecosystem Based Adaptation (EbA).",""],[1,"569","4","Climate Technology Transfer Facilitation","DoE will enhance the activities to facilitate the technology transfer on adaptation and mitigation from developed countries through Climate Technology Centre and Network (CTCN) and Joint Crediting Mechanism (JCM).",""]],"8":[[1,"715","2","Digital Bangladesh Initiative ICT Policy and Access to Information Programme","Under the digital Bangladesh Initiative (DBI) of the Government several Acts and policies have been undertaken: The ICT Policy 2009, the 'Strategies Priorities for Digital Bangladesh 2011', and ICT Policy 2015.","Government | Prime Minister's office"],[1,"724","1","Bangladesh National Enterprise Architecture Framework Roadmap","a roadmap has also been formulated to bring different ministries/departments and departments/agencies under the Bangladesh National Enterprise Architecture Framework.",""],[1,"724","1","Digital Municipality Services System","As part of the implementation of e-Government Master Plan 1 of the 46 initiatives suggested in Master Plan report is being implemented, titled 'Digital Municipality Services System'.",""],[1,"724","1","Digital Sylhet City Project","Digital Sylhet City Project has been initiated to turn Sylhet into country's first smart city.",""],[1,"724","1","Bangladesh E-Government ERP Project","For automation of different government organizations, Bangladesh E- Government ERP Project has developed common ERP software (nine modules) primarily for use of nine organizations under the Planning Division and ICT Division.",""],[1,"724","2","Digital Signature Certificate Services Expansion","These six CA organizations are now providing digital signature certificates and related services to various government and private organizations and to interested individuals.",""],[1,"724","2","Digital Signature Integration Across Public Services","In the meantime, digital signature is being used for E-TIN, e-File system of A2i, birth registration and online admittance letter of the National University.",""],[1,"724","2","Digital Signature Adoption by Organizations and Banks","Different governmental and non-governmental organizations and banks have already started using digital signatures in their own websites and individual level.",""],[1,"726","4","Smart Government Digital Innovation Adoption","The overall strategy is to (i) make the Government smart lead user of digital innovations in meeting line ministries' targets",""],[1,"727","17","Digital Innovation for Smart Public Services","every line ministry should strategically leverage digital innovations to ensure smart and personalized public service.",""],[1,"728","7","Line Ministry Digital Programmes","Develop line ministry specific digital programmes for addressing key mission objectives.",""],[1,"728","8","Line Ministry Digital Programmes and Nationwide Digital Programmes","Establish synergy line ministry specific digital programmes and establish nationwide programmes",""],[1,"747","1","Digital Bangladesh Public Service Transformation Initiative","Since the launch of 'Digital Bangladesh' in 2009, Bangladesh has become a global example of digital transformation of public services.",""],[1,"747","1","National ICT Infra-Network for Bangladesh Government Phase II","The National ICT Infra-Network for Bangladesh Government Phase II was established (which already implemented 800 video conferencing systems at different Ministries, Departments and Upazila offices with the aim to ensure 10Gbps capacity network at the Upazila levels and 100 Gbps capacity networks at the District levels).",""],[1,"747","1","Government E-Governance Initiative","The government's e-governance initiative comprises 5 components - Service Process Simplification (SPS), 'less paper office,' government services portal, land information services, and government forms portal.",""],[1,"747","1","Service Process Simplification Programme","The SPS aims to simplify processes involved in public service delivery and reduce the time required to deliver them.",""],[1,"747","1","Expansion of Citizen-Centred Digital Services","The top five action agenda proposed are: a) effective and scaled up 2000+ citizen centred services; b) paperless government; c) institutionalization of innovation culture; d) citizen's participation of innovation culture; and, e) data-driven policy framework.",""],[1,"748","8","Paperless Government Act","Introduction of Paperless Government Act",""],[1,"749","24","Digital Public Service Delivery Expansion","Enable government to seamlessly offer 2500+ digital services to citizens",""],[1,"749","33","Digital Government Services Access Expansion","Enable 120 million citizens to access government services digitally",""],[1,"750","7","E-Participation and E-Service Delivery Improvement Initiative","The 8FYP will also aim to address the issues of deteriorating e-participation (as tracked by the UN E-Gov Surveys) particularly with regard to e-service delivery.",""],[1,"752","7","E-Government Master Plan","Develop and implement an e-government master plan",""],[1,"760","13","Digital Budget Formulation System for Development Activities","Budget of development activities are formulated in digital system.","Ministry of Information"]],"9":[[1,"230","1","Institutional Performance Improvement Strategy","The Eighth Plan will maintain this focused approach to improve institutional performance",""],[1,"230","1","Governance Reform and Policy Prioritization","the 8th Plan will also prioritize the strategies and policies that were identified in the 7th Plan and are still considered for attaining the developmental transformation that are envisioned in the Perspective Plan 2041.",""],[1,"234","1","Annual Performance Agreement System","the Government has remained committed to the regular use of an effective \"Governance Performance Management System (GPMS)\" by formulating and annually using the \"Annual Performance Agreement- (APA)\", which helps ensure a systematic performance review of all ministries/divisions.",""],[1,"242","2","Public Administration Transparency, Participation and Accountability Reform","The Government is committed to democratic governance, which has motivated the public administration to harness more transparency, participation and accountability within its operations.",""],[1,"242","2","Government Administrative Capacity Strengthening","Consequently, improving the Government's administrative capacity is fundamental for enhancing its effectiveness.",""],[1,"242","3","Participatory Administrative Decision-Making Reform","The Government will ensure greater participation throughout the administrative process to ensure that its policies are formulated and implemented after completing a consultative process with all the stakeholders to enable better outcomes.",""],[1,"242","3","Administrative Transparency and Accountability Measures","This will also ensure better transparency and accountability within the administrative process.",""],[1,"242","4","Shared Vision for Public Administration Framework","The government will ensure that Vision 2041 and the associated PP2041 must be embraced by different organs of the state and government employees must understand and recognize their exact role in ensuring this vision is pursued with upmost rigour and diligence.",""],[1,"242","5","Civil Servant Specialized Training Programme","the Government is committed to offer the civil servants specialised training to general educational and management skills.",""],[1,"242","6","Public Service Commission Strengthening and Financial Autonomy Measures","The Government will continue promoting the merit-based competent bureaucratic apparatus to effectively function as a modern state",""],[1,"243","1","Annual Performance Agreement Strengthening and Expansion","The Government has remained committed to the implementation of the APA under the 7FYP and it has taken a wide range of measures to make the APA an effective institutional arrangement.",""],[1,"243","1","Government Performance Management Policy and Incentive Mechanism","i) formulation of a policy/strategy on government performance management including incentive mechanisms","Cabinet Division"],[1,"243","1","Expansion of Annual Performance Agreement Coverage","ii) extension of APA to all public sector organizations","Cabinet Division"],[1,"243","1","Employee Performance Linkage with APA","iii) linking employee performance with APA to synchronize organizational vision and objective with employee work plan","Cabinet Division"],[1,"243","1","Online APA Management System Upgrade","iv) updating online Annual Performance Agreement Management System (APAMS) for the improvement of preparation, monitoring, reporting and evaluation of the APA of public sector organizations","Cabinet Division"],[1,"243","1","Capacity Enhancement for APA Implementing Agencies","v) enhancement of the capacity of the implementing agencies.","Cabinet Division"],[1,"243","2","Central Grievance Redressal System Improvement","Under the 8FYP, the Government will improve the functioning of the central Grievance Redressal System (GRS).",""],[1,"260","3","Public Administration and Governance Strengthening","More specifically, the need for a more effective coordination mechanism continued strong political leadership, forward-looking attitude within government employees and an effective, transparent and accountable legal framework that guides governance within the public administration cannot be overstated.",""],[1,"260","3","Institutional Investment and Capacity Development","This, nonetheless, considerable investment in institutions will ensure that they are guided by the most adequate laws, infrastructure and human capital.",""],[1,"260","4","Funding for General Administration and Law and Order Services","Accordingly, the 8FYP is committed to provide adequate resources to enable the smooth function of general administration and law and order to ensure safety and security.",""],[1,"260","4","Development Projects for Public Administration Capacity Strengthening","it is understood that many development projects are necessary to enhance capacity and strengthen the underlying services.",""],[1,"260","4","Adaptive Public Administration Planning Framework","the Plan aims to be a living document - and it recognizes flexibility and adaptability are fundamental for achieving the broader objectives of the 8FYP that is linked to PP2041.",""],[1,"342","8","Public Administration Modernization","7) Develop a modern public administration that is consistent with the needs of an Upper Middle- Income Country (UMIC).",""],[1,"346","25","Public Sector Financial Management Strengthening","Strengthen public sector financial management.",""],[1,"347","1","Civil Service ICT Modernization for Decision Making","Modernise civil service decision making through introduction of ICT in policy and decision making, including e-procurement, e-service transactions, e-payments of wages, salaries, pensions, social security and public procurement contracts.",""],[1,"349","3","Digitization of Public Administration","Three broad-based initiatives that can yield considerable long-term benefits are: digitization of public administration; public financial management reforms and a comprehensive training strategy for public administration staff.",""],[1,"349","3","Public Financial Management Reform","Three broad-based initiatives that can yield considerable long-term benefits are: digitization of public administration; public financial management reforms and a comprehensive training strategy for public administration staff.",""],[1,"349","3","Public Administration Staff Training Strategy","Three broad-based initiatives that can yield considerable long-term benefits are: digitization of public administration; public financial management reforms and a comprehensive training strategy for public administration staff.",""],[1,"349","3","E-Procurement, E-Payments, and E-Service Delivery Reform","Adoption of e-procurement, e-payments, and e-service delivery can be instrumental in improving the accountability of public administration and reducing corruption.",""],[1,"349","3","Time-Bound Action Plans for Administrative Reform Areas","For each of these three areas, a time-bound action plan with performance indicators of progress should be adopted.",""],[1,"349","3","Cabinet-Level Monitoring of Administrative Reform Progress","Progress should be monitored at the cabinet level with each line Minister and Secretary responsible for implementation.",""]],"10":[[1,"646","4","Directorate General of Nursing and Midwifery Strengthening","During the implementation of 7FYP, the Government reorganized and upgraded the Directorate of Nursing Service into the Directorate General of Nursing & Midwifery (DGNM) on 6 November, 2016 in order to strengthen, modernize and speed up the development programmes related to nursing education and services, and making the nurses more effective in discharging their responsibilities.",""],[1,"646","4","Bangladesh Nursing and Midwifery Council Reconstruction","The Nursing Council has also been reconstructed into Bangladesh Nursing & Midwifery Council (BNMC).",""],[1,"646","4","Midwifery Workforce Expansion","3,000 posts of Midwives have been created.",""],[1,"646","4","Midwifery Diploma and Web-Based Masters Training","3-years diploma course in midwifery is now in operation in 38 public nursing institutions.",""],[1,"646","4","Midwifery Policy and Quality Assurance Reform","Of particular note is the development of Midwifery policy, accreditation of Midwifery educational institute, introduction of quality midwifery educational system, development of dedicated midwifery faculty, introduction of Midwife led maternal and newborn care, quality licensing examination for the midwife, creation of post in addition to existing post.",""],[1,"647","2","Regional Population Training Institutes and Continuous Provider Training","The MEFWD has also been strengthened training and research activities through NIPORT by establishing regional population training institutes and providing continuous training to the service providers of DGFP, DGHS, DGME, DGNM and others.",""],[1,"648","7","Health Care Facility Accreditation and Quality Assurance","quality assurance of health care facilities through proper accreditation",""],[1,"648","7","Health Workforce Strategy for Skilled Staffing","ensuring availability of skilled human resource (HR) based on an effective and efficient Health Workforce Strategy (HWS)",""],[1,"648","7","Public Health Facility Utilization Expansion","utilizing full capacity of the existing and upgraded public facilities at the district and Upazila level",""],[1,"648","7","Health Sector Governance and Regulatory Strengthening","strengthening governance, stewardship and regulatory functions",""],[1,"648","7","Health Sector Resource Mobilization and Budget Efficiency","mobilizing more resources for the HPN sector efficient and effective use of budget including a proper balance between new facilities and adequacy of materials and supplies",""],[1,"648","7","Rural Health Worker Retention Measures","retaining skilled health service staff in rural areas",""],[1,"649","3","Health Workforce Training Quality Improvement","Ensuring quality in the training of doctors, nurses, midwives and medical assistants.",""],[1,"649","4","Private Medical Education Regulation and Quality Assurance","Regulating the medical education institutions of the private sector and maintaining their teaching quality.",""],[1,"654","4","Medical Education and HPN Service Upgradation","Quality of medical education & training and HPN services will be ensured through upgradation of the educational facilities/institutes and service facilities, modernization of examination process, inclusion of new subjects in curricula, provision of specialty and sub-specialty positions etc.",""],[1,"656","10","Capacity Building for Service Providers","Building capacity of the various service providers under MoHFW and MoLGRD&C.","MoHFW | MoLGRD&C"],[1,"658","1","School Health Teachers' Training and Healthy School Environment Programme","Sustaining and expanding the ongoing School Health Teachers' Training activities including promotion of healthy school environment and practices, nutrition education etc.",""],[1,"658","2","Health Worker Training Programme","Carrying out appropriate training of the doctors, nurses, paramedics and field and community workers as per need.",""],[1,"658","7","Training for Health Service Providers and Community Health Workers","Carrying out appropriate training of service providers of health and community health workers.",""],[1,"663","2","Health Workforce Education Quality Improvement","MoHFW will focus on improving quality of public and private pre-service health workforce education system","MoHFW"],[1,"663","2","Health Service Management Capacity Development","capacity development to ensure better management at all levels of service delivery","MoHFW"],[1,"663","2","Medical Education Quality Assurance Strengthening","strengthening quality assurance of medical education at both private and public sector institutions through licensing and accreditation",""],[1,"663","2","Vacant Health Position Filling Initiative","During the 8FYP period, all vacant positions of MoHFW will be gradually filled up","MoHFW"],[1,"665","2","Health and Nutrition Pre-service and In-service Training Programme","DGHS, DGFP, DGME and DGNM will continue to provide pre-service and in-service training in various fields of health and nutrition services to develop skills based on a good diagnostic of the skills mix and the skills gap and generate information through research/ studies for having quality human resources in HPN services.","MoHFW"],[1,"665","5","In-Service Training for Service Delivery Staff","In-service training in various fields of service delivery of the officers and technical support staff at all levels including those of managers/administrative personnel need to be continued.",""],[1,"666","5","Health Workforce Strategy and Rolling Production Plan","Update and implement the Health Workforce Strategy (HWS) and a 5-yearly rolling plan to guide production (number with skill-mix) of doctors and nurses.",""],[1,"666","7","In-Service Local and Foreign Training for Field-Level Physicians","Health personnel specially physicians who working in the field level should be given more emphasis for in service local and foreign training to keep them in locality",""],[1,"666","8","Retention Support for Upazila-Level Health Personnel","Facilities and opportunities need to be created for the health personnel to keep them working in upazila level",""],[1,"666","9","Demand-Based Higher Studies for Health Personnel","Demand based higher studies should be made available for health personnel specially physicians",""],[1,"667","1","Expansion of Ongoing Medical Education Program","future activities/programmes including expansion of the on-going ones will need to be developed with due emphasis on producing quality human resources for health.","MoHFW"],[1,"667","7","Continuous Teacher Training for Medical Education and Health Services","Continuous training of teachers for improvement of quality medical education as well as health services.",""],[1,"667","8","Teacher Research Capacity Enhancement in Medical Education","Enhance research activity of teachers in medical education and health related issues.",""],[1,"667","16","Nursing and Midwifery Workforce Expansion and Skills Training","Increasing the number of nurses and midwives through creating additional seats in nursing institutions and continue to provide skill development training to them.",""],[1,"667","19","Online Nursing Services Expansion","Strengthen and expand online nursing services.",""],[1,"667","20","Nursing and Midwifery Work Plan and On-the-Job Training Plan","Preparation of nursing and midwifery work plan for realizing the SDGs and preparation of training plan for on the job training.",""],[1,"667","21","Specialized Nurse Training Programme","Produce specialized nurses as demanded by the specialized hospitals.",""],[1,"668","1","In-Service Training and Nutrition Research Programme","NIPORT will have to continue to provide in-service training to develop skills and generate information through research/ studies with a view to have quality human resources for nutrition service provision and promotion in HPN services.",""],[1,"668","2","Health and Family Planning Workforce Orientation and Training Curriculum Development","Preparation of training curriculum, modules, etc. and organize orientation courses for the newly recruited medical officers, senior staff nurses, FWAs, FWVs, other health and FP professionals and workers including nutrition workers, etc.",""],[1,"668","3","Trainer Training and Curriculum Update for Competency-Based Training","Conduct training of the trainers on competency-based training, updating of curriculum and printing.",""],[1,"668","5","HPN Services Operations and Collaborative Research Capacity Building","Conduct operations research and collaborative research for improvement of HPN services and improve research capacity building.",""],[1,"671","14","Nutrition Staff Recruitment Acceleration","Expedite the recruitment of relevant nutrition staff where required at community and facility level",""]],"11":[[1,"668","10","Cross-Sector Nutrition Coordination Mechanism","The key strategies and actions to be pursued during the 8FYP are continuation of nutrition service through regular government channels, micro-nutrient supplementation, treatment of severe acute malnutrition, strengthening BCC to promote good nutritional practices, coordination of nutrition activities across different sectors and mainstreaming gender into nutrition programming and promoting equity.",""],[1,"669","1","Multi-sectoral Nutrition Strategy Strengthening","The 8FYP will build on the progress and strengthen the nutrition strategy to achieve the targeted nutrition outcomes.",""],[1,"669","1","Revitalized Bangladesh National Nutrition Council Coordination Mechanism","Nutrition related policy guidance and inter/intra ministerial linkages will be facilitated through the revitalized Bangladesh National Nutrition Council (BNNC).",""],[1,"669","1","Cabinet Committee Coordination for Food and Nutrition Security","existing cabinet committees that address food and nutrition security will contribute to effective coordination of nutrition programming.",""],[1,"669","1","Inter-Ministerial Nutrition and Food Safety Collaboration","The MoHFW will collaborate with the Ministry of LGRD&C, the Ministry of Agriculture, and the Ministry of Food to address nutrition and food safety issues.","MoHFW | Ministry of LGRD&C | Ministry of Agriculture | Ministry of Food"],[1,"669","8","Food Safety Regulatory Framework Strengthening","Promote best practice to ensure food safety in agriculture sector, food processing industries, food distribution system and in food value chain · Ensure adequate food safety regulatory framework in place and monitored",""],[1,"671","9","Inter-sectoral and Inter-OP Nutrition Collaboration and Implementation Strengthening","Strengthening inter-sectoral and inter-OP collaboration and efficient program implementation for nutrition.",""],[1,"671","12","Nutrition, Food Safety, and Healthy Diets Regulatory Enforcement Mechanism","Develop and strengthen the regulatory mechanism and ensure implementation of policies, action plans, and acts on nutrition, food safety, and healthy diets.",""],[1,"671","13","Service Coverage Expansion through Inter-Ministerial Alignment","Increase coverage of services by aligning with relevant services and interventions hosted by other ministries, such as Maternal Allowance and Lactating Mothers Allowance/Child Benefit programme",""]],"12":[[1,"5","5","Rooppur Nuclear Power Plant Construction","Considering the future power demand of an economy that is aspiring to become an upper-middle-income country by 2031 and a status of a high-income country by 2041 building of the Rooppur Nuclear Power Plant is underway.",""],[1,"58","3","Power Sector Projects Acceleration","major initiatives will be taken to broaden and accelerate the implementation of other major highways and bridges, power sector projects, and providing access to serviced land to foreign and domestic investors in the context of the Special Economic Zones (SEZ) initiative.",""],[1,"61","2","Power Sector Master Plan Update and Power Expansion Programme","The 8FYP power and energy strategy will continue the ongoing good work and strengthen the strategy in several areas.",""],[1,"61","2","Renewable Energy Incentive Measures","Second, emphasis will be placed on renewable energy trough proper fuel-oil pricing and other incentives.",""],[1,"61","2","Power and Energy Sector Financial Reform","Third, the power and energy sector finances will be improved through institutional reforms and pricing policies.",""],[1,"61","2","Energy Conservation and Efficiency Improvement Measures","Fourth, energy conservation and efficiency improvements will be promoted through proper O&M of power facilities, through adoption of energy efficient technology, and through pricing and taxation of energy consumption.",""],[1,"87","4","Electricity Supply Expansion and Power Sector Reform Programme","the Government followed up on its strong progress with increase in power supply and access to electricity during the 6FYP with another round of a strong and well-rounded reform programme to increase the supply of electricity involving substantial investment, sector reforms and regional trade during the 7FYP",""],[1,"87","4","Power System Master Plan Revision","The Government, which had been implementing the power sector programmes based on the Power System Master Plan (PSMP) 2010 during the 6th Plan, revised it to PSMP 2016, to help adapt to changing scenarios during the 7FYP",""],[1,"88","2","Renewable Energy Expansion in Power Supply","The 8FYP will put stronger focus on these aspects of power and energy sector development.",""],[1,"88","2","Power and Energy Sector Financial Strengthening","The 8FYP will put stronger focus on these aspects of power and energy sector development.",""],[1,"291","1","Power Sector Investment Programme","the government is planning to invest around $70 billion in the power sector over the next 15 years",""],[1,"409","4","Energy Efficiency and Renewable Energy Expansion in the Power Sector","The Government will continue on this path, leading into the 8FYP, but with increased focus on energy efficiency gain, renewable energy and financial sustainability.",""],[1,"409","4","Competitive Least-Cost Power System Development","This will enable Bangladesh to move to a competitive and environmentally sustainable least- cost power generation, transmission, and distribution system along with greater private sector participation and own resource mobilization so as to reduce the burden on limited fiscal resources.",""],[1,"409","4","Timely Implementation of Power and Energy Projects","The 8FYP will also focus on timely implementation of all power and energy projects so as to optimize achieving the goals of Government's energy sector strategy, whose key elements are:",""],[1,"413","1","Review and Replacement of Inefficient Rental Power Plants","there should be review on the higher cost and less efficient rental and other power plants, and look for ways to closing those and replacing them with more efficient ones including increased generation from RE.",""],[1,"418","3","Optimal Reserve Margin for Power Supply","While some surplus will have to be generated as reserve margin to ensure unhindered quality power supply during the 8th plan period and beyond, this will be done in an optimum mode where efficiency of the reserve margin will also be considered.",""],[1,"428","2","Long-Term Power Development Plan","The Government has adopted polices and legislations to set up long- term power development plan in order to reduce electricity production cost and ensure sustainable development of power sector.",""],[1,"429","6","Contingent Backup Power Generation Planning","Given the uncertainties in the supply side of primary energy, contingent planning will be necessary to have back-up power generation plans that respond to these uncertainties.",""],[1,"429","7","Power Sector Development","The development of the power sector, which continued to remain on top priority during seventh plan, will continue to remain so during the Eighth Plan period.",""],[1,"429","8","Least-Cost Power Generation System Development","During the eighth plan period the effort will be to build a fiscally sound efficient least cost power generation system, with increasing renewable energy as a source for power production.",""],[1,"429","8","Retirement of Inefficient Power Generation Capacity","These need to be replaced by not only more efficient and least cost fuelled power generation, but also by higher use of renewable energy-based power generation.",""],[1,"431","11","Update of the PSMP-2016","The PSMP-2016 shall soon be updated by JICA considering demand, generation capacity, reserve margin etc.",""],[1,"432","1","Least-Cost Power Generation Mix Strategy","Move towards the strategy for achieving the least cost energy mix for generation during the 8th plan period.",""],[1,"433","1","Least-Cost Power Generation Transition","During the 8th Plan period and beyond focus would be to completely move out of the rental plant contracts and also the inefficient small scale IPPs, and move the desired least-cost power production regime where efficiency and economy of the power plants will the only consideration.",""],[1,"433","1","Competitive Power Sector Bidding Reform","This will also mean that there needs to be good competition in the bidding process so that incentives can be built in for ensuring increased efficiency.",""],[1,"433","2","Power Generation Program","Power Generation Program now under implementation and some to be completed during the Eighth Plan Period: In order to meet future demand 44 new power plants have been under various stages of construction with a total capacity of 15924 MW.",""],[1,"433","4","Additional Power Generation Expansion","During the 8th Plan period, the Power Division plans to generate approximately additional 15,700 MW (inclusive of imports but exclusive of renewable energy) of power.",""],[1,"433","7","Diversified Fuel-Mix Power Generation Projects","New projects with diversified fuel-mix identified for implementation during the 8th plan period.",""],[1,"434","4","Rooppur Nuclear Power Plant Development","Rooppur Nuclear Power Plant is one of the top priority projects of the government.",""],[1,"435","2","Review and Retirement of Inefficient Power Plants","One important area will be to look into the possibility of retirement and of the higher cost and less efficient rental and SIPP power plants, as well as any inefficient public sector power plants.",""],[1,"435","2","National Power Capacity Expansion Plan","The government plans to increase capacity to 30,000 MW by end of 8th Plan period (Table 5.17).",""],[1,"548","1","Fiscal Incentives for Renewable Energy Investment","During the 7FYP, fiscal initiatives have been designed by providing tax incentives to encourage investment in renewable energy ventures.",""],[1,"548","1","Microcredit Support for Renewable Energy Equipment","The Government has also developed a network of microcredit providers in remote rural areas to provide funding for the purchase of renewable energy equipment;",""],[1,"564","7","Renewable Energy Expansion Programme","the Government plans to sharply increase the total generation of power from renewable during the 8FYP.",""],[1,"577","1","Fuel Wood Saving Devices and Clean Cooking Promotion","Networking with relevant government agencies and NGOs promoting renewable energy will be strengthened and subsidies for adoption of improved cook stoves, solar cookers, biogas etc. will be provided among forest dependent communities.",""]],"13":[[1,"52","4","Disaster Management and Early Warning System Strengthening","The disaster management programmes have continued to perform well.",""],[1,"93","6","National Disaster Management Plan Implementation","This progress was defined by the government's implementation of the National Disaster Management Plan 2010-15, the enactment of the National Disaster Act in 2012, preparation of Disaster Management Rules in",""]],"14":[[1,"452","6","National Road Safety Strategic Action Plan","RHD has formulated the National Road Safety Strategic Action Plan (NRSSAP) 2017-20, which is being implemented in accordance with the road safety related targets set forth under SDG.",""],[1,"452","6","Strengthening Road Safety Implementation Capacity","Further efforts are needed to strengthen implementation of road safety measures.",""],[1,"459","4","Road Safety and Traffic Law Enforcement","Progress was also made in addressing road safety and enforcing traffic laws and regulations.",""],[1,"462","10","Parking and Traffic Law Enforcement","All parking and traffic laws are enforced with appropriate sanctions for non-compliance irrespective of political or administration connections.",""],[1,"462","15","Automated Vehicle Inspection Centres","Vehicle road worthiness (fitness) is well tested through automated vehicle inspection centres.",""],[1,"465","3","Transport Service Quality and Safety Policy Package","The 8FYP will seek to adopt a number of policies to improve infrastructure and service quality.",""],[1,"465","3","Road Accident Reduction and Enforcement Measures","The government has already taken a number of policy initiatives to reduce road accidents and enforce them with legal sanctions for non-compliance and liability for accidents.",""],[1,"465","4","Vehicle Exhaust Emission Standards","Vehicle exhaust emission standards will be set in line with similar standards as of neighbouring/ similar countries.",""],[1,"465","4","Automated Vehicle Fitness Test Centres","Policy initiatives will be taken to establish automated vehicle fitness test centres.",""],[1,"465","4","Driver Training and Road Safety Awareness Programme","drivers training along with mass road safety awareness programmes will be performed on priority basis.",""],[1,"467","2","Strict Axle Load Control Policy","Accordingly, strict axle load control policy would be established and enforced to reduce road damages caused by overloading.",""],[1,"467","4","Separate Slow-Moving Vehicle Lane on Roads","Additionally, to reduce the risks of accidents, there should be a separate lane for slow-moving vehicles.",""],[1,"468","4","National Road Sector Safety Action Plan Implementation","the full and proper implementation of the National Road Sector Safety Action Plan (NRSSAP) 2017-20 will be an important priority for the 8FYP.",""]],"15":[[1,"328","10","River Dredging Investment Programme","Huge investments are needed for river dredging to make them navigable and conducive to the use of modern river vessels.",""],[1,"329","1","River Dredging and Port Capacity Investment Programme","A third problem is the inadequacy of river ports and cargo handling capacities.",""],[1,"329","1","River Transport Safety Standards Monitoring and Enforcement","it is obvious that a combination of major investments in river dredging and river ports combined with effective monitoring and implementation of safety standards will substantially improve the quality of water transport and spur private investment and value-added.",""],[1,"345","17","Major River Route Dredging and Maintenance Programme","Initiate dredging of major river routes with provisions of maintenance dredging.",""],[1,"345","18","River Docking and Storage Capacity Upgrade","Upgrade river docking and storage capacities in major cities.",""],[1,"348","12","River Vessel Inspection and Load Monitoring","Strict inspection of all river vessels and monitoring of vessel loads.",""],[1,"454","1","Inland Water Transport Constraint-Offsetting and Network Improvement Programme","The 8FYP will seek to offset these constraints and improve the role of inland water transportation to improve the inter-modal balance, reduce transport cost, and protect the environment.",""],[1,"464","3","Inland Water Transport and Railway Development Priority","The 8FYP will give priority to developing these modes to reduce the pressure on roads and also to strengthen inter-modal coordination.",""],[1,"464","3","Port-to-Factory Gate River Transport Logistics Improvement","The Port to factory gate connection and vice versa via river routes, for example, can be a major improvement in trade logistics.",""],[1,"471","19","Inland Water Transport Development Strategy","Consistent with BDP2100 and the PP2041 strategy, the 8FYP will seek to harness this potential for both passenger and cargo traffic.",""],[1,"471","20","Priority River Routing and Port Infrastructure Development","Establish priority routing based on potential passenger and freight traffic flows and develop those navigability improvements and river port infrastructures.",""],[1,"471","21","River Route Navigability Improvement Programme","Sharply improve the navigability of river routes through strategic dredging, river training, and bundling as emphasized in BDP2100.",""],[1,"471","22","Inter-Regional River Connectivity Enhancement","Give priority to inter-regional river connectivity to facilitate trade, commerce and tourism.",""],[1,"471","23","Integrated Inland Water Transport with Other Transport Modes","Integrate IWT with other transport modes to maximize the benefits of IWT.",""],[1,"472","1","River Transport Safety Standards and Compliance Enforcement","Strengthen river transport safety standards by setting proper standards and ensuring full compliance.",""],[1,"472","2","Vessel Worthiness Licensing System","Vessel worthiness licensing would ensure minimum service facilities and standards of all vessels.",""],[1,"472","3","BIWTA Technical and Inspection Capacity Strengthening","Bangladesh Inland Water Transport Authority (BIWTA) will be strengthened with technical staff and qualified inspectors to administer all licensing functions efficiently and on time.",""],[1,"472","4","BIWTA Hydrological Survey, River Training and Dredging Capacity Expansion","The capacity of BIWTA to undertake hydrological surveys, conduct river training and implement dredging operations will be expanded through upgrading the managerial and technical staff and international training.",""],[1,"472","4","Private Sector Participation in BIWTA Operations through PPPs","Side by side, the private sector will be invited to participate in these operations on a PPP basis.",""],[1,"472","5","Public-Private Balance for Inland Water Transport Development","Given the large need for resources, a proper balance between the public and private sector will be maintained.",""],[1,"472","6","River Port Facilities Modernization","River port facilities will be sharply improved with modern service standards for passengers, docking and unloading services for cargo including container cargo, storage facilities and security and rescue services.",""],[1,"472","6","Customs and Inspection Services at International River Ports","International river ports of call will also provide customs and inspection services as relevant.",""],[1,"472","7","Commercially Determined Passenger and Cargo Pricing Policy","Pricing policies for passenger and cargo will be commercially determined with a view to enabling a reasonable rate of return on investment.",""]],"16":[[1,"450","2","Dhaka Mass Rapid Transit Development","Recognizing the special challenge posed by growing urbanization and urban traffic congestion, the 7FYP sought to introduce Mass Rapid Transit (MRT) starting with the capital city Dhaka and its adjoining, with a targeted completion of MRT Line-6 (the first elevated Metro Rail of Bangladesh) in December 2022.",""],[1,"459","4","Revised Strategic Transport Plan for Greater Dhaka","A Revised Strategic Transport Plan (RSTP) was prepared by Dhaka Transport Coordination Authority (DTCA) for greater Dhaka area.","Dhaka Transport Coordination Authority (DTCA)"],[1,"459","4","Dhaka Mass Rapid Transit Network Development","The Government has formulated a Time-bound Action Plan 2030 in order to establish a state-of-the-art Network of public transport system to be implemented by Dhaka Mass Transit Company Limited (DMTCL) consisting of 6 Mass Rapid Transit (MRT) or Metrorail Lines covering the distance of 128.741 Kilometres (67.57 kilometres elevated and 61.17 kilometers underground) having 104 Stations (51 elevated and 53 underground) in Dhaka and its adjoining areas.","Dhaka Mass Transit Company Limited (DMTCL)"],[1,"459","4","MRT Line-6 Construction and Completion","Based on this action plan, the targeted completion of the first elevated Metro Rail of Bangladesh, known as MRT Line-6, has been set for December 2022.",""],[1,"459","4","Construction of Additional MRT Lines","Substantial progress of construction works of four more MRT Lines (Line-1; Line-5: Northern Route; Line-5: Southern Route and Line-2) are also underway within the 7FYP (Table 6.8).",""],[1,"459","4","Dhaka BRT Line 3 Development","Work has also started on the first of the three proposed rapid bus transit (BRT) alleviated expressway.",""],[1,"459","4","Dhaka Subway Feasibility Study","Besides, Bridges Division has undertaken a feasibility study project for the construction of subway across 238 km covering the entire Dhaka city.","Bridges Division"],[1,"462","9","Urban Mass Rapid Transit and Bus Service Network","Urban traffic flows are well managed through a combination of Mass Rapid Transit (MRT) /Metro Rail Network, BRTC Double Decker/Articulated Bus Service and private options that balance commuter needs for easy transit with avoidance of massive congestion.",""],[1,"463","2","Mass Rapid Transit and Metro Rail Network Introduction","Urban transport changes are particularly dramatic as Mass Rapid Transit (MRT)/Metro Rail Network transit options are introduced initially in the capital city of Dhaka and its adjoining areas.",""],[1,"468","5","Bus Route Rationalization and Company-Based Bus Operation","Dhaka Transport Coordination Authority (DTCA) takes an initiative to implement bus route rationalization and company- based bus operation in Dhaka city.",""],[1,"468","6","Integrated Traffic Management in Dhaka City","Integrated Traffic Management: In order to reduce traffic congestion in Dhaka city through intersection improvement and Intelligent Traffic System (ITS) is being implemented by DTCA.",""],[1,"475","1","Urban Transport Strategy","The main objective of the 8FYP urban transport strategy will be to support sustainable urban development.",""],[1,"475","2","Mass Rapid Transit Metro Rail Completion","Completion of Mass Rapid Transit (MRT) Metro Rail, both elevated and underground rail, initially in Dhaka City and its adjoining areas.",""],[1,"475","3","Bus Rapid Transit System for Divisional Cities","Provision of Bus Rapid Transit (BRT) that is characterized by dedicated lanes for rapid movement of buses for all divisional cities.",""],[1,"475","8","Metropolitan Area Bus Rapid Transit and Metro Rail Linkage Development","Strengthening linkages with cities and towns around Metropolitan Areas through Bus Rapid Transit (BRT) and Mass Rapid Transit (MRT /Metro Rail).",""],[1,"614","4","Dhaka Flyover Construction Programme","For addressing the transport problems of Dhaka megacity, the government has implemented several flyover projects",""],[1,"614","4","Dhaka Metro Rail Project","and is currently implementing a metro-rail project",""],[1,"614","5","Dhaka Mass Transit Development Program","the government has initiated a major program to introduce mass transit facilities for Dhaka.",""],[1,"621","5","Integrated Urban Transportation System Development","Urban transportation strategies will focus on developing an integrated and balanced transportation system taking into consideration the needs of the road system, non-motorized transport, public passenger transport and mass transit issues such as a city's balance in the locations of employment and housing, demand management, and the roles for the public and private sectors.",""],[1,"621","6","Rail-Based Mass Transit and Bus Rapid Transit Expansion","Steps, therefore, have been taken to introduce rail-based mass transit system and Bus Rapid Transit in Dhaka.",""],[1,"621","7","Comprehensive Urban Traffic Management Plan","Preparation of comprehensive traffic management plan for major cities which includes establishment of hierarchy of roads, ensure footpath and pedestrian ways, provide sustainable and efficient public transport services and ensure multi-modal integration.",""],[1,"621","8","Sustainable Urban Public Transport Services","Provision of sustainable and appropriate public transport services in cities and ensuring regulatory measure for efficient, reliable, affordable, and convenient public transport services.",""],[1,"622","2","City-Specific Non-Motorized Transport Comprehensive Planning","Preparation of city specific comprehensive plan for Non-Motorized Transport fostering safer non- motorized vehicle operations.",""],[1,"622","3","Inclusive Urban Road Infrastructure Development","Urban road projects in large, medium and small municipalities should be developed as inclusive infrastructures i.e. roads, drains, footpath, median simultaneously.",""],[1,"622","4","Traffic and Road Discipline Enforcement Using Infrared Cameras","Imposition of traffic and road discipline strictly taking help of loses circuit infrared cameras.",""],[1,"622","5","Driver Training and Skills Development","Ensuring training and appropriate skill for drivers",""],[1,"622","6","Transit-Oriented Development Promotion","Patronizing Transit Oriented Development (TOD) in cities with high capacity public transportation (MRT/LRT/BRT).",""],[1,"622","8","Integrated Waterway, Rail, and Road Transport Development","Establishment of water ways where appropriate and integrate with rail and road",""],[1,"622","9","Transport and Public Transport Institutional Restructuring","Restructuring institutional arrangement to manage transport and public transport services and enhance capacity of the concerned institution.",""],[1,"622","10","Traffic Demand Management Measures","Introduction of traffic demand management to reduce traffic volume through such measures as parking prohibitions, fuel pricing, charges for use of specific routes, limiting entry to city centre, encouragement to public transport, pedestrianization of congested areas, etc.",""],[1,"622","11","Intelligent Transport System for Dhaka","Introduction of Intelligent Transport System (ITS) in Dhaka for covering such areas as electronic road pricing, traffic management, integrated ticketing systems for different public transport modes, and coordination of public transport modes and online timetables.",""],[1,"625","2","Public Transport Improvement and Metro Rail Development","Improvement of public transport- metro rail, Rapid Bus Transit, good rail network, good network of navigable rivers encouraging private sector participation.",""],[1,"626","1","City Transportation Plan Update with Disaster Risk Reduction Measures","Review and update the city's transportation plan to include disaster risk reduction measures (providing accessibility to and linkages with risk-prone areas).",""],[1,"627","7","Transport Connectivity Infrastructure Construction","Construct link roads, flyovers, underpasses, overpasses and bypasses",""],[1,"629","18","Urban Roads and Municipal Infrastructure Construction, Rehabilitation and Maintenance","Construction, rehabilitation and maintenance of city roads, footpaths, drains, street lights, bus-truck terminals, parking lots and other infrastructure.",""],[1,"629","22","Urban Flyover and Bridge Construction Programme","Construction of flyovers, foot over bridges and link bridges in city areas",""],[1,"630","25","Urban Transport Corridors and Ring Roads in Dhaka","The Revised Strategic Transport Plan (RSTP) has proposed the following Urban Transport Corridors and Ring Roads in Dhaka to be implemented by 2035:",""],[1,"631","6","Eastern Bypass Corridor Transport Infrastructure Development","A project is already underway.",""],[1,"631","7","Dhaka Bypass Construction under PPP","RHD has signed a contract with China Joint Venture Company to construct 48 km Dhaka bypass (Joydebpur - Debugram - Bhulta - Madanpur) in eastern side by PPP which will be completed in September, 2022.",""],[1,"631","7","Western Middle Ring Road PPP Feasibility and Construction","The western side of Middle Ring Road (Hemayetpur - Kalakandi - 3rd Shitalakkhya Bridge - Madanpur) is under consideration for construction with G2G on PPP basis with Marubeni Corporation of Japan.",""],[1,"632","2","Alignment Feasibility Study","Dhaka Transport Coordination Authority (DTCA) has taken steps to conduct a feasibility study for the alignment.","Dhaka Transport Coordination Authority (DTCA)"]],"17":[[1,"450","1","East-West Railway Linkage Development","establishment of effective railway linkages between the east and west zones of the country",""],[1,"453","9","Railway Investment Program","The Railway investment program was guided by the Railway Master Plan 2010-2030 that was approved in 2004 and updated in 2017.",""],[1,"453","9","Rail Infrastructure Expansion and Rehabilitation","which included construction of new line, procurement of rolling stock for passenger and freight, and rehabilitation of existing railway station and signalling system.",""],[1,"470","1","New Rail Line Construction","Construction of 798 km new rail line.",""],[1,"470","2","Dual Gauge Double Tracking Expansion","Implement dual gauge double tracking of 897 km to increase line capacity.",""],[1,"470","3","Rail Line Rehabilitation and Upgrade","Rehabilitate/ Upgrade 846 km existing rail line.",""],[1,"470","4","Construction of Nine Major Railway Bridges","Construct 9 important railway bridges",""],[1,"470","5","Locomotive Procurement Programme","Procure160 locomotives to enhance the efficiency, ensure reliability & punctuality of running trains and to introduce new trains.",""],[1,"470","6","Passenger Coach and Wagon Procurement","Procure 1704 passenger coaches and 2000 wagons to improve passenger service quality",""],[1,"470","7","Railway Maintenance Modernization Equipment Procurement","Procure adequate equipment to modernize railway maintenance",""],[1,"470","8","Railway Workshop Modernization","Modernize Railway Workshop and other infrastructure.",""],[1,"470","10","Station Signaling System Modernization","Modernize signaling system of 222 stations to ensure safety.",""],[1,"470","11","Bangladesh Railway Efficiency and Performance Improvement","Increase efficiency and improve performance of Bangladesh Railway",""],[1,"470","14","Bangladesh Railway Master Plan Implementation","To expand capacity and improve service, the BR has updated its Master Plan to align it in line with the PP2041 Vision and also aligning with the government's plans & policy statements like 7th Five Years Plan, Vision 2021, Delta Plan 2100 etc. to enhance operational capacity, increase market shares and improve its services.",""],[1,"470","15","Railway Expansion Program","The railway expansion program envisaged in Box 6.2 will be undertaken with due regards to projected demand for passenger and freight services with a view to maximizing the use of associated capacity expansion.",""],[1,"470","16","Regional Rail Connectivity Enhancement","Connectivity to regional train services involving neighbouring countries will be a priority.",""],[1,"470","17","Modern Railway Signalling and Telecommunications Upgrade","Introduction and/or up gradation of modern signalling system with relevant safety measures of international standard and introduction of a proper telecommunication system.",""],[1,"470","18","Mechanized Track Maintenance System","Introduction of mechanized track maintenance system.",""],[1,"470","19","Operations and Maintenance Safety Standards Strengthening","Strengthen O&M practices following internationally recognized safety standards.",""],[1,"470","21","Port-Bound Freight Train Turnaround Time Reduction","Reduction of turnaround time for the port bound freight trains.",""],[1,"470","22","Modern Train Management System with Centralized Traffic Control","Introduction of a modern train management system with the Centralized Traffic Control System.",""],[1,"470","23","Railway Station Redevelopment and Passenger Amenities Improvement","Redevelopment of stations for smooth flow and comfortable experience of passengers as also with ensuring cleanliness and hygienic environment.",""],[1,"470","25","Railway Human Resources Upgradation for Commercial Service Delivery","Up gradation of railway human resources aimed at commercializing services.",""],[1,"470","26","Coach Redesign for Passenger Comfort and Safety","Redesign of coaches to enhance travel comfort and safety.",""],[1,"471","3","Demand-Based New Train Service Expansion","Increase new train service based on demand.",""],[1,"471","4","Development of Modern Inland Container Depots","Development of new modern Inland Container Depots with the increasing number of block train to carry container from port to destination.",""],[1,"471","5","National Railway Connectivity Expansion","Ensure railway connectivity to every district of Bangladesh.",""],[1,"471","6","Railway Network Reconstruction, Modernization and Extension","Reconstruction, modernization and extension of missing links for national, regional and Trans Asian Railway Network.",""],[1,"471","7","Dedicated Freight Corridor Development","Development of dedicated freight corridors.",""],[1,"471","8","Commuter Train Services","Introduction of Commuter Train Services for reducing traffic jam in megacities.",""],[1,"471","9","Electric Traction Introduction in Bangladesh Railway","Introduction of electric traction in Bangladesh Railway.",""],[1,"471","10","Workshop Development and Rolling Stock Maintenance Equipment Procurement","Development of new Workshops.",""],[1,"471","11","Intermediate Block System and Automatic Train Supervision Installation","Introduction of Intermediate Block System and Installation of Automatic Train Supervision (ATS) including Automatic Train Protection (ATP) with existing CBI and CTC system in the selected corridors.",""],[1,"471","12","Railway Zonal and Divisional Expansion","Creation of two additional zones and four additional divisions in Railway for better and effective management of railway services.",""],[1,"471","13","Improved Customs Clearance Arrangements for Inter-Regional Services","Improved custom clearance arrangements for inter-regional services with neighbouring countries.",""],[1,"471","15","Business Planning to Expand Passenger and Freight Market Share","Strengthen business planning to capture a higher market share of passenger and freight traffic including special services for tourist and high-end users.",""],[1,"471","16","Railway Training Academy Upgradation and Construction","Up gradation/construction of railway training academy.",""],[1,"471","17","Bangladesh Railway Multi-Modal Transport Operator Reform","Bangladesh Railway to act as a multi-modal transport operator.",""],[1,"471","18","Railway Tariff Modernization","Railway tariffs will be modernized so as to cover full operating cost by FY2025.",""]],"18":[[1,"458","2","Development and Operation of Remaining Land Ports","With a view to start operation of the remaining land ports, the process for acquiring land along with the construction of necessary infrastructures are going on.",""],[1,"458","3","Land Port Development and Modernization Programme","To enhance connectivity and trade with neighbouring countries, BLPA has taken steps for development of Sheola and Ramgarh land ports along with extension & modernization of Bhomra and Benapole Land Ports with a cost Tk. 693 crore with the financial assistance of World Bank.",""],[1,"458","3","Land Port Digitalization Initiative","Necessary steps have already been taken for digitalization of land ports.",""],[1,"474","18","Land Port Modernization and Freight Clearance Efficiency Improvement","the 8FYP will seek to build on the progress made in the 7FYP and further improve the quality and lower transaction costs of land port freight.",""],[1,"474","18","Upgrading of Existing Land Ports with Modern Facilities and Digital Technology","The upgrading effort of exiting land ports with modern facilities and use of digital technology will continue.",""],[1,"474","18","Land Port Governance and ICT-Based Clearance Reform","Freight clearing time lines will be reduced through governance improvements, stronger supervision, reduction in paper work and use of ICT.",""],[1,"474","18","International Benchmarking Study of Land Port Clearance Procedures","Land port clearance procedures in Europe and North America will be studied to see how these experiences can be used to improve land port efficiency",""]],"19":[[1,"450","1","Modern Transport Technology and Capacity Improvement","Special emphasis was placed on the introduction of modern technology for increasing capacity and improving quality and productivity of the system",""],[1,"450","1","Integrated Multimodal Transport Connectivity","integration of road, rail and inland water transport",""],[1,"450","1","Regional and Global Transport Connectivity Participation","participation in global and regional transport connectivity initiatives that help to develop the land route links between South Asia and East Asia through Bangladesh",""],[1,"450","2","Public-Private Partnership Transport Financing","Mindful of the resource constraints and high investment costs, the 7FYP strategy was to combine ADP allocations with a strong public-private-partnership (PPP) effort.",""],[1,"450","2","Intermodal Transport Balance Improvement","The plan also intended to improve the inter-modal transport balance with greater emphasis on rail and inland waterways that are low- cost in nature and are environmentally friendly compared to other mode of transport.",""],[1,"450","2","Transport User Charges and Fee Reform","Efforts were also to be made to improve resource mobilization through the introduction of user charges and fees for a range of public transport services including road user charges, port fees, inland water and rail fares.",""],[1,"464","1","Transport Strategy Implementation Gap Remediation","An important priority will be to address the implementation gaps of the 7FYP strategy.",""],[1,"464","1","Transport Project Institutional Constraint Reform","The other priority will be to address the major institutional constraints that have hampered implementation of transport projects.",""],[1,"464","1","PPP Strategy Reform for Transport Investment","A third priority is the reform of the PPP strategy with a view to achieving stronger progress under the 8FYP.",""],[1,"464","1","Transformational Transport Infrastructure Investment Prioritization","This initiative already started under the 7FYP.",""],[1,"464","2","Transport Sector Master Plan 2041 Development","a fresh look will be taken to develop a long-term Transport Sector Master Plan 2041 (TSMP 2041) with international technical assistance.",""],[1,"464","3","Integrated Transport Planning Process","These and other options to improve the intermodal transport balance will be adopted based on an integrated transport planning process that will be regularly updated to reflect the changing traffic dynamics.",""],[1,"464","4","Transport Project Implementation Capacity Strengthening","The 8FYP will further strengthen this by closely monitoring completion of all large transport projects, ensuring timely release of funds, linking new investment approvals to the record of project implementation, improving procurement policies, paying greater attention to project design before project approval, ensuring project implementation readiness as an important criteria for project approval, and strengthening capacities of line ministries and public agencies through improvement in technical capacities based on training and also through recruitment of special skills from private sector on contractual",""],[1,"465","2","Strengthening the Transport Infrastructure PPP Financing Initiative","the 8FYP will seek to sharply strengthen the PPP initiative with quality international level staffs and address required legal and incentive issues to draw international financing from best possible sources.",""],[1,"466","1","Transport Authority Institutional Reform and Capacity Strengthening","The proper implementation of the proposed transport infrastructure strategy will require substantial institutional reforms in the transport sector.",""],[1,"466","1","Public Administration Strengthening Initiatives","Several initiatives introduced during the 7FYP are underway to strengthen public administration including better staff recruitment, training, incentives and performance evaluation.",""],[1,"466","14","RHD Project Implementation Capacity Strengthening","The top most priority is to strengthen implementation capacity by focusing on the implementation of core transformational projects under RHD and ensuring their timely completion (Table 6.2).",""],[1,"466","14","RHD Organizational Expansion and Staffing","Project implementation capacity of the RHD will be strengthened through organizational expansion, employment of qualified engineers & project professionals, through training and technical assistance.",""],[1,"466","14","Ministerial and NEC Project Progress Review Mechanism","Project progress will be reviewed at the Ministerial level on a monthly basis and a 6- month basis at the NEC level.",""],[1,"466","15","Road Master Plan Update and Harmonization","RHD Road Master Plan 2009-2029 has to be updated & harmonized with these national policy documents for ensuring the proper identification of transformational projects that will achieve the best value for public money.",""],[1,"469","10","Turnkey Contracting for Donor-Funded Projects","the government will increasingly adopt a strategy of negotiating project implementation for all donor-funded projects on a turnkey basis.",""],[1,"469","11","PPP Cell Capacity Upgrade","The capabilities to negotiate PPP projects involving domestic and foreign funding will be sharply strengthened through upgrading of the PPP cell with internationally qualified and experienced staff.",""]],"20":[[1,"452","3","Rural Road Network Upgrading and Reconstruction","A major focus of LGED was on improving the quality of the rural road network by paving of existing road and reconstruction of damaged paved road.",""],[1,"467","2","Concrete Pavement Use in Waterlogged Highway Sections","For example, concrete pavements are encouraged to use in waterlogged sections of highways.",""],[1,"468","2","Rural Roads Upgrading Programme","Up-grading of rural roads: This is an on-going program and its implementation will be further intensified under the 8FYP.",""],[1,"522","7","Climate- and Disaster-Resilient Rural Transportation Network Development","Development of climate, disaster and other impact resilient rural transportation network that will be able to accommodate a vibrant middle- income economy and gradually lead to a developed nation economy;",""],[1,"522","8","Prioritized Rural Roads Development","Development of roads with more economic and social priority that will be able to generate more employment, other economic-social benefits simultaneously will add more growth to rural economy.",""],[1,"522","8","Phased Development of Prioritized Roads","Development of prioritized roads at the first phase will accelerate more growth and eventually will generate money for less priority roads;",""],[1,"522","9","Multimodal Transport Development for Haor, Wetland and Hilly Regions","Multimodal transport development for Haor, Wetland and Hilly regions",""],[1,"522","10","Rural Road Master Plan Implementation","Rural road master plan will be followed and preservation of agricultural land will be considered during new road development and up-gradation.",""],[1,"522","11","Community-Based Rural Road Operation and Maintenance Framework","Active involvement of UPZs, UPs and local communities will be considered for operation and maintenance of the rural roads.",""],[1,"522","12","Technology-Driven Road Asset Information System","Technology driven road asset information system will be developed to assess the maintenance need with more accuracy and respond quickly;",""],[1,"522","13","Road Patch Repair and Pothole Management System","An efficient system for patch repairing and potholes management will be developed so that the roads can be restored immediately without further deterioration;",""],[1,"522","14","Rural Road Rehabilitation Using Build Back Better Method","For rehabilitation of rural roads after major disasters, 'Build Back Better method' of 'Sandai Framework of Disaster Risk Prevention' will be followed;",""],[1,"522","15","Rural Road Maintenance Priority and Funding Allocation","Maintenance of existing rural roads will be given priority over new road development and justified fund will be allocated according to demand for maintenance;",""],[1,"522","16","Rural Road Asset Management Policy and Strategy","A comprehensive asset management policy, strategy will be developed and required capability according to policy, strategy will be developed for a holistic management of rural road asset.",""],[1,"523","1","Rural Road Network Upgrade and Maintenance","LGED will upgrade and maintain the rural road network in the master plan.","LGED"],[1,"523","2","Upazila, Union, and Village Road Improvement Programme","The second priority will be to improve Upazila Roads, Union Roads and Village Roads including culverts/bridges which have strategic importance to connect road network, disconnected villages and major population of a village, railway, waterway and major farmlands.",""],[1,"523","3","Inter-Village and Intra-Village Roads Connectivity Improvement","The third priority will be the inter villages and intra-villages roads connectivity.",""],[1,"525","1","Rural Core Road Network Upgradation and Double-Laning","Up-gradation/ Double lane of rural core road network with climate, disaster and other impact resilient design (16000 Km)",""],[1,"525","2","Prioritized Rural Road Improvement Programme","Improvement of prioritized Upazila road, Union road and village road to establish better connectivity with villages and thus increasing Rural Access Index (RAI) to 90 per cent from 84 per cent (Survey 2018) (33,000 Km)",""],[1,"525","3","Bridge Construction, Reconstruction, Rehabilitation, and Widening Programme","Construction/ reconstruction/ rehabilitation/ widening of 165,000-meter bridges on core road network and other Upazila roads, Union roads and village roads",""],[1,"525","4","Road Safety Engineering Improvement at Junctions and Selected Union Roads","Improvement of road safety engineering at junctions of LGED roads with National Highways Improvement of the selected Union Road.",""]],"21":[[1,"630","2","Long-Term Network Planning","Introduce long-term network planning",""],[1,"630","3","Road Network Maintenance Programme","Maintain the road network at a level which, protects the value of the investment",""],[1,"630","4","Road Maintenance Financing Mechanism","Secure a sustainable means of funding road maintenance",""],[1,"630","6","Integrated Road Construction Planning Approach","Develop an integrated planning approach in road construction",""],[1,"630","7","Private Sector Participation in Infrastructure and Service Maintenance","Involve the private sector more in infrastructure, services and maintenance",""],[1,"630","8","Environmental Protection in Road Construction Program","Protect the environment from road construction program",""],[1,"630","10","Vehicle Weight Regulation","Regulate vehicle weights",""]],"22":[[1,"450","2","Transformational Transport Infrastructure Investment","On the investment side, a conscious decision was taken to prioritize transformational transport infrastructure projects that helps modernize the Bangladesh transport network so as to improve the mobility of goods and services across the nation, facilitate international trade, reduce cost and improve competitiveness.",""],[1,"451","5","Elenga-Rangpur Road Network Improvement","Work on Elenga-Rangpur road network underway.",""],[1,"451","7","Madanpur-Joydevpur Road Upgrading to Four Lanes through PPP","Upgrading of the Madanpur-Joydevpur road to 4- lane through PPP underway.",""],[1,"451","9","Hatirjheel-Demra Expressway Construction","Work on the Hatirjheel-Demra Expressway underway",""],[1,"451","10","Gabtoli-Nabinagar Expressway Construction","Work on the Gabtoli-Nabinagar Expressway underway.",""],[1,"451","11","Highway Upgrading to Four-Lane Standard","Upgrading into 4-Lane of Ashuganj River Port-Akhaura Landport Highway; Feni-Noakhali National Highway; and Comilla-Noakhali Highway underway.",""],[1,"451","12","Payra Bridge Construction Project","Construction of 4-Lane Payra Bridge over the river Payra on Barisal-Patuakhali National Highway underway.",""],[1,"451","13","Cross Border Road Network Improvement Project","Work on 17 Bridges including Kalna Bridge under Cross Border Road Network Improvement Project underway.",""],[1,"451","14","Bangladesh Bridge Improvement Project","82 Bridges under Bangladesh Bridge Improvement Project underway.",""],[1,"451","15","Hill Tracts Border Road Construction","Work on 317-kilometer border road in the Hill Tracts districts of Bandarban, Rangamati and Khagrachari is underway",""],[1,"451","17","Bangabandhu Sheikh Mujibur Rahman Highway Completion","Father of the Nation Bangabandhu Sheikh Mujibur Rahman Highway (Sylhet-Bholaganj Road) is expected to be completed by FY2021.",""],[1,"452","1","Major Bridge and Expressway Infrastructure Programme","The major on-going projects during the 7FYP are: Padma Multipurpose Bridge Project; Dhaka Elevated Expressway PPP Project; Support to Dhaka Elevated Expressway PPP Project; Bangabandhu Sheikh Mujibur Rahman tunnel under the river Karnaphuli; Dhaka-Ashulia Elevated Expressway; and BRT (Gazipur-Airport) (4.5 km elevated section) along with Bangladesh Bridge Authority taken initiative for Feasibility study of construction of Subway in Dhaka city and feasibility study for construction of bridges on Putuakhali- Amtoli-Borguna road over the river Paira, on Bakergong-Baufal road over the river Karkhana, on Bhulta- Araihazar- Bancharampur road over the river Meghna, On Barisal -Bhola road over the river Kalabadar and Tetulia and Borguna-Patharghata road over the river Bishkhali.",""],[1,"452","2","Fast-Track Project Completion Program","The projects are being implemented on a fast-track completion program and are expected to be completed by June 2022.",""],[1,"452","2","Padma Bridge Construction","The construction of the most important Padma Bridge is scheduled to be completed in June 2021.",""],[1,"452","2","Karnaphuli Tunnel Construction","The first underwater tunnel of Bangladesh named Bangabandhu Sheikh Mujibur Rahman Tunnel (Karnaphuli Tunnel) is expected to be completed by 2022.",""],[1,"463","2","Road Infrastructure Improvement","Additionally, it is expected that as the roadways expand, quality of road infrastructures gets improved, road worthiness of on road vehicle fleets are ensured both mechanically and environmentally, drivers are well trained and road users are well aware of safe uses of road ways.",""],[1,"467","1","National Highway Network Consolidation and Upgrading","The PP2041 Strategy calls for consolidating and upgrading of the National Highway Networks through multi-laning of existing highways, by establishing access-control long-distance expressways, and by creating service lanes to ease connectivity to local roads.",""],[1,"467","1","Timely Completion of Priority National Highways","the first priority would be to ensure the timely completion of the above-mentioned national highways and ensuring that these roads provide the required service road connectivity to local roads.",""],[1,"467","1","Selective Four-Laning Highway Upgrading","New 4-laning highway project up gradation will be undertaken selectively based in implementation capacity and available resources.",""],[1,"467","2","High-Speed Highway Corridor Upgrading","Attention will be given to develop quality infrastructures with hallmark attribute of high-speed mobility facilities.",""],[1,"467","2","Conflict-Free Intersection Optimization","For achieving this, the strategy would be to optimize the intersections to be conflict free on major economic corridors.",""],[1,"467","2","Bypass and Access-Controlled Expressway Development","Bypasses around towns would be planned and provided as access-controlled expressway type facilities with entry/exit at predetermined locations.",""],[1,"467","3","Road Connectivity Linkage Development","The emphasis on these linkages will be further sharpened during the 8FYP.",""],[1,"467","4","Inter-District Connectivity Upgrade Programme","ensuring inter-district connectivity for all districts that are not connected through the national highway system is an important priority.",""],[1,"467","5","Highway and Inter-District Roadside Service Facilities","the 8FYP will put emphasis on creating highway and inter-district facilities to provide restroom and food facilities for travellers and essential services such as gas stations, emergency repairs, for facilitating highway mobility.",""],[1,"468","1","Zila and Upazila Road Upgrading Programme","the upgrading of all zila and upazila roads to facilitate easy transport connectivity between production and consumption centres is an important priority in PP2041 and for the 8FYP.",""],[1,"469","8","Timely Completion of Ongoing Transformational Projects","Timely completion of all on-going projects: There are 7 transformational projects in different stages of implementation including the Padma Bridge; Dhaka Elevated Expressway PPP Project and the linked PPP- based Support to Dhaka Elevated Expressway Project; the Bangabandhu Sheikh Mujibur Rahman tunnel; the Dhaka-Ashulia Elevated Expressway; and the Bus Rapid Transit (BRT) Gazipur-Ashulia 4.5-kilometer elevated expressway Feasibility Study for the Construction of Subway in Dhaka City.",""],[1,"469","9","Paira River Bridge Construction Project","A new project was approved at the ECNEC meeting on March 10, 2020, at a total cost of Tk 1,042 crore for the construction of a 1,690 meter long bridge over the Paira River on Kachua-Betagi-Patuakhali-Lohalia-Kaliya road as part of the development of road communication network in southern region of the country.",""],[1,"469","12","Review and Possible Adoption of High-Priority Transformational Bridge Projects","The Bridges Division has identified a number of new high priority transformational projects for the 8FYP including Railway Bridge over the Jamuna river, Barisal-Bhola bridge.",""]],"23":[[1,"450","1","Seaport Development and Dhaka Transport Connectivity","development of the two seaports with smooth transport links to Dhaka",""],[1,"457","2","Port Capacity Expansion and Logistics Support","In the meantime, CPA has extended its port limit up to Kutubdia in the South and Sitakunda in the North.",""],[1,"457","2","Patenga Container Terminal Project","The construction of the Patenga Container Terminal (PCT)\" project is underway and it is expected to become operational by June 2021.",""],[1,"457","2","Chittagong Port Expansion Project","The Chittagong Port Expansion project has been planned to increase the yard facilities of Chittagong Port.",""],[1,"457","2","Maheshkhali-Matarbari Area Development Projects","Moreover, the government of Bangladesh with the Japanese support will implement 34 projects in Maheshkhali-Matarbari area to accelerate the pace of economic development in Bangladesh.",""],[1,"457","2","Matarbari Port Development Project","Besides, deep sea port with coal-based power plant, special economic zones, coal jetty and LNG terminals will be built in Matarbari.",""],[1,"457","2","Matarbari Port Development Project","Upon completion of the Matarbari Port Development Project, which is being implemented under the Chattogram Port Authority, it will be treated as a commercial hub of the region.",""],[1,"458","1","Payra Port Phased Development and Project Implementation","The main task under the 7FYP is project implementation, using a phased approach.",""],[1,"458","1","Payra Sea Port Basic Infrastructure Development","Limited scale operational activities of Payra Sea Port started on August 13, 2016 developing some basic infrastructures and transferring the goods through sing barges by inland waterways.",""],[1,"458","1","Payra Port Core Infrastructure Land Acquisition","Some 6,500 acres of land is under acquisition for development of core port infrastructures.",""],[1,"458","1","Payra Port Capital Dredging and Terminal Construction","It is expected that by 2023 Payra will be fully operational as an international sea port through completion of capital dredging project and constructing at least three terminals with 12 berths and channel depth (CD) of 10.5 m.",""],[1,"458","1","Payra Port Second-Phase Dredging and Capacity Expansion","As per long-term plan, it is expected that by 2035 the Para Port will be able to function with at least 14.0m CD through a second phase capital dredging and capacity to handle about 89.8 million MT cargos and 5.1 million TEUs container.",""],[1,"461","6","Pyra Port Development","the government has sought to increase port capacity by launching the Pyra port",""],[1,"461","6","Chittagong Port Expansion Programme","the government has sought to increase port capacity by launching ... a program to expand the Chittagong Port",""],[1,"461","6","Strategic Dredging of the Passur River","Progress in addressing the CD issue of the Passur River through strategic dredging is a welcome move, but stronger efforts are needed to enhance the use and productivity of this underutilized asset through strategic planning and greater resource allocation.",""],[1,"461","6","Mongla Port Connectivity and Investment Coordination","Opening up the port to neighbouring countries is a smart move, but this must be facilitated by coordinated investments to enable the full use of the potential of the Mongla port.",""],[1,"474","2","Mongla Port Capacity Expansion and Efficiency Improvement","Emphasis will be placed on removing all the constraints to the use of the Mongla Port to its full capacity through a combination of investments in strategic dredging and investments in port equipment and facilities to support expanded and efficient cargo handling.",""],[1,"474","3","Chittagong Port Capacity Expansion Programme","The investment programmes for the expansion of Chittagong Port capacity will be fast tracked along with other investments for expanding container traffic handling and management.",""],[1,"474","5","Pyra Port Investment Programme Fast-Tracking","The investment programmes for the Pyra Port will be fast tracked for speedy completion of all required physical work to enable service by 2022.",""],[1,"474","6","Port Productivity Modernization","Each port would focus on the improvement of productivity - both ship berth-day and gang-shift output further through modernisation, induction of more sophisticated equipment in handling cargo, etc.",""],[1,"474","7","Outsourcing and Privatization of Handling Operations","Handling operations in selected areas will gradually be outsourced/ privatised for injecting more competition and increasing output.",""],[1,"474","8","Cargo Handling Mechanization in Major Ports","Efforts would be made for full mechanization of cargo handling operation and movement in major Ports.",""],[1,"474","9","Port Storage Area Expansion","The storage area in the ports will be expanded.",""],[1,"474","10","Private Sector Port Policy Formulation","Formulation of Private Sector Port Policy.",""],[1,"474","11","Port Vessel Turnaround Time Improvement","Efforts would be made to reduce pre-berthing detention and to improve turn -time of vessels through minimization of both port and non-port related factors.",""],[1,"474","12","Required Dredging for Larger Shipping Capacity","Required dredging to allow handling of bigger shipping will be carried out.",""],[1,"474","13","Terminal Cargo Handling Capacity Expansion","Terminal capacity for handling higher cargo off-loading will be expanded.",""],[1,"474","14","Deep-Water Container Hub Port Construction","Capacity to handle large container traffic will be expanded by constructing deep water-container hub ports.",""],[1,"474","15","Inter-Modal Transport Connectivity with Ports","Inter-modal transport connectivity with ports will be ensured for speedy forward transport to the final destination of imports as well as easy transit factory gate to port for exports.",""],[1,"474","16","Modern Cargo Handling Techniques for Major Ports","Modern cargo handling techniques would be introduced to improve port performance in the major ports, particularly in the dry bulk cargo, conventional and unitized general cargo trades.",""],[1,"474","17","Integrated Port Operations System Automation","Port service efficiency and productivity will be enhanced by introducing of state-of-the-art technology/internet to implement integrated Port Operations System and to move towards paperless regime so as to reduce dwell time and also reduce transaction cost to the users.",""],[1,"474","17","Port Automation and Digital Systems Package","The major areas where such automation is aimed at include: Vessel Traffic Management System (VTMS); Information Technology in Scientific Application, the Cargo/Container handling operations and non-operation area; Surveillance System and Safety & Security System; and Electronic Commerce (EC)/Electronic Data Interchange (EDI).",""]],"24":[[1,"342","10","Foreign Investment Promotion in Export-Oriented Services","Foreign investment in export-oriented services will be promoted, especially with a view to importing technology and thereby increasing service quality and export competitiveness.",""],[1,"342","10","Foreign Joint Venture Promotion","Wherever possible, joint venture with foreign partners will be encouraged.",""],[1,"343","2","Private Shipping Sector Consultation and Reform Initiative","To facilitate the growth of private shipping the government should immediately organize a consultation session with local and international private shipping companies to find out major obstacles and constraints to improve the shipping industry including regulatory barriers and taxation issue.",""],[1,"343","2","National Shipping Sector Reform Programme","Based on this, necessary reforms should be initiated to strengthen the national shipping sector.",""],[1,"343","3","Biman Airline Twinning and Commercial Management Reform","the Government will explore the option of twining arrangements between Bangladesh Biman and a reputed international airline.",""],[1,"343","4","Promotion of Joint Ventures in Domestic Aviation","Regarding domestic aviation, the possibility of joint ventures with international partners will be encouraged.",""],[1,"343","4","Exploration of Joint Ventures in International Shipping","The possibility of joint ventures in international shipping should also be explored.",""],[1,"343","4","Special Study on Aviation and Shipping Reforms","For both areas, a special study should be commissioned to highlight the constraints and identify specific reforms.",""],[1,"344","1","Aviation Capacity Upgrade Programme","The 7FYP adopted a significant programme to upgrade both the international and domestic aviation capacities.",""],[1,"344","1","Long-Term Aviation Plan Development","a longer-term aviation plan to meet the air travel needs of a high- income country will be developed with technical assistance of international aviation experts.",""]],"25":[[1,"826","1","Gender-Responsive Transport Services and Infrastructure","Gender responsive transportation (land, water, air) services and infrastructure: Infrastructure and transport services are keys to increase women's participation in public spheres.",""],[1,"826","1","Transport Safety Enforcement and Awareness Measures","Road safety should be ensured through enforcement of traffic rules and laws.",""],[1,"826","1","Employer-Provided Transport Support for Women Workers","Factories/employers employing more women should be guided to operate transport services for staff/workers and they can be provided loan facilities to operate transport services for staff.",""],[1,"843","7","Rural Road Development and Agricultural Market Linkage","Necessary steps should be taken to develop rural roads and establish market linkage for locally produced agricultural products.",""]],"26":[[1,"5","5","Bangladesh Delta Plan 2100","Moreover, we have also prepared the 'Bangladesh Delta Plan 2100' to offset the negative externalities of climate change and natural calamities.",""],[1,"10","1","Bangladesh Delta Plan 2100 Implementation","The push toward achieving water safety and reducing long-term risk from climate change and natural disaster gained momentum through the adoption of a techno-economic Bangladesh Delta Plan (BDP2100) covering the whole twenty-first century.",""],[1,"52","5","Bangladesh Delta Plan 2100","The push toward reducing long-term risk from climate change and natural disaster gained momentum through the adoption of a comprehensive long-term water management strategy known as the Bangladesh Delta Plan (BDP2100) that integrates water, land, environment, climate change and biodiversity in ways",""],[1,"53","1","Implementation of the First Phase of the Bangladesh Delta Plan 2100","The 8FYP will give top priority to implementing the first phase of the BDP2100.",""],[1,"54","2","Bangladesh Delta Plan Implementation","strong implementation of the Bangladesh Delta Plan for ensuring the sound management of water resources, climate change, natural disasters and other environmental hazards will be a major focus for the Eighth Plan.",""],[1,"56","2","BDP2100 Public Investment Programme Phase One","The implementation of the first phase of the BDP2100 public investment programme will strengthen water management, lower flood risk, reduce water logging and reduce soil salinity.",""],[1,"58","2","Bangladesh Delta Plan 2100 Implementation","The main focus of the ADP will be to sharply improve and strengthen health infrastructure, to build the social protection system, alleviate infrastructure constraints to private investment and GDP growth by fast tracking nationally important projects, and implement the BDP2100.",""],[1,"58","3","BDP2100 First Phase Implementation","Finally, strong efforts will be made to implement the first phase of the BDP2100.",""],[1,"64","1","BDP 2100 Long-Term Delta Risk Management Strategy","the implementation of this comprehensive long-term strategy for managing the risks posed by the deltaic formation of the country along with the incidence of natural disasters and climate change will substantially reduce the vulnerability of the population to climate change and natural disasters.",""],[1,"64","2","Delta Plan Resilience and Vulnerability Reduction","Implementing the Delta Plan to build resilience and reduce vulnerability to climate change;",""],[1,"64","3","Bangladesh Delta Plan 2100 Implementation","the 8FYP will prioritize the ongoing efforts to ... implement the BDP2100",""],[1,"94","2","Delta Plan Implementation","The implementation of the Delta Plan during the 8FYP will play a major role in implementing the government's strategic shift towards better management and reduction of natural disaster incidence, especially from flooding, sea-level rise, salinity and water logging.",""],[1,"94","2","Long-Term Water Management Investments","the government's attention has to shift to better management of the environmental and climate change risks by taking long term investments in water management.",""],[1,"99","3","Bangladesh Delta Plan 2100 Implementation","Strong implementation of the Bangladesh Delta Plan (BDP2100) for sound management of water resources, climate change, natural disasters and other environmental hazards will be a major focus for the Eighth Plan.",""],[1,"125","1","Water, Education, Training and Health Investment Programme","Additionally, water investments, as advocated in the BDP2100, and investments in education, training and health care would be critical to strengthen the resilience of agriculture and the rural economy, fight COVID-19 and build up human capital.",""],[1,"127","3","Rural Infrastructure and Water Resources Investment","Strong emphasis was also placed on rural infrastructure (rural development and water resources).",""],[1,"128","3","BDP2100 Rural Economy Resilience Implementation","towards increasing the resilience of the rural economy by strengthening the implementation of the BDP2100",""],[1,"128","3","Multi-year Water Management Projects","the BDP2100 implementation will require a strong focus on several multi-year and transformational water management projects relating to flood control, river erosion management, irrigation, and environmental protection",""],[1,"146","1","Delta Plan Water Infrastructure Projects","build infrastructure and Delta Plan related water projects to strengthen growth and resilience from natural disasters",""],[1,"146","2","Public Healthcare Expansion and BDP2100 Implementation","Management of these risks requires active policy responses including a major increase in public healthcare and implementation of the BDP2100.",""],[1,"171","4","Bangladesh Delta Plan 2100 Implementation","The 8FYP is the first phase of implementing the BDP2100.",""],[1,"173","2","Bangladesh Delta Plan 2100 Implementation","two important risk mitigation strategies that will be adopted in the 8FYP to minimize the effects of anticipated shocks include the reduction in climate change and natural disaster-related shocks by the implementation of the Bangladesh Delta Plan BDP2100",""],[1,"177","4","BDP2100 Priority Public Investment Programme","Prioritizing BDP2100 PIP in favour of addressing irrigation, flood control, waterlogging and salinity problems in the lagging districts.",""],[1,"180","12","Rural Infrastructure Investment Expansion","Second, another area where public spending has to increase concerns rural infrastructure -- rural roads, rural electricity, irrigation, and flood control.",""],[1,"180","12","BDP2100 Water Investment Implementation","Furthermore, the implementation of the water investments in BDP2100 will greatly benefit farm productivity and reduce the loss of rural livelihoods and property from flooding and riverbank erosion.",""],[1,"184","1","BDP 2100 First Phase Implementation","strong efforts will be made to implement the first phase of the BDP 2100.",""],[1,"188","2","Bangladesh Delta Plan 2100 Implementation Programme","A major priority of 8FYP is to initiate the implementation of the Bangladesh Delta Plan (BDP2100).",""],[1,"194","5","Medium- and Long-Term Financing for Key Infrastructure and BDP2100 Investments","Some of the increase is to enable external financing of essential COVID-19 related expenditures in health and social protection in FY21 and FY22, followed by MLT financing of key infrastructure in transport, energy and power and BDP2100 investments.",""],[1,"197","2","Increased Investment Allocation for Bangladesh Delta Plan 2100","In addition, increasing amount of resources will be allocated to the investment programmes related to Bangladesh Delta Plan 2100.",""],[1,"505","3","Bangladesh Delta Plan 2100","The adoption of the Bangladesh Delta Plan 2100 (BDP2100) in November 2018 is a major milestone in the Bangladesh history of integrated management of water resources that is expected to radically change the rural economic environment with improved flood control, reduced salinity, reduced water logging, improved drought management and proper irrigation facilities.",""],[1,"505","3","Interagency Water Resource Management Coordination","This will also improve coordination of water resource management across the large number of public agencies involved in implementation.",""],[1,"531","7","BDP2100 Implementation","Supportive policies include the implementation of BDP2100, public investment in farm technology and productivity, support policies for strengthening fishing activities including the harnessing of the potentials of the Blue Economy, public investment in rural infrastructure, and credit policies to promote non-farm economic activities.",""],[1,"544","2","Bangladesh Delta Plan 2100 Adoption","Adoption of the Bangladesh Delta Plan 2100: Bangladesh Delta Plan 2100 documents the broad development strategies which the country can adopt as it gravitates toward the end of the 21 st century.",""],[1,"544","3","Bangladesh Delta Plan Climate Adaptation Measures","under the Delta Plan (DP) policy option, the effects of climate change are expected to be minimized, and associated adaptation measures are planned which will help us achieve higher economic growth.",""],[1,"544","4","Integrated Water Resources Management under BDP 2100","BDP 2100 also links Integrated Water Resources Management (IWRM) to economic growth as water has been considered for the sustainability of the delta.",""],[1,"545","2","Bangladesh Delta Plan 2100 Coordination Framework","However, all these initiatives need to be aligned and come under one umbrella of Bangladesh Delta Plan (BDP) 2100 to ensure better coordination and sustainability with clear budget links.",""],[1,"545","6","River Bank Erosion Mitigation and River Dredging Programme","Steps have been taken for managing water resources, land use, and mitigating effects of climate change on the environment by re-excavating small rivers, canals and wetlands across the country and assimilation of the Climate Smart Integrated Coastal Resource Database (CSICRD).",""]],"27":[[1,"389","2","Integrated Water Management and River Dredging","Efforts to implement integrated water management continued in the 7FYP with focus on flood control prevention of river bank erosion, and supply of irrigation water, River dredging to improve river navigability also continued.",""],[1,"390","1","Groundwater Management in Agricultural Activities Bill 2018","The Groundwater Management in Agricultural Activities Bill 2018 will ensure the best possible use of water and its management for continuing the trend of development in the agriculture sector.",""],[1,"390","2","National River Conservation Commission River Protection and Restoration Mandate","The National River Conservation Commission (NRCC) established in 2014 under the National River Conservation Commission Act 2013, is responsible for the prevention of illegal grabbing of river land, and conserving the river water and environment from pollution with all kind of waste, ensuring the multidimensional use of river system for inclusive development, and restoring natural flows of the river with proper maintenance and all season navigability.",""],[1,"390","3","Valuing Water Position Paper Publication","Jointly with the Ministry of Water Resources, the High-Level Valuing Water Committee and Technical Valuing Water Committee are in the process to publish a Position Paper on Valuing Water in Bangladesh.","Ministry of Water Resources"],[1,"391","4","Major River Restoration and Basin Cooperation","Restoration of major rivers and their off takes as well as enhanced regional cooperation in the Ganges- Brahmaputra-Meghna basins will ensure availability of more flow in dry season.",""],[1,"393","2","Integrated Water Management Scale-Up","The objective of the water sector in the 8th plan is to scale up existing good practices of water conservation and management and apply more widely integrated water management, including flood control and prevention schemes, flood early warning systems, irrigation improvement, and demand-side management as advocated in BDP2100.",""],[1,"393","4","Water Use Efficiency and Surface Water Irrigation Enhancement","Increasing water use efficiency in crop production and enhance the utilization of surface water irrigation;",""],[1,"393","5","Integrated Riverbank Erosion Protection Measures","Protecting riverbank from erosion through integrated long-terms measures;",""],[1,"393","6","Conjunctive Surface and Groundwater Irrigation Management","Ensuring conjunctive use of surface and ground water for sustainable irrigation, securing groundwater conservation;",""],[1,"393","7","Regional and International Cooperation for Trans-boundary River Basin Management","Strengthening regional and international cooperation for basin-wide water resources development and management of trans-boundary rivers;",""],[1,"393","8","Saline Intrusion Prevention through Freshwater Flow Augmentation","Preventing of saline intrusion through augmenting the freshwater flow in the southwest region including the Sundarbans;",""],[1,"393","9","Modern Early Warning Systems Development","Developing modern early warning systems to minimize economic losses from flood and other disasters;",""],[1,"393","11","Integrated Coastal Zone Management Strategies","Implementing integrated coastal zone management strategies;",""],[1,"393","12","Institutional Capacity Strengthening for Water Resource Management","Strengthening capacities of the institution in the water resource management;",""],[1,"393","13","Mainstreaming Valuing Water in Public Investment Decisions","Mainstreaming Valuing Water into Public Investment Decision Making in collaboration with Planning Commission to allow for future investment decisions which further support sustainable water resources management and thus sustainable economic development;","Planning Commission"],[1,"393","14","Valuing Water Integration in Private Sector Decision-Making","Identifying and demonstrating options to incorporate Valuing Water into private sector decision making in order to lead to more sustainable investment and operational choices.",""],[1,"394","13","Well-Planned Irrigation Management System","Therefore, a well- planned irrigation management system is essential for a gradual increase of cropping intensity as well as yield.",""],[1,"394","13","Modern Water Management Technology Promotion","Irrigation efficiency will be ascertained and modern water management technology will be promoted to enhance irrigation efficacy and water productivity through optimal use of available water resources.",""],[1,"394","13","Water Reservoir and Rainwater Harvesting Promotion","As part of the strategy, water reservoirs and rainwater harvesting in rainfed, coastal and hilly areas will have to be encouraged, and small-scale water resources systems would be developed along with monitoring the maintenance of the small-scale water resources infrastructure at local levels by ensuring community participation and taking care of environmental and social issues.",""],[1,"395","1","Restoration and Redesign of Flood Control, Drainage and Irrigation Structures","Restoration, redesign and modification of embankments and structures",""],[1,"395","2","Spatial Planning and Flood Hazard Zoning Framework","Adopt spatial planning and flood hazard zoning:",""],[1,"395","3","Flood Early Warning System Upgrade and Expansion","The flood early warning system needs to be updated and the lead time needs to improve.",""],[1,"395","3","Flood Warning Dissemination System Improvement","The dissemination system will improve for delivering the warning to the local people with a higher lead time.",""],[1,"395","3","Community-Based Early Warning Services Expansion","Community based early warning services will be extended, including flood agents and networks for communication and action.",""],[1,"395","3","Institutional Cooperation for Flood Early Warning","A strong cooperation will be developed between institutions responsible for hydrology (BWDB), meteorology (BMD), modelling (institutes and centres), dissemination and early actions.",""],[1,"395","4","Operation and Maintenance System Improvement","So, improvements in the operation and maintenance system are a must for increasing the functionality of the schemes.",""],[1,"395","5","Water Body Restoration and Connectivity Improvement","Policies will be undertaken to restore water bodies and to improve connectivity between floodplains, wetlands and rivers.",""],[1,"396","5","Rainwater Harvesting Promotion Initiative","Initiatives will be undertaken to encourage rainwater harvesting where feasible.",""],[1,"396","5","Water Retention Storage Expansion","Besides, increasing storage in existing water retention bodies should be promoted.",""],[1,"396","6","Freshwater Protection and Pollution Prevention Measures","This involves both protection of environmentally valuable and sensitive areas and the prevention of pollution by enhanced treatment.",""],[1,"396","7","Coastal Drainage Capacity and Flood Risk Reduction Measures","Measures will be undertaken to restore rural rivers/canals and livelihood improvement in coastal districts.",""],[1,"396","7","Coastal Flood Risk Prevention and Preparedness Strategy","Therefore, flood risk prevention strategies and proper preparedness will be implemented in a timely manner.",""],[1,"396","8","Surface Water Irrigation Scheme Development","The BDP 2100 emphasizes on the development of surface water irrigation schemes.",""],[1,"396","9","Surface Water Irrigation Expansion through Water Reservoir Development","Augmentation of surface water for irrigation through development of water reservoirs recharges groundwater, and reduced use of groundwater.",""],[1,"396","10","Small-Scale Surface Irrigation Development","The development of small-scale surface irrigation in the southern part of the country requiring new infrastructure and capacity building;",""],[1,"396","11","Reduction of Deep Well Irrigation Reliance","Partially reduce reliance on deep well irrigation in the northern part of the country, reduce costs and mitigate the risk of depleting groundwater;",""],[1,"396","12","Dyke and Embankment Rehabilitation for Cyclone-Affected Coastal Areas","Rehabilitate dykes and embankments particularly affected by previous cyclones to protect vulnerable households and production base against sea intrusion in the extreme south;",""],[1,"397","3","Water Reservoir Creation Initiative","Initiative to create water reservoirs to retain water to fulfil dry seasonal water demands has to be taken.",""],[1,"397","6","Polder Rehabilitation and Management","The focused activities that emerged from the BDP 2100 consultations are: rehabilitation of polders and their management;",""],[1,"397","6","Enhanced Surface Water Irrigation","The focused activities that emerged from the BDP 2100 consultations are: ... enhanced surface water irrigation;",""],[1,"397","6","Brackish Water Resource Management Improvement","The focused activities that emerged from the BDP 2100 consultations are: ... and improved brackish water resource management practices.",""],[1,"397","9","Maintenance and Expansion of Flood Control, Drainage and Irrigation Systems","These existing FCDI projects should be maintained with developing integrated water control structures in response to the future climatic scenarios (rainfall intensity and peak discharges of the major rivers) developed by in the Bangladesh Delta Plan 2100.",""],[1,"397","9","Strategic Dredging and Re-Excavation of Flashy Rivers","Also, increasing the conveyance capacity of the flashy rivers through strategic and maintenance dredging, and re-excavation is needed.",""],[1,"398","3","Chattogram Hill Tracts Water Resources Management Strategy","The strategies that will be considered for the development and management of CHT water resources include protecting economic zones and towns from floods and storm surges; developing cyclonic storm surge and tidal flood risk management; Ensuring water security and sustainable sanitation; integrating erosion management in the hills by creating green belt, eco-friendly structures, soil and water conservation, and reforestation; Developing catchment and sub-catchment management plans; protecting and restoring water-related ecosystems, including forests and hill sides; and promoting sustainable cultivation practices and regeneration of degraded areas.",""],[1,"400","2","River Basin Climate Change Adaptation Strategy Development","Strategies have to be devised to combat the implications of the adverse effects of climate change upon the river basins.",""],[1,"400","9","Flood-Free Cities Drainage, Canal Dredging and Flood Control Investment Plan","Flood Free Cities Improvement of Drainage Congestion, Canal Dredging and Flood Control for Dhaka, Chittagong, Barisal, Khulna Cities Investment Plan project codes: UA 1.2; UA 1.3; UA 3.1; UA 9.3; UA10.1; UA 11.1.",""],[1,"400","12","Barind New Food Belt Revitalization and Hurasagar/Atrai Rivers Rationalization Project","Barind New Food Belt Revitalization and Rationalization of Hurasagar / Atrai Rivers and Kurigram Irrigation Project Investment Plan project codes: DP 1.2; DP 1.21; DP 1.3; DP1.4/1.5",""],[1,"401","3","Polder Rationalization Programme","Rationalization of polders",""],[1,"401","3","Catchment Management Plan Development","Development of Catchment Management Plans",""],[1,"401","3","Kaptai Lake Rehabilitation Study and Pilot Project","Kaptai Lake Rehabilitation Study with Pilot Project",""],[1,"401","4","Safe and Resilient Coast Integrated Coastal Zone Management and Polder Rationalization Investment Plan","Safe and Resilient Coast Integrated Coastal Zone Management (West-Gopalganj; Bhabadha Area; Bhola Island) and Polder Rationalization (Baleswar-Tentulia Basin; Gorai Passur Basin; Gumti-Muhuri Basin) Investment Plan",""],[1,"406","2","Rural Infrastructure and Agricultural Services Investment","Yet, it is heavily dependent upon public investment in rural infrastructure (rural road, irrigation, flood control, environmental protection, land management), forestry and agricultural services such as research and extension, storage facilities.",""],[1,"406","2","BDP2100 and Associated PIP Implementation","The adoption of the BDP2100 and the implementation of the associate PIP for the 8FYP will substantially rise the ADP spending, especially for water management where the gaps are large, especially in the area of flood control, river bank management and restoration of river courses to provide fresh water supply.",""],[1,"406","3","Financing Support for Large Transformational Water Projects","Financing of large transformational water projects included in the BDP2100 PIP for the 8FYP will require support from multilateral agencies like the World Bank, JAICA and the ADB and from bilateral sources such as the Netherlands, which has vast state of the art technical experience in water management.",""]],"28":[[1,"393","3","River Dredging for Navigability and Water Transport","Continuing and strengthen river dredging to enhance navigability and to facilitate water transportation;",""],[1,"394","14","Embankment and Water Control Infrastructure Development","Therefore, construction of new embankments and other water control infrastructures as well as strengthening and/or maintenance of the existing structures are needed at economic priority zones, major urban cities, etc.",""],[1,"394","14","Fish Pass and Fish-Friendly Structure Development","Moreover, building and maintenance of fish passes and fish friendly structures to ensure fish movement to facilitate seasonal migration of fish for breeding and grazing will be emphasized.",""],[1,"395","6","River Excavation and Smart Dredging Programme","Excavation and smart dredging are needed for the management of the river system.",""],[1,"397","2","Major River Dredging Effort","Increasing river water flow towards the south, in particular involving Major River dredging effort.",""],[1,"397","4","Major River Barrage Construction Programme","Steps have to be taken towards construction of Brahmaputra Barrage, 2nd Teesta Barrage and Padma Barrage.",""],[1,"397","6","River Dredging Programme","The focused activities that emerged from the BDP 2100 consultations are: ... dredging of rivers;",""],[1,"397","7","Coastal Land Reclamation Research and Cross-Dam Project","Extensive research will be conducted on morphological behaviour to gather knowledge about the influence of land reclamation and to realise the potential of further development and artificial interventions for enhancing accretion process.",""],[1,"397","7","Strategic Cross-Dam Construction for Land Reclamation","Building cross dams at the strategic locations would be useful for accelerating land reclamation process for which potential cross dam projects would be undertaken with proper feasibility studies.",""],[1,"397","7","Reclaimed Land Protection and Zoning Measures","Land reclaimed through accretion process need to be protected and developed with land zoning and other appropriate measures.",""],[1,"397","8","Newly Accreted Char Area Development Measures","Appropriate measures will be undertaken for the development of newly accreted char areas.",""],[1,"545","6","River Navigability Improvement and Dredging Programme","The Government has already undertaken plans to increase navigability of rivers, dredging of 510 km of rivers by 2022 to prevent river erosion and ensure supply of water during the lean season, digging",""],[1,"546","1","Irrigation Canal Re-excavation and Irrigation Structure Construction","re-excavation of 4,883 km of irrigation canals, construction and repair of 200 irrigation structures to extend irrigation facilities",""],[1,"546","1","Barrage and Rubber Dam Construction Programme","construction of 3 barrages and rubber dams",""],[1,"546","1","Flood Protection and Coastal Embankment Expansion","construction of 250 km flood protection and coastal embankment to reduce flood, salinity and water logging, renovation of 1,040 km flood protection embankments and coastal embankments, construction and renovation of 590 flood protection and drainage infrastructure, excavation and re-excavation of 1,325 km drainage canals, and conservation work of 195 km border river banks and 6 cross-dams",""],[1,"547","2","Haor Development Master Plan and Database","A 20-year Haor Development Master Plan and Database has been prepared for development of the Haor areas.",""],[1,"547","3","Transnational River Basin Cooperation for Water Management","The Government has remained committed to improve transnational cooperation for the management of rivers shared by Bangladesh and its neighbours.",""],[1,"547","3","Bangladesh-India Framework Agreement on Water Resource Cooperation","It has also signed a Framework Agreement on Cooperation for Development between Bangladesh and India in 2011 for water resource management and development of cross-border rivers through sub-regional cooperation,",""],[1,"547","3","Ganges-Brahmaputra-Meghna River Basin Organisation","under the 7FYP - the Government has taken measures to form an organization based on the Ganges-Brahmaputra-Meghna river basins, such as the River Basin Organisation/River Basin Commission.",""],[1,"551","2","Bangladesh Delta Plan 2100 Implementation","The government recognizes these limitations and aims to improve such limitations by implementing the broader strategic objectives and targets of the Bangladesh Delta Plan 2100",""],[1,"562","1","Delta Plan 2100 Implementation","The Government is giving priorities to the execution of the Delta Plan 2100 under the 8FYP and reduce the vulnerability of the population to natural hazards and climate change by implementing the Delta plan 2100 (BDP 2100).",""],[1,"562","2","Delta Wing for BDP 2100 Implementation Support","Establishment of a \"Delta Wing\" within the General Economics Division (GED) of the Bangladesh Planning Commission for offering technical support, guidance and coordination for the implementation of the BDP 2100.","General Economics Division (GED) | Bangladesh Planning Commission"],[1,"562","3","Delta Fund Establishment and Institutional Framework","Establishment of a \"Delta Fund\" and the institutional framework necessary for its usage.",""],[1,"562","4","Delta Knowledge Hub Establishment","Establishment of the \"Delta Knowledge Hub\" for hosting and offering intellectual support to the implementation of the Delta Plan by hosting, updating, collecting and sharing new data and information that can aid the agendas of the Delta Plan.",""],[1,"562","5","BDP 2100 Development Partner Investment Mobilization","The Government will present the BDP 2100 to the Development Partners to secure their investment in projects enlisted in the Investment Programme under the DP.",""],[1,"562","7","High-Powered Coordination Committee for BDP 2100 Implementation","The Government will also form a high-powered committee to manage coordination and cooperation with the upper riparian countries for the effective implementation of the BDP 2100.",""],[1,"562","8","Delta Coalition Formation and Water Technology Exchange","The Government will support the formation of a \"Delta Coalition\" to be formed by 13 countries for mutual benefit and the transfer of knowledge through exchange of water technologies for improved production and consumption of clean water.",""],[1,"562","10","Delta Plan Priority Implementation","The Government has also adopted specific targets under the Delta Plan, which will be prioritized for implementation under the 8FYP period.",""],[1,"562","10","Water and Climate Disaster Safety Measures","(i) Ensure safety against disasters linked to water and climate change;",""],[1,"562","10","Water Security and Efficiency Improvement","(ii) Ensure water security and efficiency of water usages;",""],[1,"562","10","Integrated River and Estuary Management","(iii) Ensure integrated river systems and management of estuaries;",""],[1,"562","10","Wetland and Ecosystem Conservation Programme","(iv) Conserve and preserve wetlands and ecosystems, and promote their wise usage;",""],[1,"562","10","Water Resources Governance Institution Strengthening","(v) Develop effective institutions and equitable governance for intra and trans-boundary management of water resources;",""],[1,"562","10","Integrated Land and Water Use Optimization","(vi) Achieve optimal use of land and water.",""]],"29":[[1,"619","6","Sewerage Master Plan Preparation","Preparation of sewerage master plan",""],[1,"619","7","Faecal Sludge Management Master Plan Implementation","Implementation of Faecal Sludge Management (FSM) master plan to serve the decentralized septic task",""],[1,"619","8","Sewage Collection Services for Slums and Low-Income Communities","Strengthen sewage collection services from slums and low-income communities",""],[1,"619","9","Urban Sewage Treatment Plant Development","Development of sewage treatment plant for all cities",""],[1,"619","18","Sewerage Master Plan Preparation and FSM Enabling Measures","Preparation of sewerage master plan and in that context creates an enabling environment for FSM.",""],[1,"619","19","Institutional Regulatory Framework for FSM Implementation and Scale-Up","With the IRF-FSM established, GoB will now focus on putting the framework into practice and scale up existing efforts under the 8th Plan.",""],[1,"620","2","Private Sector Engagement Support for FSM Services","Suitable business models and availability of attractive financing will be ensured to encourage/stimulating private sector engagement towards sustainable service delivery.",""],[1,"620","3","Sanitation Safety Plan Development","Similarly, a sanitation safety plan will be prepared with a view to articulate a step-by-step risk- based approach to assist in the implementation of local level risk assessment and management for the sanitation service chain.",""],[1,"620","4","Faecal Sludge Management System Expansion","In the area of sanitation, the strategy entails capturing the entire sanitation value chain for an effective faecal sludge management (FSM) in all cities and pauroshavas.",""],[1,"620","4","Safe Faecal Sludge Collection and Transport","It will aim at containing the faecal sludge by empting properly and transporting those to a treatment facility so that there is no leakage to the external environment.",""],[1,"620","4","Faecal Sludge Treatment Facility Construction and Maintenance","The treatment facilities or plants would need to be widely built and maintained in pourashovas to process faecal sludge for further use as compost or for safely discharging into the environment.",""],[1,"620","5","Faecal Sludge Treatment Plant Expansion","More recently, GoB has taken the initiative to build more than 100 FSTPs across the country with support from development partners such as World Bank, ADB, and Islamic Development Bank.","Local Government Division | DPHE"],[1,"620","5","CWIS-FSM Support Cell Establishment","The Local Government Division (LGD) has recently established CWIS- FSM (city wide inclusive sanitation-FSM) support cell in the DPHE in a notion to accelerate overall sanitation target of SDG6.2.","Local Government Division | DPHE"],[1,"621","2","Faecal Sludge Management Plant and Collection Service","The municipality owns the plant with technical support from WaterAid and NGO partner BASA.",""],[1,"621","3","Sludge Co-Composting and Compost Reuse Support","The treatment consists of 10 unplanted drying beds, and the dried sludge is co-composted with organic waste in the co-composting plant located within the FSTP compound.",""],[1,"621","4","Faecal Sludge Management Service Model Scale-Up","it has demonstrated a working modality of FSM services capturing the entire sanitation value chain, which can be scaled up further.",""],[1,"624","15","Urban Sewerage Network Expansion and Sewage Treatment","Extending the sewerage network to cover 10% of households in city areas within the plan period and bringing all sewage in treatment plant",""]],"30":[[1,"546","2","Plastic Bag Ban Enforcement","the Government has banned the use, production and marketing of polyethylene shopping bags",""],[1,"546","2","Industrial Effluent Treatment Plant Requirement","made it mandatory for the industries to set up Effluent Treatment Plants (ETPs) to treat their waste before discharging them to water bodies",""],[1,"546","2","Environmental Regulation Enforcement and Penalties","the Department of Environment (DoE) takes legal action against violators including the imposition of penalties as provided under the law","Department of Environment (DoE)"],[1,"546","2","Common Effluent Treatment for Tannery Estate","which will dispose the liquid wastes through a common ETP",""],[1,"548","3","Integrated and Participatory Noise Pollution Control Program","To expedite implementation of the Noise (Control) Rules, 2006, the Government has implemented a program titled Integrated and Participatory Program to Control Noise pollution during 2015-2017.",""],[1,"548","3","Noise Pollution Control through Collaborative and Participatory Approach","DoE has taken a project named 'Noise Pollution Control through collaborative and participatory approach' to address noise pollution problem in the country.",""],[1,"548","4","Ambient Air Quality Monitoring System","The Department of Environment under the Ministry of Environment, Forest and Climate Change has been consistently monitoring the ambient air quality of the country through its 16 (sixteen) Continuous Air Monitoring Stations (CAMS) and 15 (fifteen) Compact CAMS installed across the country.","Department of Environment | Ministry of Environment, Forest and Climate Change"],[1,"548","4","Air Pollution Policy, Legal, and Administrative Measures","To address the air pollution effectively, the Government of Bangladesh has taken necessary measures in terms of policy, legal and administrative instruments.",""],[1,"548","4","Polluting Brick Kiln Enforcement Drives","The Department of Environment in collaboration with local administrations started rigorous enforcement drives to dismantle or shut down polluting brick kilns across","Department of Environment | local administrations"],[1,"549","1","Comprehensive Air Pollution Control Guidelines","The Ministry of Environment, Forest and Climate Change issued a comprehensive guidelines or directives to relevant government and non- government entities with a view to controlling and reducing air pollution from their respective activities particularly pollution from brick kilns, construction activities, vehicles, open biomass burning, industry and others.","Ministry of Environment, Forest and Climate Change"],[1,"549","1","Clean Air Act, 2020","In order to address air pollution issues comprehensively, a separate Act 'Clean Air Act, 2020' has been formulated.",""],[1,"553","1","Urban Air Pollution Reduction Initiative","the 8FYP remains committed to reducing urban air pollution",""],[1,"558","2","Industrial Air Pollution Taxation and Monitoring Mechanism","under the 8FYP, it will develop more policies to control emission from the other polluting industries by developing a \"polluter pays principle with appropriate compensation\".",""],[1,"558","3","Industrial Water Pollution Taxation and Fines","The Government will increasingly monitor and impose taxes and fines for the pollution of water by the industrial units.",""],[1,"559","1","Household Illegal Waste Dumping Charges System","under the 8FYP, a system of pollution charges for the illegal disposal of household waste will be introduced which will improve household cooperation and compliance.",""],[1,"571","4","Cooling Water Discharge Regulation for Power Stations","Establishment and implementation of effective regulations to control the discharge of cooling water from the power stations.",""],[1,"571","5","Compliance Monitoring System Improvement for Industries and Development Projects","Improvement of the compliance monitoring system for industries and development projects and its effective implementation.",""],[1,"571","5","Online ETP Monitoring for Industries and Economic Zones","On-line ETP monitoring of all industries and economic zones.",""],[1,"571","5","IoT-Based Metering and Monitoring System","IOT based metering and monitoring for reducing leakage and corruption.",""],[1,"571","6","Expansion of Online Water Quality Monitoring System","Expansion of online water quality monitoring system to other ecologically significant areas and urban pollution hotspots.",""],[1,"571","10","Central Effluent Treatment Plant Establishment and Implementation","Establishment and implementation of Central Effluent Treatment Plant (CETP) to control the discharge of wastewater from the industrial zone.",""],[1,"571","11","Industrial Effluent Treatment Plant Installation and Online Monitoring System","Installation of ETPs in all the industries along with an online monitoring system to improve the surface water and groundwater quality",""],[1,"571","11","Zero Discharge Plan for Effluent-Discharging Industries","Implementing Zero discharge plan in the effluent discharging industries to ensure better resource management.",""],[1,"571","12","Noise Pollution Control Enforcement and Awareness Programme","under the 8FYP, the following activities will be carried out to control noise pollution: {i} Execution and enforcement of the 'Noise Pollution Control Regulation-2006'; {ii} Undertaking programmes through electronic and social media to raise awareness among drivers on noise pollution;",""],[1,"571","12","Urban Green Buffer Planting for Noise Reduction","The Government will Plantation of green trees and shrubs along roads, hospitals, educational institutions etc. by the Government to help reduced noise by a considerable extent;",""],[1,"571","12","Noise Monitoring and Silence Zone Establishment","Collection of information/data on the level of noise in different divisional cities and publication of reports on it; (v) establishing silence zones near the residential areas, educational institutions and above all, near hospitals.",""],[1,"615","6","National Minimum Standards for Environmental and Air and Water Quality","minimum standards will be defined for such issues as environmental protection, water quality and air quality and these standards are monitored by the higher government.",""]],"31":[[1,"661","3","Medical Waste Management Strategy Development","An appropriate, safe, and cost-effective strategy will need to be developed with treatment, recycling, transport, and disposal options for proper waste management and ensuring health and environmental safety.",""]],"32":[[1,"841","5","Alternative Livelihoods and Climate Protection Support","Alternative farm and non-farm-based livelihoods will be ensured for them.",""],[1,"841","5","CHT Perspective Plan Formulation","A Perspective Plan will be formulated for the development of the CHT through a consultation process with key stakeholders.",""],[1,"842","1","Alternative Farm and Non-Farm Livelihoods Support","They will be ensured alternative farm and non-farm-based livelihoods.",""],[1,"842","1","Climate and Disaster Protection for CHT Communities","They will be protected from hazards caused by climate change and other natural calamities.",""]],"33":[[1,"565","2","Municipal Solid Waste Management Improvement","Local government division is trying to manage municipal mixed solid waste with their insufficient logistics and infrastructures.","Local government division"],[1,"565","2","Waste Management Pilot Projects","DoE along with concerned stakeholders have been working for sound management of waste through few pilot projects.","DoE"],[1,"565","2","Waste Collection, Segregation, Recycling, and Safe Disposal Measures","Improved waste management includes proper collection, segregation for reuse, recycles and environmentally sound disposal.",""],[1,"565","2","Waste Sector Capacity Building and Public Awareness","Capacity building of concerned stakeholders, public awareness, strengthening monitoring and enforcement would be favourable for the improvement.",""],[1,"565","2","Waste Management Rules and Guidelines","In addition, relevant rules, guideline should be put in place for better implementation.",""],[1,"565","3","Circular Economy and Improved Waste Management Initiative","8th five-year plan will focus on the fruitful application of the improved waste management and introduction of circular economy for sustainable use of resources.",""],[1,"566","5","Single-Use Plastic Reduction Measure","Since the single use plastic (one-time cup/plates, lollypop cover, sachet, Styrofoam, plastic cutlery, cigarette filter, cotton buds, coffee stirrers, small water/juice bottles, plastic bags) as well as multilayer packaging plastic is difficult to recycle, therefore producer/manufacturer/ importer/brand owner of the products should take",""],[1,"567","1","Extended Producer Responsibility for Plastic Pollution Management","the 8th five-year plan will focus on the managing plastic pollution through EPR principle.",""],[1,"567","1","Phase-Out Plan for Single-Use Plastics","there should be a phase out plan for minimizing disposable single use plastic with the promotion of biodegradable plastic/suitable alternatives.",""],[1,"567","1","Monitoring Capacity Building for EPR Enforcement","an intensive monitoring requires capacity building of the monitoring authorities such as DoE with enhanced lab facilities, enhanced web-based online monitoring facilities, providing necessary support for sample collection facilities in the marine areas.",""],[1,"567","1","Plastic Waste Rules and Target-Setting Framework","relevant rules, guidelines need to be functional, where collection, reduction, and recycling targets should be fixed.",""],[1,"567","1","Plastic Product Fee and Recyclability Requirement System","An exclusive fee system and percentage of product recyclability, proportion of recycled material in products should be established for betterment of the environment.",""],[1,"571","13","Urban Waste Treatment Facility Construction","The Government is committed to build facilities for the treatment of waste in all major cities.",""],[1,"571","13","Green Product Tax Rebates and Incentives","This can be complemented with tax rebates and financial incentives for the production of environmentally friendly products, including energy efficient appliances, recycled materials, sustainable paper products etc.",""],[1,"571","13","Waste-to-Power Plant Development","The Government will also be committed to establish waste-based power plants which will produce electricity from solid waste and create economic incentives for both municipalities and private sector waste management companies.",""],[1,"613","3","Integrated Solid Waste Management System","The complete solution method includes integrated waste management system that includes transfer station, compost plant, biogas plant, controlled landfill cell, faecal sludge management etc.",""],[1,"619","11","Urban Waste Management Master Plan Support","Help to urban local government bodies in preparing waste management master plans.",""],[1,"619","12","Private Sector Solid Waste Recycling Investment Incentives","Incentivize private sector investment in solid waste recycling",""],[1,"619","13","Citizen Waste Sorting Awareness Campaign","Make citizens aware to sort waste at source and dump appropriately.",""],[1,"624","16","Integrated Solid Waste Management System","Treating solid waste management as a system (i.e. together with collection, disposal and resource recovery) and as a priority sector as it is tied to many ills such as waterlogging.",""],[1,"624","17","Door-to-Door Waste Collection Incentive Scheme","Incentivizing firms for door to door collection where it still does not exist.",""],[1,"624","18","Waste Sorting and Recycling Awareness Campaign","Awareness building to increase sorting and recycling.",""],[1,"624","20","Waste-to-Energy Promotion","Promoting Waste to Energy where appropriate",""],[1,"624","21","Composting Promotion Initiative","Given large organic content, encourage composting",""],[1,"629","13","Hospital Waste Collection and Management","Collection and management of hospitals' waste",""]],"34":[[1,"546","7","Bangladesh National REDD+ Strategy","Bangladesh formulated Bangladesh National REDD+ Strategy (BNRS) and established National Forest Monitoring System (NFMS) for periodical monitoring of tree and forest cover using satellite imagery.",""],[1,"547","5","Alternative Livelihood Support for Forest-Dependent Families","The Government has supported more than 10,000 families during the 7FYP to reduce their dependence on forests, which will result in lower illegal logging of timber and depletion of natural resources.","Forest Department"],[1,"547","7","Social Forestry Programme","The Government has remained committed to the objectives of social forestry under the 7FYP as it continued to offer resources to thousands of people under different social forestry schemes.",""],[1,"549","3","Ban on Timber Felling from Natural Forests","Government continues ban on timber felling from natural forests till December 2022.",""],[1,"569","5","Forest Expansion and Social Forestry Programme","Consequently, the Government will remain committed to both conserving and expanding the coverage of forests in Bangladesh to 15.2% by 2025 and to 20% by 2041.",""],[1,"569","5","Coastal Afforestation and Green Belt Reinforcement","In particular, the existing coastal afforestation, enrichment plantation and assisted natural regeneration will be continued.",""],[1,"569","5","Coastal Reforestation and Replanting Initiative","An area of 50,000 ha will be planted and replanted in the coastal areas.",""],[1,"569","5","Hill and Plain Forest Planting Programme","Additionally, an estimated 1,30,580 ha land of hill forests and 7,220 ha of plain land forests will be planted during the 8FYP period.",""],[1,"569","5","Forest Plantation Productivity Improvement","Productivity of the plantations will have to be increased.",""],[1,"569","5","Multipurpose Tree Promotion Initiative","Multipurpose trees will receive special attention to increase the productivity of land under forests.",""],[1,"572","3","Participatory Social Forestry Programme","marginal land utilization through peoples' participation for forest development have been launched in early eighties and continued till the present five-year plan.",""],[1,"572","3","Coastal Afforestation in Newly Accreted Chars","Coastal afforestation in newly accreted chars in the coastal areas was given due emphasis.",""],[1,"572","3","Roadside and Embankment Plantation Expansion","Plantation along road side and embankments were expanded.",""],[1,"573","2","Tree Coverage Expansion in Trees Outside Forest Areas","Government emphasized to increase tree coverage in tree outsides forest (ToF) and will continue for the next plan period.",""],[1,"573","4","Participatory Watershed Co-management in Chittagong Hill Tracts","Government has taken initiative for watershed management in Chittagong Hill Tracts through participatory watershed co-management activity to regulate the water cycle, reduce soil erosion, reduce deforestation and forest degradation and enhance tree coverage and carbon stock.",""],[1,"573","5","Updated Forest Policy Approval","An updated Forest Policy 2016 is yet to approve which focuses on addressing the emerging environmental and socioeconomic challenges in the context of climate change and extensive loss of forest cover in the country",""],[1,"573","5","Forest Conservation and Sustainable Management Action Plans","The FIP, FMP and National Conservation Strategy (NCS) presents strategies and action plans aimed at conservation and sustainable management of forests which requires adequate funding to implement",""],[1,"574","8","Forest Conservation and Restoration Programme","The objective of the forest sub-sector in the 8th Five Year Plan is to conserve and protect all existing forests, wildlife and other forestry resources, adhering to the principles of sustainable management and climate resilience; enrich degraded forest areas; and enhance land areas under forest/tree cover.",""],[1,"576","2","State Forest Mapping and Demarcation","All state forest land shall be mapped and demarcated clearly.",""],[1,"576","2","Site-Specific Hill Forest Protection Plans","Site specific protection plans shall be prepared to protect the remaining fragments of hill forests.",""],[1,"576","2","Forest Enrichment Plantation Programme","Enrichment plantations shall be carried out where necessary.",""],[1,"576","2","Forest Protection IEC Campaigns","Information, education and communication (IEC) campaigns shall be undertaken.",""],[1,"576","2","Forest Protection Legal Review and Reform","Legal provisions relevant to forest protection will be reviewed and improved.",""],[1,"576","2","Community-Based Natural Forest Conservation","Local communities will be actively involved in conserving natural forests even through such measures as benefit- sharing.",""],[1,"576","2","Hill Forest Watershed Co-Management","Watershed co-management activities to regulate water, increase tree cover and halt the deforestation and forest degradation will be implemented in hill forest.",""],[1,"576","2","REDD+ Forest Restoration Mechanism","Reducing Emission from Deforestation and Forest Degradation (REDD+) mechanism to support the forest restoration and enhancement of the carbon stock in hill forest will be implemented.",""],[1,"576","3","Emergency Reforestation and Restoration of Degraded State Forests","Degraded/denuded state forests will be reforested/ afforested on emergency basis.",""],[1,"576","3","Participatory Forest Management for Deforestation Reduction","Participatory forest management approach will continue for reducing the deforestation and forest degradation through involving the local and poor people.",""],[1,"576","3","Coastal Green Belt Coordination Mechanism","Inter- ministerial and departmental coordination will be strengthened to ensure the land in coastal region to establish the green belt to protect the coastal community and stabilize lands.",""],[1,"576","4","Coastal Greenbelt Creation and Afforestation Programme","Creation of a coastal green belt shall be a high priority activity.",""],[1,"577","3","Forest and Tree Monitoring and Information Systems Strengthening","Strengthening forest & tree monitoring and information systems: National Forest Inventory (bio- physical, socio economic component and land cover mapping), tree cover assessment and mapping will be conducted for monitoring the forest and tree resources and policy formulation for forest management.",""],[1,"577","4","Social Forestry Expansion and Strengthening Programme","Social forestry programmes will continue for expansion and strengthening of upazila nurseries, union level nurseries, and for strengthening nursery training centres.","Forest Department | Local Government | NGOs"],[1,"577","4","Strip Plantation Expansion Programme","An estimated 15,000 km. of strip plantations will be raised during the plan period.",""],[1,"577","4","Riparian Forest Buffer Creation Initiative","Creation of riparian forest buffer along the bank of all the rivers and canals involving the local people will be encouraged to increase the tree cover in the country.",""],[1,"577","5","Hill Forest Restoration and Conservation Measures","Therefore, special measures will be taken for hill forest restoration and conservation through resolving existing complex local politics and land tenure conflict within the plan period.",""],[1,"577","5","Livelihood Support for Hill Forest-Dependent Communities","Side by side, increased access to the livelihood benefits will be offered to the dependent communities to enhance conservation of hill forest.",""],[1,"577","5","Unclassed State Forest Development Measures","Appropriate measures will be initiated in this USF land for enhancing economic growth, ecosystem services and sustainable development.",""],[1,"577","5","Participatory Watershed Co-management and Plantation Activities","Participatory watershed co-management activities through assisted natural regeneration and enrichment plantation will continue during the plan period.",""],[1,"578","2","Trees Outside Forests Expansion Agreement Mechanism","Potential lands (e.g. marginal fellow lands, roadside, embankment etc.) can be used to increase the trees outside forest through signing agreements between Forest Department and related government organizations to increase the country's tree cover to 24%.","Forest Department"],[1,"579","3","Enhanced Forestry Resource Management","The management of forestry resources will also be enhanced through better planning, monitoring, investments and enforcements.",""]],"35":[[1,"624","6","Pond and Water Body Protection in Dhaka Detailed Area Plan","Designating all ponds/water bodies in Detailed Area Plan Map of Dhaka and protect them according to the ecological importance and public interest.",""],[1,"624","7","Wetland Development Restriction","Stopping housing estate, industries and other development work in wetlands through earth filling.",""],[1,"624","8","Avoid Water Bodies in Land Use Planning","Avoiding water bodies during planning of roads, housing and industrial estates.",""],[1,"624","9","Urban Plantation and Gardening Enhancement","Enhancing plantation and gardening to increase the natural beauty in urban areas.",""],[1,"624","10","Wetland Preservation and Buffer Demarcation","Preserving the wetlands like ponds, beels, khals demarking buffer distance as lakes.",""],[1,"627","9","Open Space and Urban Green Programme","Preserve and develop open spaces, playgrounds, parks, lakes, canals, water body and implement green programmes",""]],"36":[[1,"544","1","Wildlife Conservation and Protection Measures","The Government has formulated a wide array of measures to implement the Wildlife (conservation and security) Act, 2012.",""],[1,"544","1","Wildlife Conservation Master Plan","The Government has also formulated a Wildlife Conservation Master Plan 2015-2035, which charts out a long-term plan to improve the conservation of wildlife in Bangladesh.",""],[1,"544","1","Species-Specific Wildlife Action Plans","Bangladesh Tiger Action Plan (2018-2027), Bangladesh Elephant Conservation Action Plan (2018-2027), Bangladesh Vulture Conservation Action Plan (2016-2025) have been formulated.",""],[1,"544","1","Wildlife Protection Projects","Several projects to address the plans to protect and conserve the wildlife are under implementation.",""],[1,"545","4","Forest Investment Plan","Forest Investment Plan (FIP) (2017-2022) has been developed to identify the future investment opportunities to increase the forest cover, reducing the deforestation and forest degradation, improving the livelihoods of the forest dependent people through the implementation of participatory/social forestry.",""],[1,"545","4","Updated Forestry Master Plan","An updated Forestry Master Plan (FMP) has been developed for the period of 2017-2036 after the completion of previous FMP in 2015 to address the upcoming and on-going challenges related to anthropogenic issues and climate change.",""],[1,"547","1","Protected Area Co-management","Forest Department has implemented co-management in 22 protected areas to conserve the wildlife and biodiversity involving the forest dependent communities.","Forest Department"],[1,"549","3","SMART Patrolling in Protected Areas","At the same time SMART patrolling has started in the Sundarbans and other protected areas to conserve the wildlife and biodiversity.",""],[1,"557","20","Special Fund for Ecologically Critical Areas Management","The Government of Bangladesh is going to develop a special fund for management and improvement of Ecologically Critical Areas and create financial code of revenue budget to improve the ECAs following ecosystem based approach.",""],[1,"558","1","National Biodiversity Strategy and Action Plan Revision","During the beginning of the 8FYP, Bangladesh has to revise the NBSAP in line with the global targets under Global Biodiversity Framework.",""],[1,"558","1","Biodiversity Fund Establishment","The Government of Bangladesh is going to establish Biodiversity Fund to support activities of conservation and sustainable use at the grass root and community level.",""],[1,"558","4","Biosafety Compliance Under Bangladesh Biosafety Rules 2012","Under Bangladesh Biosafety Rules 2012, the risk of genetically modified organism (GMO) has to be controlled to ensure safe transfer and handling of GMOs, taking into risk to human health.",""],[1,"558","4","Biosafety Capacity Building Enhancement","further enhancement of capacity building is envisaged during 8FYP.",""],[1,"559","3","Forest Governance Management Information System","As a first step, it will prioritize improvements in forest governance through a proper Management Information System (MIS).",""],[1,"559","3","Timber Extraction Tax Framework","This will assist the formulation of a tax framework for on the extraction of timber by taxing excessive usages of timber by the wood furniture industry.",""],[1,"560","1","Forest Governance and Environmental Compliance Reform","steps will be taken to tackle all problems related to governance in forest management and the implementation of environmental standards and compliance.",""],[1,"561","1","Regular Environmental Outlook Reporting","The MoEFCC will also come up with the Environmental Outlook Report on Bangladesh regularly with updated information on the state of the environment and action plan for achieving the milestones, to be widely disseminated with different stakeholders.","MoEFCC"],[1,"571","8","Stringent Water Quality Criteria for Ecologically Critical Areas and Ramsar Sites","Developing stringent water quality criteria for ECAs and RAMSAR sites to improve the ecosystem and biodiversity.",""],[1,"574","5","Forest Ecosystem Services Coordination and Response System","To ensure optimum benefit of forest ecosystem services both from the forestland and tree outside forest need to enhance institutional coordination and establish effective multi-dimensional response system.",""],[1,"574","5","Institutional Framework and Training for Sustainable Forest Management","It needs appropriate institutional framework with adequately trained manpower to confront challenges for sustainable forest management.",""],[1,"574","6","Forest Department Restructuring and Capacity Strengthening","It also requires re-structuring of Forest Department for strengthening capacities.",""],[1,"574","6","Forest Conservation Monitoring and Information Systems","Moreover, multidimensional activities like wildlife and eco-tourism management, periodical updates of national forest inventory and National Red List of Flora & Fauna, regular updating of plant species information for plantation and conservation, promotion of eco-system services, climate change mitigation and adaptation activities, carbon sequestration and trading etc. are now associated with forest conservation.",""],[1,"574","7","Forest Biodiversity Knowledge Sharing Mechanism","updated information on plant and animal species is limited which needs to establish a knowledge sharing mechanism for better conservation and management of forest biodiversity.",""],[1,"575","14","SMART Patrolling for Protected Areas and Combat Against Wildlife Trafficking","Wildlife Protection (SMART patrolling in all PA and Combat trans-",""],[1,"575","15","Species Conservation Programme","Species Conservation programme (Tiger, Elephant, Gharial, Dolphin,",""],[1,"575","18","Wildlife Corridor Identification and Plantation Programme","Wildlife corridor identification and plantation-5,000 ha.",""],[1,"575","19","National Forest Inventory","Conduct one National forest inventory.",""],[1,"575","20","Establishment of Two Tissue Culture Laboratories","Establishment of Two Tissues-Culture Lab",""],[1,"575","21","Seed Orchard Establishment","Establishment of Seed orchard - 2 Nos",""],[1,"575","25","Sundarbans Prey and Predator Survey","Prey and predator survey in Sundarbans.",""],[1,"575","31","Ecotourism Development in Protected Areas","Ecotourism development in Protected Area- 40 Nos.",""],[1,"575","31","Alternative Income Generation for Forest-Dependent Communities","Scale-up alternative income generating activity for forest dependent communities-55,000 nos. families.",""],[1,"575","32","Participatory and Sustainable NTFP Management in Protected Areas","Participatory/collaborative and sustainable management of NTFPs-40 Nos. PAs-55,000 nos. families.",""],[1,"576","5","Protected Area Management and Co-management Strengthening","The protected area management including co-management shall be strengthened.",""],[1,"576","5","Expansion of Protected Area Network","The PA network will be sustainably expanded up to 25 per cent of state forests within the plan period.",""],[1,"576","5","Wildlife Governance and Enforcement Capacity Upgrade","Role and structure of Wildlife Divisions shall be reviewed.",""],[1,"576","5","Wildlife Corridor and Habitat Feasibility Studies","Feasibility studies will be conducted to identify the wildlife corridors, habitat and marine resources for biodiversity conservation.",""],[1,"576","5","Marine Protected Area Management Framework","Management framework will be developed to manage the marine protected areas.",""],[1,"577","2","Sundarbans Biodiversity Conservation and Wildlife Protection Measures","Due importance will be given to the Sundarbans Reserved Forest for its biodiversity conservation.",""],[1,"577","2","Emergency Tiger Response Team and Village Tiger Response Team Operations","The activities of 'Emergency Tiger Response Team' and 'Village Tiger Response Team (VTRT)' constituted with the local peoples of surrounding villages will be continued for relaying stray tigers.",""],[1,"577","2","Community-Based Resource Management Strengthening","Community engagement will be strengthened for resource management.",""],[1,"577","2","Sundarbans Strategic Environmental Assessment and Environmental Management Plan","A SEA report and Environmental Management Plan (EMP) will be developed for Sundarbans in the plan period which will be effective till 2041.",""],[1,"578","1","National Botanical Survey Completion Plan","A strategic action plan has taken to complete the botanical survey remaining areas of the country.",""],[1,"578","6","Wildlife Act Implementation Measures","The Government has formulated a wide array of measures to implement The Wildlife (Preserve and Safety) Act, 2012.",""],[1,"578","6","Forest Department Liaison for Wildlife Protection","Bangladesh Rubber Board is aiming to make liaison with forest department and help mitigating this wildlife crisis.",""]],"37":[[1,"540","3","Mainstreaming of Environment, Climate, and Disaster Concerns in Planning and Budgeting","The Eighth Five Year Plan will focus on integrating economic progress, environment, climate change and disaster management concerns into planning and budgeting",""],[1,"540","3","Policy and Institutional Capacity Building for Sustainable Resource Management","appropriate policy and institutional capacity building for sustainable water and land management, biodiversity conservation, climate resilient development and disaster management are crucial at all levels of government, especially with a greater emphasis at the local government level where most of the programmes are to be implemented",""],[1,"540","3","Green Growth Strategy","The Eighth Plan will also incorporate a strategy of green growth to harmonize economic growth for better environmental sustainability",""],[1,"545","2","National Adaptation Plan Formulation Process","The Government has initiated the process to formulate National Adaptation Plan (NAP) in 2019 with the support from GCF-UNDP and steered by MoEFCC.","MoEFCC"],[1,"545","2","Bangladesh Climate Change Strategy and Action Plan Update","Similarly, MoEFCC has initiated the process to update Bangladesh Climate Change Strategy and Action Plan (BCCSAP), 2009, which was supposed to be completed by this time, but could not be completed due to COVID-19 pandemic.","MoEFCC"],[1,"545","3","Climate Fiscal Framework Operationalization","The Government has also operationalized the Climate Fiscal Framework (CFF), developed by the Ministry of Finance, which provides the principles and tools for climate fiscal policy-making (CFP)","Ministry of Finance"],[1,"545","3","Climate-Lens Performance Audits","under the 7th Plan period, the Office of the Comptroller and Auditor General (OCAG), for the first time, conducted two pilot performance audits using climate lens with technical support from the Inclusive Budgeting and Financing for Climate Resilience (IBFCR) project of Finance Division","Office of the Comptroller and Auditor General | Finance Division"]],"38":[[1,"619","5","Polluter Enforcement and Capacity-Building Measures","Ensure enforcement and capacity building against polluters",""],[1,"619","17","Polluter Enforcement and Capacity-Building Measures","Ensure enforcement and capacity building against polluters",""],[1,"624","14","Environmental, Energy, and Water Audit Introduction","Introducing environmental audit, energy audit and water audit along with financial audit",""],[1,"625","1","Urban River Environmental and Ecological Restoration","Improvement of Environmental/Ecological Health of Rivers flowing through or near the cities and urban areas e.g. Buriganga, Sitalakkhya, Turag, Balu, Bongshi, Moyuri (in Khulna), Karnaphuli (Chattogram), etc.",""],[1,"625","3","Polluter Pays Principle Enforcement","Enforcement of Polluter Pay Principle",""],[1,"625","4","Department of Environment Pollution Monitoring and Investigation Capacity Building","Capacity building of DoE in monitoring, investigating, and examining pollution",""]],"39":[[1,"384","5","Fisheries Resource Management and Manpower Development","Manage resources including manpower development for ensuring optimum productivity, sustainability of production and conservation of fisheries resources.",""],[1,"384","6","Fish and Wetland Sanctuary Establishment and Maintenance","Establish and maintain fish and wetland sanctuaries which include ban on fishing in certain eco- sensitive areas.",""],[1,"384","7","Blue Economy and Sustainable Marine Fisheries Development","Harness the potential of blue economy, stock assessment of marine fisheries and promote sustainable exploitation of marine fishes, especially tuna and tuna like other pelagic fishing.",""],[1,"385","5","Sustainable and Traceable Fish Production Management System","the 8FYP will focus on sustainability (environmentally, socially and economically compatible) and quality (improved traceability for compliance) of the fish production and management system.",""],[1,"385","5","Safeguarding Mechanism for Landless and Marginal Farmers","A proper safeguarding mechanism for the landless and marginal farmers will be developed against any type of natural and non-natural shocks.",""],[1,"385","10","Fish Health Management Strategy and Aquaculture Policy","Fish health management strategy and aquaculture policy will be adopted and implemented for sustaining development of the fisheries sector;",""],[1,"385","12","Hatchery, Nursery, and Spawn Supply Monitoring Mechanism","Operation of hatcheries, nurseries and supply of spawn and fry, in which the private sector is the key player, will be constantly monitored by GO-NGO collaboration and public-private partnerships;",""],[1,"385","13","Fish and Shrimp Feed Input Market Monitoring","Production, import and marketing of fish and shrimp feed, feed ingredients, minerals and vitamin premix, and other inputs will be monitored constantly;",""],[1,"385","15","Integrated Floodplain Aquaculture and Conservation Programme","Aquaculture and conservation will be restructured to reinforce the strengths of each other, sustainable and community-based flood plain aquaculture will be combined with maintaining sanctuaries and restocking of indigenous species;",""],[1,"386","1","Conservation of Natural Breeding and Nursery Areas","Natural breeding, spawning, nursery and grow-out areas will be conserved to complete the whole lifecycle and natural reproduction process to ensure pure brood and fingerlings;",""],[1,"386","2","Shrimp Hatchery Transport and PCR Testing Requirement","Transportation and rearing in the hatcheries will be facilitated.",""],[1,"386","4","Traceability System for Fish Farming and Processing Inputs","Development of tractability system to identify the sources of contaminants/banned antibiotics and other chemicals used for fish farming and fish processing times so as to take lawful and corrective measures to improve/ratify them.",""],[1,"386","10","River and Lake Pollution Control Measures","Pollution control of river and lakes will be a major focus for government agencies.",""],[1,"386","11","Environmental Compliance for Development Projects","Any development projects must follow the environmental rules and regulations (and incorporate adequate mitigation measures in consultation with the Ministry of Fisheries and Livestock).","Ministry of Fisheries and Livestock"],[1,"386","11","Fish Pass and Fish-Friendly Regulator Construction and Maintenance","Projects and programmes will be implemented to construct and maintain fish-passes and fish-friendly regulators.",""],[1,"386","12","Fish and Wetland Sanctuaries Establishment","Fish and wetland sanctuaries which will be established with complete ban on fishing in certain eco- sensitive areas like the Sundarbans, parts of Kaptai Lake, and several sections of the river Halda, selected beels and haor areas and certain sections of the Bay of Bengal, etc.",""],[1,"386","13","Fish Conservation Strategy","Fish conservation strategy will be developed and implemented.",""],[1,"386","14","Hilsa Sustainable Fisheries Management Measures","For sustainable Hilsa fish production, Maximum Sustainable Yield (MSY) will be determined.",""],[1,"386","14","Hilsa Fisheries Monitoring and Community-Based Management","Strong monitoring, Community-based Management Approach and other precautionary measures will be applied to avoid overfishing.",""],[1,"386","14","Hilsa Sanctuary Management Strengthening","Management of Hilsa sanctuary will be strengthened.",""],[1,"386","15","Fish Act Enforcement and Revision","The Fish Act 1950 will be strictly implemented, and, if needed, the act will be revised.",""],[1,"387","1","Fishermen Social Safety and Alternative Livelihoods Support","Fishermen will have access to social safety sets like VGD and VGF and alternative livelihoods support during the restriction periods of fish catching.",""],[1,"387","6","Resource Protection and Illegal Trawler Control","Restrict and control pouching of resources and illegal entry of foreign trawlers",""],[1,"387","7","Vessel Tracking and Monitoring System","Introduce Vessel Tracking and Monitoring System (VTMS)",""],[1,"387","8","Conservation Needs Identification and Monitoring Framework","Identify conservation needs and methods that can be effectively administered and regularly monitored",""],[1,"387","9","Coastal Encroachment and Regulation Enforcement Cooperation","Cooperate with the Coast Guard and Navy on the control of encroachment and breach of regulation, also by local vessels.",""],[1,"387","10","Institutional Capacity Building and MCS Strengthening in the Bay of Bengal","Institutional capacity building of the concerned agencies, strengthening of monitoring, control and surveillance system (MCS) in the Bay of Bengal.",""],[1,"387","12","SAARC Digital Marine Fisheries Resource Mapping System","If a common DMFRM can be developed for SAARC countries that will be very useful to all the countries that at the same time will save the required investment in this respect.",""],[1,"387","14","Marine Protected Areas Establishment","Establish MPAs (marine protected areas) as breeding grounds.",""],[1,"388","6","Haor Basin Biodiversity and Fisheries Research Programme","Regular and long-term study/research on change of biodiversity, impact of sanctuary, habitat restoration; physical, chemical & biological changes of haor basin, fish production, fish migration and socio-economic condition of fisher folk will be implemented",""]],"40":[[1,"670","8","Natural Resource Restoration and Protection Measures","Restoring or enhancing natural resources · Protecting forests, promoting forest-derived foods to benefit poor/ women",""],[1,"670","8","Secure Land and Productive Resource Rights for Marginalized Groups","Securing ownership, access and management rights to land and other productive resources for poor or marginalised groups (e.g. ethnic minorities, emergency-affected populations)",""],[1,"670","8","Early Warning and Nutrition Surveillance Systems","Strengthening early warning and nutrition surveillance systems",""],[1,"670","8","Cross-Sectoral Resilience and Joint Programming","Increase collaboration with other sectors and joint programming to increase household/community resilience, especially in emergencies",""]],"41":[[1,"60","2","Poverty Reduction Package for the Poorest Districts","special attention will be given to reduce poverty in the poorest 10 districts through infrastructure supply, credit and social protection income transfers",""],[1,"83","3","Chittagong Hill Tracts Development Schemes","Several development schemes to strengthen agriculture, water management, infrastructure and to improve access to health and education have been implemented.",""],[1,"83","3","Regular Consultation with CHTA Local Population","The government maintains a regular consultation with the CHTA local population with a view to understanding their concerns and fnding solutions.",""],[1,"177","2","Refocusing ADP Spending for Lagging Districts","Refocusing ADP spending to improve the health, education, and infrastructure needs of the lagging districts.",""],[1,"177","5","Char Development Board Establishment","Establishment of Char Development Board to address the vulnerabilities of Char area.",""],[1,"177","11","Local Government Institution Block Grant and Training Support","Strengthen the LGIs working in the lagging districts through a higher share of block grants and training.",""],[1,"177","12","NGO and CBO Partnership for Local Service Delivery","Strengthen partnership with NGOs and CBOs in delivering all relevant local services including social security programmes.",""],[1,"177","13","District-Level Poverty Assessment and Targeted Programme Support","Conduct in-depth district-level poverty assessments for the top 10 poorest districts to do a more detailed and specific diagnostics of the fundamental constraints faced by these districts and tailoring public programme support to address those constraints.",""]],"42":[[1,"505","2","Rural Organization Promotion and Microcredit Support","RDCD had diverse interventions to secure the socio-economic development and accelerating rural economy through promotion of rural organizations, micro and supervised credit operation, rural capital management, facilitating production and market linkage for the rural products, developing rural micro infrastructure, conducting research and action research, etc.",""],[1,"505","2","Rural Production and Market Linkage Facilitation","RDCD had diverse interventions to secure the socio-economic development and accelerating rural economy through promotion of rural organizations, micro and supervised credit operation, rural capital management, facilitating production and market linkage for the rural products, developing rural micro infrastructure, conducting research and action research, etc.",""],[1,"505","2","Rural Micro-Infrastructure Development","RDCD had diverse interventions to secure the socio-economic development and accelerating rural economy through promotion of rural organizations, micro and supervised credit operation, rural capital management, facilitating production and market linkage for the rural products, developing rural micro infrastructure, conducting research and action research, etc.",""],[1,"505","4","Rural Employment Generation Projects","During the 7FYP, Palli Daridro Bimochon Foundation has implemented several projects aiming at rural employment generation,",""],[1,"506","2","Amar Bari Amar Khamar Program","Amar Bari Amar Khamar: This special program initiated by the Honourable Prime Minister to alleviate rural poverty.",""],[1,"526","4","Rural Microcredit, SME Credit, and Supportive Linkage Facilities","RDCD through its agencies will continue to provide micro credit, SME credit and supportive linkage facilities for the income generating activities and small entrepreneurship development.",""],[1,"530","13","Livelihood Improvement through Rural Micro Enterprise","Livelihood Improvement through Rural Micro Enterprise",""],[1,"531","2","Collateral-Free Microcredit Support for Small and Marginal Farmers","The foundation will seek to create employment opportunities and income generating activities of small and marginal farmers through access to microcredit, capital formation through small savings, and market linkages.",""],[1,"531","4","Small Entrepreneurs and Self-Employment Support Programme","During 8th plan period, PDBF will undertake activities on creation of small entrepreneurs, and self- employment programmes, awareness and skills development of rural youths with special focus on the poor and vulnerable groups in rural areas.",""],[1,"531","7","Diversified Rural Economy Strengthening","Along with efforts to improve productivity and diversity within agriculture, the on-going rural transformation whereby the income share of rural population from non-farm activities is growing will be further strengthened to provide a diversified income and employment base for the rural population.",""],[1,"531","7","Credit Policies for Non-farm Economic Activities","Supportive policies include the implementation of BDP2100, public investment in farm technology and productivity, support policies for strengthening fishing activities including the harnessing of the potentials of the Blue Economy, public investment in rural infrastructure, and credit policies to promote non-farm economic activities.",""]],"43":[[1,"507","3","Implementation of the CHT Accord","The government has made considerable effort to improve the situation as a part of the implementation of the CHT accord",""],[1,"507","3","Tribal Health, Nutrition and Population Plan","notably, the implementation of the Tribal Health, Nutrition and Population Plan (THNPP)",""],[1,"507","3","National Education Policy 2010 Implementation","notably, the implementation of the Tribal Health, Nutrition and Population Plan (THNPP), National Education Policy of 2010, the Third Primary Education Development Program (PEDP 3) and various water, flood control and irrigation projects",""],[1,"507","3","Third Primary Education Development Program","notably, the implementation of the Tribal Health, Nutrition and Population Plan (THNPP), National Education Policy of 2010, the Third Primary Education Development Program (PEDP 3) and various water, flood control and irrigation projects",""],[1,"507","5","Pre-school Education in Local Languages","Education programmes continue to facilitate the pre-school education in local languages.",""],[1,"508","10","Inclusionary National Development Policy for the Region","Making inclusionary National Development Policy for the region;",""],[1,"508","11","Ethnic Language School Curriculum Development","Developing school curriculum in ethnic language;",""],[1,"533","1","Integrated Social and Economic Development Support","ensure development in education, healthcare, food and nutrition, employment and protection of land-right, resources, and farm and nonfarm activities.",""],[1,"533","2","Monitoring and Supervision Strengthening for Service Delivery to Ethnic People","Monitoring and supervision will be strengthened so that education, health and maternal child health services, social safety nets, and nutrition and housing facilities reach the ethnic people.",""],[1,"534","3","Expansion of Social Protection for Poor and Vulnerable Groups","Social protection of the poor and vulnerable will be expanded",""]],"44":[[1,"623","1","Urban Land Bank Establishment for Housing Development","Following the National Housing Policy (NHP)-2016 urban land bank will be established in coordination with land ministry to materialize housing development process with unutilized abundant government land (Khas Land).","land ministry"],[1,"623","4","Efficient Housing Market Information and Assessment System","Creating Efficient Housing Market through continuous assessment of housing demand and supply as well as collection, analysis and dissemination of information about housing markets on a regular basis.",""],[1,"623","5","Housing Finance Mechanism Reform","Improving the Mechanism for Financing Housing by stimulating the efficiency and the dynamism of the mortgage market by ensuring a level playing field, carrying out reforms in land administration and regulatory environment, and restructuring BHBFC",""],[1,"623","8","Housing Loan Expansion for Vulnerable and Low-Income Groups","Extending housing Loans through Financial Institutions to vulnerable and disadvantaged groups, low-income people and people living in poverty.",""],[1,"623","9","Social Housing Project Design and Construction","Consider construction of social housing projects with particular emphasis on developing model and design of projects in view of the fact that large apartment buildings in social housing projects may be turned into poverty ghettos.",""],[1,"623","10","Slum and Informal Settlement Upgrading Programme","Undertaking programmes for physical improvement of the slum/informal settlements",""],[1,"623","11","Rental Housing Development for Low-Income Households","Development of rental housing, which caters for the needs of the majority of the low-income households.",""],[1,"623","12","Collective Tenure Security and Group Land Registration","Exploring the possibility of providing collective tenure security for communities so as to eliminate the need for individual titling and ameliorating land speculation and price increases.",""],[1,"623","13","Special Plot Allocation Quota for Poor and Vulnerable People","To Ensure equitable distribution of resource, special quota will be kept for poor and challenged people in allocation process of publicly developed plots.",""],[1,"623","13","Support for Community and Non-Profit Land Development Activities","Land development activities commenced by community organization and non-profit organizations will be given special support (NHP-2016)",""],[1,"623","14","Public-Private Partnership Housing Supply Initiative","For addressing backlog in housing supply PPP can be used.",""],[1,"623","15","Land Allocation Subsidy for Low-Income Households","low income people will be subsidized in land allocation process through the profit gained from selling of land at proper price to high income",""],[1,"624","2","Affordable Housing Construction and Plot Allocation","Providing housing for all including the shelter less and implementing the goals and objectives of the Housing Policy through construction of residential flats, and plots.",""],[1,"624","3","Enforcement of Real Estate and Residential Land Development Laws","Enforcement of real estate development and residential land development laws to accommodate low income population.",""],[1,"626","8","National Housing Problem Resolution Activities","Planning and undertaking of activities to solve housing problem of the country",""],[1,"626","10","Housing Sector Laws and Policies Preparation","Preparation of laws and policies to promote housing sector",""],[1,"626","14","Private Sector Engagement for Urban Housing Solutions","Creation of opportunities for involvement of the private sector in solving urbanization and housing problems with monitoring of customer delivery services and help enforcement of contracts.",""],[1,"628","5","Housing Management for Different Income Groups","Develop befitting housing management for different income groups",""],[1,"635","5","Low-Cost Housing Support Scheme","the Housing Ministry provides support to low cost housing schemes","Housing Ministry"],[1,"635","5","Serviced Land Development for Urban Housing","the Rajuk develops serviced land to facilitate urban housing","Rajuk"]],"45":[[1,"829","1","National Social Security Strategy Implementation","The NSSS is designed to addressing the specific concerns and vulnerabilities of women at different stages of the life cycle.",""],[1,"829","1","Social Insurance for Working Women","The introduction of the proposed social insurance is particularly important mitigation measure for risks faced working women.",""],[1,"830","1","National Social Insurance System Pilot","A national social insurance system (NSIS) enabling people to invest in their own social security, providing protection against the risks of old age, disability, unemployment and maternity will be initiated on a pilot basis under the National Social Security Strategy.",""],[1,"830","1","Low-Cost Contributory Insurance Model for Women","A low-cost contributory insurance model should be initiated in collaboration with private sector by providing subsidy, if necessary, so that women can access the support at a low contribution.",""]],"46":[[1,"838","7","Disability Inclusion and Rights Mainstreaming Strategy","Persons with disabilities will be brought into the mainstream of the development process.",""],[1,"838","10","Guidelines for Identification of Persons with Disabilities","Prepare guidelines for the identification of PWDs",""],[1,"838","17","Strengthen Monitoring of Schemes for Persons with Disabilities","Strengthen monitoring of schemes for PWDs",""],[1,"846","5","Disability Inclusion and Rights Promotion Strategy","The Government will promote and protecting rights of persons with disabilities to facilitate their full participation in mainstream social, political and cultural lives.",""],[1,"846","7","Implementation of the Rights and Protection of Persons with Disabilities Act","The Rights and Protection of the Persons with Disabilities Act, 2013 (RPPD) will be implemented to ensure international standards on disability rights as set out in the Act.",""],[1,"846","7","Strengthening of the National Coordination Committee for Persons with Disabilities","The National Coordination Committee for Persons with Disabilities will be strengthened to monitor and coordinate activities of different ministries/divisions in implementation of the Act.",""],[1,"846","7","Prioritization of Poor and Vulnerable Groups in Implementation","Requirements of the poor and vulnerable, including women and children, will be prioritized in all activities and implemented.",""],[1,"847","5","Disability Access and Inclusion Measures","Measures will be taken so that persons with disabilities can have access to all physical facilities and information and communication.",""],[1,"847","5","Disability Participation in Decision-Making Processes","Inclusion of persons with disabilities in various national and community level decision making processes that affect their lives will be ensured.",""],[1,"847","5","Community-Based Rehabilitation Services for Persons with Disabilities","Services like early detection and timely medical intervention, fitment of artificial aids and appliances, educational services in special and integrated schools, vocational rehabilitation including micro-credit will be provided to persons with disabilities through community based rehabilitation programmes.",""],[1,"847","6","Organization and Empowerment of Persons with Disabilities","it is necessary to support the organising of people with disabilities in order to make them 'visible' and to empower them to make their voices heard.",""]],"47":[[1,"846","1","Skills Building and Livelihood Transition Support for Sex Workers and Transgender People","The Government will, in conjecture with NGOs and the private sector, introduce provisions for skill building of sex workers and transgender who prefer to opt out of sex work and build their lives around safer occupations in the form of either small entrepreneurship or small cooperative societies.",""],[1,"846","2","Inclusion of Sexual Minority Groups in Social Protection Mechanisms","Sexual minority groups will be integrated in the national social protection mechanisms including access to social health insurance or other transfers to ensure realization of human rights and fundamental freedom of those socially excluded that are most vulnerable.",""]],"48":[[1,"834","3","Child Protection Law Enforcement and Harmonization","2) enforcing and harmonizing laws against children abuse, trafficking, exploitation;",""],[1,"834","3","Universal Birth Registration Mobilization","3) mobilizing municipal corporations to register all births;",""],[1,"834","3","National Child Labour Elimination Action Plan Implementation","4) eliminating child labour by instigating the National Plan of Action for Implementing the National Child Labour Elimination Policy 2010;",""],[1,"834","3","Child Marriage Elimination Enforcement","5) elimination of child marriages through enforcement of Child Marriage Act 2017 and 6) ensuring children are removed from abusive and exploitative circumstances.",""],[1,"840","5","Child Protection Measures for Vulnerable Children","Measures will be taken to ensure right to protection from all forms of abuse, exploitation and violence for all children, particularly those who are vulnerable such as street children and orphans.",""],[1,"840","5","Enforcement of Child Protection Laws and Policies","The policies of existing NPA will be used against sexual abuse and exploitation of children and trafficking.",""],[1,"840","5","Harmonization and Enforcement of Child-Related Laws","Laws affecting children will be harmonized and enforced.",""],[1,"840","5","Child Protection Awareness and Diversion Scheme","Awareness amongst law enforcing officials and judicial officers and the development of a diversion scheme involving the courts, social workers and probation officers as an alternative to custodial sentences will be undertaken.",""],[1,"840","5","Child Protection Social Awareness Campaign","A widespread social awareness campaign and community mobilization on protection issues will be undertaken to foster positive attitudes towards children, particularly girls, and bolster the positive attitude of parents and decision-makers on the need to protect children regardless of the socio-economic environment.",""],[1,"841","1","Universal Birth Registration Mobilization","The Municipal Corporations and Pourashavas will be mobilized to register all births.",""],[1,"841","1","Child Marriage Awareness Campaign","Awareness raising programmes through union Parishad members, and leaders of social opinion including Imams will be conducted to eliminate the practice of early marriage.",""],[1,"841","2","Child Labour Reduction and Elimination Measures","Effective measures will be taken to reduce child labour, and eliminate worst forms of child labour with a particular focus on child domestic workers, migrants, refugees and other vulnerable groups.",""],[1,"841","2","Policy for Children in the Formal Sector","a policy for children in the formal sector focusing on those caught up in the worst forms of child labour will be formulated.",""],[1,"841","2","Street Children Protection and Rehabilitation Programme","Street children will be assisted in accessing their rights and protecting them from all forms of abuse and exploitation.",""],[1,"841","3","Community Support and Reintegration for Abused Children","interventions will include developing community support for these children, providing livelihood alternatives, basic services and adoption",""],[1,"841","3","Child Abuse Prevention Policy and Legislation","implementing policies and legislation necessary for the prevention of abuse, discrimination, exploitation and violence",""],[1,"841","3","Coordination to Combat Child Sexual Abuse and Trafficking","Steps will be taken to increase efficiency to combat sexual abuse, exploitation and trafficking of children through enhanced coordination and cooperation",""]],"49":[[1,"781","3","Extreme Poverty Eradication Commitment","Bangladesh is also committed to eradicate extreme poverty by FY2031.",""],[1,"787","2","COVID-19 Relief Income Transfer for Poor and Vulnerable Families","Thus, the 8FYP will plan to transfer an additional 2-3 per cent of GDP as income transfer to the poor and vulnerable families in FY2021.",""],[1,"787","2","Expansion of Social Protection Allocation","For the medium term, the 8FYP will increase current social protection allocation of 1.2 per cent of GDP (excluding the civil service pension) to about 2.0 per cent of GDP by FY2025.",""],[1,"787","3","Mother and Child Benefit Programme","MoWCA has already piloted an improved version of both programme in 2018-19 and based on experiences has inaugurated a vision with brand named Mother and Child Benefit Programme on 24th July 2019.","MoWCA"],[1,"790","1","Vulnerable Group Development Social Safety Net Programme","The Vulnerable Group Development (VGD) programme is the largest social safety net programme under the Ministry of Women and Children Affairs (MoWCA).","Ministry of Women and Children Affairs (MoWCA)"],[1,"790","2","Universal Disability Transfer Scheme","A universal scheme invoking higher than average transfer amount should be designed for the sever disables persons.",""],[1,"790","5","Care Dependency Benefit for Families Caring for Children with Disabilities","A Care Dependency Benefit could be established/ expanded for families caring for children with disabilities.",""],[1,"791","2","Adult Disability Benefit Expansion","An adult disability benefit should be established or expanded for all those aged 19-60 with a severe disability.",""],[1,"791","5","Freedom Fighters Safety Net Allowance Programme","The Ministry of Liberation War Affairs will continue to implement safety net programmes for the freedom fighters through allocation of monthly allowances for the freedom fighters.","Ministry of Liberation War Affairs"],[1,"791","5","Freedom Fighters Health Support Programme","This ministry has been implementing special programmes for addressing the health issues of general and wounded freedom fighters.","Ministry of Liberation War Affairs"],[1,"791","5","Credit Facilities for Freedom Fighters and Families","The government will provide credit facilities to freedom fighters and their families for income generation.",""],[1,"792","1","Anti-Discrimination Legislative and Affirmative Action Measures","The Government is highly sensitive to ensuring the elimination of all kinds of socio-economic discrimination against these groups through legislative and other affirmative actions.",""],[1,"792","1","Inclusive Access to Social Security and Basic Services","The Government will also ensure that these groups have similar access as the rest of the population to all Social Security programmes and to all publicly provided basic services in education, health, nutrition, population planning, water supply and sanitation.",""],[1,"815","8","Mother and Child Benefit Programme Enhancement","Enhance Mother and child benefit programme",""],[1,"816","3","Mother and Child Benefit Programme Enhancement","Enhancing Mother and child benefit programme: This relates to enhancing facilities for mother and children though provisions of cash and in-kind transfers.",""],[1,"816","3","Early Childhood Development and Child Protection Programmes","Extensive programmes and projects are also required to be launched for the early childhood development, protection of the children from violence and repression and for overall development of the children.",""]],"50":[[1,"736","2","National Identification Database Upgrade for e-KYC and Digital ID Coverage","Strengthen national identification (NID) database: The national identification (NID) database - originally initiated for issuing voters' ID - currently registering about 110 million adult citizens has been made available for establishing an electronic know your customer (e-KYC) ID verification system, boosting the expansion of DFS through fast customer on boarding and reduced cost in the process.",""],[1,"736","3","Single Social Registry of Beneficiaries","Develop a single registry of beneficiaries: One critical challenge confronting Bangladesh's social protection system is to develop a single social registry of beneficiaries drawing on from separate databases maintained by various ministries.",""],[1,"736","4","Full Digitisation of G2P Payments","An important priority for the 8th plan would be to achieve the complete digitalisation of the G2P payment system, linking the beneficiary targeting of social security/enrolment to NID along with operationalizing the National Household Database for addressing exclusion and inclusion errors in beneficiary selection.",""],[1,"748","9","Universal Identity System Launch","Launching of Universal Identity System [UIS] with profiling for multi-purpose use",""],[1,"749","22","Universal Identity System Launch","Launching of Universal Identity System [UIS] with profiling for multi-purpose use",""]],"51":[[1,"680","3","Retirement and Pension Age Redefinition Reform","consider redefining the old age for retirement and pensions purposes from 60 plus years to 65 plus years as per international convention;",""],[1,"680","3","Old Age Program Implementation","implement the Old Age Program as defined under the NSSS 2015;",""],[1,"680","3","Universal Old Age Pension Scheme","consider implementing a universal old age pension scheme based on a combination of public and private funding and partly voluntary as explained in the Report;",""],[1,"680","3","Universal Health Care System Expansion","consider moving towards an universal health care (UHC) system that uses a mix of publicly and privately funded health insurance and low-cost public health care facilities.",""]],"52":[[1,"52","1","Ashrayan Housing Support for Landless and Homeless Families","under the Ashrayan Project the government has provided housing facilities to the landless and homeless families.",""],[1,"63","4","Government Support for Low-Cost Housing","Government subsidy and grants will be provided for low-cost housing for the poor.",""],[1,"96","16","Homeless Housing Construction Programme","Construction of home for homeless people",""],[1,"97","14","Homeless Housing Construction","Construction of home for homeless people",""],[1,"164","3","Ashrayan Housing for Landless and Homeless Families","Ashrayan Project with the government allocation of Tk. 1160 Crore in the first phase aims to provide 65,726unit house along with 2 decimal land to the landless and homeless families, on the occasion of Mujib centenary.",""],[1,"164","3","Ashrayan Housing Expansion Phase","Another 128,000 houses will be built in the next one year.",""],[1,"164","3","Nationwide Phased Housing Construction","Houses will be constructed for 8,85,622 families from all districts of the country in phases.",""]],"53":[[1,"626","7","Sustainable and Safe Infrastructure Development for Planned Urbanization","Development of sustainable and safe infrastructure through ensuring proper planning, adequate research and optimum use of land for cost effective housing and planned urbanization.",""],[1,"626","9","Public Buildings and Infrastructure Design, Construction, and Maintenance","Preparation of architectural and structural design of public buildings and other infrastructure, their construction and maintenance",""],[1,"626","12","Government Officers and Staff Accommodation Programme","Undertaking activities to solve the accommodation problem of government officers and staff",""],[1,"627","17","Rental-Purchase Multi-Storey Residential Housing Construction","Construct multi-storied residential buildings for sale on rental-purchase basis",""],[1,"627","19","Government Employee and Women’s Housing Construction and Maintenance","Construct, repair, and maintain residential buildings for government employees, dormitories/hostels for working and job seeking women",""],[1,"627","20","Residential and Hostel Housing Architecture Preparation","Prepare architecture for residential buildings for government employees, dormitories/hostels for working and job seeking women",""],[1,"627","22","Government Employee Housing Allocation","Allot flats to government employees",""],[1,"627","24","Satellite Town Development under Public-Private Partnership","Construct satellite towns under PPP",""],[1,"631","1","Purbachal Planned Township Development","The Township will be linked with 8 (eight) lane wide expressways from the Airport Road/ Progati Swarani crossing with the distance of only 6.8 km.",""],[1,"631","3","Jhilmil New Town Development Project","Jhilmil new town project is located at Keraniganj across the Burigonga River.",""]],"54":[[1,"626","13","Urbanization and Construction Research and Innovation Programme","Conducting research and innovate technology on urbanization, housing, construction of buildings, construction materials and techniques",""],[1,"627","26","Low-Cost Eco-Friendly Housing Technology Promotion","Conduct research and promotion of low-cost eco- friendly housing technology with the special emphasis on Autoclave Aerated Concrete (AAC) blocks",""],[1,"627","27","House Building Technology Dissemination, Testing and Training","Disseminate house building technology and conduct testing and training",""],[1,"627","28","Urban Development Research Programme","Conduct research on matters related to urban Development",""],[1,"628","7","House Building Research and Training on Innovative Construction Technology","Research and training related to house building, and modern and planned In the light of the importance of innovation of house construction technology for the urbanization low-income group and the provision of training to all concerned on the innovated technology, this has been identified as the Ministry's 4th priority sector",""]],"55":[[1,"23","14","ICT for Recovery and Shock Adaptation","Harnessing the power of ICT for revival from the effect of COVID 19 and for adaptability to shocks arising from health crisis, natural disaster, climate change, or global shift in competitive landscape",""],[1,"62","2","Digital Bangladesh ICT Transformation Initiative","The ICT revolution implemented through the Digital Bangladesh initiative of Hon'ble Prime Minister Sheikh Hasina launched in 2009 holds the promise of lifting labor productivity and citizen welfare through the adoption of mobile technology.",""],[1,"62","3","ICT Tax Policy Reform","This taxation problem will be addressed speedily to enable stronger progress with ICT during the 8FYP.",""],[1,"62","4","Fixed ICT Infrastructure Investment","Public investment will focus on the supply of fixed infrastructure",""],[1,"62","4","Mobile Technology Expansion to Unserved Areas","public policy will facilitate the private sector expansion of mobile phone technology to unserved areas, incentivize the use of mobile technology, especially in rural areas, and support a more rapid growth of higher value-added mobile services such as internet, video phone and data services",""],[1,"62","4","Public Sector E-Services Digitization Programme","More rapid adoption of e-services in public sector will be encouraged through a programme of digitization of public services including staff training",""],[1,"62","4","ICT Education and Skills Development","Special effort will be made to augment ICT education and availability of skilled ICT staff",""],[1,"64","7","Online Public Service Delivery and Grievance Redress System","Strengthen service delivery through implementing online transactions for all public services with simplified application forms, pre-announced service response timelines and service charges, and an online grievance redressal system.",""],[1,"65","6","Government Data Systems and Administrative Data Access Improvement","With government investment, focused efforts can ensure data will be more useful and accessible to (1) Deliver on the SDGs by improving management information systems that collect data at the point of service delivery and by enabling access to local administrative data via portals, (2) Stimulate demand for data by making data more accessible for those responsible for decision-making as well as those seeking to hold them to account, and (3) Harmonize investments, roles, and responsibilities - across both government and development partners/agencies - to reduce overlaps and increase efficiency and effectiveness.","BBS"],[1,"95","2","ICT-Based E-Governance and E-Transactions Expansion","An important instrument of governance improvement has been the adoption of ICT-based solutions to public business and transactions.",""],[1,"95","2","Transfer of E-Governance Instruments to Local Governments","Instruments of e-governance are also being transferred to local governments for greater transparency and efficiency of services.",""],[1,"164","4","Digital Bangladesh Service Delivery Initiative","Digital Bangladesh initiative aims to bring government services to the doorsteps of the people and ensuring transparency and accountability in every sector.",""],[1,"235","5","E-Governance and Public Service Digitalization","E-governance allows citizens to communicate effectively with the government and allows them to experience public services digitally.",""],[1,"235","5","Ministry Information Publication Through Public Websites","the Government has made all necessary information of the Ministries available through various websites which are completely accessible to the public.",""],[1,"235","5","Public Official Training for Website Maintenance and Data Updating","the Government has trained more than 50,000 public officials to maintain these websites and update data and information regularly.",""],[1,"235","5","National Government Information Portal","the Government has also introduced a national portal containing information from all the Ministries, while e-Service centres were",""],[1,"236","1","National ICT Infra-Network Phase III Expansion","the project has now received an extension for its third phase, where it will be more citizens centric and deliver higher bandwidth.",""],[1,"236","2","E-Governance Service Delivery Expansion","The government's e- governance initiative comprises 5 components i.e., Service Process Simplification (SPS), 'less paper office,' government services portal, land information services, and government forms portal.",""],[1,"254","6","Union Digital Centre Technology Infrastructure Enhancement","Technology infrastructure in regions where UDCs are located will be enhanced to enable residents of the regions to access the services of UDCs.",""],[1,"254","6","Local Awareness Campaigns on Union Digital Centre Services","Awareness campaigns about the operations of UDCs at the local need to be launched.",""],[1,"254","7","Digital Literacy Enhancement Initiative","The level of digital literacy of the general public will be enhanced to tandem with the rapid roll out of digitization in the public systems and launching of e-services to enable them to benefit from them.",""],[1,"314","1","Rural Digital Divide Bridging Initiative","The 8FYP envisions bridging the gap.",""]],"56":[[1,"649","23","Effective Monitoring System for Digitalization","Establishment of effective monitoring system at all levels for digitalization.",""],[1,"653","8","Health Surveillance and Information Systems Modernization","Adopting new technologies to strengthen surveillance, data quality and information systems.",""],[1,"654","8","Digitalization of Health Ministry Systems and Services","Extensive digitalization at all levels of MOHFW and development of digital data management, incremental use of IT in health, population and nutrition services.","MOHFW"],[1,"656","9","Urban Health Information System Development and Use","Developing and utilizing urban HIS for effective management of urban health care.",""],[1,"664","3","National Health Card and Electronic Medical Records System","Government has been preparing to introduce Health Card for its citizen.",""],[1,"664","3","Digitalization and Automation of the Health Care System","there is strong commitment from the Government to capitalization of 4IR, and to act on that health care system needs to be fully digitalized and optimized through automation as much as possible.",""],[1,"664","3","Electronic Health Tracking and Interoperability Platform","During the 8FYP period, Health Card with linked EMR database will be established along with scaling up of electronic tracking system of the citizen's health.",""],[1,"667","10","Digital Health Data Management and Medical Education Expansion","Development of digital data management, incremental use of IT in medical institutions and making quality medical and nursing education service easily available to all concerned.",""],[1,"667","17","Technology-Based Education and Training Programme Strengthening","Strengthen technology-based education and training programmes for quality improvement and effective monitoring.",""],[1,"668","4","Technology Training and Information Exchange Initiative","Develop new ideas/thoughts for training and exchange information/data on required technology",""],[1,"681","1","National Digital Health Information System Implementation","Implementation of eMIS activities; DHIS2 activities; e-Filling activities in DGFP, etc. all over the country.",""],[1,"681","2","Digital Registration of FP-Related NGOs","Digitalization of the registration of all FP related NGOs working with DGFP.",""]],"57":[[1,"477","35","ICT-Based Postal Service Modernization","Now the Department of Posts is gradually updating and upgrading the traditional postal services through ICT based modernization process.",""],[1,"481","6","Mail Processing and Logistics Service Centre Project","14 new modern mail processing centres will be set up to provide maximum service to the postal customers by replacing the 40/50- year old traditional mail processing centres with a combination of article, sorting and delivery system through the implementation of the \"Mail Processing and Logistics Service Centre project\".",""],[1,"481","7","Digital Financial Inclusion through Postal Services","Postal Money (Dak Taka) has been introduced through post offices to ensure balance transactions for the people who are deprived of banking facilities.",""],[1,"482","1","Postal Cash Card Service Expansion","Postal cash card service is being provided in 638 post offices across the country including all District and Upazila post offices.",""],[1,"497","8","District-Level Digital Transformation Support and Monitoring","Ensuring institutional presence in all the districts to accelerate the digital transformation, assessment of the network and technology requirements and digital divide, coordinating with the service providers and government entities along with government policy implementation monitoring regarding digital connectivity and services in the locality.",""],[1,"497","9","Digital Postal Services Introduction","Introducing digital postal services along with traditional postal services;",""],[1,"497","12","ICT-Based Mail Transport Supervision","Bringing Mail transportation, collection and distribution under ICT based strict supervision;",""],[1,"497","16","IT-Based Entrepreneur Development in Rural Post Offices","Adopting activities for making at least one IT based entrepreneur in each of rural post offices.",""],[1,"497","17","Mailing Operator and Courier Service Licensing Capacity Enhancement","Increasing the capacity of mailing operator and courier service licensing authority in order to ensure quality service.",""],[1,"497","18","Expansion of Nagad Digital Financial Services","Expansion Department of Posts digital financial service 'Nagad' provided remote areas across the country.",""],[1,"497","19","National Digital Post Office Coverage","Bringing all the villages of the country under the services of digital post office.",""],[1,"497","20","Nationwide Ad-Mail Service","Introduction of nationwide ad-mail service by 2021.",""],[1,"497","21","In-House Digital Commerce Hubs","Establishment of in-house digital commerce hubs across the country.",""],[1,"497","22","Education Insurance for School-Going Girls","Introduction of education insurance \"Sukanya\" for school going girls.",""]],"58":[[1,"117","2","Expansion of ICT, Science and Technology, and R&D Infrastructure","the 8th FYP should allocate adequate resources to continue expansion of existing infrastructure for ICT growth, science and technology and research and development.",""]],"59":[[1,"298","1","E-Commerce Promotion and Entrepreneurship Project","Other projects under MoC i.e., 1) Bangladesh Regional Connectivity Project 2) Export Diversification and Competitiveness Development Project (Tier-2), 3) E- banijjo korbo, nijer babsa gorbo project will certainly contribute to establish digital Bangladesh as envisaged under the \"Vision-2021\" and the Perspective Plan 2021.","MoC"],[1,"298","1","Digital Commerce Policy Implementation","Digital Commerce Policy-2018 has been approved by the Cabinet and duly made operational.",""],[1,"298","1","E-Commerce Cell Coordination Mechanism","Under this policy, an e-Commerce Cell will work to coordinate and boost up electronic commerce in Bangladesh.",""]],"60":[[1,"341","2","Review of ICT and Banking Tax Policy","The tax rates on ICT services and banking services are very high and may need to be revisited, especially to spur the expansion of ICT.",""],[1,"342","11","ICT Policy Review for Private Incentive Alignment","the Government will review all ICT policies to ensure their consistency with private incentives",""],[1,"343","1","ICT Tax Policy Review","The tax policy for ICT will be re- examined comprehensively to check for its consistency with the development objective of faster growth of this high return enterprise.",""],[1,"777","3","ICT Taxation Reform","So, the reform of ICT taxation is an essential policy reform that will provide a substantial boost to GDP growth and employment in Bangladesh, including youth employment.",""],[1,"777","4","Regulatory Simplification for Self-Employed ICT Services","the regulatory framework for self-employed ICT specialists and other ICT-based services must be made conducive to their growth.",""]],"61":[[1,"494","15","Cybersecurity Guidelines Publication","Publishing guidelines to reduce the risks, including prevention or mitigation of cyber-attacks consisting tools, policies, security concepts, security safeguards, guidelines, risk management approaches, actions, training requirements, best practices, assurance and technologies for the providers and users.",""],[1,"494","16","Telecom Security Guidelines Formulation","Formulating Security guidelines for the Telecom providers according to the ITU-T recommendations and international best practices including ETSI, FIRST, IETF, IEEE, ISO/IEC JTC 1, OASIS, OMA, TCG, 3GPP/3GPP2 etc. standards.",""],[1,"494","17","Secure Private Networks and Applications Guidelines","Formulating guidelines for implementing secure private networks and secure applications.",""],[1,"494","18","Telecommunication System Security Assessments","Perform security Assessments for all building blocks of the telecommunication system including CPEs and applications.",""],[1,"495","1","Public Telecom Network Audit and Compliance Review","Auditing the public telecom networks to ensure the conformity with the guidelines of the assurance framework.",""],[1,"495","2","Critical Network Security Assessment and Certification","Perform security assessments and issue time-bound certificate for the important networks of the country.",""],[1,"495","3","On-Demand Security Assessment and Reporting","Performing on-demand security assessments and provide report/recommendations.",""],[1,"495","4","National Security Operations Centre Establishment","viii) Establishing a National Security Operations Centre (SOC).",""],[1,"495","5","Digital Security and Privacy Coordination Enhancement","Enhance National and international coordination and cooperation pertaining digital security and privacy.",""],[1,"495","6","Digital Privacy and Critical Information Legislation","Formulation of appropriate legislations in order to safeguard privacy, private data and critical information in the digital space.",""],[1,"495","7","Institutional Framework for Research Activities","Establishing institutional framework for conducting research activities.",""],[1,"495","8","Dedicated Digital Security Training Facility","Establishing dedicated training facility on digital security in order to provide regular training to the Management/governance personnel; Architect/designer (digital infrastructure, software, Authentication and Authorization Infrastructure etc.); Admins/operators (Systems management, system administrators, telecom/network engineers); Security specialists; User coordinators (responsible for group of users, main contact point); Users and special communities; Software developers; and the People responsible for acquisition of hardware, software).",""],[1,"495","9","National Telecommunication and Digital Standards Body","Establishing a dedicated national telecommunication and digital standards body.",""],[1,"495","10","National Telecommunication and Digital Standards Strategy","Formulation of a national telecommunication and digital standards strategy and review relevant laws, regulations, and policies.",""],[1,"495","11","Mandatory National Standards for Procurement and Product Development","Mandating national use of standards, either in product procurement or product development.",""],[1,"495","15","Formulation of Native IoT/M2M Standards","Formulating native standards for IoT/M2M harmonized with global standards.",""],[1,"495","17","Revision of the National Numbering Plan for IoT/M2M","Revisiting National Numbering Plan to accommodate the numbering needs of IoT/M2M.",""],[1,"495","18","Inter-Operator Roaming and Inter-Network Mobility Guidelines","Addressing the issues related to Inter-Operator Roaming and Inter-Network Mobility through proper guidelines or directives.",""],[1,"495","19","Privacy and Data Protection, KYC, and Customer Traceability Measures","Addressing the issues related to privacy and data protection along with KYC and customer traceability.",""],[1,"495","21","Indigenous Manufacturing and IoT/M2M Device Development with Product Certification","Promoting indigenous manufacturing and development of IoT/M2M devices with product certification.",""],[1,"496","1","Inter-Ministerial IoT/M2M Awareness and Coordination Initiative","Coordinating with different ministries/departments/bodies in order to provide information on the applicability and benefits of using IoT/M2M in different sectors especially health, agriculture, safety and surveillance system, health etc.",""],[1,"496","2","Public Cloud Provider Certification and Cloud Regulatory Framework","Assigning a government body with appropriate authority and responsibility in order to certify/accredit qualified public cloud service providers within and outside the country along with formulation and enforcement of cloud framework, standards, risk assessment methodologies, security and data protection aspects, supervision guidelines and relevant regulations.",""],[1,"496","4","Scalable Pilot Project for Transformation and Consolidation","Initiating a scalable pilot project and starting the transformation and consolidation to prove the concept.",""],[1,"496","5","Campaigns, Workshops, and Training for Public, Private, and Government Entities","Promoting campaigns and workshops for both public and private sectors and providing training for government entities, post graduates, SMEs.",""],[1,"496","6","Legal Framework for Cloud Data Protection and Confidentiality","Addressing legislative issues of protection of personal data, confidentiality, public archive, bookkeeping etc. related to cloud infrastructure and services.",""],[1,"497","1","Innovation Ecosystem Synergy for Product Development","Promoting synergy amongst manufacturers, R&D centers, academia, service providers and other stakeholders for the development of high-quality new products and equipment.",""],[1,"497","3","Local Presence Promotion for Global Equipment and Software Vendors","Encouraging global equipment and software vendors to set up meaningful local presence in Bangladesh.",""],[1,"497","4","National Institute for Digital Sector Research and Human Resource Development","Establishing a National Institute for research and human Resource Development for digital sector.",""],[1,"497","5","Local Value Addition for Imported Digital Products","Encouraging a minimum amount of local value addition to the imported digital products to enhance local capacity and participation.",""],[1,"497","6","Institutional Boundary Reassessment for Emerging Technologies","Re-evaluating and re-defining the boundaries of incumbent institutions considering the emerging convergence and disruptive technologies and their possible role in future.",""]],"62":[[1,"488","1","Second Communication Satellite Development","Right now there is a requirement of a second satellite as the broadcasting sector is already become dependent on the country's own satellite.",""],[1,"488","1","Satellite-Based Digital Broadcasting Services Expansion","Furthermore, new satellite- based services such as Digital Audio Broadcasting (DAB), Satellite Phones etc. have to be introduced depending on the market needs.",""],[1,"488","2","Satellite-Based Vessel Tracking and Monitoring System","Satellite based 'Vessel Tracking & Monitoring System (VTMS)' will facilitate detect fleet patterns and aids monitoring, control, and surveillance efforts whenever needed, especially in case of natural disasters.",""],[1,"488","2","Satellite-Based Stock Assessment Support","VMS data of Bangladesh's satellite system also can support development of improved stock assessments.",""],[1,"488","2","Satellite Applications for Land, Weather, Water, and Pollution Monitoring","Satellites system has the potential to be utmost useful in land management, weather forecasting, water resources management and tracking of oil spills, potential polluters, temperature change and changes in the bio-system under the deep sea.",""],[1,"488","2","Satellite-Based E-Education and Telemedicine Services","Furthermore, with the help of e-education and telemedicine through Satellite Systems, the digital divide can be minimized.",""],[1,"493","17","National Space Strategy Formulation","Formulation of a comprehensive national space strategy for the peaceful use of space technology to support the development needs of the country.",""],[1,"494","1","Blue Economy Support through Space Technology","Planning and implementing activities in order to support the blue economy with the space technology.",""],[1,"494","2","Communication Satellite-Based Services Development","Developing new services and usage of communication satellite-based services which can be applied to various sectors including road and water transport, agriculture, health, education, resource management etc.",""],[1,"494","3","Private Sector Innovation Investment Promotion","Encourage private sector entities and entrepreneurs for investments in innovative solutions and applications.",""],[1,"494","4","Next-Generation Satellite Systems Development","Implementing the next generation of satellite systems considering future requirements of satellite services and for providing redundancy of 'Bangabandhu Satellite-1'.",""],[1,"494","4","Bangabandhu Satellite-2 Launch","Launching 'Bangabandhu Satellite-2' within 2023.",""],[1,"494","5","Space Technology R&D and Knowledge Transfer Programme","Enhancing and expanding R&D, coordinating programmes and national efforts and the development of national expertise and partnerships in space technology along with undertaking specialized programmes for knowledge transfer.",""],[1,"494","6","Satellite Communication Services for Hard-to-Reach Areas","Establishing effective communication system in riverine char, coastal, hilly and hard to reach areas through proper implementation of satellite services.",""],[1,"494","7","Satellite Services for Disaster and Crisis Management","Ensuring the utilization of satellite services and technologies in national disaster and crises management.",""],[1,"494","9","Space Technology Transfer Programmes and Mechanisms","Developing programmes and mechanisms to transfer the space technology solutions to other vital sectors.",""],[1,"494","10","Satellite Control and Operations Capacity Enhancement","Enhancing the satellite control and operations capacities.",""],[1,"494","13","Space Sector Regulatory and Authorization Framework","Developing a comprehensive regulatory and authorization framework for the space sector and monitor compliance.",""],[1,"494","14","Spectrum and Orbit Management Standards and Procedures","Developing standards and procedures to increase the efficiency of spectrum and orbit usage as well as situational awareness.",""]],"63":[[1,"822","2","Expand Women's Access to ICT and Business Opportunity Information","Access to modern technology related to business and jobs should be expanded at a low cost.",""],[1,"831","1","National Cyber Safety Awareness and IT Crime Protection","Protection from IT based crime and cyber safety awareness should be developed all over the country.",""]],"64":[[1,"761","2","BTV National News Network Expansion","The establishment of a full news network of BTV across the country and forming the news team of BTV in every district between 2021.",""],[1,"761","4","BTV World Satellite Channel Establishment","Between 2022, BTV World will be established as a separate satellite channel with distinct features",""],[1,"761","5","Virtual Studio and Animation Unit Establishment","By 2023, the establishment of a virtual studio and the latest animation unit will be created.",""],[1,"761","6","Nationwide Digitalization of BTV Terrestrial Broadcasting","Between 2024, 100% digitalization of BTV's terrestrial broadcasting system will be made across the country",""],[1,"761","7","Divisional TV Centre Establishment Programme","A full-fledged TV centre will be set up in every division of the country by 2024 for the preservation and promotion of local culture",""],[1,"761","8","BTV Digital Archive Establishment","By 2024, the complete digital archive of BTV itself will be established.",""],[1,"761","9","Global Expansion of BTV Broadcast Network","By 2030, the broadcast network of BTV will be established in the whole world.",""],[1,"761","10","FM Broadcasting Network Expansion","By 2021, 12 new FM Broadcasting Centre will be established of Bangladesh Betar and by 2030; the entire country including coastal areas will be brought under the network.",""],[1,"761","11","Modernization and Digital Equipment Upgrade for Bangladesh Betar Centres","By 2024, modernization and digital equipment will be set up in different centres of Bangladesh Betar",""],[1,"761","12","Bangladesh Betar Central Archive Establishment","The central archive of Bangladesh Betar will be established by 2025.",""],[1,"761","13","Bangladesh Betar Government Quarter Construction","Government quarter will be established at Bangladesh Betar's own place for officials and employees of the Bangladesh Betar by the year 2025.",""],[1,"761","15","Bangladesh Betar Digital News and Reporting Upgrade","Between 2030, there are plans to launch online newsletters of Bangladesh Betar, establishment of self-archiving cell, launch of spot reporting, separate news studio, mobile journalism, and complete correspondence structure.",""],[1,"761","16","District Information Office Expansion","26 district information offices of the Department of Mass Communication and District Information Complex will be built between 2025 and the remaining 42 will be established within 2030.",""],[1,"761","18","Digital Communication and Documentation Center Establishment","The Digital Communication and Documentation Center of the Department of Mass Communication will be established by 2025.","Department of Mass Communication"],[1,"762","1","Rural Awareness and Outreach Events","Between 2030, adequate film exhibition, song, workshop, meeting rally will be organized for the work of rural population for the purpose of good health, poverty alleviation, education, gender equality, supplementary drinking and sanitation.",""],[1,"762","9","Rural Public Awareness Media Distribution Campaign","In order to increase awareness among rural people, in the year 2030, 596 TV filers, 83 docudramas, 192 documentaries based on various issues will be distributed to the field of publicity in the field of publicity for publicity, BTV and various private TV channels.",""],[1,"762","10","BSS Journalist Capacity-Building for Audio-Visual News Production","By 2022, necessary measures will be taken to increase the capacity of BSS journalists to launch audio visual news of BSS and create audio visual news.",""],[1,"762","11","Digital Media Management Cell and Archive Establishment","Digital Media Management Cell and archive will be established by 2022.",""],[1,"762","12","Journalist Workplace Safety and Security Awareness Measures","By 2022, necessary action will be taken to increase the awareness and efficiency of the safe workplace and security of the journalists.",""],[1,"763","7","Digitalization of Publicity Activities","Digitalization process of publicity activities should be continued and state of the art technologies should be adopted for keeping pace with the rest of world.",""]],"65":[[1,"53","4","Investment Climate Improvement Initiative","The 8FYP will focus utmost attention to improving the investment climate for domestic and foreign private investment with a view to offsetting the lack-lustre private sector investment performance in the 7FYP.",""],[1,"57","3","Investment Climate Improvement and FDI Promotion Drive","A key strategic focus of the 8FYP would be to accelerate FDI inflows into Bangladesh through a massive drive to improve the investment climate and strengthen the capabilities of BIDA to do policy-based research, advocacy and deliver speedy and efficient services to foreign investors.",""],[1,"58","2","Investment-Friendly Environment Creation","the government's role will be to create the investment-friendly environment, restore and strengthen human health and welfare in the post COVID-19 world, and ease infrastructure constraints.",""],[1,"58","3","Serviced Land Provision under Special Economic Zones Initiative","major initiatives will be taken to broaden and accelerate the implementation of other major highways and bridges, power sector projects, and providing access to serviced land to foreign and domestic investors in the context of the Special Economic Zones (SEZ) initiative.",""],[1,"72","6","Renewed Efforts to Improve the Investment Climate","Both these areas would require renewed efforts in the 8FYP, with particular attention to improving the investment climate for private investment.",""],[1,"98","10","Private Investment Expansion","This will not be possible without substantial increases in domestic and foreign private investment.",""],[1,"99","1","Investment Climate Improvement for Private Investment","attention to improving the investment climate for domestic and foreign private investment",""],[1,"125","2","Foreign Direct Investment Expansion","foreign direct investment is projected to play a bigger role in the 8FYP",""],[1,"125","3","FDI Regulatory Streamlining and One-Stop Shop Reform","The main focus of these reforms has been to streamline the regulatory environment for FDI and reduce the transaction costs by reforming the Bangladesh Investment Board into a one-stop shop for managing all clearance requirements and facilitating FDI.",""],[1,"125","3","Free-Trade Zone and Special Economic Zone Development","The establishment of the Free-Trade Zones (FTZ) and Special Economic Zones (SEZs) have sought to address the important constraint emerging from serious land shortage and the associated complex land acquisition process.",""],[1,"126","1","Investment Climate Improvement for Foreign Investment Attraction","With concerted efforts to improve the investment climate, Bangladesh can claim a larger share of the foreign investment pie.",""],[1,"126","3","Investment Climate and Regulatory Reform Package","The strategy for mobilizing domestic and foreign private investment for the 8FYP will focus on a number of policies including: prudent macroeconomic management to ensure that inflation is contained, the exchange rate is stable but competitive, private sector credit supply is adequate with reasonable cost of borrowing, essential infrastructure such as power, transport services are available through efficient public sector investments, continued emphasis will be placed on the supply of serviced land through the EPZs and SEZs, trade logistic costs are lowered through ICT based and simplified clearance procedures and expansion of port capacities, and most importantly there will be an overhaul in the investment regulatory regime.",""],[1,"126","3","Bangladesh Investment Development Authority Capacity Building","This progress will be continued through building up of the capacity of the Bangladesh Investment Development Authority (BIDA) so that it can truly function as one stop shop for all investment approvals.",""],[1,"126","3","Investment Promotion Based on Research","BIDA will also be geared up to do effective investment promotion activities based on sound research.",""],[1,"126","3","Online Clearance and Regulatory Simplification Reform","Strong effort will be made to simplify the regulatory regime to minimize the need for clearances and where clearances are necessary these will be streamlined and mostly delivered online using ICT solutions.",""],[1,"126","3","Service Standards for Investment Clearances","Service standards will be established for clearances, especially property registration and getting electricity connection, which have been a severe constraint to improved investment climate.",""],[1,"126","3","Bankruptcy and Contract Enforcement Legal Reform","Areas where prudent regulations ae needed, such as bankruptcy law and contract enforcement, will be strengthened and made more effective through the appropriate legal measures that are based on good practice business experiences.",""],[1,"130","5","Foreign Direct Investment Facilitation in Export Sectors","In order to facilitate FDI in the traditional and new sectors, the government is accelerating the process of setting up Special Economic Zones under both",""],[1,"131","1","Special Economic Zone Handover to Foreign Investors","It also plans to hand over SEZs to investors exclusively from Japan, China, India and other countries in order to accelerate investment from those countries.",""],[1,"131","2","Plan-Supported Infrastructure and Industrial Import Financing","The massive increase in investment envisaged under the Plan-supported by FDI and public sector infrastructure investment-would also tend to increase import payments.",""],[1,"131","4","Foreign Direct Investment Mobilization Strategy","FDI inflows will assume a major role over time, growing up to 3% of GDP by FY25.",""],[1,"146","1","Private Investment Enhancement in Manufacturing","Private investment enhancement in manufacturing, in a balanced mix of domestic and FDI-based investments will be key",""],[1,"146","1","Investment Climate Improvement Reform","a big push to improving the investment climate will be essential",""],[1,"147","1","Private Sector Supportive Reforms and Policies","Overall, the 8.5% growth target by the end of the 8th Plan should be attainable, provided necessary supportive reforms and policies are put in place for the private sector to come forward and invest in the future of Bangladesh.",""],[1,"164","10","Investment Development Initiative","Investment Development initiative has been adopted to increase foreign direct investment (FDI) and local investment by creating an investment-friendly environment through extensive infrastructure development, including power, ICT and communication.",""],[1,"164","10","Mega Infrastructure and Special Economic Zones Development","The mega projects like construction of Padma Bridge, Metrorail, Elevated Expressway, Karnaphuli Tunnel, Matarbari Thermal Power Station, Payra Seaport, 100 Special Private Economic Zones etc. will create necessary physical infrastructure conducive to fostering both local and foreign investment.",""],[1,"185","1","Foreign Direct Investment Expansion Strategy","increasing the inflow of FDI in Bangladesh to 3% of GDP from current levels of about 1% would be critical for achieving the investment target under the 8FYP",""],[1,"185","1","Private Sector Investment Share Increase","The investment role of the private sector will be enhanced under the 8FYP based on an expanding role of FDI, with private investment accounting for 75% of the total investment",""],[1,"185","1","Private External Borrowing Expansion","the share of FDI in private investment Bangladesh and some limited external borrowing in foreign currency by the private sector, will increase markedly to 7%, compared with 3% in the 7FYP",""]],"66":[[1,"231","10","Bangladesh Investment Development Authority Institutional Reform","this issue received significant attention by the government in 2016, which motivated to form the Bangladesh Investment Development Authority (BIDA) under the Bangladesh Investment Development Authority (BIDA) Act 2016.",""],[1,"278","2","Investment-Friendly Business Environment Reform","creating an investment-friendly environment by transforming the state's role as a facilitator of economic and investment activities, strengthening economic and political governance, including the interaction of the state with the private sector; improving law and order; addressing the critically constraining infrastructure bottlenecks (in power, overland and port transport, and communications); establishing a sound and well-functioning financial sector; and addressing other barriers to productivity growth and international competitiveness.",""],[1,"291","4","Foreign Direct Investment Attraction Strategy","Therefore, courting FDI in the future to capture and expand supply chains will have to be an essential strategy for Bangladesh's export-oriented industrialization.",""],[1,"292","1","FDI-Driven Global Value Chain Industrialization Strategy","It needs to translate its RMG experience with GVC on to other sectors like Footwear and Leather goods, electronics, light engineering, toys, plastics, and other sectors with an aggressive strategy of FDI-driven GVC over the course of the next decade.",""],[1,"293","5","Completion of Industrial Parks and Special Economic Zones","Speedy completion of all on-going facilities and making those available on a timely and business-friendly way will be an important factor to spur domestic and foreign investment.",""],[1,"293","5","Business Environment Reform Package","The Government is focusing top attention on reducing the time it takes to (i) get electricity (ii) register property (iii) obtain credit (iv) trading across borders (v) enforce contracts and (vi) resolve insolvencies.",""],[1,"294","1","Investment Climate Improvement Programme","Improvements in the above areas are being developed under the direct supervision of the Prime Minister and coordinated by the Bangladesh Investment Development Authority (BIDA).",""],[1,"294","1","Global Investment Promotion Campaign","a strong marketing effort is being launched by BIDA and Commercial Wings in Bangladesh's diplomatic missions around the world (especially Europe and North America) to highlight and showcase the progress made on the investment climate front as a means to attract FDI.",""],[1,"294","3","Inclusive Economic Institutions Strengthening","what is needed is building and nurturing inclusive economic institutions that are effective in enforcing property rights, creating a level playing field for small and large entrepreneurs, SMEs and big business, and encouraging investment in innovation, adoption of new technologies and developing skills for the future.",""],[1,"294","4","Institutional Strengthening for Market Efficiency","Transforming the Bangladesh economy into a high-income economy over the next 25 years will require strengthening of institutions that promote sound economic fundamentals, enhance functioning of markets for efficient resource allocation, and foster competitive discipline.",""],[1,"294","4","Pro-Competition Market Governance","Intervention in markets would have to be kept to a minimum.",""],[1,"294","4","Conducive Policy Environment for All Investors","That means we need to revisit the approach to \"thrust sectors\" providing instead a conducive policy environment for all investors and let those with the best potential success.",""],[1,"296","2","Product Market Regulation and Fair Competition Measures","Product market intervention that includes domestic market entry regulations, regulatory control and tax policies to ensure fair competition between domestic and foreign firms, promoting domestic content requirements.",""],[1,"319","7","Investment Climate Improvement through Red Tape Reduction","Improving investment climate by reducing red tape and other complexities will encourage recipients to use remittance money for investment purposes, whose effect is more long lasting and less volatile than that of consumption",""]],"67":[[1,"115","2","Regulatory Reform and Public Infrastructure Support for Services Sector Investment","This transformation will be further enhanced by creating incentives for domestic and foreign private investment through regulatory reforms and supportive public investment in related infrastructure.",""],[1,"115","3","Services Export Expansion Strategy","A major growth and employment driver that will be supported is the expansion of services exports.",""],[1,"115","3","International Shipping Services Market Expansion","There is a huge trade gap in international shipping services and efforts will be made to capture a larger share of this market.",""],[1,"115","3","ICT Sector Tax Reduction and Regulatory Reform","The 8FYP will boost ICT activities through reductions in ICT taxes, through expansion of ICT education and training and through eliminating all regulatory barriers.",""],[1,"171","2","Services Sector Transformation Support","The 8FYP will accelerate this transformation of the services sector through support for access to credit, through the strengthening of ICT, and promotion of ICT exports and skills upgrading through training.",""]],"68":[[1,"340","4","Service Sector Deregulation and Private Provision Promotion","Over the years, through a series of deregulation drives and associated policies, the service sector was progressively deregulated and private provision encouraged.",""],[1,"340","4","Private Provision Expansion in Public Service Sectors","This deregulation policy has continued with recent efforts focused on encouraging private provision even in areas that are traditionally considered the domain of the public sector: education, ICT services, aviation and electricity.",""],[1,"342","2","Private Investment Incentive Policy Reform for Services","Improve the incentive policies for boosting private investment in services.",""],[1,"342","3","Public Investment in Key Service Sector Infrastructure","Increase public investment in key service sector infrastructure.",""],[1,"342","7","Public Institution Strengthening for Service Sector Development","Strengthen public institutions to support the growth of service sector and improve service quality, safety and accountability.",""],[1,"342","10","Service Sector Deregulation and Regulatory Reform","the deregulation drive to motivate greater private provision of service sector activities should be strengthened.",""],[1,"342","10","Stakeholder Consultation on Service Regulation","Each line Ministry concerned with regulating a particular service should undertake dialogue with concerned service providers through public meetings with business chambers and conduct special purpose surveys as necessary to obtain specific feedback on regulatory burden or other constraints.",""],[1,"342","10","Policy and Institutional Reform Based on Consultation Findings","The findings of these consultations and surveys will be used to reform policies and institutions as relevant.",""],[1,"348","3","Service Sector Regulatory Framework Modernization","all regulatory authorities dealing with transport, trade, education, health, tourism and ITC should be asked to look at the adequacy and relevance of all concerned regulatory issues, both prudential and enabling, with a view to upgrading and modernizing the regulatory framework for service sector.",""],[1,"350","6","Regulatory and Incentive Policy Improvement for Service Sector Investment","The improvements in regulatory and incentive policies will spur the expansion of private domestic and foreign investment.",""],[1,"350","7","Service Sector Investment Expansion","To secure the modernization of the service sector both public and private investment will need to go up as a share of GDP.",""]],"69":[[1,"481","4","Telecom Equipment Manufacturing and Assembly by Telephone Silpa Shangstha","Telephone Silpa Shangstha (TSS) is manufacturing/assembling Digital telephone sets, Digital PABX, Laptop, Multi-functional digital energy meter and battery/charger for mobile telephone sets to support the needs of telecommunication/ICT sector.",""],[1,"492","1","Expansion of Digital Device and Accessory Production","The Telephone Shilpa Sangstha Limited may also extend production of all sorts of digital devices and accessories to meet the domestic demands and export.",""],[1,"492","2","Local Presence and Value-Addition Requirements for Digital Products","global software and equipment vendors will have to be encouraged to set up meaningful local presence in Bangladesh in order to support and service their products sold into the Bangladesh market and into regional and global markets.",""],[1,"492","2","Stakeholder Synergy for New Product Development","synergies amongst manufacturers, R&D centres, academia, service providers and other stakeholders are essential for the development of high-quality new products and equipment.",""],[1,"492","6","Industrial Digital Transformation Regulatory Reform","Revising and/or formulating directives, guidelines, regulations, rules and other legal framework in order to support the digital transformation of the industry in minimum time.",""],[1,"492","7","Digital Connectivity and Analytics Infrastructure for Industrial and SME Areas","Making available high- speed internet connectivity, IoT, Cloud services and AI based analytics platform in the industrial areas, economic zones, export processing zones and SME populated areas.",""],[1,"492","10","Smart Factory and Smart Production Pilot","Piloting smart factory and smart production in collaboration with manufacturing entities in different location of the country.",""],[1,"492","11","Smart Cities and Smart Agriculture Piloting Initiative","Piloting 'smart cities' and 'smart agriculture' in different location of the country.",""]],"70":[[1,"523","5","Growth Centre and Market Development near Economic Zones","More Growth centre/markets (GCs) will be developed near the economic zones to create synergy in development and thus more employment opportunities;",""],[1,"523","6","Special Growth Centers for Localized Products","Special GCs will be developed at some areas to promote special localized products such as mangoes, watermelon, vegetables, guavas etic;",""],[1,"523","7","Growth Centre Service and Value Chain Support","The GCs will be facilitated to provide e-commerce, bank-agent banking, cold storage facilities and food processing and agricultural value-chain creation;",""],[1,"523","8","Growth Centre Development for Rural Economy and Value Addition","The GCs will be a hub of dynamic rural economy, restoring environment and adding beauty to landscape.",""],[1,"525","5","Growth Centre-Centric Urban Centre Development","Development of 500 Growth Centre centric urban centre with physical planning, water supply, waste management,",""],[1,"525","6","Growth Centres and Rural Markets Development","Development of growth centres and Rural Markets -1200 Nos.",""],[1,"525","14","Farmer-Market Linkage for Product Marketing","Ensure linkage among farmers, non-farm employees and markets for marketing products.",""],[1,"526","7","Rural Market Linkage and E-Commerce Development","Along with infrastructure the organized and efficient market linkage facilities will be developed with the provision of corporate marketing.",""],[1,"527","3","Rural Storage Facilities for Group-Based Farmers","BRDB envisioned to provide rural storage facilities for group/society based farmers in the rural area under 8FYP to ensure short time preservation and fair price for producer and consumers.",""],[1,"617","5","Economic Development Centers Development","Development of EDCs will be helpful in balancing population pressure and distribution of economic development across a range of cities (small, medium and large).",""],[1,"617","5","Special Economic Zones Development and Specialization","This will also help development of Special Economic Zones (SEZs) in the country.",""],[1,"628","12","Growth Centre and Hat-Bazaar Development and Management","Develop, maintain and manage growth centres and hats-bazaars connected via Upazila, Union and village roads",""]],"71":[[1,"550","2","Special Economic Zone Development and Administration","The introduction of Special Economic Zones (SEZ) has helped offer more structure to environmental management as it concentrates industrialization in few specific regions, allowing environmental regulators to monitor industrial pollution more accurately.",""],[1,"550","3","Green Technology Refinance Scheme","Bangladesh Bank established the refinance scheme for supporting environment friendly technology such as solar energy, bio-gas plants, and Effluent Treatment Plants (ETP).",""],[1,"553","2","Industrial Relocation to Economic Zones","The Government of Bangladesh is establishing Economic Zone, now time to shift all industries from residential area/building as well as from metropolitan.",""],[1,"565","4","Cleaner Coal Technology Adoption","the government will actively pursue the adoption of the cleanest form of technology for generation which carries the lowest environmental implications.",""],[1,"566","2","Expansion of Special Economic Zones with Environmental Regulation","the Government is committed to increase the number of Special Economic Zones (SEZ) with proper environmental regulations and infrastructure to ensure that industrial pollution is monitored and regulated under the 8FYP.",""],[1,"566","2","Environmental Fiscal Reforms Enforcement in Special Economic Zones","This will also allow the concerned authorities to effectively impose Environmental Fiscal Reforms (EFR) by effectively by monitoring pollution closely and enforcing any fines for the violation of environmental regulations.",""],[1,"566","3","Green Brick Production Transition","under the 8FYP, the Government will enhance its focus on moving to greener bricks by promoting the adoption of cleaner technological options.","Department of Environment"],[1,"566","4","Green Building Rating System Initiative","a national initiative will be taken to create public or private voluntary green building rating systems that serve the purpose of assessing buildings against a set of performance criteria and recognizing their superior environmental performance.",""],[1,"566","4","Low Carbon Construction Materials Promotion","Adoption and enforcement of Green Building Rating System and Low Carbon Construction Materials:",""],[1,"566","4","Sustainable Building Training and Certification Programme","Expertise in sustainable buildings is promoted through training, sharing of practical resources, certification and professional accreditation.",""],[1,"567","2","Blue Economy Exploration and Investment Planning","under the 8FYP, the Government will explore the potential of the Blue Economy through a sustainable mechanism and identify adequate policies which will help formulate an optimal investment plan",""],[1,"567","2","Blue Economy Capacity Building and Awareness Projects","From CCTF, two projects are being taken for capacity building, awareness raising and socio- economic development under blue economy.",""],[1,"567","3","Green Technology Financing and Fiscal Incentive Support for RMG","Nonetheless, the Government will remain committed towards supporting the commercial initiatives which aim to \"go green\" through cheap financing instruments and favourable fiscal incentives that reduce their carbon footprints and environmental damages in Bangladesh.",""],[1,"567","4","Environmentally Friendly Agricultural Technology Adoption","The Government of Bangladesh is committed to incorporate environmentally friendly technologies in the agricultural sector.",""],[1,"568","2","Green Transport System Support and Emissions Control Measures","During the 8FYP, the Government will support \"green transportation system\", which involves banning the vehicles that are old and emit excess smoke.",""],[1,"568","2","Fiscal Incentives for Hybrid and Electric Vehicles","Levels of pollution resulting from an inefficient transport system will be reduced by providing fiscal incentives for hybrid technologies, electric vehicles and imposing strict penalties for the violation of environmental codes by polluters in the transportation sector.",""],[1,"568","3","Eco-Tourism Fiscal Support","The Government will increase fiscal support for ecotourism under the 8FYP, which protects the ecological integrity of tourist sites and facilitates the protection of bio-diversity in Bangladesh.",""],[1,"568","4","Sustainable Consumption and Production Promotion","During the 8FYP, the Government will promote sustainable consumption and production, which is about getting more done with lesser resources.",""]],"72":[[1,"663","6","World-Class Modern Pharmaceutical Industry Establishment Programme","EDCL has also undertaken a programme for establishing one world class modern pharmaceutical industry at Gopalganj, which in addition to essential medicines will also produce birth control pills, injectables, iron tablets and IV fluids.",""],[1,"681","7","Contraceptive Manufacturing Plant Development","Promoting setting up of contraceptive manufacturing plant such as Implant, IUD for availability of product as and when required.",""]],"73":[[1,"723","1","Hi-Tech Park, Software Technology Park, and IT Training and Incubation Centre Establishment Initiative","Bangladesh Hi-Tech Park Authority (BHTPA) has taken initiatives to establish Hi-Tech Park, Software Technology Park and IT Training & Incubation Centre throughout the country to promote IT/ITES sector and to attract local & foreign investment.",""],[1,"723","3","IT and IT-Enabled Services Incentive Scheme","Government has declared attractive incentives for the promotion of IT/ITEs sector.",""],[1,"723","4","Income Tax Exemption for Park Developers","12 years exemption of Income Tax for park developers.",""],[1,"723","5","Income Tax Exemption for Investors","10 years exemption of Income Tax for investors.",""],[1,"723","6","Tax Exemption for Local Production of ATM Machines and CCTV Cameras","Exemption of Import Duty, Regularity Duty and Supplementary Duty for locally production of ATM machine and CC camera;",""],[1,"723","7","Duty Exemption for Investor Imports","Exemption of Duties on importing Capital Equipment and Construction Materials by the Investors;",""],[1,"723","9","Tax Exemption for Investor Income Streams","Exemption of Income Tax on Dividend, Share Transfer, Royalty, Technical Fees for investors;",""],[1,"723","11","Income Tax Exemption for Declared Dividends of Park Developers","Exemption of Income Tax on declared Dividend by Park Developers;",""],[1,"723","12","VAT Exemption for Production-Level Goods","Exemption of VAT during production level of goods by the Investors;",""],[1,"723","13","Duty Exemption for Hi-Tech Park Development Inputs","Exemption of Duties on importing Goods/Materials to be used for the development of Hi-Tech Parks by the Park Developers;",""],[1,"723","14","Duty Exemption for Imported Transport by Investors","Exemption of Duties on importing Transport by the investor;",""],[1,"723","15","Stamp Duty Exemption for Deed and Mortgage Registration","Exemption of stamp duty on the deed registration/ mortgage deed registration;",""],[1,"723","16","Online One Stop Service System for Investors","BHTPA has launched online One Stop Service system under the One Stop Service law.",""],[1,"731","12","Development of Specialized Industrial Parks and High-Tech Incubator","The government of Bangladesh has been working on developing specialized industrial parks to support the growth of high-tech economy.",""],[1,"731","12","Linking High-Tech Parks with Innovation Ecosystem Actors","the strategy should be linking high-tech parks with universities, research establishments, intermediate goods and service providers, and start-up initiatives making high-tech parks as the nucleus of innovation economy of Bangladesh.",""],[1,"732","16","Low-Interest Financing and Office Space Support for IT/ITES Companies","Providing financial support with low interest to IT/ITES companies to allow them to purchase fixed assets and by allocating low-cost space for offices in the hi-tech parks.",""],[1,"732","17","Financial Support and Low-Cost Space for Companies in Hi-Tech Parks","Number of Companies get financial support and low-cost space in Hi-Tech Parks",""],[1,"752","1","ICT Investment Taxation Reform","The Government is mindful of the taxation issue and will take actions to resolve it satisfactorily and ensure that Bangladesh remains an attractive destination for ICT investments.",""],[1,"752","2","Completion of Ongoing ICT Projects","Ensure rapid and satisfactory completion of all on-going ICT projects.",""],[1,"752","9","Investment Climate Incentives and Institutional Reform","Provide physical incentives & Institutional reform to create appropriate investment climate",""]],"74":[[1,"725","4","ICT Industry Promotion Project","ICT project has promoted local IT and ITES capabilities into the global market leading to improved global awareness and perception of Bangladesh for IT and ITES business.",""],[1,"725","4","Innovation and Entrepreneurship Support Academy","Innovation Design & Entrepreneurship Academy (IDEA) Project is promoting innovation and entrepreneurship across the country and provided funds to 64 start-ups totalling over Taka 5 crore.",""],[1,"725","5","IT Start-up Incubation and Support Scheme","Bangladesh Hi-Tech Park Authority is nursing and promoting IT Start-ups/IT Entrepreneurs to establish giant IT Company like Google/Apple/ Microsoft/Amazon/Alibaba.",""],[1,"726","1","BPO/KPO/IT Company Certification Promotion","Bangladesh Hi-Tech Park Authority is promoting local BPO/KPO/IT Companies for getting international standard like CMMIL-5, CMMIL-3, ISO- 9001 and ISO- 27001 etc.",""],[1,"726","3","Made in Bangladesh Policy Finalization","Made in Bangladesh Policy is going to be finalized soon.",""],[1,"726","4","Private Sector ICT Innovation Competitiveness Support","The overall strategy is to (iv) encourage private sector to leverage ICT innovations in addressing competitiveness",""],[1,"726","4","ICT Industry Investment and Innovation Scaling Initiative","The overall strategy is to (v) empower ICT industry to scale up investment and innovations to create global success stories by taking home market as the stepping stone",""],[1,"732","14","Digital Devices Manufacturing Promotion in High-Tech Parks","Encourage local and foreign companies to manufacture digital devices and its backward linkage products in Bangladeshi High- Tech Parks.",""],[1,"735","11","ICT Destination Branding Initiative","Branding Bangladesh as an ICT destination for hardware, software and BPO",""],[1,"740","6","Business Process Outsourcing Policy and Regulatory Support","Policy and regulatory measure could be taken to encourage outsourcing customer care and back office services to develop local expertise and capacity for scaling up the export revenue.",""],[1,"743","1","Invest Bangladesh Start-up Information Platform","e) set-up Invest Bangladesh as a holistic information platform for start-ups by 2025.","ICT Division"],[1,"744","3","Software Sector Market Intelligence Development","The ICT Division proposed on the following immediate short term interventions: a) develop market intelligence through assessing local and global market demands and opportunities;","ICT Division"],[1,"744","3","Software Sector Promotional Strategy Reform","b) remodel promotional strategies;","ICT Division"],[1,"744","3","Local Software Product Promotion and Self-Sustainability Support","e) promote local software products and services, employment and self- sustainability.","ICT Division"],[1,"744","4","Digital Device Manufacturing Hub Development","The need for Bangladesh's own manufacturing hub of digital devices became more significant.","ICT Division"],[1,"745","1","Local Digital Device Production and Certification Support","b) incentivize quality assurance certification of local digital device products; e) provide policy support to incentivize local production/assembling;",""],[1,"745","1","Promotion of Made in Bangladesh Products","c) promote \"Made in Bangladesh\" products in local/global markets;",""],[1,"745","1","Hi-tech Park Foreign Investment Attraction","d) attract foreign investment and foreign companies in the Hi-tech parks;",""],[1,"745","2","BPO Promotion and Branding Strategy","b) remodel promotional strategies and branding;","ICT Division"],[1,"745","2","BPO Market Expansion and Skills Development Initiative","c) aggressive marketing; d) penetrate into post COVID-19 target markets; and e) invest in developing necessary skills for leveraging new opportunities.","ICT Division"],[1,"747","2","Local Manufacturer Global Marketplace Linkage Initiative","The ICT Division proposes the following interventions: a) address the digital divide; b) launch digital online training program; c) link local manufacturers with global marketplaces; and, d) digitize workforce database.","ICT Division"],[1,"747","6","Made in Bangladesh Policy for Digital Devices","Development and enactment of 'Made in Bangladesh' Policy for digital devices for domestic and foreign market",""],[1,"747","8","National Policy for Start-ups","Introduction of National Policy for Start-ups to promote growth of the ecosystem, while also attracting foreign investment",""],[1,"752","11","Bangladesh ICT Industry Global Promotion Initiative","Support in promotion of Bangladesh ICT Industry in the global market to brand Bangladesh as a destination for software, hardware, BPO, freelancing and ICT Innovation.",""]],"75":[[1,"721","1","Measures to Extract Economic Value from Internet Data","The 8FYP will promote deliberate measures to extract economic value from growing production and sharing of internet data to enhance productivity of public services.",""],[1,"724","1","Bangla Language in ICT Research and Development Project","Enhancement of Bangla Language in ICT through Research & Development (1st Revised) project has been working to standardize various features of Bangla language and develop Tools, Technologies and Contents for Bangla computing.",""],[1,"727","17","Digital Support for Local R&D, Start-ups, and Industry","Focus should be on taking advantage of emerging digital innovations supporting local R&D, innovations, start-ups and industry.",""],[1,"728","6","Local R&D and Innovation Support for Value Addition","Vendor driven procurement of imported ready to use approach should be supplemented with envisioning the future possibilities and supporting local R&D for increasing local value addition, strengthening academia, and fostering innovation, start-ups and industry.",""],[1,"728","9","Digital R&D Issue Identification and Industry-Academia Collaboration Support","Identify R&D issues for exploiting digital opportunities, and support industry-academia collaboration to carry out them",""],[1,"728","10","Local Value Addition Demonstration Projects","Take a series of demonstration projects, in partnership with industry and academia, for increasing the scope of local value addition, and reducing risks in implementation",""],[1,"728","11","Engineering Programme Redesign for Government Technology Needs","Redesigning engineering programmes to meet the technological requirements of the Government and supporting local digital innovation industry",""],[1,"728","13","Industry-Academia-Government Linkage Program","Program activities for linking industry, academia, and government are shown in Table 12.2.",""],[1,"729","10","R&D Policy Implementation Incentives and Academic Engagement","Provide incentives in detecting R&D issues for implementing above policies and engage academia to pursue them.",""],[1,"730","13","University-Industry R&D Linkage for Innovation Support","This strategy will also start increasing the high-tech patent portfolio, and opening the opportunity of linking universities with industrial R&D for supporting innovation need of the industry.",""],[1,"732","9","University R&D Support for High-Tech Redesign Assignments","Offer R&D supports to universities to undertake redesign assignments from high-tech firms",""],[1,"732","11","Collaborative Projects Between Firms and University-Based Incubators","Support collaborative projects between firms operating in high- tech parks, and university-based incubators",""],[1,"732","12","High-Tech Park and ICT Innovation Collaboration Platform","Support the collaboration between firms operating in high-tech parks, ICT industry, universities, and line ministries so that local industry can succeed in innovating and manufacturing needed innovations to support mission need of respective line ministries","line ministries"],[1,"737","13","Industry-University R&D Linkage Support","Engage industry through associations, and provide R&D supports to link universities and R&D facilities to industry focus innovations",""],[1,"742","2","National Innovation Ecosystem Acceleration","It will be that of an innovation intermediary and knowledge leader that will spearhead the country's ability to spot, understand and integrate new development approaches, work to strengthen institutional linkages across the whole-of-government and whole-of-society, and play a catalytic role in fostering inclusive, citizen-centric governance and societal innovation in Bangladesh.","ICT Division"],[1,"752","4","R&D Funding for ICT and Science and Technology","Provide funding for R&D in ICT & Science and Technology",""],[1,"752","8","Product Innovation and Creation Ecosystem Support","Support product innovation & creation ecosystem",""]],"76":[[1,"729","3","Digital Product and Process Redesign Support for Industry","Encourage industry to pursue redesign of products they are producing now by adding digital technology-based features to products as well as processes",""],[1,"729","6","Digital Technology-Enabled Industrial Production Expansion","Encourage industry to start producing those products where MVA could be increased by leveraging digital technologies",""],[1,"729","7","Digital Innovation Support for Marginalized Groups in Industry","Encourage industry to pursue innovative solutions around digital technologies for marginalized groups",""],[1,"729","8","Digital Adoption and Flexible Production Support for Industry","For leveraging digital possibilities, encourage industry to adopt flexible and decentralized production; supply chain connectivity, delivery, performance and logistics; agile, adaptive organization",""],[1,"729","9","Circular Economy Promotion in Industry","Encourage the industry to pursue circular economy through recycling efficient use of resources; remanufacturing, refurbishment and reuse of products and components; product as service, sharing models, and shifting in consumption patterns",""],[1,"729","12","Start-up Success Support through Continued R&D and Intellectual Asset Creation","In order to turn this loss into profit continued R&D is needed to make the innovation better as well as cheaper.",""],[1,"730","3","R&D Incentive Scheme for Patents and Intellectual Assets","Provide incentive in undertaking R&D for producing patents and expanding intellectual asset base",""],[1,"730","8","Academic R&D Support for Intellectual Asset-Based Start-Up Formation","Foster academic R&D in supporting the generation of intellectual asset-based start-up formation and growth",""],[1,"730","10","Startup Intellectual Asset Portfolio Support","Create awareness and provide support to start- ups for managing Intellectual Asset (IA) portfolio, and leveraging it to the valuation and fund raising.",""],[1,"730","12","Youth Digital Start-up Asset Support","These youths should be empowered with IA/IP asset base to turn those ideas into profitable venture.",""],[1,"730","13","High-Tech Product and Process Redesign Capability Development","This opportunity should be exploited for increasing MVA through ideas of redesign.",""],[1,"730","13","Process Redesign for High-Tech Manufacturing","Moreover, such redesign should also focus on process redesign as well.",""],[1,"730","14","Patent Portfolio Development for High-Tech Manufacturing","Bangladesh must start building patent portfolio for increasing MVA in high-tech.",""],[1,"731","3","Tax and Incentive Redesign for MVA Linkage","Link tax and other incentives to MVA through ideas of redesign",""],[1,"731","6","Product Redesign Research and Development Support","Support R&D for redesign of products by leveraging digital technologies",""],[1,"731","7","Digital Technology R&D Support for Product Redesign","Support R&D for adapting and advancing digital technologies to support product redesign",""],[1,"731","8","High-Tech Manufacturing Support and Incentive Scheme","Support infrastructure and provide incentives to start manufacturing those high-tech products which are amenable to redesign for increasing MVA through ideas.",""],[1,"732","3","Ecosystem Incentives for Knowledge Inputs to High-Tech Manufacturing","Provide incentives to ecosystem to provide knowledge inputs to high-tech manufacture firms",""],[1,"732","5","Local Product Redesign Support for High-Tech Assemblers","Encourage high-tech product assemblers to redesign their products through sourcing of ideas and design services locally",""],[1,"732","7","High-Tech Start-Up Innovation and Park Location Support","Support start-ups to innovate high-tech products and locate into high-tech parks",""],[1,"733","10","Fourth Industrial Revolution Research and Development Facility","IT firms will make good use of the facility to undertake 4IR R&D",""],[1,"733","11","Sector-Specific 4IR Use Case Development and Diffusion","To create the demand and supply capacities of 4IR innovations, focus should be on developing sector specific 4IR Use Cases and documenting global best practices, and promoting as well as supporting their development, adoption, and diffusion.",""],[1,"735","8","Digital Technology R&D and Patent Portfolio Development","Invest in R&D in developing patent portfolio in digital technology space.",""],[1,"735","9","Value Addition Capacity Upgrading through Patent Use","Bangladeshi firms start upgrading their value addition capacity by leveraging patents ideas.",""],[1,"737","14","Resource-Efficient Product and Process Redesign","Products and processes are being redesigned to minimize material and energy need, and reduce waste",""],[1,"738","11","4IR Technology Feature Integration in Goods and Services","In both goods and services, new features will be added for leveraging technologies driving 4IR.",""],[1,"738","11","AR/VR-Based Tourism Guidance Enhancement","For example, AR/VR based features could be introduced to expand tour guidance features in hospitality and tourism industry.",""],[1,"738","16","Export and Import Substitution Product Diversification Initiative","Measures should be taken to introduce production of additional products for the purpose of both export and import substitution, particularly by leveraging 4IR (e.g., remote supervision of It's and service delivery in collaboration with Robots) so that the volume of task supply increases.",""],[1,"740","4","High-Tech Manufacturing Value-Addition Measures","The 8FYP should take measures to make progress along this line.",""]],"77":[[1,"740","5","Digital Literacy for E-Commerce and Payments","Literacy for smartphone-based service consumption and transaction, and digital payment should also be addressed.",""],[1,"742","4","Digital Economy Master Plan Development","d) devise a master plan for a digital economy to secure to secure a resilient financial ecosystem;",""],[1,"743","2","COVID-19 E-Commerce Code of Conduct and Policy","the ICT Division proposes the following immediate short-term interventions: a) develop a COVID-19 code of conduct along with e-commerce policy to promote hyper local e-commerce for the last mile","ICT Division"],[1,"743","2","Online Shopping and Digital Advertising Tax Reform","b) reform taxation for online shopping and digital advertising by 2020","ICT Division"],[1,"743","2","Assisted E-Commerce Service","c) launch assisted e-commerce service for easier adoption of online shopping practices","ICT Division"],[1,"743","2","SME Digital Platform Promotion and Startup Support","e) promote existing digital platform start-ups and services, and introduce new ones for SMEs for digital transformation by end of 2021","ICT Division"],[1,"748","13","Bottom-Up E-Commerce Support for Local Producers and Artisans","Facilitating bottom-up e- commerce for livelihood of local producers and artisans",""],[1,"748","26","Ease of Doing Business Policy for 18 Sectors","Introduction of Ease of Doing Business Policy catering to each of the 18 sectors",""]],"78":[[1,"820","2","Support for Women's Higher-Value Self-Employment","Information about opportunities, markets, skills, finance, time saving and green technology, and training can support women to participate in farm and non-farm activities.",""],[1,"820","2","Facilitation of Women's Access to High-Value Crop Production and Value Chains","Support to facilitate women's access to high value crop production, higher level of the value chain and services should be ensured.",""],[1,"820","3","Women Entrepreneurs Business Development Support Services","For economic empowerment, women need support for entrepreneurship development and business.",""],[1,"820","3","Women Entrepreneurs Business Planning and Marketing Assistance","Entrepreneurs should be assisted for business planning and marketing.",""],[1,"820","3","Women Entrepreneurs Skills Development for Business Administration","They need skills to provide required papers, business plan, financial management, and marketing at home and abroad.",""],[1,"820","3","District-Level One-Stop Support for Women Entrepreneurs","SME Foundation, Bangladesh Small and Cottage Industries Corporation (BSCIC) and JMS should expand one stop support provisions for women entrepreneurs at the district levels.",""],[1,"820","3","Women Entrepreneurs Business Incubator Expansion","Business incubator services should be expanded by the chambers and associations.",""],[1,"820","3","Women Entrepreneurs Financial Information Platform","Comprehensive information with details of financial support from different banks and financial institutions for women with criteria, procedure, required papers and guarantee, ceiling and interest rate etc. should be developed by SME foundation and updated annually for the women entrepreneurs.",""],[1,"820","3","Women Entrepreneurs Marketing Support Services","Marketing support should be provided to women by DWA, JMS, Joyeeta and others.",""],[1,"820","3","Joyeeta Model Expansion","The Joyeeta model should be expanded in the country.",""],[1,"820","3","Women Entrepreneurs Trade Fair Participation Support","BSCIC Associations and the Export Promotion Bureau (EPB) should facilitate women's participation in trade fairs at home and abroad and promote ICT and social media-based information dissemination.",""],[1,"820","3","Women Entrepreneurs Policy Change Information Service","Women entrepreneurs should be informed of all changes in industrial, tax, tariff, financing policies.",""],[1,"820","3","Women Entrepreneurs Tax Incentive Support","The National Board of Revenue (NBR) should establish criteria and support women entrepreneurs by providing tax-holiday, special incentives, tax-rebate, for newly established enterprises of women.","National Board of Revenue (NBR)"],[1,"821","3","Women-Focused Agricultural Extension and Market Access Support","All the government agencies (livestock, fisheries, agriculture etc.) should take specific measures in reaching women with support for training on technology, market information, production techniques, sources of raw materials, etc.",""],[1,"821","3","Women Farmer Input Distribution Scheme","The distribution of seeds, fertilizer, and other inputs through women farmer groups should be arranged.",""],[1,"821","3","Women Market Information and Linkage Platform","Market information and market linkages should be established for women with different chain shops, international buyers and online platforms.",""],[1,"821","4","Women’s Value Chain Skills and Market Access Support","Women should be supported to receive technical and technological knowledge about different levels of value chain of agricultural and non- agricultural products.",""],[1,"821","4","Women’s Agribusiness Development and One-Stop Service Support","Agribusiness development opportunities, access to backward linkages for industrial products should be incorporated in women's business development programmes and in one stop service facilities.",""],[1,"821","4","Support for Women in Trade Fairs and Product Market Information","Women should be supported with information on markets of different products, scope of participation in trade and export fairs.",""],[1,"821","4","Ethnic Crafts Value Addition and Diversification Support","Ethnic crafts of different areas should be supported for high value generation and diversification.",""],[1,"831","1","Support for Women's Economic Self-Reliance","support for women's economic self-reliance should continue.",""]],"79":[[1,"55","5","Agricultural Diversification Promotion","Promote agricultural diversification;",""],[1,"56","2","Agricultural Diversification and Farm Support Measures","In agriculture, the strategy will be to further increase agriculture diversification while maintaining food security through improvements in farm productivity, supply of inputs, price policy support, water supply, farm credit and marketing support.",""],[1,"113","2","Agricultural Diversification Promotion","promote agricultural diversification",""],[1,"114","3","Agricultural Diversification Promotion","Promote agricultural diversification.",""],[1,"114","10","Agricultural Diversification and Productivity Support","the strategy will be to further increase agriculture diversification while maintaining food security through improvements in productivity, supply of inputs, price policy supports, water supply, farm credit and marketing support",""],[1,"170","1","Agricultural Production and Diversification Support Package","supporting agriculture production and diversification through a range of policies including access to inputs including mechanized inputs, farm credit, marketing support, price support through public procurement, and implementing rural works programme as needed.",""],[1,"170","3","Agricultural Productivity and Climate-Resilient Farming Investment Programme","Therefore, the 8FYP will undertake investments in research and extension to increase crop productivity, especially rice, to support climate-resistant seed and production technology, invest in water resources to support farm production in drought-prone areas of the Barind region in the North-western Districts of Bangladesh and the CHT, ensure flood control and water-logging prevention investments, and take steps to prevent river-bank erosions and salinity inroads.",""],[1,"177","6","Agricultural Research and Extension Support for Lagging Districts","Focussing agriculture research and extension services to help farm productivity and incomes in the lagging districts.",""],[1,"180","12","Agricultural Diversification and Rural Labor Transition Support","There is a further need to diversify agriculture into higher value- added activities and to help transfer surplus labour from agriculture to non-farm activities in rural and urban areas.",""],[1,"188","1","Agriculture and Rural Infrastructure Investment Expansion","The priority to agriculture and rural infrastructure will be preserved and strengthened with a further increase to 1% of GDP by FY25.",""],[1,"364","5","Crop Sector Productivity and Diversification Strategy","The development vision for crop sector under the 8th Five Year Plan is to ensure food security and nutrition through increasing productivity; minimizing yield gap; stabilizing price of agricultural products; improving farmers' profitability and securities; diversification of crop products towards climate-resilient production; strengthening agricultural supply chains; increasing commercialization through uses of information and communication technology (ICT); easing credit facilities for small farmers; escalating HRD for undertaking frontier research and delivery services; and ensuring efficient utilization of natural resources.",""],[1,"365","1","Crop Productivity and Production Enhancement","Increase availability of food, right to food and purchasing power by increasing productivity and production of crops.",""],[1,"365","2","Farmer Capability and Income Enhancement through Institutional Infrastructure and Technology Services","Increase farmers' capability and income through institutional infrastructure development and efficient technology services.",""],[1,"365","3","Food Production Planning for Nutritious and Safe Food Supply","Adopt and implement food production plans to meet the needs of nutritious, safe and demand-driven foods.",""],[1,"365","6","Farmer Support for Agricultural Production and Market Access","Provide assistance to the farmers in increasing agricultural production and ensuring marketing facilities of agricultural commodities and obtaining fair prices.",""],[1,"365","14","Holistic Farming System Approach for Farmers' Income Enhancement","Enhance farmers' income and livelihood through Holistic Farming System Approach (HFSA) with special emphasis on productivity enhancement of homestead areas.",""],[1,"365","16","Quality and High-Yielding Seed Supply Support","the 8FYP targets to assure the supply of quality and high-yielding seeds for production and continue and extend the supports to farmers.",""],[1,"365","16","Farmer Support Expansion","the 8FYP targets to assure the supply of quality and high-yielding seeds for production and continue and extend the supports to farmers.",""],[1,"365","16","Agricultural Production Diversification","Diversification of agricultural production with high value crops, strengthening supply channels in",""],[1,"368","2","Staple Self-Sufficiency and Production Diversification Programme","the 8FYP should concentrate on maintaining self-sufficiency in the major staple production through ensuring required increase and simultaneously diversifying the production portfolio within and beyond the crop sector",""],[1,"368","4","Crop Intensification in Vulnerable Areas","More attention is needed for crop intensification in environmentally and economically vulnerable areas such as the coastal zone, the Sylhet region and the char areas and in the northern poverty-stricken districts.",""],[1,"368","4","Seasonal Crop Diversification for Farmers","Another strategy should be to encourage farmers to devote ecologically favourable months of the Boro season for growing high return non-rice crops leaving the remaining eight months for growing two rice crops.",""],[1,"373","5","Rice Yield Gap Minimization Techniques Promotion","Promotion of Rice Yield Gap Minimization (RYMG) techniques",""],[1,"373","10","Women and Youth Agricultural Participation Support Programme","The 8FYP plan will focus on productive participation of women in agricultural employment and will seek to address the following issues, amongst others: (1) wage differences between male and female in agriculture, (2) socio-economic backwardness and constraints that women endure in a male dominated society, (3) women's access to institutions and facilities including extension and credit services and linkages with other services such as health and nutrition,, and (4) women's access to markets and high value-added agriculture.",""],[1,"798","2","National Agricultural Policy 2018","To this end, the government has prepared the National Agricultural Policy 2018.",""],[1,"801","6","Nutrition-Focused Agricultural Diversification","Accelerate nutrition-focused agricultural diversification while continuing to improve the productivity of cereals enhancement and conservation of nutrients in post-harvest storage, transformation and distribution.",""],[1,"802","1","Nutrition-Sensitive Agricultural Research Enhancement","Agricultural research will be enhanced further to promote nutrition sensitive food production.",""],[1,"802","2","Disaster Mitigation Measures in Agriculture","The measures to accomplish the objectives would include special measures for disaster mitigation in agriculture, increased supply of food through market and public distribution and investment in employment generation activities.",""],[1,"802","2","Employment Generation Investment Activities","The measures to accomplish the objectives would include special measures for disaster mitigation in agriculture, increased supply of food through market and public distribution and investment in employment generation activities.",""],[1,"802","2","Rural Non-Farm Employment Expansion","An important way of increasing purchasing power of people is to expand rural non-farm employment opportunities.",""],[1,"802","2","Rural Infrastructure Expansion for Non-Farm Activities","Expansion of rural transport infrastructure, electricity and telecommunication facilities is the prerequisites for rapid expansion of non-farm activities in rural areas.",""],[1,"802","2","Women’s Participation in Non-Farm Activities","In designing policies for rural non-farm employment, female workers need to be given priority in the participation of non-farm activities.",""],[1,"802","2","Public and Private Initiatives for Women’s Opportunities","To achieve this desired objective, opportunities for women will have to be created through both public and private initiatives.",""],[1,"802","4","Good Agricultural Practices Awareness Building","awareness building Good Agricultural Practices (GAPs) among the farming households will be crucial so that production practices can improve the quantity, diversity, and",""],[1,"803","1","Contract Farming Institutionalization and Policy Support","Contract farming can be institutionalized with necessary stipulation of provisions in the contracts to protect the interests of the contracting parties including the smallholder farmers.",""],[1,"803","1","Agribusiness Farmer Support Services","Agribusiness firms often also agree to support farmers through a variety of services, such as input supply, extension advice, and transportation of produce to their premises.",""],[1,"806","7","FFW/MFW Rural Labour Employment Programmes","Under the FFW/ MFW Programmes, a wide array of projects has been implemented by more than 8 million rural labourers.",""],[1,"817","2","Homestead Gardening and Poultry Expansion Programme","Promotion and expansion of homestead gardening and poultry in the rural and remote areas introducing climate tolerant varieties is essential in order to ensure protein and vitamin consumption.",""]],"80":[[1,"360","5","Postharvest Management, Processing, and Storage Investment","It will be difficult to sustain the growth of production of high-value and labour-intensive crops unless investment is made in the postharvest management (a 10% reduction of postharvest loss would add 10% additional food for the nation), processing and storage to stagger marketing of the crops throughout the year to match the demand that remains stable across the season.",""],[1,"360","5","Agricultural Export Competitiveness and Food Safety Upgrade","In addition, it is also important to exploit international markets with investment in packaging, Sanitary and Phyto-sanitary Standards (SPS), and safe food production through Good Agricultural Practices (GAP).",""],[1,"364","3","Storage, Agro-processing and Value Chain Facility Investment","To ensure that their production and export potential are fully realized, there is a need for investing in appropriate manufacturing capacities and infrastructural facilities.",""],[1,"365","12","Agricultural Commercialization and Value-Addition Development","Create new sectors of agricultural commercialization and employment generation through value addition, improving supply chain, demand-driven and export-oriented agricultural development.",""],[1,"369","5","Agricultural Mechanization and Value Chain Development Measures","Promote measures to expand mechanization and value chain development:",""],[1,"371","1","Good Agricultural Practices (GAP) Promotion","Research and extension will put effort jointly to promote the process.",""],[1,"371","3","Post-Harvest Management and Agro-Processing Support","The process of supporting agro-business will be continued and strengthened during the Eighth Plan period.",""],[1,"371","3","Private Sector Extension Services for Fruits and Vegetables","some specialized extension activities could be delegated to the private sector such as those related to fruits and vegetables enterprises.",""],[1,"371","5","Agro-processing Infrastructure and Manufacturing Support","To ensure that the production and export potential are fully realized, the government will continue its current commitment to investing in the relevant infrastructure and supporting manufacturing of",""],[1,"372","1","Processed Foods Support Initiatives","Special attention will be given support initiatives relating to ready to cook food, halal food export, dried fruits, canned fruits and assuring quality phyto sanitary compliance.",""],[1,"372","5","Crop Zoning and Value Addition Diversification Programmes","Formulation of programmes to promote diversification on the basis of crop zoning and value addition",""]],"81":[[1,"363","1","Expansion of Non-Rice Cropping in Dry Boro Season","Therefore, efforts should be taken to increase the acreage of non-rice crops during dry Boro season in order to minimize ground water extraction and to increase the production of high value crops like pulses, oilseeds, spices and vegetables for ensuring food and nutritional security with generation of income through processing and marketing.",""],[1,"365","8","Sustainable Irrigation Expansion and Irrigation System Improvement","Ensure sustained agricultural growth through more efficient and balanced utilization of land, water and other resources, and encourage more use of surface water for irrigation and reduction of pressure on ground water while expanding irrigation facilities through improving existing irrigation system and related infrastructures.",""],[1,"365","9","Solar-Powered Small-Scale Irrigation Installations","Installations of solar panels for small scale irrigation in rural areas will be a priority.",""],[1,"365","10","Crop Diversification Toward Low-Water High-Value Crops","Promote gradual shifting of high water- consuming crops to low water consuming high value crops.",""],[1,"369","3","Crop Diversification for Water Efficiency","Crop diversification is an effective tool for ensuring optimal use of water given that the water requirement for paddy is much higher than in other crops.",""],[1,"369","3","Irrigation Efficiency Technology Promotion","For ensuring irrigation efficiency, technologies that enhance conveyance efficiency (e.g. buried pipe, PVC/plastic/polythene pipe, etc.) and on-farm water use efficiency (e.g. drip irrigation, fertigation through drip irrigation system for the non-cereal crops, etc.) need to be promoted.",""],[1,"369","3","Volumetric Water Pricing Reform","volumetric water pricing that offers incentives to the farmers to rationalize water use will be promoted in areas under deep-tube wells.",""],[1,"369","3","Tiered Water Pricing in Barind Areas","Tiered pricing - setting lowest price at that threshold level of water use - will further encourage farmers in the Barind areas to rationalize water use.",""],[1,"372","6","Small-Scale Irrigation Technology and Surface Water Expansion","Expansion of small-scale irrigation technology and surface water for irrigation",""]],"82":[[1,"365","15","Plant Genetic Resources Conservation Programme","Maintain plant genetic resources, genetic diversity of seeds of food crops and medicinal plants and conserve local and land races for protection from extinction.",""],[1,"366","8","Organic Fertilizer and Organic Pest Management Introduction","To introduce organic fertilizer use and organic pest management system",""],[1,"366","10","Food-Based Nutrition Research and Development Activities","To take and implement research and development activities on food-based nutrition with a view to increasing the nutrition level of the people.",""],[1,"366","11","Food and Nutrition Awareness and Malnutrition Reduction Initiative","To increase awareness and to improve health reducing malnutrition problems related to food and nutrition in the country",""],[1,"366","11","Food Contamination Research and Consumer Awareness Programme","to conduct research on harmful effect of agro chemicals or heavy metals (for example arsenic, lead, cadmium etc.) contamination existing in food chain and enhance consumer awareness.",""],[1,"366","14","National Soil Survey and Land Reclamation Planning","To reconnaissance soil survey of the whole country on the basis of aerial photo interpretation and field and laboratory investigation of soils; detailed/semi-detailed soil surveys of development project areas and research farms for various beneficiary agencies; soil surveys for locating areas of problem soils (e.g., toxic, saline, alkaline or peat soils) and investigating soil degradation and erosion especially in hilly areas for planning reclamation, conservation and watershed management.",""],[1,"367","18","Ecosystem Payment Policy Instruments for Sustainable Agriculture","To offer farmers some benefits of adopting these environment-friendly technologies, Economic and Policy Instruments (EPI) for ecosystem payment should be designed.",""],[1,"367","18","Incentives for Granular Urea Adoption","To make it more popular, there can be greater incentives (e.g. higher subsidies) for using granular urea.",""],[1,"367","19","Sustainable Agriculture and Green Growth Promotion Policies","Sustainable agriculture and green growth in crop sector will be promoted through different policies.",""],[1,"368","1","Sustainable Agriculture Partnership and Capacity-Building Package","fostering partnership among the public-private and international organizations to make sustainable agriculture to work, (2) protecting and conserving environment by promoting ICM, INM, IDM, IPM (sex pheromone, botanical pesticides, biological control, etc.), surface and rainwater utilization, use of solar energy in farm activities, (3) Capacity building will be targeted at all segments of agriculture: farmers, extension providers, dealers, distributors, entrepreneurs, agribusiness people, trainers and researchers (man, woman, youth will be the target groups) through knowledge and skill development, (4) improving rain-fed agriculture, (5) technology transfer through farmers' group approach, (5) protecting biodiversity (plant, animal, fisheries, pollinator, etc.), (6) promoting food safety, nutrition and dietary diversification, (7) improving natural resource management (land, water and biodiversity), (8) Promoting agricultural exports, (9) sustaining economic viability of farming practices, (10) creating enabling environment for the institutions, (11) promoting farm mechanization, (12) exploiting newly accreted char and coast land and promoting seaweed cultivation.",""],[1,"373","3","Environment-Friendly Farming Practices Promotion","Development and promotion of environment friendly farming practices ensuring good agricultural practices.",""]],"83":[[1,"370","3","Urban Agriculture Promotion through Rooftop and Vertical Farming","Promoting urban agriculture through rainfed rooftop and vertical farming:",""]],"84":[[1,"377","6","Sustainable Livestock Production and Processing Promotion","To promote sustainable production of milk, meat and egg including processing products",""],[1,"377","7","Nutrition-Sensitive Production and Consumption Initiative","To ensure a nutritional-sensitive production system and consumption to tackle malnutrition among poor and vulnerable population groups, including the children and women",""],[1,"378","3","Livestock Entrepreneurship and Private Sector Participation Promotion","To facilitate entrepreneurship and increased participation of the private sector in the production, marketing and export of livestock products and by-products on a commercial basis.",""],[1,"379","3","Quality Feed Supply Support for Poultry and Livestock","policy options for vaccine coverage for poultry birds and ensuring quality feed supplies should be looked into.",""],[1,"379","4","Smallholder Livestock Support Measures","Immediate actions will be taken to address the constraints of smallholders in livestock rearing.",""],[1,"379","4","Support for Small and Medium Livestock and Poultry Enterprises","Support to small and medium size livestock and poultry unit will be emphasized along with large business enterprises.",""],[1,"379","4","Private Input Production Support for Livestock Value Chains","Private initiatives will be encouraged and supported for producing inputs like feed, medicines, vaccines and biological products, genetic stocks and materials for the small and medium size enterprises.",""],[1,"379","4","Livestock Product Processing and Export Support","All possible support should be extended to them also for processing and exporting livestock products.",""],[1,"379","4","Affordable Bank Financing for Smallholder Poultry and Dairy Producers","Smallholder poultry and dairy producers and entrepreneurs will be facilitated through allowing access to bank financing at an affordable rate of interest with low or no collateral.",""]],"85":[[1,"381","5","Shrimp Zoning and Coastal Area Survey","Currently, shrimp zoning activity is running through survey of coastal area by a national committee.",""],[1,"383","4","Aquaculture Traceability and Biosecurity Improvement","Traceability along with other bio-security issues shall be further improved and laboratory facilities needs to be further expanded during the 8th plan.",""],[1,"384","3","Fisher Livelihood Self-Employment Support","Alleviate poverty through creating self-employment and improvement of socio-economic conditions of the fishers.",""],[1,"384","8","Fish and Fisheries Value Chain Promotion","Promote value chain in fish and fisheries products.",""],[1,"384","10","Promotion of Good Aquaculture and Manufacturing Practices","Good Aquaculture Practice (GAP) and Good Manufacturing Practice (GMP) will be promoted at all stages of fish/shrimp supply chain to comply international standard.",""],[1,"385","5","Pond Aquaculture and Brackish Water Shrimp Culture Intensification","further intensification in pond aquaculture and brackish water shrimp culture will be required to meet the growing demand in the country.",""],[1,"385","6","Private Sector Fingerling and Fish Feed Supply Support","Supply of quality fingerlings and fish feeds through private sector will remain an important strategy for culture fisheries.",""],[1,"385","6","Promotion of Small Indigenous Species in Pond Carp Culture","Promoting small indigenous species in conjunction with pond carp culture will be given importance.",""],[1,"385","6","Fisheries Research, Technology Development, and Farmer Capacity Building","The Bangladesh Fisheries Research Institute (BFRI) will work on new varieties and technological development and provide technical support to the department of fisheries (DoF), which will be responsible for dissemination at the field level.",""],[1,"385","6","Farmer Skill Development Programme","DoF will also work extensively on developing capacity of the farmers through skill development programmes.",""],[1,"385","8","Aquaculture Intensification and Species Diversification Promotion","Aquaculture intensification and species diversification will be promoted, avoiding water pollution;",""],[1,"385","9","Farm Mechanization for Aquaculture Production","Farm mechanization and vertical expansion of aquaculture will be the major priority for sustaining and diversifying of aquaculture production;",""],[1,"385","9","Vertical Expansion of Aquaculture Production","Farm mechanization and vertical expansion of aquaculture will be the major priority for sustaining and diversifying of aquaculture production;",""],[1,"385","11","Adaptive Aquaculture and Fisheries Management Support","Introduction of adaptive aquaculture technologies and fisheries management system for the poor fish farmers/fishers of coastal region through training and farm demonstration;",""],[1,"385","14","Cage Culture Promotion in Flood Plains","Cage culture in the flood plains, with private ownership will be encouraged which can certainly contribute to productivity;",""],[1,"386","3","Contract Growing Support for Shrimp Farmers","Community organizations of shrimp farmers and other primary stakeholders will be supported with technology, input, financing and market linkage by contract growing system run by the processing plants and monitored by the DOF and partner NGOs;","DOF"],[1,"386","5","Community-Based Fish Culture Expansion","Increasing fish production by introducing different fish culture methods under the community enterprise approach in suitable habitats by conserving natural environment including rice-cum- /alternate fish culture;",""],[1,"386","6","Extension Support and Research-Extension Linkage Strengthening","Extension support and research extension linkages will be strengthened;",""],[1,"386","7","Biofloc Fish Production System","Biofloc system of fish production for landless and marginal farmers and also in the urban areas;",""],[1,"386","8","Expansion of the Daudkandi Model Floodplain Polyculture System","Market driven community based innovative flood plain polyculture system of 'Daudkandi Model' may be expanded in flood plain areas throughout the country.",""],[1,"386","9","Sustainable Conservation and Productivity Improvement for Inland Open Water Fisheries","Inland open water resources will be conserved in a sustainable way and an emphasis is given to improve productivity during the 8FYP.",""],[1,"386","10","Inland Water Resource Conservation and Fish Production Development","Inland unused water resources will be conserved and developed for fish production.",""],[1,"386","14","Hilsa Marketing System and Value Chain Improvement","Measures will also be taken to improve Hilsa marketing system and its value chain.",""],[1,"387","2","Fish Farmer Insurance Scheme","Proper insurance schemes for the fish farmers will be made available.",""],[1,"387","3","Sustainable Fishermen Community Organization and Khas Waterbody Management","The fishermen will be organized in sustainable community-based organizations and such organizations will be given management responsibility of khas 'jolmohal' on long term basis so that they conserve rather than just exploit resources.",""],[1,"387","4","Blue Economy Fisheries Activity Exploration","Collaborative efforts will be undertaken to explore blue economy-related activities concerning the fisheries sector.",""],[1,"387","4","Deep-Sea Fishermen Capacity Development Programme","The capacity development of fishermen in deep sea will be a major focus of the 8FYP.",""],[1,"387","5","Marine Fish Popularization Programme","A national programme needs to be undertaken to popularize marine fish as part of the normal diet.",""],[1,"387","13","Distant Water Fishing Development Initiative","Collaborative effort for distant water fishing (beyond 200m of EEZ and ABNJ) to explore and exploit tuna and large pelagic fishes.",""],[1,"387","16","Private Sector Investment Promotion for Fish Value Chain","Private sector investment will be promoted for fish and fisheries product value chain.",""],[1,"387","17","Motivational Activities for Adoption of Advanced Farming Technologies","Motivational activities for farmers/ entrepreneurs will be taken to adopt advanced farming technologies.",""],[1,"388","1","ICT-Based Fisheries Information Dissemination","Application of Information and Communication Technology (ICT) will be promoted to disseminate fisheries information and modern technology in the remote areas of the country for facilitating fisheries activities particularly the aquaculture",""],[1,"388","8","Modern Hygienic Dried Fish Production Facilities","considering the huge demand for hygienic dry fish in the country and abroad, the Bangladesh Fisheries Development Corporation (BFDC) will take initiative to establish modern shutki (dried fish) mohal in different strategic locations of the country to produce hygienic dry fish.",""],[1,"388","8","Coastal Dockyard Expansion for Fishing Boats","more dockyards will be established at different strategic locations in coastal areas.",""]],"86":[[1,"525","13","Promotion of Cooperative Production and Financial Resource Pooling","Promote cooperative activities in production and financial resource pooling;",""],[1,"529","5","Milk Cooperative Expansion","Expansion of Milk Cooperatives in Milk fade Upazila;",""],[1,"529","5","Alternative Livelihoods for Haor Communities","Creation of Alternative livelihood for the people of Haor region;",""],[1,"529","5","Livelihood Development for Ethnic People through Cooperatives","Livelihood development of Ethnic people of plain land through cooperatives;",""],[1,"529","5","Cooperative-Based Rural Employment Creation through Youth and Women Skills Development","Cooperative based Rural Employment Creation through Skill Development of Youth & Women;",""],[1,"529","6","Cooperative Product Marketing and Value Chain Development","Cooperative product marketing & value chain development;",""],[1,"529","6","Modern Technology Adoption in Agricultural Cooperatives","Introducing modern technology in agricultural cooperatives to increase food production and ensure fair price for small farmers;",""],[1,"529","6","Expansion of Dairy Cooperatives","Expansion of dairy cooperatives in 61 districts;",""],[1,"529","6","Cooperative-Based Agricultural Growth Centres","Establishment of cooperative based agricultural growth centres;",""],[1,"529","6","Women-Focused Dairy Production and Nutrition Support","Engaging women in dairy production and to fulfil nutrition demand of women, children and adolescents girls through expansion of dairy cooperatives.",""],[1,"529","7","Capacity Building for Cooperative Financial Institutions","Capacity building of cooperatives financial institutions including Bangladesh Cooperatives Bank for ensuring financial discipline",""],[1,"529","8","Modernization and Physical Infrastructure Development of the Bangladesh Cooperative Academy and Training Institutes","Institutional Development: Modernization & physical infrastructure development of Bangladesh Cooperative Academy and training institutes",""],[1,"530","7","Rural Stakeholder Coordination and Cooperative Infrastructure Development","BRDB will enforce the activities of coordinating among the rural stakeholders, developing local leadership as a community catalyst, promoting market linkage infrastructure through the cooperative movement and micro-infrastructure development with stakeholders' participation in its regular work strategies.",""],[1,"531","6","New Milk Cooperative Formation and Dairy Value Chain Programme","During 8th plan period, Milk Vita will undertake programmes to form new milk cooperatives; to alleviate poverty through cow rearing, milk collection, processing and distribution and to women empowerment by off-farm activities.",""],[1,"532","4","Strengthening Cooperative Unions and Cooperative Services","Strengthen the functioning of the Cooperative Unions: In coordination with LGIs, RDCD and DoC will strengthen the Cooperative Unions, and regularly monitor its Credit activities to ensure desired outcomes.","LGIs | RDCD | DoC"],[1,"532","4","Cooperative Entrepreneurship Support Services","It will also facilitate consultative services to the cooperatives to promote the cooperative-entrepreneurship.",""],[1,"532","4","Agricultural Value Chain and Cooperative Marketing Support","RDCD will promote the agricultural value chain and access to market through cooperatives, through marketing of agricultural products and raising awareness of value-chain, supporting activities related to production, and developing marketing infrastructures.","RDCD"]],"87":[[1,"737","4","Food Waste Reduction and Supply Chain Optimization","Reduce food wastage through (i) optimal harvesting, (ii) precision processing, storage, packaging and transportation, (iii) tracking the supply chain, (iv) optimal retailing.",""],[1,"737","4","Retail Demand Forecasting Improvement","Supply and demand optimization at the retail level through improved prediction",""],[1,"737","6","UAV-Based Soil Fertility and Crop Health Mapping","UAV based soil fertility and crop health mapping, and precisely distributing inputs like fertilizer, pesticide, and water;",""],[1,"739","4","IR4.0 Technology Stack for Agricultural Innovation","IR4.0 technology stack supports innovation, in both products and process levels, creating new tasks.",""],[1,"744","1","Agro Supply-Chain Empowerment for Marginal Farmers","a) empowering marginal farmers to strengthen agro supply-chain;","ICT Division"],[1,"745","4","Kiosk-Based Agricultural Mobile Application through PPP","a) kiosk-based mobile application through PPP;",""],[1,"745","4","Online Marketplace for Agro-Machinery Rental","b) online marketplace for agro-machinery rental;",""],[1,"746","1","Localized Agro-Advisory and E-Training Platform","localized agro-advisory and e-training platform for enhancing farmers' digital literacy",""],[1,"746","1","Digital Marketplace and Commodity Exchange Development","digital marketplace and commodity exchange through PPP and private sector led models",""],[1,"748","15","Digital Agricultural Commodity Exchange","Digital commodity exchange for agriculture produce connecting farmers at their doorsteps",""],[1,"749","6","Digital Agricultural Commodity Exchange","Digital commodity exchange for agriculture produce connecting farmers at their doorsteps",""]],"88":[[1,"799","4","Expansion and Improvement of Food Grain Storage Facilities","The government has therefore taken initiatives to expand and improve food grain storage facilities by building additional high-quality modern storage facilities.",""],[1,"801","1","Public Food Procurement Improvement","The goal of 8th Five-Year Plan is to improve the food and nutrition security status to the level needed to achieve the FNS-relevant SDG targets and fulfil other related national and international commitments by 2030, improving public food procurement, increasing food storage capacity and modernization.",""],[1,"801","1","Food Storage Capacity Expansion and Modernization","The goal of 8th Five-Year Plan is to improve the food and nutrition security status to the level needed to achieve the FNS-relevant SDG targets and fulfil other related national and international commitments by 2030, improving public food procurement, increasing food storage capacity and modernization.",""],[1,"801","7","Modern Food Storage Facilities Expansion","Develop and improve modern facilities for food storage along with increasing capacity.",""],[1,"801","9","ICT-Based Public Food Procurement, Storage and Distribution System","Develop and improve ICT-based public food procurement, storage and distribution system",""],[1,"802","2","Food Supply and Public Distribution Support","The measures to accomplish the objectives would include special measures for disaster mitigation in agriculture, increased supply of food through market and public distribution and investment in employment generation activities.",""],[1,"803","4","Public Food Storage Capacity Expansion and Modernization","During the 8th Plan, the Ministry of Food has set the target to increase the storage capacity up to 3.7 million MT by 2025.","Ministry of Food"],[1,"803","5","Storage Modernization and Mechanization Initiative","Increase shelf life and maintain quality: need modernization, mechanization, vertical and bulk storage.",""],[1,"803","6","Vertical Storage Promotion","Reduce use of land: promote vertical storage in place of flat go downs",""],[1,"803","7","Bulk and Vertical Storage Modernization","Reduce cost of handling and storage: bulk and vertical storage with modern bagging, weighing and handling equipment.",""],[1,"803","9","Disaster-Prone Area Storage Capacity Expansion","Increase storage capacity in disaster-prone areas to boost response capacity.",""],[1,"803","10","Fortified Food Storage Development","Develop storage to cater for the need for nutrition interventions for the storage of fortified food.",""],[1,"804","1","ICT-Enabled Food Storage and Supply Management System","Develop food storage equipped with ICT to update and quick sharing of data and information on transactions and be equipped with supply/production management applications.",""],[1,"804","2","Buffer Stock Maintenance and Food and Nutrition Security Access","Maintain Buffer stock and ensure access to food and nutrition security to the poor and vulnerable",""],[1,"804","3","Modern Food Storage Facilities Project","the government is implementing the Modern Food Storage Facilities Project, financed by the World Bank.",""]],"89":[[1,"801","2","Safe and Nutritious Food Access and Affordability Initiative","Ensure availability of safe and nutritious food for healthy diets; ensure access to safe and nutritious food at an affordable price.",""],[1,"801","4","Nutrition-Sensitive Social Protection and Safety Net Expansion","Increase access to nutrition-sensitive social protection and safety nets across life cycle with a focus on vulnerable groups and regions and strengthen promotion of nutrition through social protection and safety net programmes as well as establishing referral systems between programmes and services.",""],[1,"801","5","Innovative Programme Support Approaches","Develop and support innovative approaches to support programmes (e-vouchers for diverse foods, tele messaging, e-training, etc.)",""],[1,"801","8","Multi-sectoral Food and Nutrition Security Governance Strengthening","Strengthen multi-sectoral food and nutrition security governance, coordination and partnership for effective policy implementation.",""],[1,"801","10","National Food Safety Coordination Mechanism","Strengthen the coordination mechanism for a comprehensive national level food safety system including the establishment and operation of national codex committee.",""],[1,"801","11","BFSA Reference Laboratory Establishment and Public Laboratory Upgrading","Strengthen the capacity of food testing situation by establishing BFSA reference lab and improving other public laboratories.",""],[1,"801","12","Public-Private Partnership for Modern Food Management System","Explore Public-Private Partnership in case of large-scale investment to introduce modern food management system.",""],[1,"801","13","National Food Loss and Waste Reduction Strategy","Formulate and implement a comprehensive National Strategy/Policy for reduction of food loss and waste.",""],[1,"802","3","Inclusive and Nutrition-Sensitive Social Protection Programme","Under this initiative, the effectiveness, targeting and content of social safety net programmes are improved including by strengthening nutrition education and promotion to provide better protection of different vulnerable groups.",""],[1,"802","3","Fortified Biscuits for Schoolchildren","the Ministry of Primary and Mass Education provide fortified biscuits with vitamins and minerals to pre-primary and primary school children in high poverty prone areas.","Ministry of Primary and Mass Education"],[1,"802","3","School Meal Programme Expansion","The school meal programme has been initiated in few upazilas for ensuring nutrient food for the children which will be rolled out nationally.",""],[1,"802","3","Micronutrient-Fortified Food Distribution","efforts will be made to offer micronutrient-fortified food grains in the open market operations and through the safety net channels.",""],[1,"802","3","Fortified Rice Introduction Initiative","The Government in collaboration with development partners and the private sector is introducing fortified rice (called pushti chal) for reducing micronutrient deficiency.",""],[1,"803","1","Food Safety Market Surveillance","It is essential to increase surveillance on different market actors to promote food safety attributes.",""],[1,"803","2","Food Safety Regulatory and Monitoring Framework","Enacting of appropriate laws and introduction of proper monitoring systems require coordination among the authorities responsible for ensuring food safety.",""],[1,"803","2","Integrated Food Safety Standards and Enforcement System","An integrated view and related operational procedures are necessary for ensuring food safety so that a framework combining laws and regulations including standards, food safety management, inspection and enforcement services can be made effective.",""],[1,"803","2","Food Testing Laboratory Expansion","Implementation of regulations also requires quality food testing facilities.",""],[1,"803","2","Mobile Food Testing Laboratory Support","Mobile laboratories could be helpful with adequate supply of technicians and testing kits to run those laboratories.",""],[1,"803","2","Divisional Central Food Testing Facilities","There should also be central food testing facilities at least in every divisional city.",""],[1,"803","2","Food Safety Institutional Budget Allocation","Institutions particularly those with various mandates on food safety should be allocated adequate budgetary provisions for their activities.",""],[1,"803","3","Bangladesh Food Safety Authority Institutional Strengthening","The Parliament of Bangladesh passed the Food Safety Act 2013 under which the Bangladesh Food Safety Authority (BFSA) was constituted to strengthen collaboration among inter-ministerial and inter-agencies for ensuring food safety and food control.",""],[1,"803","3","Food Safety Regulations and Rules Finalization","Considering risk-based inspections and determining safety standards, the BFSA has drafted the following regulations: (1) Food Safety (Sample Collection, Test and Analysis) Regulation 2015, (2) Food Safety (Contaminants, Toxins, and Harmful Residues) Regulation 2015, (3) Food Safety (Food Additives) Regulation 2015, (4) Hygiene Preservation and Preparation of Food Regulation 2016, (5) Labelling of Packet Food Regulation 2016, Bangladesh Food Safety Authority Service Regulations 2016 and (7) Bangladesh Food Safety Authority Service Rules 2016 (FPMU 2017).",""]],"90":[[1,"364","3","Good Agricultural Practices Adoption for Production and Post-Harvest Management","Good Agricultural Practices (GAP) also needs to be employed for production and post-harvest management.",""],[1,"366","13","E-Agricultural Marketing","To achieve expanded digitalization of market access and market linkage activities, establishing e- agricultural marketing.",""],[1,"367","1","Balanced Fertilizer Recommendation Services for Farmers","To provide services to farmers regarding balanced fertilizer application through Online Fertilizer Recommendation System (OFRS) and Offline Fertilizer Recommendation System (Mobile Apps).",""],[1,"367","2","Farmer Capacity Building and Awareness Training on Modern Technologies","To provide capacity building training and awareness training to the farmer on uses of modern technologies, post-harvest storage etc.",""],[1,"372","3","Demand-Led Agricultural Extension Services","Demand-led agricultural extension: Transfer of technologies, diversification and intensification of crop production program through appropriate extension services are of crucial importance.",""],[1,"372","10","Field Monitoring for Agricultural Input Quality","Field monitoring for seed, pesticide and fertilizer quality",""],[1,"373","1","Decentralized Extension and Micro-Planning Approach","Adoption of decentralized extension approach, bottom up planning and micro planning",""],[1,"373","7","Extension Agency Human Resources Development Programme","Strengthening human resources development programmes of extension agencies",""],[1,"373","8","MIS and ICT-Based Agricultural Knowledge Management System","Strengthening MIS and ICT-based knowledge management system and e-agriculture",""],[1,"373","9","Farmer's Information and Advisory Centre Establishment","Establishment of Farmer's Information and Advisory Centre (FIAC) at all union level",""]],"91":[[1,"55","10","Overseas Employment Strengthening","Strengthen overseas employment.",""],[1,"57","1","Overseas Employment and Remittance Expansion Programme","The 8FYP will make a comprehensive push to expand overseas employment and remittance earnings through G2G negotiations, by lowering the cost of migration through low-cost loans from the Bangladesh Probashi Bank, by increasing training and other services to potential migrants, and by stronger support in the work place against exploitation and abuse in host countries through the local Bangladesh Embassies and High Commissions.",""],[1,"113","3","Overseas Employment Promotion Measures","The government will also take measures to boost overseas employment once the global recovery from COVID-19 is underway in FY2022.",""],[1,"114","8","Overseas Employment Strengthening","· Strengthen overseas employment",""],[1,"115","4","Overseas Employment and Remittance Expansion Initiative","The 8FYP will make a comprehensive push to expand overseas employment and remittance earnings through G2G negotiations, by lowering the cost of migration through low-cost loans from the Bangladesh Probashi Bank, by increasing training and other services to potential migrants, and by stronger support in the work place against exploitation and abuse in host countries through the local Bangladesh embassies",""],[1,"172","1","External Migration Strategy for Poverty Reduction","The external migration strategy for poverty reduction during the 8FYP consists of a number of inter-related policy actions: (i) strengthen government efforts to negotiate with existing and new potential labour- shortage host countries to export Bangladeshi workers; (ii) upgrade skill base of potential migrants through training; (iii) support outmigration from the poorest districts of the Northwest part of Bangladesh that are not well served by access to external migration through better information flow and training; (iv) find ways to reduce the cost of out-migration through partnerships with job agencies that provide low-cost services; (v) provide access to one-time credit to defray the cost of migration secured against future earnings based on a government programme administered by commercial banks; (vi) provide information and anti-exploitation services through the embassies; (vii) ensure that the exchange rate for remittance through the banking system is competitive with the curb market rates; and (viii) offer solid banking services to the migrant workers to enable the use of formal banking channels for sending remittances.",""],[1,"177","9","Migration Access Support for Lagging Districts","Improve access of lagging districts to international migration through better information, training, and credit support to meet the cost of overseas employment.",""],[1,"322","9","Central and Southeast Asian Export Market Diversification","Bangladesh also needs to explore markets of the Central Asian and South-East Asian countries for exporting its products.","Ministry of Finance | Ministry of Commerce | Ministry of Industries | Ministry of Foreign Affairs"],[1,"323","1","FDI Attraction through Cluster Collaboration","BEPZA and BHTPA can work with this cluster to attract the FDI in Bangladesh, and thus ensure employment, industrialization, export diversification and so on.",""],[1,"323","5","Overseas Workforce Migration Facilitation Programme","The Ministry will target at least 5 million new workforces for facilitating migration abroad in 8FYP, with minimum 50% in higher skilled categories.","The Ministry"],[1,"323","5","Labour Migration Market Diversification Initiative","The Ministry will target 20 new countries in 4 new geographic regions.","The Ministry"],[1,"323","5","Remittance Expansion Target","The Ministry will target reaching USD 150 Billion of remittance in 8FYP period, with an average remittance income of USD 30 Billion per year.","The Ministry"]],"92":[[1,"320","6","Migrant Worker Service Processing ERP System","The Wage Earners' Welfare Board (WEWB) introduced an Enterprise Resource Planning (ERP) system, which allows to process services for migrant workers.","Wage Earners' Welfare Board (WEWB)"],[1,"321","4","Overseas Employment and Migration Framework Reform","Make a paradigm shift in the overseas employment and migration framework so that it becomes an important strategy of poverty and unemployment reduction, macroeconomic stability and well- being of every citizen of the country;",""],[1,"321","5","Zero Migration Stance for Bangladeshi Expatriates","Promote zero migration stance until the dignity, fairness, freedom, security and human rights of all Bangladeshi expatriates, especially for women migrants, are ensured;",""],[1,"321","8","Low-Cost Migration Facilitation","Achieve low- cost migration for Bangladeshi citizens through concerted efforts of Ministries and agencies in the country as well as working along with regional and global stakeholders;",""],[1,"321","9","Safe and Protected Overseas Employment and Return Support","Make overseas employment and return of Bangladeshi citizens, after contributing to Bangladesh economy and economy of host countries, safe, assured and protected.",""]],"93":[[1,"819","6","Safe Migration Support and Pre-Departure Preparation","Safe migration should be ensured through skills enhancement, compulsory pre departure training, language skills, skills on self- defence, proper screening, and registration for women and men.",""],[1,"819","6","Overseas Labour Market Research and New Market Exploration","Market research for exploring the possibilities of external market should be undertaken and new avenues explored.",""],[1,"819","6","Women Migrant Self-Defence and Screening Measures","Aspirant women should be given self -defence training and be selected based on screening.",""],[1,"820","1","Expansion of Legal and Shelter Support for Migrant Workers","Legal and shelter support for migrant workers need expansion in countries where number of women workers is high.",""],[1,"820","1","Compulsory Health Screening and Quarantine for Returnee Migrant Workers","The returnee migrant workers need compulsory health screening and quarantine services upon return.",""],[1,"820","1","Strengthening Labour Migration Management and Worker Protection","The overall management of labour migration, protection and decent employment conditions to the Bangladeshi migrant workers should be ensured.",""],[1,"820","1","Accountability and Penalties for Recruiting Agencies","The recruiting agencies should be made accountable to ensure proper job condition and should be penalized if failed.",""],[1,"820","1","Promotion of Women's Professional Employment","Women's employment in professional category should be promoted through education, training, linkage, information and support.",""]],"94":[[1,"53","2","Banking Sector Reform Programme","Tax reforms and banking reforms will become even more important as the nation faces to fight the COVID-19 adverse economic effects.",""],[1,"58","4","State-Owned Enterprise and Public Bank Reform","SOEs including public banks will be reformed to earn profits and eliminate dependency on budget transfers.",""],[1,"64","9","Bangladesh Bank Strengthening and Prudential Regulation Enforcement","Strengthening of the Bangladesh Bank with recruitment of high-quality staff and implementation of all prudential regulations for the entire banking system.",""],[1,"64","9","Public Bank Reform to Reduce Non-Performing Loans","Urgent reform of public banks to reduce non- performing loans, bad lending decisions and to earn profit with zero recourse to Treasury funding.",""],[1,"65","1","State-Owned Enterprise Reform and Hard Budget Constraint","The SOEs will be urgently reformed to reduce leakage of resources and to enable all enterprises to fully recover cost and earn a reasonable rate of return on assets.",""],[1,"136","15","Banking Regulation Tightening and Basel Implementation","Banking regulations have been progressively tightened in the context of implementation of BASEL I and II guidelines.","Bangladesh Bank"],[1,"136","15","Bangladesh Bank Supervision Capacity Strengthening","Efforts have also been made to improve the supervision capacity of the regulator, the Bangladesh Bank, through a range of technical assistance.","Bangladesh Bank"],[1,"136","15","Basel III Implementation","Bangladesh started implementation the BASEL- III framework in the 7FYP but progress has been halting.",""],[1,"137","2","Banking Sector Performance Reform Package","The government is committed to improve banking sector performance during the 8FYP.",""],[1,"137","2","Bangladesh Bank Regulatory Autonomy Enhancement","A series of policy reforms are envisaged during the 8FYP including greater autonomy to the Bangladesh Bank for implementing its regulatory and supervision responsibilities including for public banks",""],[1,"137","2","Basel III Implementation","A series of policy reforms are envisaged during the 8FYP including ... full implementation of Basel III regulations",""],[1,"137","2","Public Bank Corporatization and Profitability Reform","A series of policy reforms are envisaged during the 8FYP including ... improving the performance of public banks through corporatization and requiring them to earn a profit",""],[1,"137","2","High-Risk Borrower Exposure Reduction","A series of policy reforms are envisaged during the 8FYP including ... reducing the exposure to high-risk borrowers",""],[1,"137","2","Loan Recovery Policy for Wilful Defaulters","A series of policy reforms are envisaged during the 8FYP including ... implementing a well- thought out policy for recovery of loans from wilful defaulters.",""],[1,"140","2","Banking Sector Governance and Supervision Strengthening","Bangladesh Bank and the government will strengthen significantly banking sector governance and supervision in order to reduce the lending rate without creating market distortions","Bangladesh Bank | the government"],[1,"146","1","Banking and Capital Market Reforms","the banking and capital market reforms are also essential",""],[1,"146","1","Banking Sector Interest Rate Reform","Banking reforms are critical to lower the spread between deposit and lending rates and enable the maintenance of positive real interest rates for deposit mobilization while keeping real lending rates in line with marginal productivity of capital",""]],"95":[[1,"141","8","Bangladesh Securities and Exchange Commission Capacity Strengthening","strengthen market stability by enhancing the role and capacity of the Bangladesh Securities and Exchange Commission (BSEC);",""],[1,"141","9","Capital Market Development and Governance Reform","enhance market facilitation by developing a long-term vision for capital markets, upgrading accounting and auditing standards, expediting adjudication of enforcement actions, improving governance of listed companies, and pursuing demutualization of the stock exchanges",""],[1,"141","10","Capital Market Development and Institutional Investor Mobilization","incentivize the issuance of equities and bonds, develop liquid capital markets, and catalyze institutional investors.",""],[1,"142","1","Special Rediscount Window for Stock Market Lending","Recently Bangladesh Bank has introduced a special rediscount window for every bank to borrow up to Tk. 2 billion from the central bank at a subsidized interest rate for on-lending to institutional investors in the stock market.","Bangladesh Bank"],[1,"144","5","Increase IPOs of Large Financially Sound Companies","Increasing the number of IPOs of large and financially sound companies and attracting foreign investment will help support the market stability and growth.",""],[1,"144","5","Attract Foreign Investment for Market Stability","Increasing the number of IPOs of large and financially sound companies and attracting foreign investment will help support the market stability and growth.",""],[1,"144","6","Stock Exchange Demutualization Reform","the demutualization of stock exchanges to segregate ownership, management and trading rights of members will help convert the two major exchanges (Dhaka and Chittagong) into commercially and professionally run organizations",""],[1,"144","6","Stock Market Governance Improvement","Improved governance structure should also help develop the market and attract new investors",""],[1,"144","7","Equity Market Confidence Restoration Reforms","In order to enhance supply and demand for equities over the 8FYP, effort will be made to restore confidence through the following reforms:",""],[1,"144","8","Accounting and Auditing Standards Upgrade","Upgrading of accounting and auditing standards to enhance market confidence.",""],[1,"144","8","Financial Reporting Council Monitoring Function","The newly established Financial Reporting Council (FRC) will adopt and monitor the implementation of",""],[1,"145","2","Audit Committee Establishment","Establish an Audit Committee to supervise companies' internal controls, accounting policies, and compliance with IAS",""],[1,"145","3","Mutual Fund Industry Development","developing an organized investor base through a robust mutual fund industry will require going beyond what has been done so far and observe how the sector responds to the steps already taken.",""],[1,"145","3","ICB Mutual Fund Regulatory Compliance","making the playing field even by requiring ICB funds to be fully compliant with all mutual fund regulations will be important.",""],[1,"250","8","Capital Market Capacity and Effectiveness Enhancement","the following activities will be undertaken under the 8FYP to ensure greater capacity and effectiveness of the capital market:",""],[1,"251","1","BSEC Capacity Building and Institutional Reform","Government will undertake a long-term capacity building of Bangladesh Securities and Exchange Commission (BSEC) in areas of skilled human capital, modern technologies and prudential regulations.",""],[1,"251","1","Securities Law and Regulation Reform","The Commission is also redefining securities laws and regulations in order to ensure prudential regulations and supervision of issuers and market intermediaries in the capital market.",""],[1,"251","2","Primary Market Governance and Securities Regulation Reform","Bangladesh will build a vibrant, dynamic and good-governed primary market.",""],[1,"251","3","XBRL Technology Platform for Market Transparency","A technology platform of extensible business reporting language (XBRL) shall prove critical to this end of transparency and accountability for stock exchanges, issuers and other market intermediaries.",""],[1,"251","3","Enforcement of IFRS, ISAs, and Corporate Governance Compliance","BSEC will invest heavily to enforce observance of issuers and market intermediaries with International Financial Reporting Standards (IFRSs), International Standards of Auditing (ISAs) and modern corporate governance codes.",""],[1,"251","4","Diversified Capital Market Development","Government is committed to building a diversified capital market involving both bond and derivative markets so that financing of business moves from banking system to the capital market.",""],[1,"251","4","Derivative Market Capacity Building","The Commission shall closely work with stock exchanges for this important capacity building.",""],[1,"251","5","Capital Market Coordination Mechanism","The Government will evaluate the need of an institutional mechanism to facilitate this coordination between Bangladesh Bank and BSEC for building a modern capital market.",""],[1,"251","5","Regulatory Conflict-of-Interest Task Force","It will also create a task force to detect conflicts of interest within the regulatory bodies and financial institutions, especially amongst those who have an exposure to the stock market.",""],[1,"251","6","Stock Market Surveillance and Trading Infrastructure Upgrade","The Government will improve the surveillance software/systems to prevent manipulation of the transaction of securities in the stock market and to ensure greater transparency.",""],[1,"251","7","Securities Law Enforcement Capacity Building","Inquiry, supervision and enforcement of securities laws will comprise a critical capacity building for BSEC and stock exchanges.",""],[1,"251","7","Corporate Financial Reporting Compliance Enforcement","The Government will take measures to ensure that companies comply with the financial reporting and disclosure rules of the BSEC.",""],[1,"251","7","Capital Market Tribunal Case Transfer Mechanism","More stock market related legal cases need to be transferred to the special tribunal on capital market for quick disposal of the cases.",""],[1,"251","8","Tax Incentives for Stock Exchange Listing","The Government will improve the tax incentives further for the private sector companies to be listed with stock exchanges and to commit to enhanced transparency and accountability.",""],[1,"251","8","Capital Market Listing Incentive Reform","An option to go for listing shall be made attractive for an issuer of capital and tax policies will be geared to this end.",""],[1,"251","8","Transition to Capital Market-Based Financing","The Government is committed for a transition from the current bank-based borrowing to capital market-based financing.",""],[1,"252","1","Financial Reporting Council Operationalization and Coordination","The Government will make FRC to be further operational and effective for enforcing accounting and auditing standards.",""],[1,"252","1","Capital Market Accounting and Auditing Standards Upgrade","Under the 8th Plan, the Government is committed to upgrading the accounting and auditing standards of the capital market.",""],[1,"252","2","Investment in Financial Literacy Institutes","The Government is committed to invest in both the institutes and making them effective for financial literacy.",""]],"96":[[1,"834","3","National Child Participation Platform","1) creating a national platform for allowing children to express opinions on their needs;",""],[1,"839","3","Child Participation in Programme Design and Evaluation","ensuring participation of children in defining their needs, developing programmes, implementing interventions, and evaluating their success",""],[1,"840","4","National Child Voice Platform","it would be necessary to create a national platform for allowing children to express opinions on their needs and expectations and means of addressing them.",""],[1,"841","4","Public Advocacy and Child Rights Coordination Mechanism","The Ministry of Women and Children Affairs will conduct public advocacy and coordinate interventions for children's well-being and rights.","Ministry of Women and Children Affairs"],[1,"841","4","Inter-Ministerial Child Rights Coordination Committee","An inter-ministerial coordination committee consisting of government ministries with children's portfolios and organizations representing children's mandate will be chaired by the Secretary of the Ministry of Women and Children Affairs and will coordinate implementation of the Children Act 2013, CRC, CEDAW, and the World Fit for Children Plan of Action.","Ministry of Women and Children Affairs"]],"97":[[1,"532","6","Chittagong Hill Tracts Accord Implementation and Monitoring Coordination","the MoCHTA will coordinate inter-ministerial activities of the region, will provide assistance to the CHT Accord Implementation and Monitoring Committee to have fullest implementation and proper monitoring of the issues of the CHT Accord","MoCHTA"],[1,"533","3","Hill District Councils Election and Management Compliance","The election and management of the Hill District Councils will follow the Hill District Council Act, 1989.",""],[1,"533","4","Strengthening of CHT Governance Institutions","As per the CHT treaty of 1997, the MoCHTA, CHT Regional Council and Hill District Councils will be strengthened to facilitate development in the region.","MoCHTA | CHT Regional Council | Hill District Councils"],[1,"533","5","Chittagong Hill Tracts Land Disputes Resolution Rules Enactment","The Rules of the CHT Land Disputes Resolution will be enacted soon so that CHT Land Disputes Resolution Commission can function for settling land disputes in the region.",""],[1,"533","5","Land Commission Tribal Land Rights Resolution","Following Dispute Resolution Act 2001, the Land Commission will resolve the disputes and ensure land rights of the tribal people.",""],[1,"533","6","Consultative Land Survey and Land Policy for CHT Disputes","A land survey will be carried out in consultation with stakeholders as per provisions of the CHT Accord.",""],[1,"533","6","Land Dispute Resolution Policy for the CHT Region","An appropriate land policy will be adopted to deal with the land disputes in the region.",""],[1,"533","14","Institutional Capacity Enhancement for Hill District Councils and CHT Institutions","Enhance institutional capacity of three Hill District Councils (HDCs), CHTRC and CHT Development Board (CHTDB) urgently.",""],[1,"533","15","Institutional Capacity Strengthening Measures","Institutional capacity will be increased through Annual Performance Agreements, National Integration Strategy, innovation, domestic and foreign training, monthly coordination meetings, monthly development review meetings and project inspections.",""],[1,"534","1","Coordinated Socio-Economic Development in the CHT Region","Following the agreement and the subsequent legislations, the concerned ministries will consult with the MoCHTA, and implement activities in coordination with the ministry.","MoCHTA"],[1,"842","4","CHT Peace Accord Implementation","The government will ensure full implementation of the CHT treaty signed in 1997.",""],[1,"844","3","Hill District Councils Election and Management","Election and management of the Hill Districts Councils following the Hill District Council Act, 1989 will be ensured.",""],[1,"844","3","Capacity Development for Ministry, CHTRC, CHTDB and HDCs","Capacity development of the Ministry, CHTRC, CHTDB and HDCs will be enhanced by increasing manpower and other facilities.","Ministry | CHTRC | CHTDB | HDCs"],[1,"844","4","Chittagong Hill Tracts Perspective Plan Formulation","The Government will formulate a Perspective Plan for the development of CHT through a consultation process with key stakeholders.",""],[1,"844","5","Accelerated CHT Development Financing","Additional finance will be allocated on priority basis for implementation of programmes/projects to reduce poverty and to attain middle income status by 2021.",""],[1,"844","5","CHT Development Fund Channeling through Ministry of CHT Affairs","All funds of line Ministries for CHT development will be channelled through the Ministry of CHT Affairs.","Ministry of CHT Affairs | line Ministries"],[1,"844","5","Ethnic Group Participation in Development Projects","Representatives of the ethnic groups will be included in development projects undertaken in their areas.",""]],"98":[[1,"794","21","CO-OP Trust Investment Services","CO-OP Trust Investment Services: Invest funds",""],[1,"805","7","Coordinated Disaster Management and Resilient Infrastructure Rulemaking","Aims to make disaster management activities coordinated, object-oriented, and strong in formulating rules to build infrastructure for resilience.",""],[1,"805","11","Mainstreaming of Disaster Risk Reduction and Climate Change Adaptation","Calls for comprehensively addressing DRR and CAA in all development plans, programmes, and policies through assessing climate change risk, emphasizing community-based programmes, building public awareness, improving early",""],[1,"805","13","Climate Adaptation Priority Activities","Identifies 15 priority activities for adaptation action, including general awareness raising, capacity building, and project implementation in vulnerable regions, with a focus on agriculture and water resources.",""],[1,"805","18","Disaster Management Duties and Responsibilities Awareness Programme","Works to make relevant persons understand and perform their duties and responsibilities regarding disaster management at all levels.",""],[1,"806","1","Revision of Upazila Development Planning Proforma","the local level (Upazila) development planning proforma is being revised by the Local Government Division where inputs provided by the Ministry of Disaster Management and Relief will make it more effective for disaster risk reduction","Local Government Division | Ministry of Disaster Management and Relief"],[1,"806","13","Legal Framework for Disaster Standing Orders","under the 8FYP, the Government is committed to develop an effective legal framework that offers the SOD a legal footing.",""],[1,"806","14","Stakeholder Training for SOD Coordination","More training will be offered to enhance the knowledge and skills of the stakeholders.",""],[1,"806","14","Advanced and Refresher Training for SOD Coordination Bodies","Advanced training, refresher training, on",""],[1,"807","1","Job Training Arrangement","the job training etc. will also be arranged.",""],[1,"807","1","Incentive Restructuring for Disaster Management Stakeholders","The Government will also offer greater motivation for better performance by reshaping the incentives, such as: rewarding the best Union Disaster Management Committee (UDMC), rewarding the best UDMC member, rewarding the best volunteer etc.",""],[1,"807","2","Operationalization of Standing Orders on Disaster","Hence, the Government will mitigate existing challenge for better operationalization of SODs through joint collaboration and adopting multi-sectoral approach.",""],[1,"807","3","Upazila Disaster Management Committee Monitoring Support","the Government will ensure that the Upazila Disaster Management Committees (UDMC) remains committed to monitor the activities of Union Disaster Management Committee (UDMC) regularly and provide proactive support as and when required.",""],[1,"807","4","Resource Support for Union Disaster Management Committees","The Government will pay due attention to this concern so that the UDMCs have the adequate resources for better implementation of the SOD and the Disaster Contingency Plan.",""],[1,"807","4","Union-Level Disaster Contingency Fund","Similarly, the Government will ensure provisions for the Disaster Contingency Fund at the Union level.",""],[1,"807","4","Local Disaster Contingency Fund Mobilization","The Union Disaster Management Committees (UDMCs) will also take collective initiatives to generate the Disaster Contingency Fund through the mobilization of local resources.",""],[1,"807","5","Multi-stakeholder Disaster Risk Reduction Collaboration","Collaborative efforts will be undertaken to strengthen the activities for preparedness at all levels and reduce the impact of disasters.",""],[1,"808","1","Citizen and Media Integration in Disaster Preparedness","Hence, they will be increasingly integrated in the work on preparedness for disasters.",""],[1,"808","7","Integrated Disaster Risk Reduction and Climate Change Adaptation Policy","The Government will develop a comprehensive policy on the integration of Disaster Risk Reduction (DDR) and Climate Change Adaption (CCA) to address the losses and damages from the impacts of both extreme events and slow onset processes.",""],[1,"808","8","Loss and Damage Policy Wing Support Bodies","The Government will establish a policy body under the Ministry of Planning (MoP) and technical bodies at both the Ministry of Environment, Forest and Climate Change (MoEFCC) and the Ministry of Disaster Management and Relief (MoDMR), to serve as a knowledge hub and to provide expertise in DRR and CCA respectively to the Loss and Damage Policy Wing of the MoP.","Ministry of Planning (MoP) | Ministry of Environment, Forest and Climate Change (MoEFCC) | Ministry of Disaster Management and Relief (MoDMR)"],[1,"808","9","Integrated Disaster Risk Reduction and Climate Change Adaptation Institutional Framework","The Government will integrate the DRR and CCA in a multi-level institutional framework to address the losses and damages from both extreme events and slow onset processes under a common mechanism.",""],[1,"808","10","Accreditation of National Funding Entities as National Implementing Entities","Obtain accreditation for the existing National Funding Entities (NFE) to become National Implementing Entities (NIE) in order to access support from the international funding mechanisms - both within and outside the United Nations Framework Convention on Climate Change (UNFCCC) - to address losses and damages, including through adaptation, mitigation, technology and capacity building.",""],[1,"809","5","Private Sector Disaster and Climate Resilience Partnerships","Promote private sector resilience to disasters and climate change risks through improved public private partnerships.",""],[1,"809","6","Adaptive Disaster and Climate Research Programme","Develop adaptive research on disaster and climatic issues",""],[1,"809","8","Vulnerability Index for Equitable Resource Allocation","Develop a vulnerability index which will help channelize equitable resources to the targeted districts.",""],[1,"809","11","Business Process Improvement and Financial Management Reform","Improve business processes and initiate financial management reform in MoDMR and DDM and relevant GoB agencies.","MoDMR | DDM | relevant GoB agencies"],[1,"809","12","Government Coordination Mechanism Strengthening","Develop a better coordination mechanism within the ministry and across the government.",""],[1,"809","14","Disaster Management Skills Development and Cyclone Preparedness Partnership Programme","Support skill development by giving training to GOs, NGO officials and volunteers concerned in Disaster Management and develop greater partnership with NGOs to improve \"cyclone preparedness\" capacity.",""],[1,"809","15","Disaster Management Best Practices and Technology Integration","Incorporate best practices and technology in Disaster Management of Bangladesh from around the world.",""],[1,"809","16","Road and Water Safety Guidelines Improvement","Improve guidelines for Road and Water Safety.",""],[1,"809","17","Industrial Safety Guidelines Improvement","Improve guidelines for Industrial Safety.",""],[1,"809","26","Emergency Response and Information Management Guidelines","Improve Emergency Response and Information Management Guidelines.",""],[1,"810","11","Legal and Regulatory Environment Reform","Establish conducive legal and regulatory environment.",""],[1,"810","12","Institutional Capacity, Accountability and Oversight Improvement","5. Improve institutional capacity, accountability and oversight.",""]],"99":[[1,"183","1","Integrated National Financing Framework for Accelerating Achievement of SDGs","The Government has initiated the implementation of a Joint Programme called Integrated National Financing Framework for Accelerating Achievement of SDGs in Bangladesh.",""],[1,"199","8","Development Partner Partnership and COVID-19 Assistance Mobilization","Thus, one of the key strategies of the 8FYP will be to ensure effective partnership with development partners, especially multilateral development finance institutions to mobilize swift COVID-19 assistance and to ensure better use and results of existing pipeline and new loans.",""],[1,"199","10","Local Consultative Group Coordination Platform","Anchored in the JCS, Local Consultative Group (LCG) is the main platform for coordination between the government and DPs is Bangladesh.",""],[1,"199","10","Joint Cooperation Strategy for Aid Effectiveness","Bangladesh has established a formal mechanism of partnership with development partners working in Bangladesh through the signing of a Joint Cooperation Strategy (JCS) in 2010.",""],[1,"200","1","Development Partner Coordination Mechanism Strengthening","During the 8th Five Year Plan period, government will continue its efforts to strengthen the JCS and the LCG, keeping up with the evolving partnership needs.",""],[1,"200","2","Acceleration of Existing Pipeline Projects","A top priority is speed up the use of existing pipeline, focusing specifically on slow-moving problem projects to restructure and speed up implementation.",""],[1,"200","2","Alignment of Development Partner Assistance Strategies","The 8FYP envisages that all DPs will align their country assistance strategies with the goals and sectoral targets of the Government.",""],[1,"200","2","Leadership of Line Ministries in LCG Sectoral Working Groups","Leadership of government line ministries in the LCG sectoral working group is key to ensure DP policy alignment and system harmonization.","government line ministries"],[1,"200","2","ERD Foreign Assistance Outreach Work Plan","The ERD as development assistance coordinator should map comprehensive work plan to reach out to all government line ministries to ensure that they all are on the same wave length when dealing with foreign assistance.","ERD | government line ministries"],[1,"200","3","Right to Information and Information Commission Framework","The government is proactively creating enabling environment for disclosure of public documents with the enactment of Right to Information Act and establishment of the independent Information Commission.",""],[1,"200","3","Public Aid Data Disclosure and AIMS Data Sharing System","The 8FYP stipulates that all aid data be made public and the Aid Information Management System (AIMS) should be the principal means of data sharing by DPs in Bangladesh.",""]],"100":[[1,"480","6","Cyber Threat Detection and Response Project","'Cyber Threat Detection and Response' project has been implemented by Department of Telecommunications (DoT) to prevent internet users from accessing websites/content that are inconsistent with the country's values, including porn and gambling sites.","Department of Telecommunications (DoT)"],[1,"481","1","Coordination with Global Online Service Providers to Counter Harmful Content","Initiatives have been taken with the authorities of Facebook, Google, Microsoft and other online media to prevent, monitor and counter harmful content such as anti-social and anti-social propaganda, rumours and religious extremism on social networking sites.",""],[1,"724","5","Digital Security Awareness Training","Various groups in society, namely, girls, students, teachers, journalists, and government officials, have been imparted training on cybercrime, related laws, safety strategies on social network platforms, ways to get rid of crime, and specific procedures to register complaints, and so on.",""],[1,"726","2","ICT Policy and Regulatory Framework Development","ICT Division has been formulating acts, guidelines, rules and policies related to ICT.","ICT Division"],[1,"735","4","Data Protection Regulation Update","To protect citizens in the digital space, update data protection regulation, along the line of EU's General Data Protection Regulation.",""],[1,"735","5","Data Protection and Legal Enforcement Measures","Measures are taken to safeguard data of citizens, corporates, and the Government.",""],[1,"735","6","Antitrust and Data Privacy Regulatory Strengthening","Address regulatory weaknesses and strengthen international collaboration in dealing with antitrust and data privacy issues .",""],[1,"747","10","Data Interoperability and Data Protection Legal Reform","· Enactment of Data Interoperability Law · Enactment of Data Protection and Privacy Law [e.g., GDPR] · Revision of Digital Security Act, 2018 to connect with independent law on data protection and privacy",""],[1,"748","10","Inter-Agency Working Group for Data Governance Legislation","Inter-agency working group for appropriate design and roadmap for UIS Enactment of Data Interoperability Law Enactment of Data protection and Privacy Law [ e.g., GDPR]",""]],"101":[[1,"557","19","Increased Budgetary Resources for MoEFCC Capacity Building","The government will progressively increase in its budget to reach the target of 0.1% of GDP by 2025 and 0.5% of GDP by 2041, so that it can improve capacity through better staffing, including technical professional staff, establishing a strong digital Management Information System (MIS) based on a data bank that gets regularly updated, and regular monitoring and evaluation of environmental compliance.","Ministry of Environment, Forest and Climate Change"],[1,"560","1","MoEFCC Capacity Strengthening and MIS Development","During the 8FYP, the Government will address the weak technical capacity of the MoEFCC to expedite the implementation of EFR.","MoEFCC | Forest Department | Department of Environment (DoE) | BCCT"],[1,"560","4","Compliance Improvement Initiative","Regular dialogue with the stakeholders including public hearings and participatory policy development will be undertaken to improve compliance and the",""],[1,"578","4","Forestry and Biodiversity Research Support Grants","The Bangladesh Forest Research Institute (BFRI), Bangladesh National Herbarium (BNH) and other institutions and universities involved in forestry research will be supported through regular research grants.",""],[1,"578","4","BFRI and BNH Institutional Capacity Upgrading","Institutional issues, such as staff shortages, IT infrastructure, research facilities, etc. faced by the BFRI and BNH shall be resolved at the earliest.",""],[1,"578","4","Forestry Sector Capacity Building Training Programme","The capacity building training programmes for the people involved in the forestry and diversity sector with emphasis of scientist of BFRI will be organised on a regular basis for developing human resources.",""],[1,"578","5","Bangladesh Rubber Board Institutional Capacity Strengthening","Bangladesh Rubber Board is planning to improve its institutional capacity through recruiting staffs, increasing modern equipment and laboratory facilities, strengthening the present manpower situation as well as human resource development.",""],[1,"578","6","International Rubber Sector Development and Policy Reform","Finding out, collect and cultivate the most suitable rubber breed for our country, formulating and implementing international standard rubber policy and actively participating in the competitive rubber market are some key objectives of these memberships.",""],[1,"578","6","Natural Latex Production Expansion","Bangladesh Rubber Board aims to increase the production of natural latex to self-sufficient level, thus meeting the local demand and save foreign currency.",""],[1,"579","3","Strengthening of the Lead Environmental Coordination Ministry","The capacity of this lead ministry will be sharply strengthened to play this coordinating role, to liaise with the international agenda for climate change and for monitoring progress.","Ministry of Environment, Forest and Climate Change"],[1,"579","3","Increased ADP Allocation for the Ministry of Environment, Forest and Climate Change","Accordingly, the Eighth Plan proposes a significant increase in the ADP allocations for the Ministry","Ministry of Environment, Forest and Climate Change"]],"102":[[1,"822","5","Gender-Responsive Training for Women Public Sector Employees","Training, orientation and knowledge enhancement opportunities should be provided to all women employed in the public sector.",""],[1,"822","5","Capacity Enhancement of Training Institutions on Gender","The capacity of the existing training institutions should be enhanced with faculty experienced and trained on gender.",""],[1,"822","5","Leadership and Decision-Making Training for Women Government Employees","Women government employees should be trained to be gender responsive, confident in leadership and decision making.",""],[1,"822","5","Women’s Confidence and Participation Support Initiative","Women's confidence should be enhanced through orientation, support and participation in extra curriculum activities.",""],[1,"827","3","Gender Capacity Building for Staff","Gender capacity building should also be prioritized.",""],[1,"828","1","Gender Strategy Capacity Building and Training Programme","Orientation of the policy makers, training and capacity building of staff in different institutions should continue and expand.",""],[1,"828","1","Gender Mainstreaming in Institutional Training Programmes","All training programmes of different institutions should integrate gender issues relevant to the sectors' or departments' operation and monitoring of the same.",""],[1,"828","1","Strengthening of PLAU and DWA Gender Monitoring Capacity","The capacity of Policy Leadership and Advocacy Unit (PLAU) and DWA should be enriched to ensure that the staff are able to monitor performance and can guide other agencies and ministries, if needed.",""],[1,"828","1","Gender Analysis in Foundation Training Courses","Gender analysis should be part of all foundation training courses.",""],[1,"828","1","Private Sector Gender Mainstreaming Initiative","Private sectors should be encouraged to incorporate gender perspectives in their operation and employ gender specialists, if needed.",""],[1,"828","1","Gender and Sectoral Operations Courses in Education Institutions","The education institutions should be encouraged to initiate additional courses to develop technical knowledge on how to address gender in different sectoral operations.",""],[1,"832","3","Gender Analysis Capacity-Building and Training Programme","It is important to increase the number of technically competent persons who can carry out gender analysis, assessment, planning, implementation and monitoring.",""],[1,"832","3","University Courses on Gender in Sectoral Operations","the education institutions should be encouraged to initiate additional courses to develop technical knowledge on how to address gender in different sectoral operations.",""],[1,"832","5","Gender Strategy Capacity Building Across Government and Sectors","Orientation of the policy makers and training and capacity building of existing staff contingent in different institutions has to be continued and expanded.",""],[1,"832","5","Gender Mainstreaming in Institutional Training Programmes","All training programmes of different institutions should integrate gender issues that are relevant to the sectors' or departments' operation with specific actions identified and monitoring of the same.",""],[1,"832","5","Private Sector Gender Mainstreaming and Specialist Recruitment","Private sectors should be encouraged to incorporate gender perspectives in their operation and employ gender specialists, if needed.",""]],"103":[[1,"827","1","Strengthening Institutional Mechanisms for Women's Advancement","The existing institutional mechanism for women's advancement needs to be more effective with accountability, capacity and authority.",""],[1,"827","1","Regular Guidance and Functioning of Gender Coordination Committees","Regular guidance from NCWCD, functioning of the committees and the Gender Focal Point mechanism should be ensured.",""],[1,"827","1","Assignment of Institutional Roles for Gender Equality","Other institutions should also be assigned specific roles in promoting gender equality to achieve SDG targets.",""],[1,"827","1","Regular Production of Sex-Disaggregated Statistics","Bangladesh Bureau of Statistics (BBS) should regularly provide sex disaggregated data synchronized with the national, sectoral and SDG indicators and the reporting needs for CEDAW, SDG, ICPD, CRC and such others.","Bangladesh Bureau of Statistics (BBS)"],[1,"827","1","Gender Equality Results Monitoring by IMED","IMED should be responsible to monitor gender equality results of projects/programmes including for programmes under revenue budget.","IMED"],[1,"827","1","Gender Budget Audit by the Office of the Auditor General","The Office of the Auditor General (OAG) should be given responsibility of auditing gender budget expenditure to assess the outcome.","The Office of the Auditor General (OAG)"],[1,"827","1","Gender Research and Labour Market Analysis Capacity","Similarly, Bangladesh Institute of Development Studies (BIDS) can be assigned for necessary gender research and BMET strengthened for analysis of labour markets.","Bangladesh Institute of Development Studies (BIDS) | BMET"],[1,"827","1","Strengthening Gender Analysis in Statistics Agencies","Other statistics generating organizations like Bangladesh Bureau of Educational Information and Statistics (BANBEIS), National Institute of Preventive and Social Medicine (NIPSOM) should also be strengthened to provide gender analysis of data generated.","Bangladesh Bureau of Educational Information and Statistics (BANBEIS) | National Institute of Preventive and Social Medicine (NIPSOM)"],[1,"827","1","Integration of National Action Plans into Annual Performance Agreements","The Annual Performance Agreements should integrate actions that are consistent with the National Action Plans and SDG targets.",""],[1,"827","2","Strengthening Institutional Capacity for Gender Equality and Women's Advancement","Capacity of the key institutions like the agencies under MoWCA including DWA and PLAU, IMED, BBS, OAG and Planning Commission should be strengthened in performing their roles as per mandate in design, review, implementation, and monitoring of gender equality and women's advancement related actions and results.","MoWCA | IMED | BBS | OAG | Planning Commission"],[1,"827","2","Enhanced Oversight and Monitoring Capacity for MoWCA","MoWCA's capacity should be strengthened for a robust oversight role and to uphold its position to monitor gender equality with allocation of adequate resources.","MoWCA"],[1,"827","2","Sex-Disaggregated Data Collection and Analysis System","BBS has to be assigned to ensure regular collection, collation and analysis of sex disaggregated data on different sectors as per agreed gender and SDG indicators.","BBS"],[1,"827","2","Capacity Building for Local Government Institutions and Implementing Agencies on Gender Mainstreaming","Capacity of LGIs and implementing agencies should be strengthened for gender mainstreaming.",""],[1,"827","3","Resource Allocation for Gender Equality Action Plans","Allocation for financial and human resources to implement the several action plans and their targets is to be ensured.",""],[1,"827","4","Institutionalization of Gender-Responsive Budgeting Results Assessment","Analysis and assessment of gender budget for result has to be institutionalized with a comprehensive assessment of utilization.",""],[1,"827","4","Monitoring of Local Government Women Development Forum Allocations","In addition, the allocation in LGIs for Women Development Forum for promoting gender equality should also be monitored for results.",""],[1,"827","4","Review of Local Government Fund Utilization Guidelines","The guidelines for utilization of local government fund should be reviewed, particularly to ensure specific allocation and their proper utilization for women and girls.",""],[1,"827","4","Technical Support and Training for GRB Implementation","It is necessary to ensure availability of sufficient technical support and training for effective implementation of GRB.",""],[1,"827","4","Gender Perspective Review of Completed Projects","Monitoring and review of the completed projects from gender perspectives should be introduced.",""],[1,"827","4","Capacity Building for Gender Focal Points","Capacity of gender focal points on gender budget analysis should be ensured.",""],[1,"827","4","Gender Auditing of Large Projects","Introduction of gender auditing of big projects will also strengthen the GRB initiative.",""],[1,"828","2","Gender Impact Monitoring Mechanism","The review of the 8th FYP and the SDGs should effectively incorporate monitoring of gender equality results.",""],[1,"828","2","IMED Gender Equality Progress Monitoring","The IMED monitoring system should integrate monitoring of progress of women's empowerment and gender based on project/ programme targets.",""],[1,"828","2","Institutionalized Gender-Responsive Budget Monitoring","Rigorous monitoring of GRB should be institutionalized with capacity enhancement across agencies, sectors and field level.",""],[1,"828","2","Gender Audit Oversight by the Office of the Auditor General","The Office of the Auditor General (OAG) should monitor expenditure and results in gender through the audit.","Office of the Auditor General (OAG)"],[1,"828","2","Transparent Budget Disclosure and Review Procedures","Transparent procedures at different levels should include open meetings, publicly available financial disclosure, and budget review.",""],[1,"828","3","Integration of Gender Indicators into National Monitoring Systems","At the national level all progress indicators of the government's performance should integrate gender indicators besides measuring growth, investment, deficit etc.",""],[1,"828","4","Gender Equality Accountability System","A system of accountability for the achievement of gender equality targets and results must be established.",""],[1,"828","5","Inclusive and Gender-Sensitive Citizen Accountability Mechanisms","The Government should ensure oversight and establish partnership for ensuring accountability.",""],[1,"831","2","Gender Equality Resource Mobilization","The available resource envelop for 8FYP would be reviewed, resource requirements to address gender equality objectives and targets should be estimated and additional resources should be sought, as needed.",""],[1,"831","3","Sex-Disaggregated Progress Reporting System","To ensure results from actions related to gender equality all reporting of national progress including those related to SDG agenda would be based on sex disaggregated data to allow a better understanding the progress in the area of gender equality and women's empowerment.",""],[1,"831","5","Strengthening Institutional Mechanism for Women's Advancement","The existing institutional mechanism for women's advancement will be made more effective with accountability, capacity and authority.",""],[1,"831","5","Regular Guidance and Committee Functioning for Women's Advancement","Regular guidance from NCWCD, functioning of the committees and the WID Focal Point mechanism would be ensured.",""],[1,"832","1","Strengthening the Commission for Gender Equality Action Design and Monitoring","Commission would be strengthened in performing their roles as per mandate in design, review, implementation, and monitoring of gender equality and women's advancement related actions and their results.",""],[1,"832","1","Reorienting the Ministry of Women and Children Affairs to an Oversight Role","MoWCA would be geared more towards an oversight role like other regulatory ministries with review of its mandate to promote its roles to monitor gender equality with allocation of adequate resources.","MoWCA"],[1,"832","1","Gender-Disaggregated Data Generation by BBS","The BBS will be tasked with generating gender disaggregated data synchronized with the national and sectoral indicators and the reporting needs for CEDAW, SDG and such others.","BBS"],[1,"832","1","Gender Equality Results Monitoring by IMED","IMED would have accountability to monitor gender equality results","IMED"],[1,"832","1","Auditing of Gender Budget Expenditure by the Office of the Auditor General","the Office of the Auditor General (OAG) should be given responsibility of auditing gender budget expenditure.","Office of the Auditor General (OAG)"],[1,"832","2","Resource Allocation for Gender Mainstreaming","It is therefore important to allocate both financial resources as per targets of each agency and projects and human resources in the institution with capacity development support.",""],[1,"832","2","National Action Plan Reference for Women's Empowerment Resource Allocation","The National Action Plan would be used as a reference point while allocating resources for women's empowerment and gender equality.",""],[1,"832","3","Strengthening of PLAU and DWA Monitoring Capacity","The capacity of PLAU and DWA should be enriched so that their staff are able to monitor performance and can guide other agencies and ministries, if needed.",""],[1,"832","4","Transparent Monitoring Mechanisms for Gender Equality and Gender Budget","Transparent monitoring mechanisms established and implemented to measure impact of public policies and programmes: The review of 8FYP programmes should incorporate monitoring of gender equality results.",""],[1,"833","1","Gender Equality Results Monitoring Framework","A compilation of defined gender equality results with indicators would be integrated in the plan document for all sectors for monitoring purpose.",""],[1,"833","1","National Gender Equality Indicator Set","At the national level, a list of gender equality indicators would be identified, agreed and monitored.",""],[1,"833","1","Gender-Disaggregated Poverty Assessment","The poverty assessment and income data would be gender disaggregated in all wealth groups so that women's poverty reduction is effectively measured.",""],[1,"833","2","Gender Equality Accountability Framework","Accountability for the achievement of gender equality targets and results must be ensured.",""],[1,"833","3","National Gender Equality Monitoring and Evaluation Framework","For establishing good monitoring and evaluation (M&E) mechanism, it is critical to have a list of agreed gender equality indicators at the national level for measuring the progress of gender equality.",""],[1,"833","3","Sectoral Key Performance Indicator Monitoring System","At the sectoral level, a few key performance indicators (KPI) in each sector would be identified and monitored.",""],[1,"833","3","Gender Equality Indicator Finalization by Planning Commission","The GED of the Planning Commission would finalize the indicators with support from sectoral ministries.","Planning Commission | sectoral ministries"],[1,"833","3","Stakeholder Information and Results Monitoring Arrangement","All relevant stakeholders working in the sector should be informed of the expected results and indicators so that they are also active in implementing actions and monitoring for those results.",""]],"104":[[1,"138","12","Treasury Bills and Bond Market Development","The development of the treasury bills and bond market will be keys to enhancing the transmission mechanism and effectiveness of monetary policy.",""],[1,"140","4","Treasury Bill Market Liberalization","The government can spur the development of the bond market by opening up the market for Treasury bills (T-bills) for private trading.",""],[1,"141","7","Capital Market Development Program II","the government undertook a substantial capital market development program -CMDPII -- with support from the ADB.",""],[1,"185","3","Sovereign Bond Financing for Large Infrastructure Projects","Access to international capital market to finance large infrastructure projects by issuing sovereign bonds may also be considered as a source of external financing for domestic public investment.",""],[1,"193","4","Diversification of Government Financing Sources","However, the government would need to diversify its sources of financing with proper mix of domestic and external financing, and on both fronts identify market based additional sources of financing.",""],[1,"193","4","Development of Long-Term Government Securities Market","On the domestic borrowing front, dependence on National Savings Schemes and short-term treasury bills should give way to long-term treasury bills and bonds, infrastructure bonds, etc. with proper secondary market and a well-developed yield curve.",""],[1,"193","5","External Financing Diversification Strategy","On the external front, the access to traditional concessional borrowing from official bilateral and multilateral sources should be increased and at the same time complemented with additional borrowings in the form of sovereign bonds of various maturities and other sources of financing.",""],[1,"193","5","Sovereign Bond Issuance","The government should try to establish its relations with the international capital market by launching its first sovereign bond soon because external and domestic conditions are favourable for such a launch.",""],[1,"193","5","Government Financing and Debt Management Strategy","These strategic transformations should be done on the basis of a comprehensive Government Financing and Debt Management Strategy to be prepared by the Debt Management Wing of the Ministry of Finance.","Ministry of Finance"],[1,"194","4","Fiscal Prudence and Debt Management Strategy","For the 8FYP, the debt strategy consists of maintaining fiscal prudence, with fiscal deficit stabilizing at around 5% of GDP after the initial rise to finance COVID-19 related expenses in the face of falling tax revenues.",""],[1,"194","4","Low-Cost Public Borrowing and Priority Investment Financing","Public borrowing will actively pursue reliance on low-cost options, use borrowed resources wisely on high-priority investments.",""],[1,"194","4","Debt Servicing Capacity Strengthening Measures","At the same time, efforts will be made to strengthen debt servicing capacity by expanding tax revenue and exports, and focus on accelerating GDP growth.",""],[1,"194","5","Shift Budget Financing Toward Lower-Cost Medium- and Long-Term Borrowing","Much of the increase is in external debt ratio as the financing of the budget deficit moves away from high-cost domestic saving certificates and bank borrowing towards lower-cost MLT borrowings.",""],[1,"195","9","8FYP Fiscal Framework for Debt Sustainability","This dramatic improvement emerges from the implementation of the 8FYP fiscal framework that calls for a 3.4 percentage points increase in the tax to GDP ratio over the tax rate in FY2019 and a substitution of high cost domestic borrowing from national saving certificate lower-cost domestic borrowings and greater reliance on low-cost foreign MLT loans",""],[1,"196","1","Prudent External Borrowing and Concessional Financing Strategy","The external financing strategy under the Plan will essentially maintain the current strategy of prudent external borrowing on best possible terms with maximum utilization of concessional official bilateral and multilateral borrowing.",""],[1,"196","1","Concessional Financing for Major Infrastructure Projects","Many of the infrastructure projects in the transport and energy sector (like Matarbari Power Hub; Dhaka Metro Rail; Karnaphuli River Tunnel etc.) can be financed from concessional borrowing.",""],[1,"196","1","Acceleration of Donor-Funded Project Implementation","There is also scope for accelerating the pace of donor funded project implementation and reduce the large aid pipeline which currently stands at more than $29 billion (about 6 years of aid utilization).",""],[1,"196","2","External Financing Diversification Strategy","The external financing strategy under the Plan would also entail broadening of the sources of external financing, creating greater scope for private investors to secure external financing on better terms through reduced country/sovereign risk, and continued reliance on official bilateral and multilateral sources for financing large public sector projects or achieving social sector objectives under the Plan.",""],[1,"196","3","Domestic Debt Strategy Reform","the domestic debt strategy for the 8FYP will continue to ensure that the government's borrowing requirements are consistent with inflation targets and allocation of credit to private sector.",""],[1,"196","3","Reduction of High-Cost Domestic Public Borrowing","Efforts will also be made to reduce the high cost of domestic public borrowing in Bangladesh.",""],[1,"196","3","Shift to Market-Based Domestic Borrowing Instruments","the excessive dependence on non-bank borrowing in the form of issuing non-tradable old-fashioned national Savings Certificates at very high cost would give way to market-based instruments and interest rate savings.",""],[1,"196","3","Domestic Interest Payment Containment","Efforts will be made under the Eighth Plan to slow down the growth of domestic interest payments by reducing dependence on high cost borrowing.",""],[1,"196","4","Debt Management Reform","Accordingly, debt management reforms will be undertaken to make public borrowing cheaper and to help develop domestic bond market.",""],[1,"196","4","Rationalization of National Savings Instrument Interest Rates","The Government will also continue to keep rationalizing the interest rate structure of national savings instruments in line with interest rate developments in the money/bond market.",""],[1,"201","2","Rationalization of Domestic Financing Sources and Borrowing Costs","The sources of domestic financing and the interest rates paid on non-bank borrowing would need to be rationalized with the developments in the market-based interest rate structure",""],[1,"201","2","Domestic Debt Diversification and Bond Market Development","Development of domestic bond market with proper development of the regulatory regime and the demand and supply side of the domestic bond market will be important for diversifying the domestic financing sources.",""]],"105":[[1,"663","2","Human Resources Information System Operationalization","operationalization of the Human Resources Information System (HRIS) for evidence-based decision","MoHFW"],[1,"663","2","Health and Family Planning Organogram Review and Update","The organograms of all health and family planning agencies along with their facilities will be reviewed and updated for provision of quality HPN services",""],[1,"663","4","Health Sector Stewardship Strengthening","the stewardship role and capacity of the MoHFW will further be strengthened through improved monitoring of quality of care and safety of patients in both public and private sectors.","MoHFW"],[1,"663","4","Periodic Facility Inspection System","DGHS will develop a periodic inspection system of facilities and services, with necessary support, on a regular basis at all levels and act upon the findings to improve client satisfaction.","DGHS"],[1,"663","5","Health Sector Regulatory Capacity Strengthening","In the 8FYP, HSD will continue to update the mandates, structures and build capacity of the various national regulatory bodies to increase their effectiveness and functionality and review structure and capacity of the HSD Directorates to strengthen supervision and enhance institutional management.","HSD"],[1,"663","5","NGO and Private Sector Regulatory Partnership","HSD also intends to partner with NGOs and private sector for strengthening existing regulatory mechanisms and creating new ones.","HSD"],[1,"664","2","Implementation of the Gender Equity Strategy in Health Services","The existing Gender Equity Strategy of HSD are being implemented to overcome barriers of various gender related issues including human resource management at facility level, housing, promotion for women workforce, etc.",""],[1,"664","2","Decentralized and Funded Regional Health Service Adaptation Measures","The 8FYP will adopt specific measures and adjustments in approaches and services to ensure that the needs of the various regions and groups are identified, analyzed and appropriate measures taken through decentralizing authority and allocating special funds.","MoHFW"],[1,"664","2","Mainstreaming Voice and Accountability in Health Governance","Voice and accountability mechanisms will be mainstreamed into the governance and stewardship functions of the overall health program.",""],[1,"664","2","Local Health Accountability Mechanism","A local level accountability mechanism will be developed in participation with the community people and local NGOS to improve utilization of health services by the local communities and the disadvantaged groups.",""],[1,"664","4","NGO Partnership for Health Service Delivery","Building and strengthening linkages with the NGOs will be an approach to complement government efforts in increasing access of the poor, the disadvantaged and the hard-to-reach populations to HPN services.",""],[1,"665","1","Health Sector Public-Private Partnership Expansion","The PPP in service delivery and in the areas of medical and allied education will be further expanded and strengthened during the 8FYP with effective regulatory mechanisms.",""],[1,"665","3","Health Sector Coordination and Collaboration Platform Strengthening","During the 8FYP, efforts will be made to further improve upon existing platforms of coordination between MoHFW and relevant stakeholders including the private sector and explore feasible new modes for maximization of available resources to ensure equity.","MoHFW"],[1,"665","3","Urban and Ethnic Minority Health Coordination Arrangements","Key areas of such coordination and collaboration would include - urban health (MoLGRDC) and ethnic minority health (MoCHTA) for resource sharing, program planning, implementation and review;","MoLGRDC | MoCHTA"],[1,"665","3","Parallel Project Coordination to Avoid Duplication","parallel projects (both GoB and DP) to avoid duplication and develop complementarities;",""],[1,"665","3","NGO and Private Sector Facility Management and Service Delivery","NGO/private sector for management/operation of non-functional facilities and/or providing services in hard-to-reach areas or for exploring feasibility of new services/technology;",""],[1,"665","3","Community and Local Government Oversight of Health Facilities","community, public representatives and local government's involvement in augmenting resources, management and oversight of service facilities in their locality;",""],[1,"665","3","Multi-sectoral Health Outcomes Coordination","The 8FYP will also put increased focus on establishing stronger coordination and collaboration among multiple sectors affecting health outcomes (e.g. malnutrition, NCDs);",""],[1,"666","1","Health Service Harmonization for More Effective Delivery","Operationalize harmonization of services of the service providers (DGHS, DGFP, DGNM) towards a more effective and efficient service delivery.",""],[1,"666","2","Five-Year Training Plan for Budgeting and Planning Skills","Enhance capacity for evidence -, need- and result-based budgeting and planning through development of a five-year training plan for skill development training of the key workforce.",""],[1,"666","4","Project Rationalization and Risk Pooling for Universal Health Coverage","Reduce and rationalize projects outside the SWAp Program and establish risk pooling and purchasing mechanism towards UHC.",""],[1,"666","10","Procurement Management Rationalization","Rationalize procurement management.",""],[1,"668","9","HED Reorganization and Capacity Strengthening","Therefore, HED needs to be reorganized during the 8FYP.",""]],"106":[[1,"666","11","Health Sector Monitoring and Review Mechanisms","MoHFW through the two divisions viz., HSD and MEFWD has been monitoring progress of regular programmes and other project activities in line with government's existing monitoring systems.","MoHFW | HSD | MEFWD"],[1,"666","11","Inter-Ministerial Review Committees for Multi-Sector Health Issues","Besides, there are committees to review OP/Project Implementation, inter- ministerial committees for reviewing multi-sector issues like nutrition, urban health, food safety, etc. mechanisms are also regularly followed.",""],[1,"666","11","Health Partnership Monitoring Platforms","In addition, as the HPN sector program is also financed by a large number of DPs, well-tested platforms of monitoring consisting of GOB and DP representations, such as Local Consultative Group on Health, and various Task Groups and the Steering Committees will be continued with focus on improving results from specific HPN services and their supporting health systems.",""],[1,"666","12","Monitoring and Evaluation System Strengthening","Besides, a number of activities to support capacity building, streamlining, and scaling up of M&E systems are being implemented during the 7FYP period through the financing from 4th HPNSP.",""],[1,"666","12","Program Implementation Reporting and Review Mechanisms","development of six-monthly program implementation report (SmPR), annual program implementation report (APIR) internally and annual program review (APR) by independent review team (IRT) to monitor progress of OP implementation and sector performance; tracking of DLI progress through DLI Monitoring Committee, etc. institutional mechanisms along with capacity building of relevant staff will continue to be pursued during the 8FYP period as well.",""],[1,"668","6","Facilities, Demography, and Health Survey and Research Dissemination","Conduct surveys on facilities, demography & health, etc., research and studies and disseminate the findings.",""],[1,"670","8","Nutrition-Sensitive Monitoring and Evaluation System","Monitoring & evaluation systems include nutrition relevant indicators",""],[1,"672","2","Nutrition Monitoring, Evaluation and Research Strengthening","Strengthen monitoring, evaluation and research to generate evidence to inform policy decisions by improving interoperability of routine information management systems, surveys, assessments and surveillance, establish feedback mechanisms, and closely monitor provision and utilization of essential nutrition services with innovative approaches to understand the level of sustainability and accountability in terms of equity, access, coverage and quality, to generate evidence for informed policy decisions.",""]],"107":[[1,"178","2","Land Administration and Land Market Reform","The 8FYP will strengthen the land administration regime and related land market through a range of institutional, regulatory, and fiscal policy reforms.",""],[1,"181","2","Modern Property Tax Introduction and Local Government Assignment","Moreover, the introduction of a modern property tax and assigning this to the local governments can be a substantial boost for their fiscal autonomy while providing fiscal resources.",""],[1,"191","6","Property Tax System Reform for Local Government Financing","By end of FY2022, introduce a proper system of property taxes with revenues earmarked for local governments",""],[1,"236","3","E-Mutation Land Administration System","The e-mutation that started in July 2019 all over the country except three districts of hill tracts is a major step in restructuring the land sector; this will ensure more accountability and transparency on the part of administration.",""],[1,"236","3","Deed Registration Digitalization","The Government is also presently undertaking Deed Registration Digitalization in 3 Districts and 5 sub-registry offices - which is expected to reduce the mismanagement of documents and disputes over the ownership of land.",""],[1,"253","5","Land Management Digitization","Land record digitization will be completed so that it is available to the three nodal offices: (i) land registration, (ii) Assistant Commissioner of land (ii) Deputy Commissioner of districts.",""],[1,"253","5","One-Stop Land Service Delivery System","Moreover, a one-stop service delivery system needs to be introduced for better public service delivery.",""],[1,"254","1","E-Registration and Digital Land Registration System","The Government will continue the process of ensuring that land ownership is managed transparently and fairly.",""],[1,"254","2","Improved Coordination for Land Administration E-Services","To ensure efficient and effective delivery to land- administration-related e-services, the coordination between Ministry of Land (MoL) and Ministry of Law, Justice and Parliamentary Affairs (MoLJPA) will be improved, both at the national and at the field level.","Ministry of Land (MoL) | Ministry of Law, Justice and Parliamentary Affairs (MoLJPA)"],[1,"254","2","Capacity-Building Programme for Land Administration Staff","Capacity-building programmes need to be conducted to improve the skills of staff in the office of the Assistant Commissioner (Land).",""],[1,"254","2","Regular Monitoring and Reporting of Land Offices","Regular monitoring of the work of land offices along with regular publication of monitoring reports will be ensured.",""],[1,"254","2","Institutional Strengthening for Land Administration Authorities","The authorities, involved with land administration, will be strengthened with adequate staff, financial resources and logistical support.",""],[1,"370","2","Automation of Land Records and Transfers","Automation of land records and transfers will further reduce the associated transaction costs and anomalies.",""],[1,"370","2","Land Management Project","Ministry of Land is implementing 'Automation of Land Management Project'","Ministry of Land"],[1,"370","2","Capacity Development for Digital Land Survey","Ministry of Land is implementing 'Capacity Development of Land Records and Surveys to Perform Digital Survey Project' in this regard.","Ministry of Land"],[1,"370","4","Comprehensive Land Use Planning","A comprehensive land use planning through integration of economic, ecological, social and cultural values in production will be given priority.",""],[1,"370","4","Soil and Water Conservation, Land Development, Drainage, Flood Control, and Reclamation Programme","The 8th plan will broaden emphasis on soil and water conservation, land development, drainage and flood control, and reclamation programmes.",""],[1,"370","4","Crop Zoning-Based Production Management","Land use planning will be promoted and production programmes will be managed based on crop zoning.",""]],"108":[[1,"238","3","City Governance Project","The Government is presently implementing numerous projects to improve the state of governance in urban local government.","LGD"],[1,"238","3","Capacity Development for City Corporation (C4C)","The Government has also undertaken a project for Capacity Development for City Corporation (C4C), which has the following objectives: (i) a medium to long-term strategy for improvements in governance is developed; (ii) a Plan-Do-Check-Action cycle of administrative improvement activities in alignment with the strategy is established; (iii) an appropriate tax assessment and collection procedures are established, and tax collection is conducted in a fair manner; (iv) a procedure of recurrent expenditure planning according to revenue is established.",""],[1,"238","3","National Strategy for Paurashava Governance Improvement","Furthermore, for improving urban management and facilitating governance improvements in Paurashavas, the Government has articulated the National Strategy for Paurashava Governance Improvement (2016-2025).",""],[1,"238","3","Upazila Parishad and City Corporation Governance Improvement Strategies","The LGD has also adopted two essential strategy documents-Mid and Long-Term Strategy for Upazila Parishad Governance Improvement and Strategy for Governance Improvement of City Corporations (SGICC), 2020-2030, which will offer strategies and policy alterations that can help improve the governance performance in both rural and urban local government bodies.","LGD"],[1,"238","4","Local Government and Rural Development Sector Strategy Paper","Under the 7FYP, the Government prepared the \"Local Government and Rural Development Sector Strategy Paper (LGRD SSP)\", which is a planning tool intended to help translate national goals and priorities outlined in the 7FYP into sector strategies and objectives.",""],[1,"245","1","Union Parishad Capacity Strengthening","The Government will increase the capacities of the Union Parishads (UP) that operate as a key institutional arrangement guiding arbitration among people within their communities.",""],[1,"252","3","Local Government Institution Reform Programme","The Government of Bangladesh recognizes the need of improved governance in the local government administration to take up the decentralization agenda, and intends to undertake a wide array of initiatives under the 8FYP.",""],[1,"254","5","Increased Resource Allocation for Governance-Related Institutions","The Government will mobilize more resources to increase ADP allocation to justice institutions, public sector capacity development, digitization and automation of public sector organizations, ACC, NBR and PSC's operations, LGIs for effective decentralization, reform of the banking sector and capital markets.",""],[1,"254","5","Timely Disbursement and Utilization of ADP Project Funds","Moreover, it will take measures to ensure that the financial resources earmarked for the ADP projects are disbursed and utilized in a timely manner.",""],[1,"346","24","Civil Servant Training Programme Strengthening","Strengthen training programmes for civil servants.",""],[1,"347","2","Local Government Staff Capacity-Building Training Programmes","Institute training programmes to strengthen capacity of local government staff.",""],[1,"349","4","Devolution of Health and Education Services to Local Governments","a key reform is the devolution of health and education services to the local governments.",""],[1,"501","3","Local Government Fiscal Empowerment Reform","Parliament shall, by law, confer powers on the local government bodies to impose taxes for local purposes, to prepare their budgets and to maintain funds",""],[1,"502","16","Fiscal Transfer Institutionalization","Institutionalizing fiscal transfer",""],[1,"511","6","Formula-Based Union Parishad Transfer Allocation","Transfers to UPs are now made on a formula basis that includes population and performance.",""],[1,"516","3","Clarification of Local Government and Regional Development Institution Functions","Define functions of LGIs and RDIs at all levels and clarify roles and responsibilities between sectoral ministries / agencies and LGIs for service delivery to the people",""],[1,"516","4","Guidelines for Linking Local and National Development Plans","Update guidelines for linking local development plan with the national development plan",""],[1,"516","5","Capacity Strengthening for Local and Regional Development Institutions","Strengthen capacity of LGIs, RDIs and associated agencies",""],[1,"516","6","Local Level Participation in LGI Planning and Monitoring","Ensure local level participation in planning and monitoring the functions of LGIs",""],[1,"516","7","Performance-Based Incentive System for Local Government Institutions","Promote the performance- based incentive system for the LGIs",""],[1,"516","8","Local Development Action Research and Dissemination","Conduct action research on local development and disseminate results",""],[1,"516","9","Women's Empowerment in Local and Regional Development Institutions","Promote women's empowerment in the LGIs and RDIs",""],[1,"516","13","E-Governance System and Services Improvement","Improve e-governance system and services",""],[1,"516","16","Reform of National Transfers to Local Government Institutions","Reform national transfers to LGIs by making them criteria base, transparent and predictable",""],[1,"516","17","Local Government Resource Mobilization Strengthening","Sharply strengthen LGI resource mobilization focused on property taxes and cost recovery of services",""],[1,"517","1","Local Government Institution Governance Reform","the Government will prioritize the implementation of three strategic documents under the FYP",""],[1,"517","4","Upazila Parishad Governance Improvement Strategy","Mid and Long-Term Strategy for Upazila Parishad Governance Improvement: This strategy document aims to clarify the basic policy directions to achieve efficient and accountable Upazila Parishads (UP).",""],[1,"518","3","Sharique Local Governance Capacity-Building Project","The Sharique project started in 2006 which was supported by the Swiss Agency for Development and Cooperation (SDC) and implemented by HELVETAS Swiss Intercooperation.",""],[1,"518","5","Proactive Public Integration Policies for Excluded Groups","No group will be excluded from facilities and proactive public integration policies will be implemented for the impoverished, religious minorities, disadvantaged groups, women, etc.",""],[1,"518","6","Entitlements Distribution and Public Procurement Reform","Proper distribution of entitlements and rigorous public procurement practices are part of the agenda.",""],[1,"518","7","Accountability and Right-to-Information Mechanism","People should have right to information, be able to give recommendation/feedback on services they receive and bring forth changes, if necessary.",""],[1,"518","7","Performance Reward and Abuse Sanction System","The controlling agencies will reward those who perform well and punish those who abuse power.",""],[1,"518","9","Local Government Information Transparency Measures","Public should obtain information from the LGIs about decisions they take and changes they plan on implementing.",""],[1,"518","11","Inclusive and Accountable Local Governance Reform Package","Steps towards inclusive and accountable local governance have been planned in five major steps and two transversal elements: (i) Awareness raising and assessing governance; (ii) Strengthening coordination structures; (iii) Opening up participatory spaces; (iv) Integrated planning; (v) Budgeting and finance management; and (vi) Gender equality and pro-poor governance.",""],[1,"518","11","Citizen Information and Accountability Measures for Local Governance","Revealing information to the citizens and owning up for any misuse of power by the concerned officials are the main elements of enforcing effective local governance practices.",""],[1,"519","3","National Integrity Strategy Implementation and Expansion","The Government has been actively promoting the NIS as a part of strengthening transparency and accountability of both State and non-state organizations.","Cabinet Division"],[1,"519","3","Accountability Mechanisms Strengthening Package","Therefore, the Cabinet Division has taken activities for strengthening the mechanisms of accountability, including the Citizen's Charter, Grievance Redressal System (GRS), Annual Performance Agreement (APA), Public Hearing, One Stop Service Centres, Small Improvement Program, Right to Information (RTI), e-Governance and e-service delivery.","Cabinet Division"],[1,"519","3","Ethics Committees and Integrity Focal Points","During the 7FYP, the Cabinet Division has been promoting the NIS mainly to the Ministries/Division and State Institutions mentioned in the Strategy, by forming Ethic Committees, assigning Integrity Focal Points, formulating and implementing NIS work-plans led by quarterly monitoring and annual evaluations.","Cabinet Division"],[1,"519","3","Local-Level National Integrity Strategy Expansion","However, this division has also started expanding the NIS to the local levels by issuing the guidelines for departments/attached bodies and regional/field level offices to formulate and implement the NIS work-plans.","Cabinet Division"],[1,"519","4","National Integrity Strategy Localization and Support Project Phase II","the Cabinet Division during 8FYP will promote localization of the NIS, with central roles of the Local Government Institutions (LGIs).","Cabinet Division"],[1,"519","4","Upazila Ethics Committees for NIS Work-Plan Implementation","Upazila Ethic Committees, headed by the Upazila Nirbahi Officers (UNO) and with Chairperson, Upazila Parishad as advisor, will develop, implement and monitor the progress of NIS work-plan.",""],[1,"519","4","Expanded NIS Promotion in State and Non-State Institutions","there are plans to strengthen the promotion and practice of the NIS in other state and non-state institutions.",""],[1,"520","2","Routine Review and Update of Local Government Acts","Thus, these laws will be routinely evaluated and updated.",""],[1,"520","3","Local Government Development Planning and Budget Linkage","each tier of the LGIs is mandated to prepare annual and/or multi-year development plans, to which the allocation of budgets should be well linked.",""],[1,"520","3","Improved Predictability of ADP Grant Transfers","Predictability of the amount and timing of the transfer of Annual Development Programme (ADP) grants will be improved, considering the due process of preparing annual budgets.",""],[1,"520","3","Transparent and Accountable Annual Development Plan Budget Process","the preparation, execution and reporting of Annual Development Plans/Budgets will be undertaken through a more transparent and accountable process for the respective citizens.",""],[1,"520","3","Upazila Parishad Coordination with Transferred Line Departments","For the Upazila Parishads, adequate coordination with Transferred Line Departments will be prioritized as it is essential for preparing comprehensive development plans.",""],[1,"520","4","Local Government Revenue Mobilization Strengthening","Administrative capacity for the collection of taxes will be improved, especially for holding tax, which is the major source of own revenue for the LGIs.",""],[1,"520","4","Fiscal Decentralization Reform for Local Governments","There is a large potential to increase domestic resource mobilization through fiscal decentralization which would involve more revenue-raising and expenditure authority divested to the LGIs.",""],[1,"520","4","Review of Local Government Resource Transfer Mechanisms","The existing resource transfer mechanism from the budget through the ministries to the local government will be reviewed along with the block resource transfer formula to local government, including the municipalities and city corporations taking into account, equity and efficiency considerations.",""],[1,"520","4","Review of Reverse Revenue Flow Arrangements","The reverse flow-of revenue proceeds from the municipal/city corporation, upazila and union levels to higher levels of the LGI and government system also needs serious review.",""],[1,"520","5","Local Government Revenue Sharing Mechanism Reform","A new formula for revenue sharing mechanism will be devised, which incentivizes the LGIs to increase revenue mobilization and make them more vibrant at the local level in serving local residents.",""],[1,"520","5","LGI Public Financial Management Capacity Strengthening","The recommended measures also require strengthening the capacity of LGIs in PFM in particular.",""],[1,"520","5","LGI Staffing Rationalization and Skills Upgrading","They also require rationalizing and selective filling of the large number of existing vacancies and selective increases in staff strength to address the mismatch between the needed skills and existing skills among staff.",""],[1,"520","5","LGI Fiscal and Financial Management Training Programme","Of critical importance also, is the training and up gradation of fiscal and financial management capacity, starting with basic book-keeping, financial reporting, and audit management practices of existing LGI staff.",""],[1,"520","5","Decentralized LGI Systems Upgrade","Finally, upgrading the LGI systems to operate in a stronger decentralized system will be accompanied by measure to ensure responsiveness, public participation, partnership with NGOs and community-based organizations, while maintaining high standards of transparency and accountability.",""],[1,"521","1","Increase Inter-Governmental Fiscal Transfers to Local Government Institutions","more allocation of ADP for the LGIs will be directed to implement public investment projects - so that they can directly manage their own planning and budgeting systems.",""],[1,"521","1","Introduce a Fiscal Formula for Upazila ADP Allocation","the Government will put in place a fiscal formula, which will partially determine the amount of ADP an Upazila receives as basic ADP on the basis of its socio-economic needs by taking into consideration key socio-economic factors such as population, area, remoteness and poverty rate, etc.",""],[1,"521","1","Performance-Based ADP Allocation System","a share of the ADP will be shaped by the fiscal and developmental performance of an Upazila Administration and will be institutionalized as Performance Based ADP.",""],[1,"521","2","PFM Staffing and IT Capacity Upgrade for Local Governments","Hence, GoB will ensure that each UZP and municipality will have one budget officer, one trained financial management specialist, one trained IT staff, and computer facilities.",""],[1,"521","3","Strengthening LGD Supervision and Monitoring Capacity","As such, monitoring and supervision capacities of LGD will be substantially strengthened.",""],[1,"521","4","Local Government Budget Training and Monitoring System","LGI officials will be trained and mandated to use the budget document to achieve development objectives.",""],[1,"521","5","Multi-Year Budget Formulation","A multi-year budget approach, as opposed to an annual budget, will be formulated under the 8th Plan period in order to more efficiently assess future revenues and expenditures and the stability or instability related to these budget items.",""],[1,"521","6","Expansion of Local Government Taxation Authority","The Government will facilitate an expansion of taxing power that allows local governments to decide how and how much to tax in order to best match their community's demographics, budget and political realities.",""],[1,"521","6","Computerized Property Taxation System","The top priority is to strengthen the system of property taxation through proper and computerized land record, proper land and property valuation and sensible tax rates that allow some minimum revenue mobilization.",""],[1,"521","7","Tax Administration Improvement and Revenue Collection Simplification","The Government will ensure improvements in tax administration including proper assessments, avoiding harassment of citizens, effective consultation with taxpayers and community leaders to develop business partnership, and property accounting and record keeping of revenues.",""],[1,"521","8","IBAS++ Accounting Expansion to Local Government Institutions","The Government will consider the extension and adoption of IBAS++ in the LGIs during the 8FYP.",""],[1,"522","1","Strengthening of Local Government Institution Audits","Audit of LGI operations will be strengthened in meaningful and practical ways.",""],[1,"522","2","Local Revenue and Resource Mobilization Enhancement","Enhance mobilization of local revenue and resources",""],[1,"522","4","Development Programme Coordination, Implementation, and Monitoring","Ensure better coordination in planning, implementation and monitoring of development programmes",""],[1,"522","5","Local Government Coordination and Linkage Strengthening","Improve both horizontal and vertical coordination and linkages among LGIs",""],[1,"522","6","Resource Mobilization and Allocation Policy","Ensure appropriate policy for adequate resource mobilization and allocation.",""],[1,"524","17","Coordination Mechanism for My Village-My Town Evaluation","Appropriate coordination between UPZs/UPs and concerned ministry to evaluate activities under My Village-My Town;",""],[1,"534","4","Donor Coordination for Rural and Urban Development","The Ministry of LGRD&C will lead the donor coordination on behalf of the major government stakeholders: LGD and RDCD, Planning Commission, Finance Division, Ministry of Agriculture, Road Transport and Highways Division and the Ministry of Commerce.","Ministry of LGRD&C | LGD | RDCD | Planning Commission | Finance Division | Ministry of Agriculture | Road Transport and Highways Division | Ministry of Commerce"],[1,"534","4","Local Government and Sector Coordination for Rural Development","Given the involvement of MoLGRD&C in rural development, rural roads, rural CMSEs and CHT rural infrastructure, the MoLGRD&C departments will ensure proper coordination with the concerned line ministries to ensure donor coordination and maximize the support benefits.","MoLGRD&C"],[1,"535","1","Local Government Own-Source Revenue Mobilization Reform","a key objective of the 8FYP is to strengthen own resource mobilization from property taxes and cost recovery for all LGIs, especially the urban-based LGIs",""]],"109":[[1,"50","2","Economic Stimulus Packages for Income Protection and Recovery","On the economic front, the government has adopted a series economic stimulus packages estimated at Taka 1196.4 billion (4.3% of GDP) with a view to protecting the income of the poor and vulnerable and helping the revival of economic activities.",""],[1,"51","4","Corrective Policy Measures for Job Creation Slowdown","the slowdown in the rate of job creation in manufacturing, construction and modern services need stronger monitoring with corrective policy measures in the 8FYP",""],[1,"53","4","Job Creation Priority","Job creation accordingly will be a top priority of the 8FYP.",""],[1,"57","2","Prudent Macroeconomic Management","The 8th Plan will continue the emphasis on prudent macroeconomic management.",""],[1,"57","2","Inflation Reduction Policy","the objective of higher growth will be balanced with efforts to further reduce inflation to an average of 5.0% during the plan period.",""],[1,"57","2","Fiscal Prudence Restoration","fiscal prudence will be restored by increasing tax revenues to bring back the fiscal deficit to around 5% of GDP by FY2023.",""],[1,"57","3","Public Investment Expansion for Growth Support","Public investment will also need to increase by an additional 1.2% of GDP to support growth through investments in infrastructure and human capital.",""],[1,"58","2","Public Investment Expansion","Public investment will grow from 8% of GDP in FY2019 to 9.2% of GDP by FY2025",""],[1,"58","2","Public Investment Program Financing","the total size of the 8FYP Public Investment Program (PIP) will be Tk. 16.1 trillion in FY2021 prices.",""],[1,"58","2","Annual Development Programme Allocation","Of this, some Tk. 11.9 trillion will be funded through the Annual Development Programme (ADP).",""],[1,"58","2","Fast-Tracking Nationally Important Projects","The main focus of the ADP will be to sharply improve and strengthen health infrastructure, to build the social protection system, alleviate infrastructure constraints to private investment and GDP growth by fast tracking nationally important projects, and implement the BDP2100.",""],[1,"58","3","Transformational Infrastructure Project Completion","in addition to completing the ongoing transformational infrastructure projects",""],[1,"58","4","Annual Budget and ADP Synchronization for Plan Implementation","Annual Budget and ADP will be synchronized to use them as tools for achieving the objectives of the 8FYP.",""],[1,"95","6","COVID-19 Socioeconomic Mitigation Work Plan","To mitigate the adverse socioeconomic impact of 'global pandemic' from COVID-19, the Government of Bangladesh has adopted a Work Plan with four major strategic programmes to be implemented in immediate, short-term and medium-term span.",""],[1,"96","1","Public Employment-Generating Expenditure and Luxury Spending Restraint","Increased public expenditure with a target to create jobs in both formal and informal sectors.",""],[1,"96","4","Monetary Liquidity Support Measures","Increase money supply to maintain liquidity of the economy so that the financial shock from the pandemic can be absorbed and day to day businesses can be operated smoothly.","Bangladesh Bank (BB)"],[1,"99","1","Job Creation Priority under the 8FYP","Job creation accordingly will be a top priority of the 8FYP.",""],[1,"111","1","COVID-19 Economic Recovery Support and Monitoring","The government will continue to monitor the COVID-9 situation and provide continuous support to protect the recovery of economic activities as already seen in the first six months.",""],[1,"111","1","Additional Economic Stabilization Policies","Additional policies will be taken as necessary to ensure that the economy remains buoyant and economic recovery and growth momentum remains on track as projected in the PP2041 and reflected in Table 2.7.",""],[1,"113","1","Inclusive Growth and Pro-Poor Job Creation Strategy","the 8th Five Year Plan focuses on strategizing inclusive growth.",""],[1,"113","2","Employment-Intensive Growth and Job Creation Measures","the 8FYP will seek to take policy measures that increase the employment impact of growth.",""],[1,"125","1","Monetary, Fiscal, Exchange Rate, Trade and Investment Climate Reforms","For the private sector monetary, fiscal, exchange rate, trade and investment climate reforms are important determinants of the quality and efficiency of private investment.",""],[1,"127","2","Implementation of Tax Reforms","This was possible owing the implementation of some important tax reforms that allowed the tax to GDP ratio to grow from 8% of GDP in FY11 to 9.5% of GDP in FY2015.",""],[1,"127","2","Long-Term Fiscal Target and Fiscal Policy Framework","In recognition of this, the Perspective Plan 2041 has developed a long-term fiscal target and associated fiscal policy framework.",""],[1,"127","2","8FYP Medium-Term Fiscal Policy Framework","The 8FYP medium- term fiscal policy framework is based on the implementation of PP2041 fiscal policy framework.",""],[1,"129","1","Financial Savings Incentive Policy","Government will encourage financial savings by offering real positive interest rates to the savers.",""],[1,"129","1","Revenue Mobilization Efforts","A part of the increased national savings would also come from the public sector through increased revenue mobilization efforts.",""],[1,"146","9","Prudent Macroeconomic Management and Economic Reform Acceleration","The Government will remain vigilant about the emerging external and domestic risks, and will continue to pursue prudent macroeconomic management and accelerate the pace of economic reforms as envisaged under the Plan.",""],[1,"147","1","Domestic Resource Mobilization for Plan Financing","Mobilization of resources, particularly with greater focus on sustainable increase in NBR tax revenue, will be essential for financing the Plan as discussed in Chapter 5 of this part of the plan document.","NBR"],[1,"180","15","Fiscal Policy Strategy to Mobilize Additional Social Sector Funding","A closer look will suggest that a strategy to mobilize this additional funding is certainly within the reach of public policy and is incorporated in the 8FYP fiscal policy discussed in greater detail in chapter 5.",""],[1,"184","2","Annual Budget and ADP Synchronization for Plan Implementation","Annual Budget and ADP will be synchronized to use them as tools for achieving the objectives of the 8FYP.",""],[1,"184","2","Tax Policy and Administration Reform and Modernization","Financing of this National Plan will require increased private and public sector savings, rapid income growth for the private sector and increased revenue mobilization through reform and modernization of tax policy and tax administration.",""],[1,"185","3","Public Investment Financing Plan","The Eighth Plan will build on the gains made so far with a view to allocating Tk.16.1 trillion in constant FY21 prices of public investment, accounting for 25.3% of total investment in the economy.",""],[1,"185","3","Domestic Public Investment Financing through Savings and Borrowing","Of the total public sector investment, Tk. 12.8 trillion will be funded by domestic resources (80%), comprising of public savings (36%) and domestic bank and non-bank borrowings (44%)",""],[1,"185","3","External Financing for Public Sector Development Spending","External financing, primarily in the form of concessional loans from official multilateral and bilateral sources will continue to supplement the public sector development spending, contributing on a net basis to 20% of the public investment financing.",""],[1,"185","4","Fiscal Policy Reform and Revenue Mobilization Effort","a concerted fiscal policy reform effort will be undertaken to arrest the downward trend of revenue and allow for a substantial expansion in the tax to GDP ratio.",""],[1,"185","4","Restoration of the Public Expenditure Programme","the higher revenue mobilization will provide a basis for restoring the public expenditure programme to address the key development priorities of the 8FYP.",""],[1,"185","4","Fiscal Deficit Restoration to Medium-Term Target","this will be overcome swiftly and restored to the 5% of GDP level based on tax revenue mobilization and continued commitment to prudent fiscal policy management.",""],[1,"187","6","Fiscal Revenue Mobilization Framework","The fiscal framework for the 8FYP projects to increase tax to GDP ratio to grow from 8.9% of GDP in FY19 to 12.3 in FY25.",""],[1,"187","6","Non-tax Revenue Expansion","Some increase in non-tax revenue is also projected that grows total revenues as a percentage of GDP from 9.9% in FY19 to 14.1% in FY25.",""],[1,"197","2","Public Investment Prioritization for Recovery and Eighth Plan Targets","Public investment priorities will be determined on the basis of recovery form COVID-19 and the realization of key Eighth Plan targets with respect to real GDP growth, poverty reduction and social protection for the poor and vulnerable, human resource development, enhancing social equity through inclusive growth and ensuring the sustainability of growth through continued macroeconomic stability.",""]],"110":[[1,"173","4","National Multidimensional Poverty Index Development","the government, during the 7th FYP, has taken initiative to develop the National Multidimensional Poverty Index (MPI) and linked Child Multidimensional Poverty Index (C-MPI) as a prelude to preparing a national MPI for Bangladesh.",""],[1,"174","1","National Multidimensional Poverty Index Implementation","It is expected that the fruitful realization of national MPI and Child MPI during the 8th FYP would enable the government to fight against non-monetary deprivations, which will reduce regional inequality and mainstream marginalized groups into the development process.",""],[1,"177","14","District-Level GDP Estimation","Require BBS to re-introduce district level GDP estimates to help understand the pattern of district level income paths and whether convergence is happening.",""],[1,"211","3","Bangladesh Bureau of Statistics Strengthening Initiative","Under the 8FYP, the BBS will be greatly strengthened to generate high quality data in a timely fashion.",""],[1,"211","4","Implementation of the National Strategy for the Development of Statistics","Some progress was made in the implementation of the NSDS under the Seventh Plan, but progress was constrained by the slowdown in the procurement of the required technical assistance to strengthen BBS capacity.",""],[1,"211","5","Small-Scale Interim Survey Monitoring System","Second, the BBS will undertake small scale surveys for enabling regular and frequent monitoring and evaluation exercise.",""],[1,"211","6","National Accounts System Improvement","the government will dedicate substantial resources to improving the system of national accounts.",""],[1,"211","6","Quarterly GDP Data Production","the BBS needs to focus on producing GDP data on a quarterly basis.",""],[1,"211","6","National Population Register Preparation","Statistics and Informatics Division is mandated for preparing National Population Register (NPR) according to the Allocation of Business, 1996 (revised up to April 2017), Statistics Act 2013 and National Strategy for the Development of Statistics (NSDS).","Statistics and Informatics Division"],[1,"212","1","National Population Register Preparation and Updating","will prepare and update the NPR to provide information of each and every individual of the country with a unique identification number for ensuring effective service delivery.",""],[1,"212","2","District-Level Production and Fiscal Accounts Compilation","BBS will take initiative to start compiling district level production and fiscal accounts of LGIs.",""],[1,"212","3","BBS Data Quality Strengthening","Finally, strong emphasis will be given to strengthening the quality of BBS data.",""]],"111":[[1,"239","2","Machine-Readable Passport and Visa Issuance Programme","Under the 7FYP, the DIP has successfully offered Machine Readable Passports (MRP) to all new applicants and is following the guideline of the International Civil Aviation Organization (ICAO) to issue and extend the validity of Machine-Readable Visa (MRV).","Department of Immigration and Passports (DIP)"],[1,"239","2","e-Passport Rollout","DIP has also started issuing e-Passports to its citizens, making Bangladesh the first South Asian country and 119th country in the world to issue such advanced travel documents.","Department of Immigration and Passports (DIP)"],[1,"239","2","Passport and Visa Process Simplification Measures","The DIP has also taken measures to enhance the acceptability of Bangladesh passports and visas around the world and have simplified the process of obtaining Bangladesh visas.","Department of Immigration and Passports (DIP)"],[1,"239","2","Passport Issuance Simplification for Labour Mobility","Additionally, measures have been taken to simplify the process associated with the issuance of passports to Bangladeshi citizens, which will help accelerate the export of labour force to the overseas markets.","Department of Immigration and Passports (DIP)"],[1,"255","1","Visa Process Simplification","DIP is committed to the simplification of the process of obtaining Bangladesh visas.","Department of Passport and Immigration (DIP)"],[1,"255","1","Passport Modernization and E-Passport Rollout","Simplification and modernization of the issuing of passports to Bangladesh nationals will also help to accelerate export of labour to the overseas markets.","Department of Passport and Immigration (DIP)"]],"112":[[1,"197","1","Enhanced Plan Implementation Capacity and Results-Based M&E","Accordingly, the Government will be paying enhanced attention to implementation capacity, governance and result-based monitoring and evaluation (M&E) under the Plan.",""],[1,"207","1","Results-Based Monitoring and Evaluation System","This results-based M&E system has been incorporated to flexibly use as an instrument of securing mid-term corrections.",""],[1,"207","2","8FYP Results Framework and Monitoring Arrangements","The objective of this brief chapter is to discuss the strategy underlying the DRF for the 8FYP, its strategic role in planning, the institutional arrangements for results-based monitoring, data mobilization arrangements, mid-term and end evaluation of the plan.",""],[1,"207","3","Results-Based Monitoring and Evaluation System","a results-based M&E is recognized as critical to helping the Government track and monitor progress and take corrective measures when major gaps or divergences emerge.",""],[1,"209","19","Plan Monitoring and Evaluation Focal Point","GED is the focal point for monitoring and evaluation of mid and long-term plans.",""],[1,"210","1","Review and Revision of the National SDG Action Plan","the GED will review the \"National Action Plan of Ministries/Divisions by Targets in the Implementation of Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs)\" that was developed in alignment with the 7FYP.","GED"],[1,"210","1","Preparation of the Revised National SDG Action Plan","Based on the review of the National SDG Action Plan and feedbacks from the consultation with the ministries/divisions/agencies, revised National SDG Action Plan will be prepared by identifying projects and programmes that would be undertaken during FY2021-FY2025 to achieve the development aspiration of the 8FYP.","ministries/divisions/agencies"],[1,"210","1","National SDG Action Plan Monitoring and Evaluation Tool","Along with the DRF of the 8FYP, the National SDG Action Plan will also be used as an M&E tool to review the progress of implementation of this mid-term plan document (8FYP).",""],[1,"210","2","Government Officials Training on Results-Based M&E","The GED will continue such training even for a larger audience on the 8FYP for effective understanding and operationalization of the result-based M&E system.","GED"],[1,"210","2","Sector Strategy M&E Framework Development","Moreover, the GED will help develop M&E framework for the sector strategies to line ministries so that each ministry knows its commitments and the benchmark against which performance will be evaluated.","GED | line ministries"],[1,"210","3","Medium-Term Budgetary Framework","The adoption of the medium-term budgetary framework (MTBF) and assigning this role the Ministry of Finance has strengthened the link between the budget and the national plan on the one hand and between macroeconomic and sectoral programmes on the other through the involvement of sectoral line ministries.","Ministry of Finance | sectoral line ministries"],[1,"210","3","Nationwide Monitoring and Evaluation Framework","The Planning Commission rightly focuses on developing a nation-wide M&E framework in coordination with the Ministry of Finance and the line ministries.","Planning Commission | Ministry of Finance | line ministries"],[1,"210","3","Sectoral Results-Based Monitoring and Evaluation","This aggregate-level M&E effort needs to be complemented with two other levels of results-based M&E: sectoral M&Es conducted by line Ministries and M&E of individual investment projects done by the Implementation Monitoring and Evaluation Division (IMED) under the Ministry of Planning.","line Ministries | Implementation Monitoring and Evaluation Division (IMED) | Ministry of Planning"],[1,"210","4","Systematic Review of the Public Investment Portfolio","The IMED has made some progress in doing systematic review of the entire project portfolio to distil the key lessons of project selection and management and strengthen the development impact of the public investment program.",""],[1,"210","5","Expanded Project Impact Assessment and M&E Capacity Development","IMED will undertake an increased number of impact assessments of projects with the help of both experimental and non-experimental data so that M&E at the micro-level moves beyond simply tracking the financial and physical completion of the projects.",""],[1,"210","5","Research and Collaboration Capacity Building with Think Tanks and Universities","The IMED will develop its capacity and learning through a process of research and collaboration with the national think tanks and the universities.",""],[1,"210","6","Strengthening the Line Ministry Monitoring and Evaluation System","The line ministries/divisions are critical actors in revamping the M&E system.",""],[1,"211","2","Line Ministry M&E Capacity Building Plan","a capacity building plan will be developed which will pinpoint how line ministries will design an M&E strategy.",""],[1,"211","2","Results-Based M&E System Revision","revision of existing good practice for a results-based M&E from relevant international experience so that some lessons can be drawn to improve the existing results- based M&E system of line Ministries.",""],[1,"211","2","Strengthening of Line Ministry Planning Wings","the planning wings of line ministries will be strengthened with trained officials and technology to prepare project performance reports and results data.",""],[1,"211","2","Sectoral Data Mobilization and Website Publication","line ministries will be encouraged to mobilize the relevant sectoral data and put that into the respective websites.",""],[1,"212","4","Mid-Term and Final Plan Review Mechanism","Two M&E reviews will be conducted during the 8FYP to assess the degree of achievement against targets set in the plan document.",""],[1,"212","5","Mid-Term Review of the Plan","The Mid Term Review will be conducted in FY2023.",""],[1,"212","6","Final and End Review Dissemination Workshops","The findings of Final/End Review of the 8FYP will be disseminated through workshops with stakeholders.",""],[1,"212","7","Results-Based Monitoring and Evaluation System Strengthening","official channels for collecting information should be maintained and their dissemination must occur in a user-friendly manner.",""],[1,"212","7","Government Accountability for M&E Ownership","there is inherent need to ensure accountability of the government to own the M&E effort.",""],[1,"212","7","Continuous M&E Capacity Building","Finally, continuous capacity building efforts are necessary.",""],[1,"239","3","Results-Based Monitoring and Evaluation Strengthening","The Government of Bangladesh has remained committed to strengthen its Monitoring and Evaluation (M&E) as advocated by in the both Sixth and Seventh Plans.",""],[1,"239","3","Bangladesh Bureau of Statistics Capacity Support","The Government has also widened its exercise of generating data by aiding the capacity of the Bangladesh Bureau of Statistics (BBS), which helps document a large array of socio-economic indicators and allows the examination of various policies in different sectors.",""],[1,"239","3","Project Implementation Monitoring by IMED","Implementation, Monitoring and Evaluation Division (IMED) of the Ministry of Planning also continues to focus on physical and financial aspects of project implementation.","Implementation, Monitoring and Evaluation Division (IMED) of the Ministry of Planning"],[1,"255","2","Strengthening the Implementation Monitoring and Evaluation Division","With a view to ensuring sustainable development, more measures will be taken to strengthen IMED for effective implementation of project.",""]],"113":[[1,"7","4","Eighth Five Year Plan Implementation","Eighth Five Year Plan (July 2020-June 2025), which has been approved by the National Economic Council (NEC) on 29 December, 2020 will help to execute the political, social and economic agenda of the present government led by the Hon'ble Prime Minister Sheikh Hasina.",""],[1,"9","3","Eighth Five Year Plan Implementation of Perspective Plan 2021-2041","The main objective of the Eighth Five Year Plan is to start the implementation of PP2021-2041 in a way that it brings Bangladesh closer to the goals of achieving UMIC status by 2031 and attaining SDGs targets through managing the challenges of LDC graduation, which will also help to eliminate extreme poverty by 2031.",""],[1,"10","2","Eighth Five Year Plan Preparation and Coordination Mechanism","Initially, a 'National Steering Committee' was formed under the chairmanship of the Honorable Minister of Planning to oversight the preparation of the plan.",""],[1,"10","2","Expert Panel for Plan Formulation","A 'Panel of Economists', under the chairmanship of Dr. Wahiduddin Mahmud, has also been formed comprising luminous Bangladeshi economists, sociologists, educationalists and experts on relevant fields, who gave continuous support in shaping the Eighth Five Year Plan.",""],[1,"10","2","Inclusive Stakeholder Partnership for Plan Formulation","In this noble initiative, GED has ensured partnership of all the government ministries/divisions/agencies, policy makers, academia, civil society organizations, NGOs, development partners, think-tanks and thought leaders in formulating this plan.",""],[1,"10","3","Eighth Five Year Plan Strategic Framework and Sectoral Action Measures","The plan document has been organized around two broad parts.",""],[1,"10","4","Development Results Framework Monitoring System","The Eighth Five Year Plan adopts a better informed DRF, drawing on the good experiences of the Sixth and Seventh Plans.",""],[1,"10","4","Core Macro and Sectoral Results Monitoring","Both core macro and sectoral quantitative results will be monitored, with the help of 104 DRF indicators (more than half of which are related to SDGs), to measure",""],[1,"54","2","Public Finance Reform for Equity","reform of public finances that increases the equity of tax collection and public spending are of substantial importance.",""],[1,"54","2","Equitable Public Spending on Education and Health","the equity aspects of public spending on education and health will be emphasized.",""],[1,"65","4","Results-Based Monitoring and Evaluation Strategy","A major institutional reform that has happened in the approach to planning in Bangladesh is the internalization of an effective results-based Monitoring & Evaluation (M&E) strategy to monitor the implementation of the Plan and associated programmes.",""],[1,"65","5","Data Collection and SDG Monitoring Strengthening","The Bangladesh Bureau of Statistics (BBS) will be empowered for data collection drives for DRF, including MICS, Urban child wellbeing survey, vulnerable pocket-based survey, including implementation of national data quality assurance framework for administrative data from ministries for SDGs, including SDG data monitoring.","Bangladesh Bureau of Statistics (BBS) | ministries | GED"],[1,"65","5","Partnerships for Project Data Collection and Reporting","GED, BBS along with ministries will promote partnerships with independent agencies for collecting data and reporting for specific projects.","GED | BBS | ministries"],[1,"94","4","Medium-Term Budgetary Framework Integration","Progress has also been made to improve the budgetary process by linking it to the medium-tern national development plans",""],[1,"94","5","Public Procurement and Public Financial Management Strengthening","To reduce wasteful use of public resources, utmost attention is being given to public procurement and public financial management.",""],[1,"94","5","Internal Financial Controls and External Audit Capacity Enhancement","Internal financial controls and external audit capacities are being enhanced in all line ministries and in the Comptroller General's Office.","all line ministries | the Comptroller General's Office"],[1,"95","3","Public Financial Management Reform Action Plan","The PFM Action Plan, 2018-23 has been prepared and implementation is ongoing.",""],[1,"95","3","E-Challan and Integrated Budget and Accounting System Introduction","Under PFM reforms, E-challan system and a new budget and accounting system (Ibas++) have been introduced, new accounting BACS has been completed, and automation of National Savings Certificate sales has been introduced.",""],[1,"97","24","Budget and Balance of Payments Support Mobilization","Additionally, the government has requested for budget and balance of payments (BoP) support from major development partners including the IMF.",""],[1,"99","3","Public Finance Reform for Equity","reform of public finances that increases the equity of tax collection and public spending are of substantial importance.",""],[1,"99","3","Equitable Public Spending on Education and Health","the equity aspects of public spending on education and health require considerable effort.",""],[1,"110","1","Block Grants for Basic Social Services","It uses block grants to regions and districts for delivering basic social services in health, education, agriculture, and rural roads, water, and sanitation.",""],[1,"235","2","Medium-Term Budgetary Framework Budgeting","The Government rolled out the budget based on the Medium-Term Budgetary Framework (MTBF) to strengthen institutionalization of a strategic and policy-based approach to budgeting.",""],[1,"235","3","Integrated Budget and Accounting System Installation","During the 7th Plan, the Integrated Budget and Accounting System (IBAS++) was installed to enhance the accuracy of financial data.",""],[1,"235","3","Public Debt Statistics Publication","To ensure transparency of the government's fiscal position, public debt statistics were published on a regular basis.",""],[1,"235","3","Integrated Financial Management Information System","The Ministry of Finance introduced the Integrated Financial Management Information System (IFMIS) to produce accurate estimates of its financial statement in due time.","Ministry of Finance"],[1,"235","3","Aid and Debt Management Digitalization","In keeping with 'Digital Bangladesh' initiative, the Government also digitalized aid and debt management to ensure greater transparency and mutual accountability.",""],[1,"249","1","Planning and Budgeting Process Strengthening","Efforts will be made to address these issues in the 8FYP.",""],[1,"249","6","Implementation of the Agreed Program of Actions","The 8FYP will make a strong effort to implement the agreed program of actions with a time bound implementation plan.",""],[1,"250","1","Pre-Budget Statement Publication","the Government will make the pre-budget statement available in the public domain.",""],[1,"250","1","Fiscal Data Disclosure Initiative","The government will also make available all fiscal data showing actual outcomes for both expenditure and revenues.",""]],"114":[[1,"235","4","Public Investment Management Reform Agenda","Under the 7FYP period, the Planning Commission developed and validated a set of new Public Investment Management (PIM) tools.",""],[1,"250","2","Multi-Year Public Investment Programme","Introducing Multi-Year Public Investment Programme (MYPIP): Building on the progresses and achievements in the 7FYP, the government is committed to accelerating the PIM reform in the 8FYP.",""],[1,"250","4","Project Formulation and Appraisal Reform","Improve project formulation, appraisal, and approval processes.",""],[1,"250","4","Ministry Assessment Format and Sector Appraisal Format Rollout","In the 8FYP period, Ministry Assessment Format (MAF) and Sector Appraisal Format (SAF) will be introduced and used in the assessment and appraisal process of all DPPs in two pilot sectors - (i) power and energy, and (ii) local government and rural development.",""],[1,"250","4","National Rollout of Project Appraisal Formats","After successful introduction in the two pilot sectors, MAF and SAF will be rolled out to all other sectors.",""],[1,"250","5","Strengthening Strategic Linkages Between Planning and Budgeting Instruments","Strengthen strategic linkages between ADP, FYP and MTBF.",""],[1,"250","6","Alignment of ADP/RADP Sector Classification with FYP and MTBF","The Programming Division has taken the initiative to prepare ADP/RADP based on the 14 sectors of FYP and MTBF to contribute to strengthening the linkages among FYP, ADP/RADP and MTBF processes.",""],[1,"250","7","ADP Database Management System Operationalization","In the 8FYP, the new database management system for ADP will be made fully operational, including modules of MYPIP, for all government entities.",""],[1,"250","7","ADP-FD Digital Interface Establishment","In this process, digital interface of the ADP database management system will be also established with that of FD in the preparation process of national budget.","FD"]],"115":[[1,"237","2","Information Commission Capacity Strengthening","The Government of Bangladesh has shown a steadfast commitment to the ideals of \"right to information\" and has accordingly invested in improving the capacity of the Information Commission under the 7FYP.",""],[1,"237","2","Public Agency Annual Reporting and Electronic Disclosure","The Commission has also encouraged different public agencies to publish Annual Reports and provide all essential information electronically through their respective websites.",""],[1,"237","2","Online RTI Application Tracking System","Additionally, the Information Commission also started online tracking of RTI application on a test basis during the 7th plan period.",""],[1,"254","3","Public Data Availability and Transparency Improvement","Availability of data and information will be given top priority to improve transparency and for conducting independent evaluation and assessment of government strategies, policies, activities, functions, etc.",""],[1,"254","4","Strengthening Information Commission Responsiveness and RTI Monitoring","The Government will ensure that the Information Commission authority would be more responsive to requests made under the Right to Information Act.",""]],"116":[[1,"53","2","Tax Reform Programme","Tax reforms and banking reforms will become even more important as the nation faces to fight the COVID-19 adverse economic effects.",""],[1,"53","4","Tax Reform Package","The tax performance of Bangladesh has been slipping and this must be reversed quickly with important tax reforms under the 8FYP.",""],[1,"58","4","Revenue Mobilization and Tax Administration Modernization","Financing of this large PIP will require strong revenue mobilization effort that has faced difficulties during the 7FYP.",""],[1,"58","4","Fiscal Framework Reform under PP2041","The fiscal framework of the 8FYP will implement the fiscal framework of the PP2041 that calls for an increase in the tax to GDP ratio of 3.4 percentage points, growing from 8.9% of GDP in FY2019 to 12.3% of GDP by FY2025 through modernization of tax policy and tax administration, focused on income and value-added taxes.",""],[1,"58","4","Reduction of Import Tax Reliance","The reliance on import taxes will be lowered to reduce the anti-export bias of trade policy.",""],[1,"58","4","Modern Property Tax System","A modern property tax system will be introduced to increase revenues for local governments, and SOEs including public banks will be reformed to earn profits and eliminate dependency on budget transfers.",""],[1,"64","10","Tax System Modernization and Digital Filing Reform","Strong implementation of the PP2041 fiscal framework with a special focus on strengthening personal and corporate income tax collections and the VAT through modernization of the tax system.",""],[1,"98","10","Tax Reform Acceleration","The tax performance of Bangladesh has been slipping over a long period of time and this must be reversed quickly with important tax reforms under the 8FYP.",""],[1,"127","1","Tax System Modernization and Simplification","The tax payments procedures will be simplified and made less burdensome through a major overhaul of the tax system that is a part of the government's tax modernization plan under the PP2041 fiscal policy framework.",""],[1,"146","2","Tax Policy Reform and Tax Administration Modernization","Resource mobilization by the public sector will continue to remain a major challenge and will require steadfast implementation of tax policy reforms (in both VAT and direct tax fronts), modernization of tax administration, and reform of the NBR tax administration.","NBR"],[1,"181","2","Personal Income Tax Reform and Administration Improvement","This will require the closing of loopholes that let capital gains escape the tax net, treating all sources of personal income equally for taxation purpose, and improving tax administration and compliance.",""],[1,"181","2","Value Added Tax Modernization","The modernization of VAT and improving its productivity can yield an additional 1.8% of GDP.",""],[1,"181","2","Modern Property Tax Introduction and Local Government Assignment","Moreover, the introduction of a modern property tax and assigning this to the local governments can be a substantial boost for their fiscal autonomy while providing fiscal resources.",""],[1,"184","2","Tax Policy and Administration Reform and Modernization","Financing of this National Plan will require increased private and public sector savings, rapid income growth for the private sector and increased revenue mobilization through reform and modernization of tax policy and tax administration.",""],[1,"189","2","Tax Reform Acceleration and Modernization Programme","The Government recognizes these challenges and aims to speed up tax reforms in the 8FYP.",""],[1,"190","7","PP2041 Tax System Modernization","The PP2041 tax system modernizes this to a tax system that is focused on income as the primary source of tax revenues, relies on self-assessment and on-line filing and tax payments, uses a simplified filing system for most taxes except for complicated cases, and relies on selective and productive audits that are criteria based.",""],[1,"190","8","Tax Reform Strategy under the 8FYP","The specific tax reform strategies that are possible under the 8FYP are summarized in Box 5.1.",""],[1,"190","8","VAT, Income Tax, and Customs Duty Legal and Procedural Reforms","In this first phase important legal and procedural reforms relating to the VAT, income tax and custom duties are introduced.",""],[1,"191","1","Proposed Tax Reform Package","The proposed tax reforms in Box 5.1 are extremely important and cannot be delayed further in order to restore tax revenue collections and support the needs for essential public spending as summarized in Table 5.3.",""],[1,"191","3","Alternative Dispute Resolution in Tax and Customs Acts","Incorporating Alternative Dispute Resolution (ADR) in Income Tax, VAT and Custom Acts",""],[1,"191","4","Income Tax Overhaul and Simplification","A thorough overhaul and simplification of Income Taxes with implementation in FY2023",""],[1,"191","5","Customs Act Adoption and Implementation","Adoption and implementation of the new Customs Act in FY2022.",""],[1,"191","7","Separation of Tax Planning and Tax Collection","Starting FY2024, separate tax planning from tax collection.",""],[1,"191","8","Professional Appointment Reform for NBR Leadership","Starting FY2024, selection of NBR Chair and the new Chair of the Tax Policy Unit should be done on a professional basis with a 5-year fixed term appointment.",""],[1,"191","9","Modernization of NBR and Tax Policy Unit Offices","Provide adequate resources and autonomy to NBR Chair and the Chair of Tax Policy Unit to modernize their respective offices with modern technology, professional staffing and policy and research capabilities.",""],[1,"191","10","Taxpayer Asset Ownership Monitoring and Income Assessment","Broadening of the taxpayers' base- This will require monitoring of the ownership of all sizable physical and financial assets of taxpayers and determining the income generation out of those assets.",""],[1,"191","11","Tax Base Broadening Initiative","The tax department should explore other smaller organizations in the formal sector as well various corporations.",""],[1,"191","13","Equal Tax Treatment of Household Income Sources","Treating all sources of income equally for the tax purpose without discrimination for the households.",""],[1,"191","14","TIN Registration Automation and National ID Linkage","Automation of TIN registration and linking TIN with National I.D.",""],[1,"191","15","Integrated Revenue Management Programme","Integrated Revenue Management Programme: Business Process an integrated revenue management programme seeks to connect the three departments at transactional level by linking the taxpayer identification numbers i.e. TIN and BIN in the database.",""],[1,"191","16","Integrated Revenue Management Digitalization Programme","This programme will seek to set up a country-wide integrated ICT platform to capture all tax payment information from tax returns, banks, TDS detectors, third party collection agencies etc.",""],[1,"191","16","Central Processing Centre for Income-tax and VAT Returns","Under this programme, a Central Processing Centre is to be set up for processing all Income-tax and VAT returns, whether e-filed or paper filed at one integrated processing centre.",""],[1,"192","1","E-Filing and Online Tax Payment System","E-Filing of income tax returns and online payments.",""],[1,"192","2","Withholding Tax Expansion and Enforcement Reform","Aggressive imposition and expansion of withholding taxes, particularly on individual taxes which could potentially improve tax compliance, expand the income tax base and address administrative issues pertaining to tax collection efforts through increased transparency and efficiency.",""],[1,"192","3","Taxpayer Education and Assistance Programme","The taxpayer education programme will make available a menu of offerings through remote outlets like websites, internet etc. as well as through customers facing one to one or group interface with the NBR Customer Service Wing.",""],[1,"192","4","Selective and Productive Tax Audit System","Institute an audit system where only a limited number of tax cases will be audited based on computer- based criteria.",""],[1,"192","5","New VAT Act Implementation","Implementation of the new VAT Act.",""],[1,"192","6","VAT Base Expansion","Expanding VAT base especially on businesses and organization.",""],[1,"192","8","VAT Administration Functional Reform","Reform of the VAT administration along functional lines",""],[1,"192","9","Tax Administration Automation and Central VAT Registration","Automation of the whole tax administration through Central Data base including Central VAT Registration; electronic submission and return processing",""],[1,"192","10","Taxpayer Education and Information Campaign on the New VAT Law","Comprehensive taxpayers' education and information campaign about the new VAT law and Rules.",""],[1,"192","12","Tax Administration Strengthening and Computerization Reform","The need for strengthening of the tax administration, its computerization and improvement in efficiency is integral to achieving 8FYP tax targets.",""],[1,"192","12","Income Tax Base Expansion and Withholding Mechanism Reform","Expansion of the income tax base and bringing more individuals and companies under the tax net and under the withholding mechanism would be necessary to drive the revenue growth and to achieve levels enjoyed by our neighbouring countries.",""],[1,"192","12","Formalization Incentives for the Informal Sector","Initiatives and incentives by the government to formalize these activities would greatly enhance the tax potential on the domestic side while making it possible to achieve the targets set under the 8FYP.",""],[1,"192","13","Strengthening Tax Evasion Detection Units","This needs to be addressed by strengthening tax evasion detecting unit like the Central Intelligence Cell (CIC) and other intelligence units of the NBR.","Bangladesh Bank | Anti-Corruption Commission"],[1,"192","13","Inter-Agency Tax Evasion Combat Coordination","The NBR should work together with the Bangladesh Bank and the Anti-Corruption Commission for combating tax evasion.","Bangladesh Bank | Anti-Corruption Commission"],[1,"193","1","Alternative Dispute Resolution Mechanism for Revenue Collection","The ADR mechanism will be further popularized and strengthened to collect arrear revenue.",""],[1,"193","3","Statistics and Research Department Strengthening","efforts will be made to implement the recommendations of the diagnostic report.","NBR"],[1,"193","3","Tax Compliance Social Recognition Programme","Efforts will also be made to enhance tax compliance through social recognition programme.",""],[1,"200","4","National Board of Revenue Modernization Plan","Effective implementation of the NBR modernization Plan including automation of the VAT and direct tax administration will be preconditions for the success of the domestic revenue mobilization strategy.",""]],"117":[[1,"63","1","Urban Transition Management Road Map","Accordingly, the PP2041 develops a long-term road map to manage smoothly the urban transition.",""],[1,"63","2","Urban Policy Incentives, Regulations, Investments, and Institutions","The role of public policy to influence the pattern of urbanization will depend upon incentives, regulations, public investments and institutions.",""],[1,"63","2","Decentralized and Autonomous Urban Government Reform","Global experience clearly shows the need for decentralized and autonomous urban governments as a key part of the political and administrative layout underlying an UMIC.",""],[1,"63","2","City Management Reform and Public-Private Partnership Strengthening","A sound strategy for reforming city management calls for a three-pronged approach: (i) redefining public-private roles with a view to strengthening this partnership for better services; (ii) strengthening capabilities of public urban service institutions; and (iii) establishing an accountable city government with fiscal decentralization.",""],[1,"63","3","Local Government Institutional Reform","Along with institutional reforms to promote the development of strong local government institutions (LGIs), the 8FYP will invest heavily in critical urban services like water supply, drainage, sanitation and waste management.",""],[1,"63","4","Criteria-Based Fiscal Decentralization Transfers","The 8FYP will accordingly take measures to enhance fiscal decentralization by taking a criteria-based approach to transfers to city corporations and Municipalities.",""],[1,"63","4","Modern Property Tax Mobilization for Local Governments","The first is tax mobilization through a modern property tax system as found in UMIC.",""],[1,"63","4","Private Financing for Urban Services","The second involves private financing, and the third relates to a strong cost recovery policy for urban services.",""],[1,"63","4","Cost Recovery Policy for Urban Services","The second involves private financing, and the third relates to a strong cost recovery policy for urban services.",""],[1,"63","4","Local Government Financing for Urban Operating Costs and Public Goods","While LGI tax resources and national government transfers will help finance operating costs of the city government and spending programmes on public goods like local roads, drainage systems, parks and maintenance of water bodies, cost recovery will play a dominant role for such services as water supply, sewerage and solid waste disposal.",""],[1,"63","4","Private Provision of Commercial Urban Services","Private provision of these commercial services will also be encouraged.",""],[1,"64","6","Local Government Institutional Strengthening and Fiscal Autonomy Reform","Strengthening of the local government institutions based on a well-defined legal framework that assigns responsibilities along with commensurate financial autonomy.",""],[1,"84","2","Strengthening Local Government Institutions for Social Inclusion","the successful implementation of an overarching social inclusion strategy as envisaged in the Constitution requires the institution of strong local government institutions",""],[1,"502","17","Block Grant Expansion to Selected Pourashavas","Expanding block grant to selected Pourashavas (on pilot basis)",""],[1,"502","18","Project Implementation Capacity Support","Developing capacity and supporting project implementation",""],[1,"502","20","Urban Local Government Infrastructure Improvement Mechanism","Projects have also been implemented to improve the governance of urban LGIs through infrastructure investment.",""],[1,"502","20","Urban Governance Awareness and Capacity-Building Programmes","Several programmes have been undertaken during the 7FYP to increase public awareness, women participation in municipal development, urban planning, poverty reduction, financial management and transparency, and e- governance.",""],[1,"502","20","Town Level Coordination Committees","Town Level Coordination Committee (TLCC) has been formed in many Pourashavas to ensure",""],[1,"504","2","Municipal Master Plan Preparation and Enforcement Support","However, the enforcement of Master Plans requires creation of position of the Town Planners with career development opportunity.","LGD"],[1,"515","8","Performance-Based Evaluation System for Local Government Institutions","A performance-based evaluation system has been introduced by the LGD to enhance the capacity, accountability, transparency & healthy competitions among LGIs, in particular, for UPs, City Corporations and Municipalities that are included in foreign aided projects.","LGD"],[1,"515","8","Standardized Performance Evaluation System for Urban Local Governments","For all other urban LGIs that do not get foreign financing, similar harmonic standardize system will be adopted.",""],[1,"515","8","Performance Threshold-Based Additional Allocation Mechanism","The system will continue until the performance reaches at a level of standard, which will be used as a measure of additional allocation of ADP and other dividends within the sector.",""],[1,"517","2","City Corporation Governance Improvement Strategy","Strategy for Governance Improvement of City Corporations (SGICC) (2020 - 2030): This strategic document aims to improve governance in the administration of City Corporations between 2020 and 2030, and it has four key goals - {i} formulating and implementing the legal instruments that are requited for the implementation of the City Corporation Act 2009; {ii} Introducing systems of continuous organizational improvement and development in the City Corporations; {iii} Strengthening the fiscal foundations of the City Corporations and preparing their budgets based on multi-year fiscal frameworks; and {iv} Systems for continuous development of the human resources in the City Corporations will be established by the Government.",""],[1,"517","3","Paurashava Governance Improvement Strategy Implementation","Hence, under the 8FYP, the Government will prioritize the implementation of all the identified activities for each of the respective goals that are underscored in the strategic document.",""],[1,"617","6","Urban Institutional Strengthening and Capacity Building","Urban development therefore should encompass institutional strengthening and capacity building, decentralization, community participation, and involvement of the private sector in the development of the urban sector.",""],[1,"617","6","Urban Decentralization and Local Institutional Reform","Institutional reform at the local level, therefore, will focus on the following:",""],[1,"617","7","Local Development Programme Implementation Coordination","All the organizations and institutions which operate at the local level in connection with the development and/or operation and maintenance of infrastructure and services as well as socio-economic development will be involved for implementation of Development Programmes.",""],[1,"618","1","Urban Governance Powers and Resource Allocation Reform","Clear division of powers and allocation of resources in the major areas of urban planning, development and management across different levels of governments will be ensured so that there is no overlap or gap in implementation of an agreed urban plan.",""],[1,"618","2","Local Government Capacity Building Programme","Capacity building of local government bodies would focus on strengthening managerial, technical, financial and regulatory capabilities.",""],[1,"618","5","Legal and Regulatory Standards Revision","Regulatory: revising laws and codes and setting regulatory standards.",""],[1,"618","7","Municipal Urban Planning Capacity Development","capacity development of municipalities for updating and enforcement of master plan.",""],[1,"618","8","Urban Local Body Staff Capacity Improvement","For reducing dependence of Paurashavas and City Corporations on central government agencies steps would be taken for improving the staff capabilities of these urban local bodies.",""],[1,"628","9","Local Government Strengthening and Infrastructure Development","Improve the living standard of the people by strengthening local government system, developing rural and urban infrastructure and implementing socio-economic activities.",""],[1,"628","10","Local Government Administration and Oversight","Manage all matters relating to local government and local government institutions",""],[1,"628","15","Finance, Evaluation, and Monitoring of Local Government Institutions","Finance, evaluate and monitor local government institutions and offices/organizations under Local Government Division.","Local Government Division"],[1,"628","17","Local Government Legal and Regulatory Reform","Enactment of Law, promulgation of rules and policies related to local government",""],[1,"632","12","Local Government Capacity and Skills Strengthening","Strengthening local level institutions including local governments by building appropriate capacity and skills so that these institutions become financially healthy and technically capable of ensuring access for all urban dwellers to basic urban services",""],[1,"634","4","Fiscal Decentralization Reform","A key policy and institutional challenge for the 8FYP would be to sharply strengthen resource mobilization capacity of local governments through a system of well-planned fiscal decentralization.",""],[1,"634","5","Block Transfer System for Local Government Institutions","Block transfers will be provided to all LGIs, including urban LGIs, based on pre-determined criteria that will include population, poverty, resource mobilization opportunities and performance.",""],[1,"634","6","Property Tax Modernization for Local Government Institutions","The tax will be modernized with proper valuation of property and a reasonable rate in line will be updated on a 3-year cycle with valuation changes spread over a 3-year period to ease the tax burden on the property owner.",""],[1,"634","7","Local Government Service Cost Recovery Requirement","All LGIs will be required to implement full cost recovery of services provided.",""],[1,"635","2","National Urban Priorities and Urban Reforms Design and Implementation","The Ministry can take the lead in defining and designing the national urban priorities and related urban reforms and ensuring their proper implementation in close consultation and coordination with the urban local governments.","Ministry of Local Government, Rural Development and Cooperatives"],[1,"635","2","Urbanization Progress Monitoring and Issue Resolution Mechanism","It will monitor progress with urbanization, identify emerging issues and challenges and seek to resolve them in consultation with the concerned urban LGIs.",""],[1,"635","4","Urban Resource Mobilization and Financing Strategy","Therefore, creative measures will have to be undertaken to mobilize additional resources.",""],[1,"635","4","Urban Development Budget Allocation Alignment","The allocation of development budget for the urban sector is not limited within Ministry of Housing and Public Works but also under the local government development (Chapter 7 of Part 2) to maintain consistency with the planning sectoral definition.","Ministry of Housing and Public Works"]],"118":[[1,"822","3","Women's Political Participation Capacity-Building and Support Programme","To enhance women's voices on behalf of women rights in the Parliament or LGIs-, apprenticeship, training, campaigns, and support programmes should be extended.",""],[1,"822","3","Capacity Building for Women Contesting Regular Seats","Women's participation to contest in the regular seats should be increased through capacity building and ensuring implementation of the RPO provisions.",""],[1,"822","3","Training Programme for Women Public Representatives","Training women public representatives and should be expanded.",""],[1,"822","3","Monitoring of Women's Role in Committees","Monitoring to strengthen women's role in different committees is also important.",""],[1,"822","3","Community Orientation for Women's Political Participation","Community should be oriented to support women's political participation and women in reserved seats should be oriented to play their effective role, taking leadership and gradually compete in the regular seats.",""],[1,"822","4","Enforcement of Women's Political Participation Requirements in Party Registration","The provisions of RPO 2013 related to women's participation and representation in political parties should be ensured by enforcing it within the registration criteria.",""],[1,"822","4","Direct Election of Women Parliamentarians in Reserved Seats","Provision for direct election of women Parliamentarians in reserved seat will give them opportunity to contribute to a community and be accountable to their constituency.",""],[1,"822","4","Constitutional Amendment for Direct Election of Women Parliamentarians","The extension of the provision of 50 female Parliamentarians in the reserved seats for 25 years should be combined with provision of direct election through an amendment of the Constitution.",""],[1,"823","1","Women’s Representation and Leadership Promotion Measures","Women's representation should be ensured in public institutions through instructions and directives.",""],[1,"823","2","Measures to Increase Women's Representation Across Sectors","Representation of women in different services and organizations should be enhanced by taking specific measures.",""]],"119":[[1,"145","7","Public Health Insurance Scheme","Government will introduce public health insurance to ensure health care for all the citizens.",""],[1,"145","8","Worker Accident and Death Insurance Scheme","Both the Government and the employer will take measures to introduce the insurance for workers to cover accidental injuries and deaths at workplace.",""],[1,"145","9","Mandatory Insurance Coverage for Commercial High-Rise Buildings","Public and private high rise buildings which are being commercially used or rented need to be brought under mandatory insurance coverage.",""]],"120":[[1,"641","4","Primary Health Care Service Delivery Expansion","efforts are on to bringing primary health care (PHC) service close to the communities through provision of care from a single service delivery point.",""],[1,"641","4","Mainstreaming of Nutrition Services Through Government Channels","Mainstreaming of nutrition services through the regular government channels made service provision more cost-effective and led to improved coordination at different stages of service delivery including at the Community Clinics (CCs).",""],[1,"641","4","Community Clinic and Union Health and Family Welfare Centre Programmes","The implementation of CC and UH&FWC based programmes have contributed to increasing access of the poor especially the women to HPN services.",""],[1,"641","4","Essential Service Package Update and Expansion","Updating of essential service package (ESP) and its expansion up to district hospital levels from the 4th HPNSP period has also been contributing to increased access of HPN services by the poor.",""],[1,"646","1","Essential Service Package for Primary Health Care","The ESP, being implemented from the levels of CCs to district hospitals as priority intervention for providing PHC services, represents Government's commitment to ensure the right to health and nutrition and that the whole population has access to the most essential health and nutrition services.",""],[1,"646","1","Community Clinic-Based Service Delivery","The CC based service provision at the doorstep of the people is a step forward towards achieving the UHC.",""],[1,"653","13","Universal Reproductive and Maternal Health Care and HIV/AIDS Services","Provide universal access to reproductive and maternal health care as well as NCDC, HIV/AIDS prevention, treatment, care and support.",""],[1,"653","14","Health Care Coverage and Social Protection Expansion","Provide higher coverage and adequate levels of health care including social protections, and ensure a balanced distribution of the human and financial costs of care.",""],[1,"654","2","Community-Based Primary Health Care Expansion and Consolidation","Expansion and consolidation of community based primary health care services.",""],[1,"654","3","Upgrading of Union Health and Family Welfare Centers","The UHFWCs will be upgraded with increased human resources for provision of 24/7 services.",""],[1,"654","6","Health Facility Upgradation and Expansion for Universal Coverage","Up-gradation of existing and creation of new facilities for service expansion with a view to bringing in more people under universal coverage and reducing individual out-of-pocket expenditure.",""],[1,"654","10","Primary Health Care and Essential Health Program Expansion","It will continue to emphasize on PHC, EPI, MNCH, NCD, nutrition etc. on consideration of achieving the equity goal and to implement the updated ESP as part of its strategy to achieve the UHC as proposed in SDG (Goal-3).",""],[1,"654","12","Essential Service Package for Primary Health Care","The ESP, being implemented from the levels of CCs to district hospitals as priority intervention for providing PHC services, represents Government's commitment to ensure the right to health and that the whole population has access to the most essential health services.",""],[1,"655","2","Primary Health Care Service Expansion and Quality Improvement","during the 8FYP period, exploration of various innovative approaches will be continued for expanding PHC services along with improving service quality, which would include review of existing field-based service delivery; diversification of service provision (inclusive of public-private partnership) particularly for Hard to Reach (HTR) areas; development of functional referral systems involving all levels of facilities; ensuring quality of care, etc.",""],[1,"655","2","Public Hospital Upgrading with Beds and Modern Equipment","Public hospitals at all levels will be upgraded with additional beds and modern equipment for ensuring access and utilization of quality health services by the people.",""]],"121":[[1,"641","2","Maternal, Child, and Adolescent Health Service Improvement","The first component aims to improve health services, such as maternal and child health and nutrition, Family planning, Reproductive health, Adolescent health, Non-communicable diseases, TB etc. and support the service delivery system including primary health care.",""],[1,"649","22","Expansion of Institutional Deliveries at Union-Level Facilities","Increase the percentage of Institutional Deliveries with a focus to union level facilities where 24/7 services are established.",""],[1,"653","5","Maternal, Newborn, and Adolescent Health Service Expansion","Ensuring SBAs at birth; newborn care; adolescent care; etc. and accelerating initiatives in low- performing and hard-to-reach areas.",""],[1,"653","6","Expansion of Community Clinic Nutritional and EPI Services","Expanding regular nutritional services and EPI programmes at the CC level in collaboration with DGFP.",""],[1,"656","13","Maternal and Newborn Health Service Delivery Strategy","As such a two- pronged strategy will be followed: (i) promotion of institutional services in all districts and upazilas and (ii) sustaining and expanding home-based services, in varying degrees based on local needs, particularly in places with geographic or social restrictions on seeking care from facilities.",""],[1,"657","1","Institutional Birth Promotion Campaign","Institutional births will be promoted actively through BCC at personal, group and national levels through innovative strategies incorporating the mass and electronic media.",""],[1,"657","1","Preconception and Pregnancy Service Delivery","Preconception and pregnancy related services will be provided by trained providers at the CC level and by NGOs where found feasible and appropriate.",""],[1,"657","1","Referral System Improvement Strategy","Strategies to improve effectiveness of referrals will be developed and implemented.",""],[1,"657","2","Essential Newborn Care Services Expansion","Specific attention will be given to promote essential newborn care services with emphasis on prevention and management of asphyxia and neonatal infections, and care for the Low Birth Weight and pre-term babies.",""],[1,"657","2","Community Health Worker Training and Operational Guidance","This will require extensive training of the existing community-based workers and the new community health care providers (CHCP) and supporting them through operational guidelines.",""],[1,"657","2","Sick Newborn Referral and Facility Strengthening","Sick newborn services will be strengthened at the UHCs and district hospitals with rapid referral systems of sick newborns to these facilities.",""],[1,"657","3","Nationwide Maternal and Newborn Health Services Expansion","Promoting MNH services nationwide including the urban slums, in collaboration with other health care providers including NGOs and using mass media.",""],[1,"657","4","Maternal and Neonatal Health Service Improvement","Improving quality of maternal and neonatal health services from preconception to the postnatal period in facilities from the medical colleges to CCs and including evidence-based interventions, notably to address hemorrhage and eclampsia.",""],[1,"657","5","24/7 Emergency Obstetric Care Service Strengthening","Strengthening 24/7 EmOC services gradually through improving HR development, placement and retention with skill mix at various tiers of service delivery and in identified facilities through a detailed mapping exercise considering emergency referrals, communication and transportation.",""],[1,"657","6","Skilled Birth Attendance Expansion through CSBA Training","Improving strategies to expand skilled birth attendance at institutional level and at home through continued CSBA training program.",""],[1,"657","7","Maternal Voucher Scheme Expansion","Expanding the maternal voucher scheme and other health protection schemes.",""],[1,"657","8","Maternal Morbidity Treatment, Prevention and Rehabilitation Services","Strengthening the maternal morbidity (Obstetric Fistula, Cervical Cancer, Breast Cancer, Uterine Prolapsed) related treatment, prevention and rehabilitation services with referral mechanism.",""],[1,"657","9","Child Health and Nutrition Initiative Expansion","The next sector program (during 8FYP) will sustain and expand all the on-going child health and nutrition initiatives with special emphasis on reaching the poorer and disadvantaged children more effectively and through partnering with NGOs following a mapping exercise, where appropriate.",""],[1,"657","10","Community-Based IMCI and Child Nutrition Services Expansion","Expanding IMCI particularly community based IMCI including child nutrition services.",""],[1,"657","11","Expansion of Integrated Management of Childhood Illness","Tackling ARI and diarrhea through expansion of IMCI particularly at the community level to cover the whole country with special emphasis on hard to reach areas.",""],[1,"657","12","Exclusive Breastfeeding Counseling for Growth Promotion","Ensuring growth promotion with counseling on exclusive breast feeding.",""]],"122":[[1,"679","6","Skilled Birth Attendance Capacity Expansion","Enhance the capacity to increase the percentage of births attended by trained staff from 59% to 72% by the end of the 8FYP by increasing resources and staffing in the rural health clinics and the district level hospitals.",""]],"123":[[1,"50","2","COVID-19 Containment and Health Response Measures","On the health front policy responses have sought to contain the spread of the virus through full and partial lockdowns, providing safety gears and other support to protect the healthcare workers and other essential staff, strengthening healthcare facilities with supplies and equipment, undertaking testing, and educating the masses on the adoption of health safety measures including physical distancing, use of face masks, hand washing and personal hygiene and other support measures.",""],[1,"50","3","Balanced Policy and Programme Mix for Safe Economic Reopening","The main task is to develop a balanced mix of policies and programmes that address both goals.",""],[1,"50","3","Health Expert Collaboration for Safe Economic Revival","The government is working closely with local epidemiologists and other health experts to find ways to keep workers and families safe while economic activities revive.",""],[1,"50","3","Adaptive Strategy Based on International Experience and Domestic Results","The strategy is flexible and will adapt to the lessons of international experience and the results in Bangladesh.",""],[1,"54","1","Healthcare System Overhaul","The 8FYP will need to initiate a major overhaul of the healthcare system to strengthen physical facilities, access to healthcare and availability of quality healthcare staff.",""],[1,"54","1","Universal Healthcare System Development","The COVID-19 has also reinforced the need for a universal healthcare system.",""],[1,"54","1","Safe Water and Sanitation Access Expansion","The COVID-19 also reinforces the importance of access to safe water and sanitation as important instruments for improving health and reducing the spread of COVID infection.",""],[1,"54","4","COVID-19 Rapid Recovery Measures","Rapid recovery for COVID-19 to restore human health, confidence, employment, income and economic activities;",""],[1,"55","1","COVID-19 Health Response and Recovery Package","The government has demonstrated its resolve to address the challenges emerging from COVID-19 swiftly and comprehensively with a view to minimizing the loss of lives, restoring the health of those affected, removing fear and building confidence, and putting the economy on a path of economic recovery while taking care this is consistent with the restoration of human health and confidence.",""],[1,"55","1","Health Care Capacity and Facility Strengthening","In addition to implementing the actions already taken in FY2020, the government will take a number of far-reaching steps to improve health care capabilities and facilities in the 8FYP.",""],[1,"55","1","Healthcare Financing and Public-Private Cooperation Expansion","Funding for healthcare will be increased, public-private cooperation will be strengthened, the capabilities of district-level healthcare facilities will be enhanced, and a Universal Health Care funded through a combination of private and public health insurance schemes will be introduced.",""],[1,"55","1","Safe Water and Sanitation Access Expansion","Access of the rural and urban population to safe water and sanitation will be enhanced.",""],[1,"55","1","Phased Reopening with COVID-19 Risk Minimization","The economic activity opening up will be phased and implemented in ways that risks to COVID spread are minimized.",""],[1,"55","1","COVID-19 Vaccine and Cure Procurement and International Liaison","Bangladesh will learn from the lessons of other country experience in fine tuning its health response to COVID-19.",""],[1,"55","1","Domestic Pharma and Medical Research Grants for COVID-19 Cure","The capabilities of domestic Pharma and medical research will be enhanced through research grants for research and innovation in the area of COVID-19 cure.",""],[1,"58","2","Health Infrastructure Strengthening","The main focus of the ADP will be to sharply improve and strengthen health infrastructure, to build the social protection system, alleviate infrastructure constraints to private investment and GDP growth by fast tracking nationally important projects, and implement the BDP2100.",""],[1,"58","3","Healthcare System Strengthening through Increased Funding and Private Partnership","Topmost priority will be given to develop the healthcare system through increased budgetary allocations, sharply stronger management and partnership with private healthcare.",""],[1,"59","1","Health Care System Strengthening and Universal Healthcare Policy","From the medium-term perspective, the 8FYP will increase budget allocation of healthcare spending from 0.7% of GDP in 2019 to 2.0% of GDP by FY2025, will sharply increase health care facilities, staffing, equipment and supplies, will strengthen partnership with private sector, enhance district-level health care capabilities, and promote tele-health care through ICT solutions.",""],[1,"99","2","Healthcare System Overhaul","The 8FYP will emphasize the need for a complete overhaul of the healthcare system which showed huge performance gaps in physical facilities, access to healthcare and availability of quality healthcare staff.",""],[1,"99","2","Universal Health Insurance System","The COVID-19 has also reinforced the need for a universal healthcare system with a combination of public and private health insurance scheme.",""],[1,"102","5","Rapid COVID-19 Recovery Measures","Rapid recovery for COVID-19 to restore human health, confidence, employment, income and economic activities.",""],[1,"111","5","COVID-19 Health Response and Recovery Measures","The government has demonstrated its resolve to address the challenges emerging from COVID-19 swiftly and comprehensively with a view to minimizing the loss of lives, restoring the health of those affected, removing fear and building confidence, and putting the economy on a path of economic recovery while taking care this is consistent with the restoration of human health and confidence.",""],[1,"111","5","Health Care Capacity and Universal Health Care Expansion","In addition to implementing the actions already taken in FY20, the government will take a number of far-reaching steps to improve health care capabilities and facilities in the 8FYP.",""],[1,"111","5","COVID-Safe Phased Economic Reopening","The economic activity opening up will be phased and implemented in ways that risks to COVID spread are minimized.",""],[1,"111","5","International COVID-19 Vaccine and Cure Cooperation","Bangladesh will also liaise with the World Health Organization and countries that are well advanced in medical search for vaccine and or cure.",""],[1,"111","5","Domestic Pharma and Medical Research Grants for COVID-19 Cure","The capabilities of domestic Pharma and medical research will be enhanced through research grants for research and innovation in the area off COVID-19 cure.",""],[1,"650","1","Whole-of-Government COVID-19 Response Coordination","Bangladesh adapted following \"Whole of Government Approach\" to ensure interactive process among all Ministries and to achieve the best results though openness, sharing information and cooperation amongst all concerned.",""],[1,"650","1","COVID-19 Preparedness and Response Plan","MoHFW initiated necessary preparation since January 2020 to control and contain the pandemic and prepared \"Bangladesh Preparation and Response Plan (BPRP) for COVID-19 as a living document.","MoHFW"],[1,"650","1","National Clinical Management Guidelines for COVID-19","The National Guidelines on Clinical Management of COVID-19 was also prepared on the basis of latest evidence and the WHO guidelines to be followed by every clinic/hospital, for treating COVID-19 'confirmed', 'probable', or 'suspect' cases.",""],[1,"650","2","National COVID-19 Response Coordination and Control Mechanism","From the very beginning, the Hon'ble Prime Minister has been overseeing the national response and taking feedback from the grassroots represented by government officials and political leaders and different stakeholders through videoconferencing.",""],[1,"650","2","COVID-19 Prevention, Control, and Health Care Service Delivery","The MoHFW, under guidance of Hon'ble Prime Minister, has taken all-out efforts to prevent and control spread of COVID-19 as well as to provide health care services to the infected people.","MoHFW"],[1,"650","2","Multi-Level COVID-19 Response Committees","A National Committee headed by the Minister of Health and Family Welfare was constituted to take necessary steps for the prevention and control of corona virus.","Ministry of Health and Family Welfare"],[1,"650","2","Hospital Preparedness for Coronavirus Patients","Some existing public hospitals have been made ready to provide specialized services for corona virus patients and more hospitals are being prepared.",""],[1,"650","2","Private Sector Hospital Involvement in COVID-19 Testing and Treatment","In addition to government hospitals, a number of private sector hospitals are involved in testing and treatment of corona virus.",""],[1,"650","2","Pillar-Based Multi-Sectoral COVID-19 Response Coordination","The country has been implementing the response activities with the multi-sectoral involvement representing the relevant ministries/divisions, private sectors, development partners through a pillar-based multi-sectoral coordination mechanism.",""],[1,"650","3","Community Support Team Hospital Referral Support","The CST has also been facilitating access to hospital care for those who develop a severe disease.",""],[1,"650","4","Community-Based Disease Prevention and Quarantine Response","MoHFW has rapidly implemented community-based prevention practices, case identification, and quarantining utilizing local community health capacity for slowing the spread of disease following lockdown.","MoHFW"],[1,"650","4","Procurement of PPE and Critical Care Supplies","Immediate action was taken to procure PPE, hospital equipment and supplies required to expand care of critically ill and severe patients.",""],[1,"651","2","COVID-19 Information Updating and Dashboard Monitoring","IEDCR has always been updating the information of COVID-19 in their website.",""],[1,"651","2","COVID-19 Dashboard Development and Daily Updating","A COVID-19 dashboard has also been developed by MIS, DGHS and is updated daily.",""],[1,"651","2","Expanded mHealth Services for COVID-19 Response","In response to COVID- 19, Government has increased capacity of mhealth services \"Shastho Batayon 16263\".",""],[1,"651","5","Compulsory Mask-Wearing and Safe Hygiene Enforcement","Enforcement of compulsory mask-wearing and safe hygiene practices outside the home, including within the workplace, school and, public transport.",""],[1,"651","6","Zoning Approach for Coronavirus Containment","Zoning approach to containment of the spread of corona virus is being followed.",""],[1,"651","7","Community-Based Virus Prevention and Quarantine Measures","Community-based prevention practices, case identification, and quarantining utilizing local community health capacity will be continued to tackle the virus.",""],[1,"651","8","Vaccine Procurement Liaison Mechanism","Maintaining communication and liaison with relevant countries and institutions for timely procurement of vaccines.",""],[1,"651","9","Digital Platform for Disease Spread Reduction and Behavior Change","Use of digital platform for slowing spread of disease and sustaining behavior change following lockdown.",""],[1,"651","10","Social Distancing Regulation Enforcement","Maintenance of social distancing regulations based on latest expert and industry guidance as developed by MoHFW and to be enforced by higher-level committees.","MoHFW"],[1,"651","11","Frontline Health Worker Empowerment and BCC Training","Empowerment of frontline health workers and other essential workers through BCC training to make them agents of change to turn the epidemic around and address their potential COVID-19 related fears and concerns.",""],[1,"651","12","Public Hygiene Awareness Campaign","Continuous use of electronic and print media for raising awareness of mass people in hand washing, mask wearing, maintaining social distance, other safe hygiene practices.",""],[1,"651","13","COVID-19 Pandemic Financing Support","Providing necessary funds to tackle the COVID pandemic.",""]],"124":[[1,"128","3","Human Capital Investment Expansion","The focus will need to shift strongly towards building human capital through much larger investments in health care, education and training, social security",""],[1,"146","2","Public Healthcare Expansion and BDP2100 Implementation","Management of these risks requires active policy responses including a major increase in public healthcare and implementation of the BDP2100.",""],[1,"164","8","Community Clinics and Mental Health Programme","Community Clinics and Mental Health Programme has been taken to ensure primary health care for the rural poor.",""],[1,"169","1","Universal Health Care System","The introduction of a Universal Health Care system financed through a combination of public and private health insurance schemes is of utmost importance in this regard.",""],[1,"173","2","Universal Health Care System Introduction","two important risk mitigation strategies that will be adopted in the 8FYP to minimize the effects of anticipated shocks include ... the introduction of Universal Health Care system",""],[1,"180","11","Increase Public Spending on Education and Health","The first and topmost policy priority is to raise the share of public spending on education and health to at least 3 and 2 percent of GDP respectively.",""],[1,"180","11","Education and Health Service Delivery Reform","This will also require major improvements in the delivery of public education and health services through education policies, governance, and institutional reforms.",""],[1,"184","1","Health System Infrastructure and Management Strengthening","Topmost priority will be given to rebuild the healthcare system through increased budgetary allocations, sharply stronger management of the public healthcare system and partnership with private healthcare.",""],[1,"187","8","Healthcare System Overhaul and Expansion","The most important task is to overhaul and build up the healthcare system of Bangladesh.",""],[1,"814","5","Universal and Affordable Health Care Expansion","Universal and affordable health care for all, full vaccination coverage, universal access to family planning and reproductive health care services, maternity and neo natal care, reduction of maternal mortality, reduction of adolescent pregnancy is some of the key areas to address.",""],[1,"814","5","Skilled and Institutional Childbirth Services","Ensuring all child birth under trained personnel and at institutions, reduction of maternal mortality ratio are also priorities high.",""],[1,"814","5","Adolescent SRHR and Remote Health Service Outreach","In addition, SRHR services for adolescents, reduction of healthcare expenditure, and awareness against taking services from unqualified persons need to be ensured.",""],[1,"814","5","Expansion of Health and Family Planning Services to Remote Areas","Reaching health and family planning services to the remote areas are critical.",""],[1,"816","14","Lifecycle-Based Women's Healthcare Expansion","a lifecycle-based healthcare system including tertiary care should be accessible to women within affordable cost.",""],[1,"816","14","Health Information and Motivational Campaigns","Investment on information and motivational campaigns for the need and availability of immunization, preventive care and screening services for all children, adolescents and women should be enhanced.",""],[1,"816","14","Primary Health Care and Immunization Expansion","The primary health care, immunization, maternal and ante-natal care for pregnant women and post-natal care services should be expanded in all areas and ensure equal immunization for men and women, boys and girls in the rural and",""],[1,"817","1","Reproductive Health Information and Motivation Campaigns","Information and motivation campaigns should be enhanced for reproductive healthcare, and protection from harmful diseases like Dengue, Chikungunya, HIV/AIDS and diseases associated with childbirth.",""],[1,"817","1","Low-Cost National Laboratory Testing Access","Laboratory testing for these diseases should be available at a low cost all over the country.",""],[1,"817","1","Expansion of Women and Child Friendly Hospitals","Women and child friendly hospitals should be expanded to all districts and upazilas.",""],[1,"817","1","District-Level Tertiary Care Strengthening","Tertiary care for major diseases including surgery and geriatric care should be ensured at the district levels.",""],[1,"817","1","Senior Citizen Health Service Registration and Tracking System","Registration and tracking of services and universal health insurance for the senior citizens should be introduced.",""],[1,"817","1","Universal Health Insurance for Senior Citizens","Registration and tracking of services and universal health insurance for the senior citizens should be introduced.",""],[1,"817","1","Expanded HIV Testing and Counselling for High-Risk Groups","HIV testing and counselling should be scaled up for high risk groups, migrant labourers and their spouses",""],[1,"817","3","Community-Based Reproductive Health and Family Planning Services","Counselling services on population control, reproductive health and behaviour and family planning services should continue and expand at community levels in both rural and urban areas.",""],[1,"817","3","Low-Cost Modern Contraceptive Access and Outreach","Motivation in urban slums and remote areas on modern contraceptives and availability of modern contraceptives at a low cost should be ensured.",""],[1,"817","3","Adolescent Reproductive Health Education in Schools","Teaching of the reproductive health education for adolescents in the school curriculum should be ensured.",""],[1,"817","3","Targeted Reproductive Health Support in Lowest-Performing Districts","In the lowest performing districts additional support is needed for awareness raising, and education on reproductive health among young boys and girls to prepare them as future adults.",""]],"125":[[1,"661","1","Strengthening of the National Tobacco Control Cell","During 8FYP, the NTCC will be strengthened by building capacity, advocacy and awareness campaigns.","MoHFW"],[1,"661","1","Community-Based Substance Abuse Management and Anti-Tobacco Messaging Programme","Innovative community-based management programmes, training material development, support for research on substance abuse etc. will be promoted by the Bureau of Health Education for mounting anti-tobacco and anti-substance use messages.",""],[1,"661","2","Public Awareness Campaign Against Illicit Drug Use","During the 8FYP period, MoHFW will continue public awareness building activities against illicit use of drugs including 'Yaba', 'Phensedyl, and 'Heroine' abuse.","MoHFW"],[1,"661","2","School-Based Substance Abuse Education Programme","Health education programme against addictive substance abuse will be introduced in educational institutes.",""],[1,"661","2","Substance Abuse Diagnosis, Treatment, and Rehabilitation Capacity Expansion","Capacity for diagnosis, treatment and rehabilitation of substance abuse will be increased.",""],[1,"661","2","Specialized Drug Rehabilitation Center Establishment","Necessary steps will be taken to establish required specialized rehabilitation centers for the drug addicted patients during the 8FYP.",""]],"126":[[1,"346","12","Rural Health Centre Strengthening for Maternal and Child Care","Strengthen rural health centres with focus on mother, adolescent child and neo-natal care.",""],[1,"346","13","Immunization Drive Strengthening","Strengthen immunization drive.",""],[1,"346","18","Modern Family Planning Methods Expansion","Expand and strengthen modern family planning methods.",""]],"127":[[1,"346","14","District Tertiary Public Health Facility Upgrading and Expansion","Upgrade and expand district tertiary public health care facilities.",""],[1,"346","15","Public Medical Staff Training and Capacity Strengthening","Strengthen quantity and quality of public medical staff through proper training.",""],[1,"346","16","Expansion of Higher Medical Education Facilities","Expand higher medical education facilities for creating specialized health workforce.",""],[1,"346","17","Medical and Nursing Education Quality Improvement","Expand and improve the quality of medical, nursing and other medical technical education for producing quality doctors, nurse and other technical personnel.",""]],"128":[[1,"653","4","Inclusive Education Service Delivery through Private Sector, PPP, and NGO Engagement","Increasing access to and utilization of quality services by adopting more inclusive approach - engaging the private sector for ESP delivery, public - private partnership (PPP) and NGOs.",""],[1,"653","16","Urban Primary Health Care Access and Coordinated Service Delivery","Plan to ensure that the growing number of urban residents, including the poor, have secured access to primary health care services including water, sanitation, etc. by addressing the safety concerns of women, girls, children and older persons, and by ensuring more coherent and coordinated service delivery at the national level.",""],[1,"654","5","Urban Primary Health Care Service Restructuring","Reviewing and restructuring of urban primary health care services for catering to the needs of rapidly expanding urban population.",""],[1,"656","1","Urban Health and Nutrition Services Coordination and Quality Control Mechanism","health and nutrition services in urban areas which requires increased efforts for coordination and quality control through sustained regulatory mechanisms.",""],[1,"656","2","Permanent Urban Health Coordination Structure","There is need to establish a permanent coordination structure between the two Ministries to take up the mutual mandated responsibility in a sustained and effective manner.","MoHFW | MoLGRD&C"],[1,"656","2","Consultative Planning for Urban Health and Nutrition Services","MoHFW will join in tackling this challenge through a consultative process with MoLGRD&C, city corporations and concerned stakeholders to jointly assess, map, project and plan HPN services in urban areas.","MoHFW | MoLGRD&C"],[1,"656","3","Expansion of Urban Primary Health Care Services","MoHFW will seek to extend the coverage of UPHC services through the urban dispensaries under the DGHS, which are in the process of improvement by strengthening referral system in the facilities, so that the population receives better health and nutrition services.","MoHFW | DGHS"],[1,"656","3","Urban Hospital-Based UPHC Service Strengthening","MoHFW will also provide UPHC services through the outdoors of secondary and tertiary hospitals of urban areas that will continue to be strengthened.","MoHFW"],[1,"656","3","Evening Shift Expansion for UPHC Service Delivery","Moreover, the UPHC service will be strengthened through introducing evening shifts in terms of coverage, quality and equity of service delivery in response to demand.",""],[1,"656","4","Urban Health and Nutrition Strategy with Time-Bound Action Plan","Developing an urban health and nutrition strategy with time bound action plan in collaboration with MoLGRD&C.","MoLGRD&C"],[1,"656","5","Urban Health Population Needs Study and Joint Ministry Service Coordination","Commissioning a study to review and determine how the urban population can be best served and the two Ministries can jointly work together to provide quality HPN services.",""],[1,"656","6","Urban Health and Nutrition Governance Mechanism","Establishing a permanent institutional arrangement and governance mechanism incorporating relevant ministries, agencies and institutions with responsibility to urban health and nutrition.",""],[1,"656","7","Urban Dispensary Expansion and Upgrading for Primary Health Care","Expanding/upgrading urban dispensaries for quality PHC services (including services for reproductive health, nutrition, health education and screening of diabetes and hypertension).",""],[1,"656","8","Urban Referral System and GP Feasibility Study","Defining an adequate referral system between the various urban dispensaries and the second and third level hospitals, and exploring feasibility of introducing General Physician (GP) system.",""],[1,"656","12","Health Service Delivery Expansion through Public-Private Partnerships","Expanding health service delivery through PPPs and through diversification of strategies.",""]],"129":[[1,"659","4","Expansion of Public Mental Health Treatment Facilities","where treatment facilities will also be expanded.",""],[1,"659","4","Autism Corners and Child Development Centers","autism corners and child development centers will be established in medical colleges and upazila and district level hospitals.",""],[1,"659","4","Autism Genetic Testing Facilities","Genetic testing facilities for autism (in genetic origin) will be developed in every medical college hospital.",""],[1,"660","2","Early Hearing Loss Detection and Management Initiative","Early detection at the primary level and management of these cases at the secondary and tertiary level will be initiated for control of hearing disability (Deafness) during the 8FYP.",""],[1,"662","3","Strengthening of Ayurvedic, Unani and Homeopathic Medicine Services","During 8FYP, required strengthening of the research, monitoring, production and publication, workshop and training will be made.",""],[1,"662","3","Strengthening of Existing AMC Colleges and Hospitals","Existing two AMC colleges and hospitals including outdoor services will also be strengthened.",""]],"130":[[1,"659","5","Elderly and Palliative Health Care Service System Development","There is a need for reorienting the existing institutional arrangements for health service delivery and to increase investment - both financial and human resources - in developing an appropriate Elderly and Palliative Health Care (EPHC) service system.","MoHFW"],[1,"659","5","Multi-sector Collaboration for Elderly and Palliative Care","MoHFW will promote multi-sector collaboration with other ministries (e.g., Ministry of Social Welfare), private sector, NGOs, CSOs, etc. for providing EPHC- friendly health care in the country.","MoHFW | Ministry of Social Welfare"],[1,"659","5","Palliative Care Unit Expansion in Medical College Hospitals","During the 8FYP period, awareness building, establishing palliative care units in all medical college hospitals, introducing modern medicines and advance equipment to all medical college",""],[1,"660","1","Palliative Care Measures","steps will be taken up regarding palliative care.",""],[1,"660","1","Elderly Health Expenditure Card","Special card for the elderly people to reduce health expenditure in hospitals will be introduced.",""],[1,"660","1","Geriatric Health Workforce Capacity Development","Capacity of the health workforce regarding handling the geriatric patient will be enhanced.",""]],"131":[[1,"660","6","Health System Emergency Preparedness and Response Strengthening","during 8FYP the main strategic aims are to increase the level of readiness at all tiers of the health system and improve the capacity of the sector for coordinated post-disaster management.",""],[1,"660","6","Mass Casualty Management Guidelines and Local Health Response Manual","Standard national guidelines for mass casualty management as well as manual for local level health response will be issued and necessary training will be conducted.",""],[1,"661","4","Climate Change and Health Promotion Unit","To build capacity and strengthen health systems to combat the health impact of climate change, the Climate Change and Health Promotion Unit (CCHPU) has been formed to strengthen necessary activities.",""],[1,"661","5","Health System Emergency Preparedness Strengthening","During 8FYP, the level of readiness at all tiers of the health system will be strengthened for emergency response;",""],[1,"661","5","Coordinated Post-Disaster Health Management Capacity Building","capacity of the sector will be increased for coordinated post-disaster management and protecting people's health from climate change.",""],[1,"662","1","Local-Level Health Response Manual and Emergency Preparedness Strengthening","as manual for local level health response will be issued, necessary training will be conducted and emergency health supplies and their stockpiling will be standardized.",""],[1,"662","1","Health Sector Partnership for Emergency Preparedness","Partnership will be forged with disaster management agencies, groups and individuals for improving emergency preparedness, prevention and mitigation.",""],[1,"662","1","Climate and Health Research Agenda Expansion","The existing health research agenda will include the adverse effect of climate change on health, and field surveys and studies will be conducted to identify effects of climate change on health.",""]],"132":[[1,"660","7","Occupational Health and Safety Preventive and Control Measures","During 8FYP, HSD will continue its preventive and control measures in collaboration with other relevant ministries (e.g., Ministry of Industries, Ministry of Labor and Employment) to address occupational health hazards, diseases and risks in a cost-effective manner.","HSD | Ministry of Industries | Ministry of Labor and Employment"]],"133":[[1,"662","4","Behavior Change Communication for Health and Social Awareness","BCC activities of the Bureau of Health Education (BHE) are intended to bring about behavioral changes among the people towards safe motherhood, breast feeding, climate change, emerging and re-emerging diseases, food safety, vaccination, vitamin A administration, neonatal care, violence against women, nutrition etc. through special emphasis on interpersonal communication, electronic and print media.",""],[1,"662","4","Comprehensive Community Health Education Programme","Comprehensive BCC programmes will be developed in building community knowledge and skills to promote use of MNCH services and to enhance basic health education in schools/madrassas for children",""],[1,"663","1","Health and Nutrition Behaviour Change Communication Campaign","Promoting health and nutrition services through electronic and print media and motivational programmes in the form of feature films, posters, local dramas, etc. will continue to be the materials of BCC activities.",""],[1,"665","3","Social Behaviour Change Communication for Healthy Lifestyles and Environment","promoting healthy lifestyles and environment through comprehensive social behaviour change communication (SBCC) in collaboration with all relevant Government agencies, private sector participants, DPs and other stakeholders.",""]],"134":[[1,"666","6","Health Facility Management and Utilization Improvement","Also strengthen increased use of health facilities along with their professional management.",""],[1,"668","8","Health Facility Development and Upgrading Programme","Facilities will be developed during the 8FYP period to cater to the needs of making public HPN services accessible to the entire population.","Health Engineering Department (HED) | MoHFW"],[1,"681","3","Physical Facilities Establishment, Upgradation, and Maintenance","Establishment of new physical facilities & up-gradation of existing ones and repair and maintenance of the facilities.",""],[1,"681","4","Maternal and Child Welfare Center Upgradation","Upgradation of Maternal and Child Welfare Centers (MCWCs) for increasing institutional delivery and quality Maternal, Child, Reproductive and Adolescent Health (MCRAH) services through 24/7 service.",""]],"135":[[1,"668","10","Nutrition Service Continuation Through Government Channels","The key strategies and actions to be pursued during the 8FYP are continuation of nutrition service through regular government channels, micro-nutrient supplementation, treatment of severe acute malnutrition, strengthening BCC to promote good nutritional practices, coordination of nutrition activities across different sectors and mainstreaming gender into nutrition programming and promoting equity.",""],[1,"668","10","Micronutrient Supplementation Programme","The key strategies and actions to be pursued during the 8FYP are continuation of nutrition service through regular government channels, micro-nutrient supplementation, treatment of severe acute malnutrition, strengthening BCC to promote good nutritional practices, coordination of nutrition activities across different sectors and mainstreaming gender into nutrition programming and promoting equity.",""],[1,"668","10","Severe Acute Malnutrition Treatment","The key strategies and actions to be pursued during the 8FYP are continuation of nutrition service through regular government channels, micro-nutrient supplementation, treatment of severe acute malnutrition, strengthening BCC to promote good nutritional practices, coordination of nutrition activities across different sectors and mainstreaming gender into nutrition programming and promoting equity.",""],[1,"668","10","Nutrition Behavior Change Communication Strengthening","The key strategies and actions to be pursued during the 8FYP are continuation of nutrition service through regular government channels, micro-nutrient supplementation, treatment of severe acute malnutrition, strengthening BCC to promote good nutritional practices, coordination of nutrition activities across different sectors and mainstreaming gender into nutrition programming and promoting equity.",""],[1,"668","10","Gender Mainstreaming in Nutrition Programming","The key strategies and actions to be pursued during the 8FYP are continuation of nutrition service through regular government channels, micro-nutrient supplementation, treatment of severe acute malnutrition, strengthening BCC to promote good nutritional practices, coordination of nutrition activities across different sectors and mainstreaming gender into nutrition programming and promoting equity.",""],[1,"668","10","Nutrition Supply Chain Strengthening","Simultaneously, availability of adequate skilled human resources and nutrition logistics and commodities through improved supply chain management will be prioritized and ensured.",""],[1,"670","12","Multidimensional Nutrition and Micronutrient Intervention Package","To that end, the Government will consider a multidimensional approach to address the intergenerational health impact.",""],[1,"670","12","Infant and Young Child Feeding Strategy Implementation","The national strategy for infant and young child feeding will be implemented.",""],[1,"670","12","Vitamin A Supplementation Distribution","Existing half-yearly Vitamin A capsules distribution for children will be continued.",""],[1,"670","12","Post-partum Vitamin A Distribution Scale-up","Post-partum Vitamin A distribution to improve vitamin A status of neonates through breast milk will be scaled up.",""],[1,"670","12","Salt Iodization Monitoring Strengthening","Monitoring of salt iodization will be strengthened.",""],[1,"670","12","Zinc Treatment Promotion for Diarrhoea","Zinc for treatment of diarrhoea will be adequately promoted.",""],[1,"670","12","Intestinal Parasite Treatment and Deworming Expansion","Expansion of intestinal parasite treatment, including the distribution of albendazole tablets, along with a separate deworming programme will be considered.",""],[1,"670","12","IMCI Zinc Tablet Provision","With the coverage of IMCI, zinc tablets are expected to be freely provided to children with diarrhoea.",""],[1,"671","2","Vitamin A Supplementation, Deworming, and Food Fortification for Children","Providing high potency Vitamin, A supplementation and de-worming to children during measles vaccination and to children 1-5 years during national events and through fortification of food with vitamin A, iron and iodine for children.",""],[1,"671","3","Micronutrient Supplementation for Mothers and Newborns","Providing micronutrient supplementation to pregnant women (Iron folate) and Vitamin-A supplementation to mothers and neonates at postnatal period.",""],[1,"671","4","Nutrition Education and Counseling for Women and Adolescent Girls","Providing nutritional education and counseling to adolescent girls, pregnant and lactating mothers on appropriate caring and feeding practices, breast-feeding, supplementary feeding, micronutrients, etc.",""],[1,"671","5","Wasting Prevention and Treatment Quality Improvement Programme","Strengthen quality improvement of the wasting prevention and treatment programme, and other nutrition services at facility level.",""],[1,"671","6","Community-Based Malnutrition Prevention and Nutrition Services Expansion","Ensuring expansion of community-based prevention approach of malnutrition with nutrition services through C- IMCI programmes as preventive measures to malnourishment along with programmes in the CCs and managing malnourished cases at community and facility level, IYCF, etc.",""],[1,"671","7","Social Behaviour Change Communication for Nutrition Improvement","Improve positive nutrition practices through Social Behaviour Change Communication (SBCC) including awareness on uptake of essential nutrition services from public and private facilities and at community level, as well as on food safety and healthy diet, as well as complementary issues such as water and sanitation, EPI, and prevention of NCDs.",""],[1,"671","11","Growth Monitoring and Promotion Integration in EPI Platforms","Integrate growth monitoring and promotion in EPI platforms",""]],"136":[[1,"679","5","Sexual and Reproductive Health Outreach Campaign","Strengthen the outreach and campaign on sexual education and reproductive health issues to increase the adoption of modern contraceptive practices with special attention to the lagging districts, the rural poor, the urban slums and the adolescent girls.",""],[1,"679","5","Rural Health Clinic Strengthening for Contraceptive Services","The rural health clinics (Community Health Clinics and Union Health and Family Welfare Centers) need to be adequately staffed and equipped to meet the demand for modern contraceptive devices and counselling.",""],[1,"679","5","NGO Community Health Worker Partnership Expansion","Partnership with NGO-based community health workers should be strengthened to reach out the women in the urban slums and to provide services to rural women at the door step.",""],[1,"680","4","Family Planning Outreach Expansion","Progress with the implementation of the highly successful family planning activities will continue in the 8FYP with focus on reaching out the less-served areas and adolescent girls who face the greatest risk of early pregnancies.",""],[1,"680","5","Family Planning Target Achievement Measures","Gear up all kinds of activities for achieving FP related targets by 2025 through increasing use of CPR by 75%, institutional delivery by 72% by the SBAs and through 24/7 services, etc.",""],[1,"680","5","Reduce Family Planning Dropout and Unmet Need","Also reducing dropout rates and unmet needs to 15% and 8% respectively.",""],[1,"680","6","Urban Family Planning and Reproductive Health Service Expansion","Strengthen urban FP services by expanding FP, mother, child, reproductive and adolescent health services in the city corporations.",""],[1,"680","7","Unit-wise Family Planning Expansion in Sitmahals","Expand unit-wise FP activities in the Sitmahals.",""],[1,"680","8","Additional Adolescent-Friendly Service Centres","Establish additional adolescent friendly 200 service centres.",""],[1,"681","5","Family Planning Service Expansion in Urban Areas","Expansion of FP service in City Corporation, pouroshova, cantonment areas, etc.",""],[1,"823","4","Reproductive Health Information and Education Expansion","Information and education should be available to enhance women's control over their own reproductive health.",""],[1,"823","4","Reproductive Health Education for Employment and Self-Reliance","The education for employment and economic gain for women's self-reliance and confidence should include information on elements of reproductive health care, and availability of such care.",""],[1,"823","4","Counselling Services in All Health Care Centres","Counselling services should be made available in all health care centres for men, women and couples.",""],[1,"823","4","Inclusive Reproductive Health Care for Single Women","Reproductive health care should also be available to the single women whose needs go unrecognized.",""],[1,"839","5","School-Based Child and Reproductive Health Education","The specific activities will include sensitizing primary and secondary students about critical child health and reproductive health issues, healthy practices and worm infestation, and supplying iron and folic acid tablets for schoolgirls.",""],[1,"839","5","Adolescent Health Strategy Development","Activities will be undertaken to develop an adolescent health strategy including counselling, building awareness for adolescents on hygienic practices, nutrition, puberty, RTI/STD and HIV/AIDS.",""]],"137":[[1,"746","2","Robust Health Referral and Medical History Management System","a) establish a robust referral system with medical history management;",""],[1,"746","2","Real-Time Private Health Facility Data Integration","b) connect all private facilities with the GoB system to get real-time data on patients, ICU, HDU and other facilities;",""],[1,"746","2","Health Facility Inventory Management and Decentralized Procurement System","c) establish inventory management system for all facilities and introduce decentralized procurement;",""],[1,"746","2","ICT-Based Health Grievance Redress Mechanism","d) develop a grievance mechanism policy, addressing system using ICT where sufferers can submit their complaints and receive solutions;",""],[1,"746","2","Coordinated Telemedicine Expansion and Standardization","e) introduce telemedicine in a coordinated and standardized manner, involving community clinics and pharmacies, and policy revisions ensuring service quality and mental health at the forefront.",""],[1,"748","7","Health System Accountability Framework","Development of an accountability framework for both public and private facilities",""]],"138":[[1,"845","9","Universal HIV Treatment, Care and Support Services","People infected and affected by HIV/AIDS will be given universal access to treatment, care and support services.",""],[1,"845","9","Targeted HIV Prevention and Support Services for Key Populations","There will be increased coverage on interventions (basic educational, counselling, referral and legal supportive services) for key populations including people living with HIV, along with implementation of services to prevent new HIV infections.",""],[1,"845","9","Opiate Substitution Therapy for People Who Inject Drugs","This will include opiate substitution therapy for people who inject drugs.",""],[1,"845","9","Public Information Campaign on HIV Treatment Availability","The Government will inform about the availability of effective treatment for adequate and timely antiretroviral treatment, since unawareness may discourage people from getting tested.",""],[1,"845","10","HIV and AIDS Mass Awareness Campaigns","the Government will, in partnership with civil society organisations, undertake mass awareness campaigns and population specific awareness and education campaigns on HIV and AIDS.",""],[1,"845","11","NGO Capacity Building and HIV Outreach Partnership","The Government will work together with NGOs as they are often in a better position than the public sector to expand the outreach of the service to reach more close to the clients, particularly to reach high- risk groups, such as sex workers and injecting drug users.",""],[1,"845","11","NGO Capacity Building for HIV Prevention","The Government will build the capacity of NGOs, especially the small ones, and combine their reach with the resources and strategic programmes of the Government as an effective way to change behaviour in high-risk groups and prevent the spread of HIV virus to the general public.",""]],"139":[[1,"847","4","Early Disability Detection and Primary Medical Rehabilitation","Action will be taken in the health sector to: (i) strengthen early detection of symptoms of disability and provide primary medical rehabilitation;",""],[1,"847","4","Nutrition Programme for Pregnant Women","Action will be taken in the health sector to: (ii) undertake a nutrition programme for pregnant women;",""],[1,"847","4","Training and Deployment of Caregivers for Disability Services","Action will be taken in the health sector to: (iii) appoint trainee doctors, nurses and other caregivers to deal with disability issues;",""],[1,"847","4","Assistive Devices Support Services at Health Centres","Action will be taken in the health sector to: (iv) introduce support services of assistive devices and equipment at health centres.",""],[1,"847","5","Disability Access and Inclusion Measures","Measures will be taken so that persons with disabilities can have access to all physical facilities and information and communication.",""],[1,"847","5","Community-Based Rehabilitation Services for Persons with Disabilities","Services like early detection and timely medical intervention, fitment of artificial aids and appliances, educational services in special and integrated schools, vocational rehabilitation including micro-credit will be provided to persons with disabilities through community based rehabilitation programmes.",""]],"140":[[1,"377","1","Animal Vaccine Subsidy Rationalization","The use of subsidies in vaccine production needs to be rationalized to encourage private investors.",""],[1,"377","1","Standard Vaccination Quality Control System","Quality control for standard vaccination needs to be developed for both local and imported varieties.",""],[1,"377","1","Animal Disease Diagnostic Capacity Expansion","The facilities of disease diagnostic are also limited and there is a shortage of skilled manpower for this.",""],[1,"379","2","Expansion of Veterinary Services to Union Level","Measures will be taken to extend veterinary services up to union level with adequate service provider and infrastructural facilities.",""],[1,"379","2","Autonomous Veterinary Quality Control Agency","An autonomous quality control agency would be established to ensure quality of veterinary drugs, vaccines, feeds, feed ingredients and breeding tools and materials.",""],[1,"379","2","Animal Disease Prevention and Deworming Programme","A massive programme on disease prevention and control of cattle and poultry diseases, awareness building and mass programme for de-worming of animals against parasitic diseases will be designed.",""],[1,"379","2","Private and Community Veterinary Services Development Support","Policy support will be provided to accelerate the development of private and community-based veterinary services, including compliant private veterinary diagnostic centres, clinics and hospitals.",""],[1,"379","3","Poultry Vaccination Coverage Expansion","policy options for vaccine coverage for poultry birds and ensuring quality feed supplies should be looked into.",""]],"141":[[1,"318","2","Remittance Mobilization for Development Finance","To get the most developmental outcome from remittances, one goal of the 8FYP will be to channel remittances as a source of development finance to support development and poverty reduction, including the building of local infrastructure, expansion of CMSMEs, and augmenting productive capacity.",""],[1,"319","2","Remittance Mobilization and Productive Use Measures","it will be important to take appropriate policy measures to keep the inflow of remittances on a higher growth trajectory.",""],[1,"319","6","Wallet-to-Wallet Remittance Flow Promotion","Encouraging wallet-to-wallet remittance flows with cash transfers in increasing saving by recipients (and senders)",""],[1,"320","3","Bank-Post Office Partnership for Remittance Delivery","Remittance impact could be maximized by establishing partnerships between leading banks and the government post office network in countries that do not have access to banking services in rural areas",""],[1,"320","5","Financial Product Regulation Easing for Low-Income Migrant Households","Regulations must be eased so that there's a wider range of financial products available to low- income migrant households.",""],[1,"321","1","PKB Service Innovation and Diversification Reform","The ability of PKB to function properly to serve the needs of the Migrant workers requires innovation, service and product diversification for various stages of migration, service to the families of the migrants and bringing commercial principles of operation.",""]],"142":[[1,"283","2","Tariff Modernisation and Trade Policy Reform Programme","Streamlining trade and tariff policies calls for a five-year program of adjustment culminating in a trade and tariff regime that is reflective of or trending towards a UMIC economy, a goal that is set for 2031 in the Bangladesh Perspective Plan 2021-41.",""],[1,"285","7","Tariff Regime Restructuring and Rationalization","Bangladesh faces an immediate challenge to restructure its tariff regime in order to gradually phase out effective protection levels and anti-export bias.",""],[1,"285","8","Phased Removal of Industrial Protection","Protection, particularly for those industries that have enjoyed protection for ten years or more, will have to be phased out in five years.",""],[1,"285","8","Time-Bound and Performance-Based Protection Regime","Activities that have enjoyed protection for less than ten years will have to be notified that further protection will be made time-bound and performance-based on output/employment or exports.",""],[1,"287","1","Tariff and Protection Structure Rationalization","The critical step needed to break ground on export diversification and to get traction under these policy circumstances is to rationalize the tariff and protection structure to change the current policy tilt in favour of import substitute production.",""],[1,"287","4","Protection Policy Review and Time-Bound Protection Mechanism","Consider reviewing protection policy, scale down the level of protection, and institute a mechanism of time-bound protection for import-substitutes.",""],[1,"287","5","Tariff Rationalization Strategy","NBR must adopt a strategy of lowering average NPRs by 3-5 percentage points every year until 2025, largely by reducing NPR on import-substitute consumer goods.",""]],"143":[[1,"410","2","Transmission and Distribution System Development","Development of transmission and distribution system in line with generation.",""],[1,"410","3","Private and Joint-Venture Investment Mobilization in the Power Sector","Mobilizing private and joint-venture investment in power sector.",""],[1,"410","9","Cross-Border Electricity Trading Exploration","Exploring electricity-trading options with neighbouring countries (India, Nepal, Bhutan and Myanmar).",""],[1,"413","4","Private Sector Power Generation Mobilization","The Government, as part of the Private Sector Power Generation Policy (PSPGP) of Bangladesh of 1996, has been trying to increase share of the private sector in power generation since the 6FYP, being mindful of the financial constraints in the public sector.",""],[1,"414","2","Regional Power Trade Expansion","Bangladesh has successfully been increasing participation in regional power trade and has been increasing electricity import from India.",""],[1,"414","3","Cross-Border Electricity Trade Facilitation","Bangladesh has also been taking concrete initiatives to help open up new avenues for cross border electricity trade with other neighbouring countries - Nepal, Bhutan and Myanmar - through bilateral cooperation.",""],[1,"414","3","Hydropower Import from Nepal","Efforts are being made for import of hydropower from Nepal.","BPDB"],[1,"414","3","Hydropower Import and Joint Power Plant Development with Bhutan","There is also an initiative to facilitate import hydropower from Bhutan.",""],[1,"414","3","Regional Energy Cooperation through Multilateral Platforms","Bangladesh is also using multilateral platforms like UN-ESCAP, SAARC, BIMSTEC, SASEC and D-8 for increasing regional cooperation in energy trade.",""],[1,"415","4","Transmission and Distribution System Development","Development of transmission and distribution system: Transmission of generated power from power plants to the load centres and then distribution to the end users' needs to be ensured to achieve the real benefits out of successful generation expansion program presented above.",""],[1,"416","2","Integrated Power Distribution Expansion Program","The government, through those entities, has undertaken an integrated power distribution program to increase the distribution network so as to bring 100% of the population under electricity coverage by 2020, while also improving on customer service delivery.",""],[1,"428","3","Benchmark Pricing System for Private Participation in Power Generation","The BERC has now introduced \"benchmark pricing system\" for enhancement of private participation in the power sector.",""],[1,"428","4","Electricity Sector Unbundling and Governance Reform","The unbundling of electricity system along functional lines, substantially improved O&M practices, computerization of metering and billing practices, follow-up on bill payments and accounts receivables suggest considerable improvement in sector governance and management practices.",""],[1,"428","4","Electricity Regulatory and Power Trade Institutional Reforms","The establishment and functioning of the BERC, the successful implementation of the IPP policy and the increase of power trade with India, and initiation of process for power import from Nepal and Bhutan are also important indicators of on-going institutional changes that have already a very positive effect on power sector performance over the longer term.",""],[1,"428","5","Electricity Connection Simplification Reform","Government also has taken action to reduce the required documents and steps for getting electricity connection.",""],[1,"429","5","Power Sector Restructuring and Regulatory Strengthening","Nevertheless, there are several areas where reform efforts need to continue, including: further unbundling where feasible along the functional line; strengthening generation and distribution companies already in place to improve operating performance and customer satisfaction; implementing the power sector restructuring plan; adjusting electricity price gradually to average cost level; and strengthening BERC to be able to perform its agenda on licensing, energy pricing, quality of utility performance including energy efficiency, and consumer satisfaction/dispute resolution.",""],[1,"431","3","Electricity Generation Capacity Expansion","Continue to enhance the generation capacity to match expansion of demand from all segments of the economy, particularly industry and manufacturing, so as to ensure supply of unhindered quality power from the grid, with 100% population connected to quality electricity supply.",""],[1,"431","5","Energy Sector Investment Climate Reform","undertake necessary reforms that can create a more conducive and healthier environment for the participation of private sector (IPPs and PPPs), domestic and foreign, in energy sector development under the supervision of effective regulatory authority.",""],[1,"436","5","Cross-Border Power Trade Expansion","Building on this experience, the Eighth Plan will further expand trade with India and also explore hydropower import opportunities with Nepal and Bhutan.",""],[1,"436","6","Cross-Border Hydropower Import Road Map Implementation","A road map to increase and stabilize the imported power has been proposed in PSMP 2016, which will be strategically considered and implemented during the 8th Plan period.",""],[1,"436","6","Power Import Risk-Mitigation Measures","There are, however, certain challenges/risks, linked to power import, and will need to be addressed, and risk-mitigating measures will have to be put in place.",""],[1,"436","6","PSMP 2016 Power Import Measures Review","In this context some of the measures suggested in the PSMP 2016 document will be considered.",""],[1,"437","1","Transmission and Distribution Coordination Programme","During the 8th Plan period the Government will continue to maintain proper coordination of investment in transmission and distribution to ensure that the benefits of generation investments reach the people.",""],[1,"437","1","Power Supply Quality Improvement Programme","Efforts will also continue to further reduce distribution system losses from 9.35 % in FY2019 to below 7.5 % by FY2025.",""],[1,"437","1","Transmission and Distribution Development Programme","large transmission and distribution development programmes will be needed to ensure uninterrupted power distribution and achieve the target of quality 24/7 power supply for all.",""],[1,"437","1","Northwestern HVDC Interconnection Development","HVDC interconnections with a capacity of around 500-2,000 MW will be required in the north western part of Bangladesh.",""],[1,"437","1","Utility-Led Power Projects","Required projects have been taken by the concerned utilities.",""],[1,"437","2","Electricity Transmission Network Expansion","For meeting growing demand, the Government is giving priority for transmission network development as well, and in this regard plans to construct 3358 ct.km.",""],[1,"437","2","Moheshkhali to Dhaka 765 kV Transmission Line","Besides, it has been planned to construct new 700 ct.km transmission line of capacity 765 kV from power hub being developed at Moheskhali to Dhaka, which will be completed by 2025",""],[1,"437","3","Integrated Power Distribution Programme","An integrated power distribution programme will need to be undertaken to increase the distribution network in order to bring 100% population under electrification by 2020 as well as improving the customer service.",""],[1,"437","3","Electricity Loss Reduction and Bill Collection Initiative","Government also wants to further reduce system loss and collect the outstanding bills, and provide 100% access to electricity to households.",""],[1,"437","4","Power Distribution Digital Modernization","Distribution utilities are now implementing computer-based technologies to modernize their design, planning, and maintenance and analysis applications in an un-integrated way.",""],[1,"438","1","Power Distribution Network Expansion and Automation Projects","a number of distribution projects have been identified for implementation during the period FY 2021-25, which include expansion of network, GIS implementation and SCADA installation.",""],[1,"438","1","Substation and Reactive Power Compensation Investment","Besides there are also 36,590 MVA substations and 955 MVAR capacitor banks for reactive power compensation.",""],[1,"438","2","Rural Electricity Distribution System Expansion and Upgrading","Bangladesh Rural Electrification Board (BREB) has been investing in development, expansion and up-gradation of existing distribution system to help achieve 100% access to electricity.","Bangladesh Rural Electrification Board (BREB)"]],"144":[[1,"120","1","Renewable Energy Access and Promotion Initiative","Promoting efficient and renewable energy which will enable increased access to energy creating new business opportunities and employment.",""],[1,"164","7","Electricity for All Initiative","Electricity for All initiative aims to provide electricity to every household in order to increase national growth, alleviating poverty and developing the country's socio-economic and human resources.",""],[1,"417","4","Renewable Energy Expansion by BREB","BREB, which has been the pioneer of Solar Home System, continues its pursuit in providing renewable energy.",""],[1,"419","2","Aggressive Renewable Energy Generation Strategy","During the 8FYP the RE generation strategy will have to be aggressively pursued so that all that is planned gets implemented in time and where policy support is required should be given forthwith.",""],[1,"426","1","Renewable Energy Policy Implementation and SREDA Establishment","After the formulation and start of implementation of renewable energy policy from 2009, the government had established 'Sustainable and Renewable Energy Development Authority (SREDA)' in 2014 under Sustainable and Renewable Energy Development Authority Act, 2012 to facilitate sustainable energy i.e. renewable energy as well as energy efficiency.",""],[1,"426","2","Renewable Energy Expansion Programme","The Eighth plan will continue on the seventh plan focus on two main areas of renewable energy: solar and wind power.",""],[1,"426","2","Solar Home Lighting and Rooftop PV Deployment","There is already significant success in the area of solar energy in home lighting.",""],[1,"426","4","Renewable Energy Policy Implementation Improvement","There will be renewed effort to improve the focus and implementation of the RE policy during the 8th plan period.",""],[1,"427","6","Country Action Plan for Clean Cook Stove","Preparation and implementation of Country Action Plan for Clean Cook Stove",""],[1,"427","9","Grid Integration Guidelines for Solar Irrigation Pumps","Formulation of Guidelines for the Grid Integration of Solar Irrigation Pumps-2020",""],[1,"431","6","Energy Mix Optimization and Renewable Energy Expansion","Enhance the exploitation of gas, coal, renewable resources, increased energy imports particularly hydropower from neighbouring Bhutan and Nepal in order to optimize the energy mix and reduce the dependence on imported furnace oil and HSD.",""],[1,"434","4","Renewable Energy Expansion Plan","There is also plan for adding 2,362 MW renewable energy, which is given in Table 5.18 below.",""],[1,"435","4","Renewable Energy Expansion Programme","efforts underway to increase share of renewable energy (RE) in share of fuel mix during the 8th plan and beyond.",""],[1,"435","4","Renewable Energy Generation Capacity Target","The government has set an ambitious target of achieving 10% of total power generation capacity from renewable energy.",""],[1,"435","5","Renewable Energy Policy and Regulatory Support","the government has been taking different policy and regulatory actions to facilitate scope for increased production of environment- friendly electricity from renewable energy.",""],[1,"435","5","Private Sector Renewable Energy Supply Expansion","One key strategic focus proposed under the PP2041 strategy will be the encouragement of RE supply by private producers, including supply to the grid as well as direct sales to households.",""],[1,"435","5","SREDA Renewable Energy Investment Facilitation and Regulation","SREDA has been facilitating and regulating private and public investments in renewable energy.",""],[1,"435","5","Private Delivery of Commercial Renewable Energy Projects","There is a decision that the commercial RE projects were to be implemented by the private sector (IPPs), while social projects by the different ministries and agencies as a part of social responsibility of the Government.",""],[1,"436","1","Grid-Connected Solar Park Development","Some of the identified commercial projects that can be implemented by the private sector are: (a) Solar Park (grid connected);",""],[1,"436","1","Solar Irrigation Deployment","Some of the identified commercial projects that can be implemented by the private sector are: (b) Solar Irrigation;",""],[1,"436","1","Solar Mini-Grid and Micro-Grid Deployment","Some of the identified commercial projects that can be implemented by the private sector are: (c) Solar Mini-grid/micro-grid;",""],[1,"436","1","Solar Rooftop Deployment","Some of the identified commercial projects that can be implemented by the private sector are: (d) Solar rooftop.",""],[1,"436","1","Rural Health Centre Electrification with Solar Power","The social projects are: (a) Rural health centres;",""],[1,"436","1","Remote Educational Institute Electrification with Solar Power","The social projects are: (b) Remote educational institutes;",""],[1,"436","1","Union e-Centre Electrification with Solar Power","The social projects are: (c) Union e-Centres;",""],[1,"436","1","Remote Religious Establishment Electrification with Solar Power","The social projects are: (d) Remote Religious Establishment;",""],[1,"436","1","Off-Grid Railway Station Electrification with Solar Power","The social projects are: (e) Off-grid Railway Stations;",""],[1,"436","1","Off-Grid Government Office Electrification with Solar Power","The social projects are: (f) Government and Semi-Government Offices in the off-grid areas.",""],[1,"436","2","Competitive Bidding and Incentive Support for Renewable Energy IPPs","Bangladesh is currently preparing the competitive bidding by IPPs, drafting FIT and providing other incentives (mainly financial ones) for renewable energy businesses.",""],[1,"436","2","Grid Network and Operations Capacity Upgrade","As Bangladesh increases the grid-connected renewable generation capacity, network and operation capacity will also need to be improved.",""],[1,"436","3","Renewable Energy Generation Expansion","There have also been initiatives by BPDB and through IPPs to increase renewable energy generation, by way of solar power projects, utility scale PV projects, and wind energy projects.",""],[1,"436","4","Waste-to-Energy Project Implementation","Thus, BPDB has undertaken the adoption/implementation of waste-to-energy (WTE) projects in various city corporations / major municipalities in the IPP sector as a ground-breaking step of the government for power generation from waste with utmost importance on waste management.",""]],"145":[[1,"410","6","Power Sector Efficiency and Loss Reduction","Improving power sector efficiency and reducing transmission and distribution losses.",""],[1,"419","5","Full Cost Recovery for Power and Energy Products","Full cost recovery for all power and energy products is an important goal for the 8FYP.",""],[1,"420","2","Power Sector Financial Action Plan","the government has adopted a financial action plan to maintain power sector receivable at no more than 2 months' billed amount equivalent and reduce receivables from autonomous, public entities and private customers to an acceptable limit.",""],[1,"421","1","Review of IPP Regime and Power Purchase Agreements","an area that needs to be revisited is the IPP regime and the PPAs to see if improvements can be made, particularly in areas like possibility of further transferring commercial risks to the private producers.",""],[1,"421","2","Pre-Paid Meter Installation Reform","The reforms for reducing system loss continue through installation of pre-paid meters.",""],[1,"426","5","Energy Efficiency and Conservation Programme","The Government continued to accord high priority to the promotion of Energy Efficiency (EE) and Energy Conservation (EC) programmes during the Seventh Plan, with aim of achieving energy conversation targets of 15% by 2020 and 20% by 2030; putting in place energy efficiency and savings programmes for electrical and electronic appliances; and implementation of energy standard and energy star labelling program by BSTI.",""],[1,"426","5","Energy Efficiency and Conservation Master Plan","The government has formulated 'Energy Efficiency and Conservation Master Plan up to 2030', and 'Energy Efficiency and Conservation Rules and Action Plan', and numbers of interventions have been identified for implementation within stipulated time.",""],[1,"427","3","Energy Efficiency and Conservation Promotion Financing Project","'Energy Efficiency and Conservation Promotion Financing Project' has been started to promote energy efficiency in industries as well as in residential sector through introducing energy efficient equipment, appliances and electrical gadgets at 4 per cent interest loan",""],[1,"427","5","Energy Efficiency and Conservation in Building Code","Provision of Energy Efficiency and Energy Conservation has been included in 'Bangladesh National Building Code",""],[1,"427","7","Improved Rice Parboiling System Implementation","Implementation of Improved Rice Parboiling System",""],[1,"427","12","Energy Price Adjustment by BERC","During the 8th Plan period price adjustments by BERC will need to be pursued so that need for subsidy can be avoided, and resources used for necessary investments in the energy sector.",""],[1,"428","2","Bangladesh Energy Regulatory Commission Tariff Regulation","The energy sector is regulated by Bangladesh Energy Regulatory Commission (BERC) to look after the tariff of the consumer and industry.",""],[1,"428","2","BPDB Strategic Business Unit Reform","BPDB is in the process of identifying Strategic Business Unit (SBU) for its generation and distribution sectors as a new reform initiative.",""],[1,"430","4","Power Sector Efficiency and Loss Reduction Strategy","the strategic focus needs to not only having a generation pipeline that will be meeting the demand, but also to ensure better quality and efficiency in (a) generation through ensuring optimal primary fuel mix, including efforts to make increased use of domestic coal and gas through mining and exploration; (b) transmission and distribution of electricity through further reduction of T&D losses; and (c) maximizing use of renewable energy and energy trade.",""],[1,"431","2","Least-Cost Power Production and Grid Loss Reduction","Move to an efficient least-cost power production structure based on (a) an optimal and efficient primary fuel mix; and (b) transmission, and distribution of electricity through further reduction of T&D losses;",""],[1,"431","4","Regular Power Tariff Adjustment Reform","have regular power tariff adjustments to ensure long term sustainability of power generation and moving away from budgetary subsidy that is now prevalent.",""],[1,"431","8","Energy Efficiency and Conservation through Demand-Side Management","Improve Energy Efficiency & Conservation through demand side management.",""],[1,"432","5","Power Utility Financial Viability Improvement","Another strategic action that will be untaken during the 8th plan will be to improve financial viability of all the power utilities through regular prices adjustments.",""],[1,"432","5","Transmission and Distribution Loss Reduction","All aspects of cost reductions including further reduction in T&D system losses and achieving the strategic goal of least- cost power generation will help contain the cost of power generation and power prices.",""],[1,"438","3","Power Plant Operations and Maintenance Improvement Strategy","During the 8FYP this PP2041 strategy will be implemented and a key target will be to improve the efficiency of the power plants with increased focus on O&M.",""],[1,"438","4","Energy Efficiency and Conservation Measures","several new policies have been adopted to conserve power and improve the operational efficiency of the power sector.",""],[1,"438","4","Energy Use Efficiency Initiatives","It has also undertaken a number of initiatives to ensure efficient use of energy, which will get implemented during the 8FYP.",""],[1,"438","4","National Energy Consumption Savings Target","the Government has set the target of saving l5% of total energy consumption by 2021.",""],[1,"438","5","Efficient Power Procurement for Electricity Investments","So, efficient procurement decisions will be critical to ensuring timely implementation of new electricity investments, and the power utilities will need to",""],[1,"439","1","Efficient Power Plant Contracting and Procurement System","acquire the capability to timely and efficiently implement large power plant contracts.",""],[1,"439","3","Cost-Based Energy Pricing and Cost Recovery Policy","To achieve this objective, power prices will have to be set in ways that enables enterprises to recover the cost of production and earn a reasonable rate of return on assets.",""],[1,"439","3","Clean Energy Pricing and Tax Incentives","proper pricing and taxing can encourage the adoption of clean technology and investments in renewable energy.",""],[1,"440","4","Energy Subsidy and Pricing Reform","The 7th Plan had identified the following policy actions that are needed in the primary energy sector: vii) Energy subsidy and pricing",""],[1,"441","1","Energy Tariff Reform for LPG and Gas Pricing","energy tariff (gas and LPG) reform should simultaneously be applied.",""],[1,"441","1","Biogas Incentive and Utilization Policy","the use of Biogas will have to be incentivized through the gas use policy as the alternative of pipeline natural gas.",""],[1,"442","4","Energy Subsidy and Pricing Policy Coordination","Therefore, the Government needs to determine the extent to which Energy Subsidy could be allowed in high priority sectors that also maintains budgetary discipline.",""],[1,"442","6","Energy Sector Financing Strategy","a sound financing strategy for the energy sector is essential.",""],[1,"442","6","Public-Private Partnership Financing for Power Generation","This will be a combination of PPP financing for power generation plus measures to contain energy subsidies.",""],[1,"442","6","Gradual Reduction of Power Subsidies","The Eighth Plan assumes that the subsidy on power will be reduced gradually.",""],[1,"443","1","Targeted Primary Energy Subsidy and Electricity Pricing Reform","For primary energy, the Eighth Plan assumes that the level of subsidy will be capped at around 0.2% of GDP throughout the plan period.",""],[1,"443","1","Targeted Subsidy Support for Renewable Energy Expansion","The subsidy will be targeted to the poor and for supporting the expansion of renewable energy programmes.",""],[1,"443","1","Electricity Cost-Reflective Pricing Policy","In power the Government will ensure that the average price of electricity must be at least equal to the average cost of production.",""],[1,"443","2","Power Sector Restructuring and Corporate Reform","continue unbundling along the functional line, carry out corporatization of generation and distribution, strengthen generation and distribution companies already in place to improve operating performance and customer satisfaction, implement the power sector restructuring plan; upgrade electricity price gradually to cost level and strengthen BERC to be able to perform its agenda on licensing, energy pricing, quality of utility performance including energy efficiency, and consumer satisfaction/dispute resolution.",""],[1,"443","5","Power Sector Commercialization and Financial Management Strengthening","The power sector needs to be run and managed as a commercial enterprise and not as a typical state-owned enterprise.",""],[1,"443","5","Power Sector Financial Management Capacity Improvement","the challenge of generating a surplus in the power sector will require substantial improvement in financial management capabilities of the power sector.",""],[1,"443","5","Power Pricing Regulation through BERC","the de-politicization of power pricing through the BERC has been a positive step forward,",""],[1,"443","5","Power Sector Consumer Service and Public Interface Improvement","There is a lot of effort that is needed in the area of public interface and consumer service.",""],[1,"443","5","Uninterrupted Power Supply and Consumer Grievance Response","Ensuring uninterrupted power service and responding to consumer issues with service quality, billing and payments requires substantial additional effort.",""],[1,"443","6","Electricity Act Amendment and Enforcement Reform","Amendment to the Electricity related Acts could be undertaken regarding several kinds of obligation rules and their penal provisions in order to enhance effectiveness, and thus help with improvement in customer service and ensuring regular quality supply of electricity to end users.",""],[1,"445","3","Foreign Direct Investment Mobilization for Energy","and greater mobilization of FDI in the energy sector.",""]],"146":[[1,"438","4","Energy Efficiency and Conservation Planning and Regulatory Framework","Government has prepared Energy Efficiency & Conservation Master Plans up to 2030, Energy Efficiency & Conservation Rules 2016, Energy Audit Regulation 2018 and Action Plan to ensure Energy Efficiency & Conservation both at supply & demand side.",""],[1,"439","4","Demand-Side Management Policy","Demand-side management (DSM), is being actively pursued by power sector as a means for modifying energy use to maximize energy efficiency, so as to get maximum benefit out of existing energy generation.",""],[1,"439","5","Energy Management Programme","SREDA, which has been set up to support bring efficiency in the energy sector, has been entrusted with following major responsibilities: (1) Energy Management program, which includes (i) certification mechanism of Energy Manager and Energy Auditor, and (ii) designation of large energy consumers in industry and building sectors, those who are obligated to appoint/ nominate energy managers, implement the energy management for energy saving, prepare and submit annual energy reports and",""],[1,"440","1","Energy Audit Improvement Plan for SREDA","improvement plan to SREDA, and implement the energy audit periodically;",""],[1,"440","1","Energy Efficiency Labelling Program","(2) Energy Efficiency Labelling Program, which intends to promote sales of high efficiency products in the market, mainly home appliances such as room air-conditioner, refrigerator/ freezer, TV, motors, lighting, and fan, through officially certified star rating labels on them;",""],[1,"440","1","Energy Efficiency Building Program","(3) Energy Efficiency Building Program which intends to promote energy efficiency in public and private buildings;",""],[1,"440","1","Energy Awareness and Behaviour Change Campaign","(4) Awareness raising program that intends to induce behavioural change among people so that they are motivated to save energy and hence build an energy conscious nation.",""],[1,"440","2","Incentive and Promotional Mechanisms for Energy Conservation","Full implementation would require clear incentive and promotional mechanisms.",""],[1,"440","2","Strengthening SREDA for Energy Conservation Strategy Implementation","Concerted efforts will be needed to make SREDA fully functional with a clear mandate to implement the Government's energy conservation strategy.",""],[1,"440","4","Demand-Side Management and Energy Conservation","The 7th Plan had identified the following policy actions that are needed in the primary energy sector: v) Demand side management and energy conservation",""],[1,"442","2","Demand Side Management and Energy Conservation Measures","The policy effort involves substitution of low thermal efficient gas-fired power plants with more energy efficient plants; incentives for adoption of improved fuel use efficiency and energy conservation technology in industry; and conserving gas consumption by households through proper metering and pricing based on volume of gas consumed rather than a monthly flat rate per stove.",""],[1,"443","4","Power Sector Efficiency and Conservation Policies","Several new policies have been adopted to conserve power and improve the operational efficiency of the power sector.",""],[1,"444","1","Periodic Inspection Institutionalization","So, there is necessity of institutionalization of periodic inspections.",""],[1,"444","1","Technical Standards Institutionalization","There is also necessity of institutionalization of technical standards, so as to regulate and help reduce the amount of accidental trouble and disasters.",""],[1,"444","1","Operations and Maintenance Legal Framework","So, there should still be in place an O&M Legal Framework to ensure that this is achieved.",""],[1,"445","1","Demand-Side Management Coordination Mechanism","The implementation of DSM initiatives will require proper dialogue and coordination with the industry and transport sector.",""]],"147":[[1,"410","4","Primary Fuel Diversification for Electricity Generation","Diversification of primary fuel for electricity generation, with special focus in increasing renewable energy generation.",""],[1,"410","5","Efficient Least-Polluting Coal Power Plant Programme","As part of its pursuit of the strategy of least cost power generation, continue to have some highly efficient least polluting coal plants",""],[1,"421","6","Primary Energy Supply Expansion and Energy Security Measures","The supply of primary energy comprising oil, gas and coal is to help meet energy demand of the country by undertaking exploration, production, development and appraisal of oil, gas, and coal fields and subsequent energy reserve enhancement, and to meet energy shortfalls through imports.",""],[1,"423","5","Liquefied Natural Gas Import and Regasification Initiative","In order to meet demand-supply gap and future growth of energy, the government has taken steps to import LNG.",""],[1,"424","1","Onshore LNG Terminal Development at Matarbari","Government has also a plan to set up an onshore LNG Terminal at Matarbari, Cox's Bazar with a capacity of 7.5 million tons per year having an expansion provision up to 15 million tons per year.",""],[1,"424","1","Feasibility Study for BOOT-Based LNG Terminal Investment","Before construction of onshore (Land Based) LNG terminal, Government has decided to conduct Feasibility Study to attract the investors in construction of the terminal on BOOT basis.",""],[1,"424","2","Development of Jamalganj and Khalaspir Coal Fields","Petrobangla has a plan to develop other two coal fields at Jamalganj and Khalaspir by the year 2041.",""],[1,"424","3","Phased Domestic Coal Development Strategy","So, a phased approach will be used.",""],[1,"424","3","Rampal Power Project","Several programmes are underway, like the Rampal Power Project using coal imported from India, and the Matarbari Coal Transshipment Terminal (CTT).",""],[1,"424","3","Matarbari Coal Transshipment Terminal","Several programmes are underway, like the Rampal Power Project using coal imported from India, and the Matarbari Coal Transshipment Terminal (CTT).",""],[1,"424","4","Petroleum Storage and Supply Capacity Expansion","BPC has taken several initiatives, including setting up a new unit of the existing refinery (ERL Unit-2) of the 'Eastern Refinery Limited (ERL)'. and initiating several pipeline projects to improve supply capacity.","Bangladesh Petroleum Corporation (BPC) | Eastern Refinery Limited (ERL)"],[1,"425","6","Fuel Oil Quality Assurance and Anti-Adulteration Measures","Thus, lack of quality and quantity assurance in terms of procuring fuel oil is one of the serious concerns in this sector, and needs to be addressed and rectified during the 8FYP period.",""],[1,"425","6","Oil and Gas Market Deregulation and Pricing Reform","PP2041, as part of long-term strategy, has expressed intention to broaden the role of the private sector in the development of the oil and gas markets through deregulation and pricing reforms.",""],[1,"425","7","Primary Fuel Infrastructure Development for Power Generation","Develop the required infrastructure for primary fuel to bring efficiency in power production: LNG and imported coal will grow to be the key primary fuel source for generating power; and both are heavily infrastructure-dependent fuel options.",""],[1,"425","7","Coordination of Power and Fuel Infrastructure Investments","Without proper coordination, the related power investments will fail to deliver.",""],[1,"429","7","Primary Fuel Supply Diversification and Expansion","the progress with diversifying and increasing the supply of primary fuel has been very limited, though some large-scale coal fired power plants are under different stages of implementation and that imported LNG having been added to the pipeline.",""],[1,"430","1","Primary Fuel Policy and Coal Policy Development","Policy on primary fuel, particularly coal policy is urgently needed.",""],[1,"430","1","Institutional Reform for Energy Project Implementation","The other important priority will be to address some of the major institutional constraints that have hampered implementation of energy projects.",""],[1,"430","1","PPP Strategy Reform for Primary Energy Investment","There also needs to be reform of the PPP strategy with a view to achieving stronger progress with investments in primary energy during the Eighth Plan.",""],[1,"430","1","Energy Pricing Liberalization and Market-Based Investment Reform","This will need to change as country moves towards with greater reliance on market forces that will promote greater private investment in the oil market, conserve energy, eliminate the fiscal burden and support the production and use of clean energy.",""],[1,"431","9","National Petroleum Supply Line Network","Establishment of supply line network for the transportation of petroleum in quick, safe, efficient and environment friendly way all over the country.",""],[1,"431","10","Energy Hub Establishment Programme","Establishment of a number of energy hubs in the country including Matarbari Ultra supercritical Coal-fired Power Plant centric energy hub.",""],[1,"439","2","Cross-Border Electricity Trade and Energy Investment Initiative","Capacities need to be strengthened to negotiate and monitor implementation of energy trade contracts with neighbours.",""],[1,"439","2","Regional Energy Import Diversification","Regional opportunities should be explored intensely to secure the energy requirement of the economy.",""],[1,"439","2","Trans-Border Hydropower Import and Power Sector Investment","Hydro-electricity of Bhutan and Nepal can be imported by Bangladesh.",""],[1,"440","4","Gas Allocation Policy","The 7th Plan had identified the following policy actions that are needed in the primary energy sector: i) Gas Allocation Policy",""],[1,"440","4","Domestic Gas Exploration Policy","The 7th Plan had identified the following policy actions that are needed in the primary energy sector: ii) Domestic gas exploration policy",""],[1,"440","4","Domestic Coal Utilization Policy","The 7th Plan had identified the following policy actions that are needed in the primary energy sector: (iii) Domestic coal utilization",""],[1,"440","4","Energy Import Policy","The 7th Plan had identified the following policy actions that are needed in the primary energy sector: iv) Energy import",""],[1,"440","4","Improved Cooking Stove Programme","The 7th Plan had identified the following policy actions that are needed in the primary energy sector: vi) Improved Cooking Stove (ICS)",""],[1,"440","5","Gas Allocation Policy","During the 8th plan period the Government will be encouraged to adopt a gas allocation policy in line with what had been proposed under the 7th plan, so as to best utilize the limited domestic reserve.",""],[1,"441","2","Domestic Gas Exploration and Development Investment","Therefore, Bangladesh will need to focus on investment for exploration and development.",""],[1,"441","2","Joint Venture and Production Sharing Arrangements for Gas Exploration","To address such technical and financial issues, Joint Venture or \"Strategic Partnership\" between BAPEX and foreign companies may be sought or Production Sharing Agreement with IOCs.",""],[1,"441","2","LNG FSRU Terminal Operations","Two LNG FSRU terminals (Excelerate and Summit) are now in operation with a nameplate capacity of 500MMCFD for each terminal.",""],[1,"441","2","Onshore and Offshore Oil and Gas Exploration","Therefore, both onshore and offshore oil and gas options could be pursued.",""],[1,"441","3","Domestic Coal Utilization Policy","Such utilization would contribute to the higher value- added economic activities, and should be directed by the articulated Domestic Coal Utilization Policy, as had been proposed in the 7th plan.",""],[1,"441","4","LNG Supply Diversification and Co-purchasing Measures","it will be critical for Bangladesh to take various measures, such as diversification of gas suppliers, and co- purchasing of natural gas with other countries.",""],[1,"441","4","Periodic Gas Contract Review","periodic contract review to seek more favourable conditions of a contract, while domestic resource development is actively pursued.",""],[1,"442","1","Imported Coal Supply and Energy Hub Development","The Government has launched its program to change power mix ratios and rapidly develop coal-fired power plants.",""],[1,"442","3","Improved Cooking Stove Promotion Programme","During the 8th plan the on-going efforts of the 7th plan will continue with increased focus on implementation of financial incentives and regulatory schemes.",""],[1,"443","3","Revision of the Power Generation Master Plan 2016","The PSMP 2016 needs to be revised in light of the experience during the 7th plan period and also to account possible changes in demand situation, particularly in the aftermath of COVID shock and also any uncertainties in the supply side of primary energy.",""],[1,"443","3","Contingent Backup Power Generation Planning","Based on the findings contingent planning is necessary to have back-up power generation plans that respond to these uncertainties.",""],[1,"444","2","Energy Supply and Power Planning Coordination Mechanism","Effective coordination mechanism to synchronize power and primary energy needs.",""],[1,"445","1","Primary Energy Reform Implementation","The successful implementation of an efficient power generation strategy is critically dependent upon the implementation of these reforms relating to primary energy.",""],[1,"445","1","Energy Market Negotiation Capacity Strengthening","There will be need for improvements in the technical and negotiation capacity of the Ministry and associated energy agencies.","the Ministry | associated energy agencies"],[1,"445","1","Energy Sector Administrative and Technical Capacity Expansion","Administrative and technical capacities also need to expand in a number of areas related to domestic gas exploration, negotiation of IOC investments, development and implementation of renewable energy programmes and the implementation of DSM initiatives.",""]],"148":[[1,"826","4","Women's Energy Access Expansion","Women's access to energy (power, fuel and green) should be increased for reducing their drudgery and saving time for productive employment and increase their access to information.",""],[1,"826","4","Women's Renewable Energy Access Programme","Women's expanded access to renewable energy should be ensured in both grid and off-grid areas to facilitate their economic participation.",""],[1,"826","4","Clean Cooking and Solar Access Support","The energy policy should enhance women's access to solar power, bio-gas, improve cook-stoves etc.",""]],"149":[[1,"843","6","Expand Electricity Supply in the Chittagong Hill Tracts","Supply of electricity through the national grid in different upazilas of the Chittagong Hill Tracts should be increased.",""],[1,"843","6","Solar Electrification for Remote Chittagong Hill Tracts Areas","In the remote areas of the Chittagong Hill Tracts, where electricity is not possible to be accessed through the national grid, it will be necessary to cover the electricity through installation of solar panels in all areas.",""],[1,"843","6","Mobile Network Expansion and Internet Cost Reduction","Necessary steps must be taken to ensure a modern standard of living by expanding the network of mobile phones and reducing the cost of internet.",""],[1,"843","7","Uninterrupted Power Supply for Small and Medium Industries","Besides, uninterrupted power supply must be ensured for the development of small and medium industries.",""]],"150":[[1,"697","1","Education for All Strategy","One of the main focuses of the PP2021 strategy is to achieve Education for All (EFA).",""],[1,"697","1","Non-Formal Education Coverage Expansion","An important component of the government's EFA is the coverage of non-formal education (NFE).",""],[1,"697","1","Adult and Youth Literacy and Continuing Education Programme","Non-Formal Education (NFE) especially literacy and continuing education for adults and youths including life skills & livelihood skills development, is considered as the process of empowerment that contributes to human resource development and poverty reduction.",""],[1,"697","2","Literacy and Non-Formal Education Programmes","The Government has been implementing Literacy/NFE programmes in various forms since its Independence in 1971.",""],[1,"697","2","Non-Formal Education Policy","The government has adopted NFE Policy in 2006 aimed at reducing the number of illiterates, offering need-based continuing education, promotion of equivalency between formal and non-formal education, ensuring community ownership and sustainability of NFE programmes.",""],[1,"698","1","Basic Literacy Project","Since 2014, the BoNFE have been implementing the Basic Literacy Project (64 Districts), with an aim of providing transformative basic literacy skills to 4.5 million between the age of 15 and 45.",""],[1,"698","1","Continuing Education Centres Expansion","A total of 39,331 continuing education centres have been opened nationwide, housed with 78,621 teachers (equal number of male and female students and teachers), and 1,967 supervisors.",""],[1,"702","1","Education Equity and Access Expansion Measures","Accordingly, the government has adopted various policies to improve the equity of education during the 6FYP and the 7FYP.",""],[1,"702","1","Education for All Policy","These include endorsing the education for all (EFA) policy, adopting universal education up to grade 8, providing stipends to girls and the needy, ensuring better access to education facilities at all Thana levels and in remote areas, and spreading the reach of non-formal education.",""],[1,"702","1","Universal Education up to Grade 8","These include endorsing the education for all (EFA) policy, adopting universal education up to grade 8, providing stipends to girls and the needy, ensuring better access to education facilities at all Thana levels and in remote areas, and spreading the reach of non-formal education.",""],[1,"702","1","Education Stipends for Girls and the Needy","These include endorsing the education for all (EFA) policy, adopting universal education up to grade 8, providing stipends to girls and the needy, ensuring better access to education facilities at all Thana levels and in remote areas, and spreading the reach of non-formal education.",""],[1,"702","1","Expansion of Education Facilities in Remote Areas","These include endorsing the education for all (EFA) policy, adopting universal education up to grade 8, providing stipends to girls and the needy, ensuring better access to education facilities at all Thana levels and in remote areas, and spreading the reach of non-formal education.",""],[1,"702","1","Non-formal Education Expansion","These include endorsing the education for all (EFA) policy, adopting universal education up to grade 8, providing stipends to girls and the needy, ensuring better access to education facilities at all Thana levels and in remote areas, and spreading the reach of non-formal education.",""],[1,"711","2","Compulsory Free Twelve-Year Education Expansion","Under the SDG target 4.1, compulsory free education of the first 12 years has to be achieved for all children by 2030.",""],[1,"713","6","Lifelong Learning and Adult Literacy Strategy","The 8FYP will build on the progress made during the 7FYP and continue the march towards 100 per cent adult literacy rate for both male and female by the end of the plan.",""],[1,"713","6","Basic Literacy and Lifelong Learning Support","The strategy will emphasize imparting basic literacy skills with a view to moving towards the global concept of lifelong learning, which has been included in the SDG education goal and targets.",""],[1,"713","6","Non-formal Education Learning Facilities and Resources","This will be done by connecting literacy to basic skills development and lifelong learning opportunities and envisage learning provisions, facilities, and resources complementing and supplementing the formal education system.",""],[1,"713","6","ICT-Enabled Community Learning Centre Network","Widespread use of ICT resources for organised lifelong learning, e.g., through a nationwide network of community learning centres, and expanding self-learning opportunities, will be key features of non-formal education and lifelong learning.",""],[1,"713","6","Lifelong Learning Strategy for Literacy and Life Skills","Literacy level of the population, non-formal and informal livelihood and life skills development, and ICT- based access to information and self-learning tools and resources would be supported and promoted in a coordinated way through a lifelong learning strategy.",""],[1,"714","8","Basic Literacy Project","Continued operation of the Basic Literacy Project;",""],[1,"714","12","Establishment of Non-Formal Education Board","Establishment of Non-Formal Education Board",""],[1,"714","14","Non-Formal Education Board Establishment","Establishment of NFE Board.",""]],"151":[[1,"767","13","School Sports and Physical Education Strengthening Programme","During the 7th Five Year Plan period, efforts have been made to strengthen sports and physical education programme at the school stage, right from the primary level and gradually develop and systematize them up to the College and University levels.",""],[1,"767","13","Sports Facilities Development Programme","Significant progress has been made in development of sporting facilities such as building and developing open stadiums and indoor stadiums from the national to upazila levels, also building swimming pools across the country to encourage swimming sports and fitness.",""],[1,"767","13","Football Development Through Tournaments and Academy Management","The game of football has been developed through various tournaments and organized management of the Football Academy in Sylhet.",""],[1,"767","13","Cricket Facilities Upgrading Initiative","The standard of cricket has also been raised through a number of different initiatives, including building and upgrading facilities to meet the international standard.",""],[1,"767","14","Athlete Training and Sports Facilities Support","The Ministry of Youth and Sports is dedicated to raise the standard and achievements of promising athletes and sportsmen through providing latest training programmes and modern facilities through its operational units such as Bangladesh Krira Shikkha Protishthan (BKSP) and the National Sports Council (NSC).","Ministry of Youth and Sports"],[1,"768","2","Talent Identification and Sports Training Programmes","Proper talent identification through arranging talent hunting and training programmes for all kinds of sports.",""],[1,"768","4","Playground and Sports Facility Expansion","Develop and expand playgrounds and sports facilities at the Upazilla and Union levels.",""],[1,"768","5","Sports Infrastructure Development","Develop sports infrastructural facilities for both men and women, as well as facilities for indoor games.",""],[1,"768","6","Upazila Sports Infrastructure Development for Football and Cricket","Develop and provide sports infrastructural facilities for football and cricket games at the upazila level.",""],[1,"768","7","Development of Regional Sports Institutions","Development of regional sports institutions with proper facilities.",""],[1,"768","8","National Cricket and Football Stadium Renovation Programme","Continued development and renovations of national cricket and football stadiums to maintain and uphold international standards.",""],[1,"768","9","District-Level Tennis Sports Infrastructure Development","Develop tennis sports infrastructure at the district level.",""],[1,"768","10","Division-Level National Sports Complex Construction","Construction of Division level National Sports Complex.",""],[1,"768","11","Sports Infrastructure Development at Upazila and Zila Levels","Establish sports related infrastructures at the Upazila and Zila levels.",""],[1,"768","12","District-Level Indoor Stadium and Swimming Pool Development","Develop indoor stadiums, swimming pools at District levels.",""],[1,"768","13","Union-Level Play Field Development Programme","Develop over 1000 play fields in the country at the union level.",""],[1,"768","14","Women's Sports Complex Construction and Upgrading","Construct Women's Sports Complex in all Divisions and further develop existing Women's Sports Complex.",""],[1,"768","15","District-Level Youth Sports Complex Construction","Construction of Sports Complex for Youth at District levels.",""],[1,"768","16","Sports Complex Construction for Persons with Disabilities","Construction of sports complex for the persons with Disability (PWD) in Dhaka and other divisional cities.",""],[1,"768","17","Construction of International Standard Cricket and Football Stadiums","Construction of international standard cricket and football stadiums",""],[1,"818","5","Girls' Participation in Sports and Cultural Activities","Women's participation in sports and cultural activities would be ensured from school to build self-confidence amongst girls.",""],[1,"818","5","Extracurricular Activities Support in Educational Institutions","Extra-curricular activities would be encouraged and supported in educational institutions and outside.",""]],"152":[[1,"688","1","Pre-Primary Teacher Quality Improvement Initiative","Initiatives must be taken to improve the quality of teachers engaged in pre-primary education.",""],[1,"688","4","Primary Education Development Programme IV","To continue with this progress, the PEDP-IV was launched in July 2018 with an aim of providing quality primary education to all Bangladeshi children by enhancing institutional management through decentralization.",""],[1,"688","4","Primary and Pre-primary School Participation and Learning Support","The PEDP-IV envisages that all children in the appropriate age group will participate in pre-primary and primary education and acquire necessary skills and learning from school.",""],[1,"688","4","Family Incentives for School Attendance","Importantly, families of these children will be given incentives so that they can continue sending their children to school.",""],[1,"688","5","Primary Education Stipend Project","since mid-2017, the government has been transferring the stipends directly to the mobile banking accounts of nearly 10 million mothers of 13 million children enrolled in the project.",""],[1,"688","6","Free Textbook Distribution Programme","Distribution of free textbooks to primary and secondary students is an on-going and popular practice of the government.",""],[1,"689","1","National School Meal Policy","more than three million students in 15,700 primary schools are covered under the National School Meal Policy, which provides midday meals to students to meet a minimum 30 per cent calories and 50 per cent micronutrient needs of primary school going students.",""],[1,"689","1","Universal Midday Meal Coverage for Government Primary Schools","The target is to bring students of all government primary schools under the universal midday meal coverage by 2023.",""],[1,"689","1","Primary Education Curriculum Modernization Review","a review of primary education is being undertaken to modernize the curriculum and introduce new educational activities at the primary schools.",""],[1,"689","3","Stipend Distribution to Mothers of Primary Students","Schemes such as stipend distribution to mothers of primary students through mobile banking have been undertaken to encourage increased participation by students/families from disadvantaged backgrounds.",""],[1,"689","3","School Quality Improvement Through Better Inputs and Teacher Training","Progress has been made on quality front through supply of better inputs like materials and supplies, teacher training and introduction of ICT.",""],[1,"708","5","Family Incentives to Reduce Primary School Dropout","Greater incentives to families to keep their children in school, specially the girl, will be developed under the 8FYP.",""],[1,"708","5","Regular Parent-Teacher Engagement Meetings","In addition, regular parents-teachers meeting will be done to discuss students' performances and progress, inform parents about the current system and children's future career path, and deliberate on feasible future options.",""],[1,"708","5","Teacher Attendance Accountability and Digital Roster System","Greater accountability of teachers and heads to maintain regular attendance and timeliness will be maintained.",""],[1,"708","5","Digital Roster System for Teaching Staff","ICT and development of digital rosters for the teaching staff will be done.",""],[1,"708","6","Education Quality Improvement Programme","The 8FYP will place emphasis on improvements in the quality of education outcome.",""],[1,"708","8","Learning Outcomes Measurement Tools Development","Under the 8FYP, there will be greater focus on developing tools to properly quantify the learning-outcomes by the students that focus on competency and understanding, not just ability to pass an exam.",""],[1,"709","1","Strengthening Implementation of PEDP-IV and SESIP","Implementation of these programmes will be strengthened.",""]],"153":[[1,"690","7","Inclusive Secondary School Infrastructure and Materials Upgrade","The government aims to reach 80 per cent by the end of 2025.",""],[1,"691","1","ICT Courses and Computer Centre Expansion in Secondary Education","ICT courses in secondary education have been introduced as well as setting up computer centres in institutions and providing training to teachers to use them.",""],[1,"691","1","Multimedia Classroom Digitalization Projects","Digitalization of classrooms is currently an ambitious on-going venture operating through two separate projects under MoE and MoPME.","MoE | MoPME"],[1,"691","1","Secondary School Electricity, Computer, and Internet Access Expansion","By 2019, 94.86 per cent of secondary schools have access to electricity and the aim is to reach 100 per cent by 2025.",""],[1,"691","3","Secondary Education Sector Investment Program","The largest and most prominent out of these projects is the Secondary Education Sector Investment Program (2013-2023) (SESIP).",""],[1,"692","1","Transforming Secondary Education for Results Program","the government is implementing the Transforming Secondary Education for Results (TSER) program, to enhance the quality of teaching and learning in secondary education; improve retention and completion with special focus on the girl students and students from poor households by providing financial assistances, stipends, and school grants; modernize the curriculum; and facilitate professional development and accountability of teachers.",""],[1,"707","1","Education System Reforms to Improve Relevance","The 8FYP will undertake necessary reforms to strengthen the relevance of the education system.",""],[1,"707","2","Teacher Quality and Skills Strengthening","Teachers will be trained and made familiar with this approach, and be incentivized sufficiently in performing their jobs.",""],[1,"707","2","Competency-Based Curriculum Review","Future curriculum reviews will focus towards developing competency, not content-learning.",""],[1,"708","7","Curriculum Upgrading for Civic and Life Skills","Create better citizens: upgrading of the curriculum may comprise inclusion of modules about basic moral, safety, and awareness issues of day-to-day lives (such as daily health care, climate change, environmental pollution, etc.) at the primary, and perhaps all levels.",""],[1,"708","7","Community Engagement Activities in the Curriculum","There may also be some activities/practical experience in the curriculum on community engagement for developing social responsibility of the future generation.",""],[1,"709","2","Secondary Level National Learning Assessment","a similar national assessment at secondary level will be undertaken as a first step.",""],[1,"709","3","Student Examination and Assessment Reform","Ministry of Education has embarked on reforming the examination and evaluation method of students learning.","Ministry of Education"],[1,"709","4","Science Enrolment Increase Programme","Training for science teachers, identification of high-potential students at a young-age and streamlining them into the science streams will address this problem.",""],[1,"709","4","Student-Parent Career Guidance and Remedial Support","Regular correspondence between institutions and students/parents, to discuss future plans and career aspirations, and additional remedial assistance for struggling students will be provided.",""],[1,"709","5","Introduction of a Unified Secondary Curriculum up to Class X","Considering all these aspects government has decided introducing a unitrack curriculum instead of multi group curriculum up to grade-X.",""],[1,"710","2","ICT-Based Learning Infrastructure Expansion","A number of ICT labs have already been established in secondary level institutions and finally all institutions will be equipped with modern ICT labs.","Ministry of Education"],[1,"710","2","Teacher ICT Training Programme","Teachers are given training on ICT subject and ICT-based learning system.",""],[1,"710","2","Multimedia Classroom Conversion Programme","Conversion of classrooms into Multimedia Classrooms is underway.",""],[1,"710","2","Permanent ICT-Based Learning Infrastructure Initiative","Ministry of Education has undertaken initiatives to build permanent ICT-based learning infrastructure that would help keeping the students' losses at minimum level during any natural disaster.","Ministry of Education"],[1,"710","2","ICT Integration Acceleration Initiative","To speed up the integration of ICT with the education system, the Government's a2i project initiated several steps with the Ministry of Education.","Ministry of Education"],[1,"710","2","Web-Based Learning Framework in Schools","The 8FYP will adopt a framework to ensure that at least one hour of learning in using these web contents in all primary and secondary schools in school premises are in place.",""]],"154":[[1,"693","4","Ebtedayee Madrasa Monthly Pay Order Inclusion","There are plans to bring the Ebtedayee madrasas under Monthly Pay Order (MPO).",""],[1,"693","4","Madrasa Teacher ICT and Arabic Training Initiative","An initiative was taken at the end of 2019 to provide ICT training to 19,200 madrasa teachers and special communicative Arabic courses to 9,600 teachers.",""],[1,"693","4","Smart Classroom Expansion in Senior Madrasas","smart classrooms were to be established in 560 senior madrasas and around 120,000 students trained in basic ICT, computer training, and use of Internet.",""],[1,"700","3","TVET Integration into Madrasa Education","The Technical and Madrasa Division (TMED) has also been created in the Ministry of Education to introduce TVET into the madrasa stream","Ministry of Education"],[1,"711","3","Madrasa Education Streamlining and National Board Integration","under the 8FYP, madrasa education will be streamlined and brought under the national education board.",""],[1,"711","4","Madrasa Teacher Training and Recruitment Programme","As improvements are made to the curriculum and new subjects emphasized on, the existing teachers will be provided appropriate training to be able to teach the new material.",""],[1,"711","4","Female Madrasa Teacher Recruitment Support","The 8FYP will provide resources to encourage, train and subsequently recruit more female trained teachers for madrasas.",""],[1,"711","5","Introduction of Technical Education in Madrasa Levels","To make that happen, 8FYP will introduce technical education at the Dakhil and Alim level.",""],[1,"711","5","Madrasa-TVET Partnership Initiative","Madrasa-TVET partnerships will play catalytic roles in transforming pedagogical architecture of the madrasa.",""],[1,"711","6","ICT in Madrasa Education Initiative","Availability of computer and a multimedia-device in Aliya madrasas, introduction of ICT- based education, and programming courses will be undertaken under the 8FYP.",""],[1,"711","7","Qawmi Madrasa Funding Transparency Framework","Under the 8FYP, transparency in funding will be established to help strengthen the management of these madrasas.",""]],"155":[[1,"695","2","Strategic Plan for Higher Education","In order to keep up this positive trend in the sector, the government has adopted the Strategic Plan for Higher Education in Bangladesh: 2017-2031.",""],[1,"696","1","Independent Higher Education Accreditation Council","In 2017, the Accreditation Council Bill was passed in the parliament that stipulates an independent council to evaluate programmes of both public and private universities.",""],[1,"696","1","Higher Education Quality Enhancement Project","The Higher Education Quality Enhancement Project (HEQEP), which was implemented with the help of the World Bank through the University Grants Commission, aims to improve the quality, and relevance, on higher education institutions in Bangladesh by i) encouraging innovation within universities, ii) demanding greater accountability from the university authorities, and iii) Instituting capacity development of higher education institutions and the sector as a whole.","University Grants Commission"],[1,"696","2","UGC Strengthening and Higher Education Quality Improvement","The Ministry of Education has also undertaken steps to further strengthen and empower UGC to improve the quality and scope of higher education and make it internationally competitive through appropriate curriculum development, support for Science and Technology (S&T), encouragement of research, and using high level training to prepare and equip the next generation to successfully meet the challenges of globalization and contribute to Bangladesh's socioeconomic development.","Ministry of Education"],[1,"712","1","Tertiary Education Investment and Consolidation","The implementation of these strategies will be further consolidated in the 8FYP.",""],[1,"712","5","Women-Only Public Universities and Scholarship Support","Establishing public universities just for women, generous scholarships and other funding packages under the 8FYP will help narrowing and eventually eliminating the gap.",""],[1,"712","6","International University Campus and Academic Collaboration Initiative","In order to increase competition, reputed universities of the world may be allowed to open their campuses in Bangladesh.",""],[1,"713","1","STEM-Focused University Prioritization","STEM focused universities should be prioritized.",""],[1,"713","1","University Curriculum Update Collaboration","in the short-run, UGC can partner with a few universities and follow their guidance to regularly update the curriculum.",""],[1,"713","2","Faculty Research and Publication Incentive Reform","Much emphasis is needed to place on faculty research and publication.",""]],"156":[[1,"700","3","National Technical and Vocational Qualifications Framework","the National Technical and Vocational Qualifications Framework (NTVQF) has been designed to standardize the technical and vocational qualifications",""],[1,"700","3","Skills for Employment Investment Project","ADB is helping the government to implement the NSDP2011 with a major skills enhancement program called the Skills for Employment Investment Project (SEIP)",""],[1,"700","4","Skills for Employment Investment Program","A particularly useful instrument is the SEIP that has shown considerable promise in terms of delivering results (Table Box 11.1).",""],[1,"700","4","NGO-Led Rural and Informal Sector Skills Programmes","Programmes introduced by various NGOs are also helping improve the skill base of the rural population and in the informal sector.",""],[1,"700","4","Skills Gap Closure Effort Under the 8FYP","the skills gaps are large and will require concerted efforts during the 8FYP to close the gap.",""],[1,"701","4","National Skills Development Coordination and Strategy Implementation","The goal of NSDA is to formulate and implement all strategies to develop skills and bring coordination between different institutions and stakeholders regarding skills training, etc.",""],[1,"701","4","Inclusive Skills Training Access for Disadvantaged and Special Needs Groups","The NSDA bill specifically targets disadvantaged people and people with specialized needs and provides them with access to education and training.",""],[1,"701","6","Industry Skills Council Linkage and Skills System Strengthening","ISC provide linkages between industries and TVET institutions.",""],[1,"701","8","National Skills Development Authority Coordination and Facilitation","NSDA has been established.",""],[1,"701","10","Demand-Driven Training System Development","This training material is designed to develop a system to deliver demand-driven training, primarily through encouraging private sector industry partnership with training institutions.",""],[1,"701","22","Industry Association and Public Institute Training Programmes","Training programmes are on-going by industry associations and public institutes.",""],[1,"701","22","Executive Development Training in Universities","Executive Development Training has started in three universities, enrolling 669 trainees so far;",""],[1,"705","8","Integrated Human Capital and Skills Development Framework","To achieve UMIC status by 2031, the 8FYP will align country's human capital development strategy with the overall economic development strategy.",""],[1,"705","8","Regulatory Framework for Skills Development","A holistic approach and a regulatory framework for skill development will be adopted, where all tiers of education and vocational training will be interlinked.",""],[1,"705","8","Skills Policy for Employer-Based Worker Training Incentives","the skill development policy will specify how to incentivize the training of the workers for the employers since learning or skill acquisition occurs most at the industry level through on-the-job training.",""],[1,"705","8","Soft Skills Integration Guidelines","the importance of soft skill will be integrated and strategic guidelines will be prepared on how to educate these skills.",""],[1,"706","5","Private Sector Engagement in Education Investment and Curriculum Development","The 8FYP will continue with this policy.",""],[1,"706","5","Public-Private Partnerships for Skills for Employment Programmes","The 8FYP will seek inputs from private businesses in curriculum development and develop public-private partnerships in the development and delivery of skills for employment programmes",""],[1,"706","6","Parent Consultation in Education Development","Accordingly, the 8FYP will seek to involve parents in education development.",""],[1,"712","3","Public-Private Partnership for TVET and Skills Development","The 8FYP will undertake polices in this context and to strengthen the partnership between GO and NGOs.",""],[1,"712","4","Expansion of Trainer Training Institutions","The 8FYP will take steps to increase the number of training institutions for trainers.",""]],"157":[[1,"705","8","Pre-Primary Soft Skills Curriculum Integration","This training will start from the pre-primary level of education and will be an integral part of the curriculum.",""],[1,"707","1","Early Childhood Development through Pre-Primary Education","One potential low-cost intervention can be early-childhood development through pre-primary education.",""],[1,"707","5","Pre-Primary and Early Childhood Education Development","The 8FYP will place strong emphasis on the development of pre-primary and early childhood education drawing on the Bangladesh and relevant global experiences.",""],[1,"708","1","Expansion of Pre-Primary Education on an Equity Basis","the 8FYP will expand the pre-primary education on the basis of equity.",""],[1,"708","2","Pre-Primary Curriculum Development and Teacher Training Programme","Develop appropriate curriculum and train teachers for pre-primary: Appropriate curriculum design and training of teachers is vital at this stage.",""],[1,"708","3","Public-Private Partnership Expansion for Pre-Primary Education","The 8FYP will continue encouraging these institutions to upscale and involve more interested private stakeholders and strengthen the public-private partnership.",""]],"158":[[1,"847","3","Expansion of Inclusive Education Institutions for Children with Disabilities","Along with an expansion of integrated education programme for visually impaired children, existing institutions for hearing impaired and mentally retarded children will be expanded.",""],[1,"847","3","Establishment of New Disability Education Institutions","New institutions will be established to provide access to more children with disabilities at primary, secondary and tertiary levels.",""],[1,"847","3","Multi-Stakeholder Disability Education Expansion and Teacher Training","A collaborative effort involving the government, NGOs and the private sector will be encouraged to expedite an expansion of existing institutions, establish new institutions and undertake teachers' training on disability.",""]],"159":[[1,"346","4","ICT Education Expansion","Rapidly expand ICT education at all levels",""],[1,"346","8","Educational Institution Technology Adaptation Support","Help educational institutions adapt to the rapidly changing technology landscape driven by the COVID19 pandemic.",""],[1,"346","9","Evidence-Informed Education Technology Decision-Making","Increase the use of evidence to inform decision-making about education technology.",""],[1,"346","10","Digital Learning Ecosystem Development","Develop a Digital Learning Ecosystem by equipping each institution with all required digital infrastructure facilities through public-private-partnership.",""],[1,"346","11","Centralized Educational Resource Repository","Develop a centralized educational resource repository for curating all innovative solutions in preparation for future emergencies",""],[1,"347","3","E-Learning and International University Partnerships","The Government should also facilitate e-learning and encourage partnership arrangements with international universities.",""],[1,"725","2","ICT-Based Quality Education and Digital Labs Expansion","To enhance the quality of education through ICT, the Department of ICT (DoICT) is responsible to spread ICT based quality education and developed IT skilled resource pool.","Department of ICT (DoICT)"],[1,"725","2","Sheikh Russel Digital Labs Nationwide Expansion","Phase by phase another 15,000 labs will be set up in Primary, Secondary and Higher educational institutions.",""],[1,"725","2","School of Future Comprehensive Education Initiative","These schools will lead \"School of future\" with comprehensive plan.",""],[1,"725","2","Student Digital Skills Training Programme","100,000 students of primary & secondary level will be trained in \"Basic Programming, IT Security and MS Office\".",""],[1,"725","2","Teacher Master Trainer Development Programme","36,000 teachers as master trainers and 20,000 youth in 9 different languages will be trained in future.",""],[1,"743","3","Blended Learning Policy Facilitation","a) policies to facilitate the growth of blended learning before 2021;","ICT Division"],[1,"743","3","Virtual Schooling Infrastructure Development","b) development of multi-sectoral participation and infrastructure for virtual schooling before end of 2020;","ICT Division"],[1,"743","3","Tech-Based Learning Support through Public-Private Partnerships","c) develop IT infrastructure and provide incentives to support tech-based learning through public-private partnerships by 2021;","ICT Division"],[1,"743","3","Rural Group Education Methods","d) encourage group education methods in rural areas;","ICT Division"],[1,"743","3","Private Sector Investment for Education Access","e) enable private sector investments to ensure improved access to education for all by 2030.","ICT Division"],[1,"750","8","Digital Learning Support for Educational Institutions","For COVID 19 response, the ICT Division will help educational institutions adapt to the rapidly changing technology landscape driven by the COVID19 pandemic.","ICT Division"],[1,"750","8","Evidence-Informed Education Technology Decision Support","It will facilitate use of evidence to inform decision-making about education technology.","ICT Division"],[1,"750","8","Digital Learning Platform Development","Furthermore, ICT Division will develop a Digital Learning","ICT Division"],[1,"751","1","Digital Infrastructure for Educational Institutions through Public-Private Partnership","Ecosystem by equipping each institution with all required digital infrastructure facilities through public- private-partnership.",""],[1,"751","1","Centralized Educational Resource Repository","It will develop a centralized educational resource repository for curating all innovative solutions in preparation for future emergencies.",""],[1,"751","1","Teacher Professional Development for Online and Distance Learning","The division will ensure teachers' professional development so that they can host online/distance learning facilities for students.",""],[1,"751","1","AI-Enabled Student Assessment and Personalized Learning Initiative","It will design and initiate student-led assessments and personalized learning spaces using artificial intelligence and/or other means where it is feasible.",""]],"160":[[1,"323","3","Expansion of Technical Training Centres and Marine Technology Institutes","Currently, 64 Technical Training Centres (TTC) and 6 Institute of Marine Technologies (IMT) are in operation and 70 more are under process of establishment.",""],[1,"323","3","Universal Upazila Technical Training Centre Coverage","During 8FYP all Upazila will have TTCs.",""],[1,"323","9","Upazila Technical Training Center Expansion","The Ministry will establish one TTC in every Upazila by 2025, which will allow potential migrants to go for longer training outside of their home.","Ministry"],[1,"323","10","International Skills Certification Accreditation and Mutual Recognition Initiative","The Ministry will initiate in association with the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and other relevant entities pursuing international accreditation of certification of skills and mutual recognition of skills for at least 20 countries by the end of 8FYP period.","Ministry | Ministry of Foreign Affairs"],[1,"324","1","Skills Competency Assessment and Certification for Migrant Workers","The Ministry will introduce skills competency assessment and certification as a new precondition for the issuing of Smart Card exit permit.","The Ministry"],[1,"324","1","Assessment Centres for Outward Migrant Workers","It will establish Assessment Centres for outward migrant workers with international accreditation.",""],[1,"324","2","Skills Recognition of Bangladesh TVET Qualifications in CODs","The Ministry will work closely with the Ministry of Foreign Affairs to induct Skills Recognition of Bangladesh TVET qualifications in COD's.","Ministry | Ministry of Foreign Affairs"],[1,"325","8","E-learning Programmes for Migrant Worker Skills Refreshers","The Ministry will launch e-learning programmes, with appropriate design so that migrant workers get refreshers for their skills with support distance-based learning","The Ministry"]],"161":[[1,"834","3","Early Childhood Development and Inclusive Education Expansion","The children's access to good quality education was expected to be strengthened through early childhood development strategies and access to formal and non-formal education.",""],[1,"840","2","Early Childhood Development Awareness and Community Childcare Programme","The intervention for early childhood development will include an awareness raising programme for parents to make them aware of early childhood development benefits, promote community-based childcare centres for clusters of families where literate mothers are trained to become caregivers and design facilities for early learners.",""],[1,"840","2","Expansion of Pre-Primary Education","Pre-primary education (for children 3-5 years) will be expanded to make formal education more effective.",""],[1,"840","2","Primary Education Access and Quality Improvement Measures","Highest level priority will be given to increase enrolment rate and decrease dropout rate, train primary teachers, increase the attendance rate, increase contact hours, and maintain gender parity in access and achievement.",""],[1,"840","2","Vocational and Technical Education Expansion","Vocational and technical education will be accorded high importance, to create better conditions for future gainful employment.",""],[1,"840","2","Street Children and Orphans Education Inclusion Initiative","Special efforts will be made to reach out street children and the orphans and bring them in the fold of child education network.",""],[1,"840","2","Non-Formal Education and Skills Training for Out-of-School Children","Non-formal education will be provided to diverse types of children deprived of education, like un-enrolled or drop-out children and hard-to-reach children to enhance their employability and productivity through skill training.",""]],"162":[[1,"669","4","Nutrition and Hygiene Education in School Curriculum","Incorporate nutrition and hygiene education in curriculum, including school vegetable garden and cooking demonstrations",""],[1,"669","4","School Health and Nutrition Days","Ensure regular Health and Nutrition Days in the school's calendar",""],[1,"669","4","Girls' Secondary Education Completion Support","Ensure completion for girls' education at least up to high school",""],[1,"669","4","School Feeding Nutrition Promotion","Promote and protect good dietary practices among children in places where there are school feeding programmes",""],[1,"669","4","School Sanitation Facilities Improvement","Improve sanitation facilities in schools",""],[1,"671","10","Nutrition and Healthy Diet Education Curriculum Reform","Introduce/revise/strengthen education on nutrition and healthy diets for students in the curriculum",""],[1,"671","15","Nutrition Education Training for Health and Agriculture Workers","To improve the knowledge base and capacity of health personnel regarding nutrition, health and family planning workers as well as agricultural extension workers will be appropriately trained in nutrition education.",""],[1,"671","15","Nutrition Capacity Building for Frontline Workers and Farmers","Capacity building in nutrition of Upazila health and agriculture workers, school teachers and women farmers will be undertaken through the NNS Operational Plan of IPHN.",""],[1,"671","15","Community Nutrition Awareness Campaign","Community awareness regarding health and nutrition will be strengthened through disseminating messages.",""],[1,"671","15","Community-Based Nutritious Recipe Promotion","Community based arrangements will also promote preparation of low-cost nutritious recipes, processing",""],[1,"680","1","Low-Cost Day Care Facility Expansion","Additionally, to enable labor force participation of young mothers, efforts should be made to increase the supply of low-cost day care facilities.",""]],"163":[[1,"681","10","Increase Public Investment in Education","Bangladesh must increase the investment in education from 2.5 per cent of GDP in FY2019 to at least 3.5 per cent by the end of 8FYP.",""],[1,"706","4","Public Education Expenditure Increase","Sharply increase public education expenditure, as a percentage of GDP:",""]],"164":[[1,"700","4","Fourth Industrial Revolution Skills Monitoring and Adaptation","the new skills challenges emerging from the 4IR require constant monitoring and change to adapt to market demand.",""]],"165":[[1,"756","2","Cultural Heritage Digitization Initiative","To restore and preserve many of the intangible and tangible cultural heritages that are on the verge of extinction, digitization efforts were implemented.",""],[1,"756","2","Archaeological Survey and Conservation Programme","The Ministry also reiterated the importance of archaeological sites by conducting national surveys and conservation programmes for further development.",""],[1,"756","2","Museum and Folk Art Development Programme","Programmes were undertaken to develop museums and folk art.",""],[1,"756","3","Archaeological Site Renovation and Preservation","proper renovation, preservation and development of archaeological sites have also created employment opportunities for the poor people.",""],[1,"756","3","Archaeological Tourism Promotion and Local Enterprise Expansion","Higher tourist visits to archaeological sites and museums have led to the expansion of business and commerce of local impoverished population and new employment opportunities were created.",""],[1,"757","4","Intangible Cultural Heritage Documentation and Preservation Programme","Many of the intangible cultural heritages like language literatures, arts, performing arts, music and other areas are at the verge of extinction and require urgent efforts and intervention to document preserve and uphold them.",""],[1,"757","4","Cultural Heritage Restoration, Preservation, and Digitization Initiative","Significant attention needs to be given to the restoration, preservation and digitization of these emblems of our cultural heritage.",""],[1,"757","4","Cultural Heritage Institutional and Human Resource Development","There is also a dearth of institutional establishment as well as human resources for such delicate works, and these resources needs to be developed urgently.",""],[1,"757","5","Archaeological Site Preservation and Restoration Planning","Adequate and systematic planning is required to address this and like most other sectors, perspective, and medium-term and long-term plans needs to be carried out.",""],[1,"758","4","Liberation War Heritage Preservation Programme","Promote the spirit of liberation war; preserve, protect and development of historical and liberation war monuments, memorial plazas, mass graveyard etc.",""],[1,"759","1","Antiquities Act Amendment for Heritage Protection","Amend the Antiquities Act to strengthen the protection of archaeological sites and historical monuments.",""],[1,"759","4","National Archaeological Site Survey and Facilities Development","National survey on archaeological sites will be carried out and physical facilities for the department of archaeology will be developed for enhancing archaeological tourism;",""],[1,"759","12","Archaeological Sites, Museums, and Historical Monuments Preservation Programme","Programmes for further development of archaeological sites, museums and ethnological museum will be undertaken and historical monuments will be identified and preserved;",""],[1,"759","14","Major Archaeological Site Conservation Programme","implementation of conservation of major Archaeological sites, during the 8th Five Year Plan period.",""],[1,"759","15","World Heritage Research, Survey, and Documentation Expansion","To extend the research, survey and documentation activities to incorporate more sites in UNESCO World Heritage list.",""]],"166":[[1,"756","2","Ethnic Community Language, Arts, and Culture Preservation Centres","Within the framework of national unity, steps were taken to preserve and promote language, arts and culture of ethnic communities through cultural centres in tribal areas.",""],[1,"758","1","National Cultural Activities Promotion","Under the 8FYP, healthy growth of cultural activities will be promoted throughout the country.",""],[1,"758","1","Literature and Arts Promotion Initiative","In addition to promotion of literature, fine and performing arts, attention will be given to create and promote a culture attuned work, towards perseverance, confidence and creativity.",""],[1,"758","5","Liberation War Media and Youth Motivation Programme","Creation of liberation war-based videos and films and running motivational programmes for future generation, particularly youths.",""],[1,"758","14","Good Citizenship Sensitization Campaign","Promote good citizenship through sensitization of rights, duties and responsibilities.",""],[1,"758","16","Preservation and Promotion of Minority Language Arts and Culture","Preserve and promote language arts and culture of small ethnic groups/communities within the framework of national unity and awareness.",""],[1,"758","17","Ethnic Minority Cultural Heritage Support Programme","Development interventions will be carried out to patronize and nourish indigenous intangible and tangible cultural traits and elements.",""],[1,"758","19","Promotion of Traditional and Local Culture for Youth","Practicing traditional or local culture will be encouraged to fight terrorism, drug addiction and other negative impact of modernisation by giving more attention to younger generation.",""],[1,"759","10","Tribal Cultural and Language Centres Expansion Programme","Regional and ethnic minority's cultures will be promoted and preserved through various programmes viz. erection of more tribal cultural and language centres within the tribal areas;",""],[1,"759","11","School-Based Liberation War History Dissemination Programme","Continue dissemination of the real history of liberation war among the young generations.",""],[1,"759","17","Cultural Engagement for Social Harm Prevention","Socially negative issues like social abuse, terrorism, gender biasness and other socially negative elements will be addressed minutely in all forms of cultural practice.",""],[1,"759","17","Youth Participation in Cultural Activities","Involvement of young generation in cultural activities will be increased in a manner to fight against all forms of negative social elements.",""]],"167":[[1,"844","2","Climate Change and Landslide Adaptation Measures in CHT","Consideration the effect of climate change and landslides in CHT and necessary measures to adapt and mitigate climate change related hazards.",""],[1,"844","3","Technology-Enabled Infrastructure and Hazard Mitigation Works","Technology will be used to construct roads, dams, bridges, culverts, infrastructure for mitigating earthquakes, landslides related hazards.",""]],"168":[[1,"829","3","Climate Change Adaptation and Resilience Capacity Building","Adaptation capacity against climate change impacts should be enhanced amongst community including women.",""],[1,"829","3","Disaster Preparedness and Climate-Resilient Livelihood Investment","Investment in disaster preparedness, adaptation capacity building, and climate resilient livelihood for women and men should be enhanced.",""],[1,"829","3","Climate Change Gender Action Plan Implementation","Full implementation of the Climate Change Gender Action Plan should be ensured.",""],[1,"829","3","Adaptive and Diversified Livelihood Services Expansion","Provision of adaptive and diversified livelihood services (e.g. low gestation and less water intensive crops, food storage and preservation technology, nutrition, and food preservation during calamities) should be expanded to ensure food security amongst vulnerable groups, including climate induced migrants of urban areas.",""],[1,"829","3","Women’s Access to Employment and Skills Support Schemes","Providing women with greater access to employment guarantee schemes, public work programmes, skills development, technology, entrepreneurship support and training should also be extended.",""],[1,"829","3","Women’s Climate Change Mitigation Capacity Enhancement","Women's capacity and engagement in climate change mitigation like technology with low carbon emission, forest and bio-diversity conservation, water management, renewable energy, and scientific waste management, should be enhanced.",""],[1,"829","4","Climate-Resilient Information Services for Calamity Preparedness","Information services to strengthen resilience to climate change, calamities and shocks: Information services before, during and after calamities should be ensured for preparation and safety measures during and after calamities (fire, earthquake, disease).",""],[1,"829","4","Community Radio and Network-Based Disaster Information Campaigns","Provision of services, shelters, livelihood support etc. should be disseminated to women and men through community radio, campaign and strengthening community networks.",""]],"169":[[1,"338","14","Tourism Policy and Service Improvement Programme","These programmes will be continued and expanded during the 8FYP.","Ministry of Civil Aviation and Tourism | Bangladesh Parjatan Corporation"],[1,"338","23","Tourist Site Identification and Development Programme","Identifying potential tourist spots scattered over different places of the country and modernizing and expanding existing ones",""],[1,"338","26","Tourism Infrastructure and Management Improvement through Public-Private Partnerships","Creating infrastructure and improving management of the tourism industry through Public Private Partnership (PPP) arrangements",""],[1,"338","27","Tourism Documentary Film Production and Event Publicity","Producing documentary films on Bangladesh Tourism & publicising tourism events",""],[1,"338","29","Participation in Tourism Fairs and Related Programmes","Participating in tourism fairs organized home and abroad and arranged related programmes",""],[1,"342","10","Visa on Arrival Facilitation for Tourists","the visa requirements for visitors will be further simplified through visa on arrival facilities.",""],[1,"342","10","Visitor Safety and Courtesy Measures","Steps will also be taken to ensure the full safety and courteous treatment of all visitors.",""],[1,"344","2","Tourism Infrastructure and Facilities Upgrade","the strategy consists of two broad elements: Expansion of fixed infrastructure to facilitate an expanded and safe aviation system in Bangladesh and second to expand and upgrade the tourism industry facilities comprising of visa and currency exchange facilities, hotels, restaurants, tourist resorts and inland transportation.",""],[1,"344","3","Premium Shopping Outlets Development","the strategy will focus on 5 entry points: (1) establishing at least 3 premium shopping outlets that meets international standards in the cities of Dhaka, Chittagong and Sylhet",""],[1,"344","3","Eco-Nature Integrated Resort Development","developing an eco-nature integrated resorts near Sundarbans",""],[1,"344","3","Teknaf to Sundarbans Riviera Development","development of a strait Riviera linking Teknaf to Sundarbans",""],[1,"344","3","Archaeological Site Promotion Initiative","promoting the archaeological sites",""],[1,"344","3","Eco-Park Establishment Programme","establishing eco parks in Chittagong and Sylhet",""],[1,"344","4","Focused Marketing Support in Priority Markets","Devise and ensure the right level of marketing support in the priority markets.",""],[1,"344","6","Tourism Environment Improvement Measures","Improve the tourism environment: Improve offerings and accessibility for key tourism enablers (such as taxi services, restaurants, hotels and resorts), access to funding, security and regulations as well as improving the service quality of front-line staff.",""],[1,"344","7","Visa Facilitation Services Rollout","Rollout of visa facilitation services: Ensure that tourists from target markets have easy visa procedures including online 48to 72-hour approvals and visa on arrival facilities.",""],[1,"344","8","Tourism Public-Private Partnership and Investment Promotion","Successful implementation of the tourism strategy will require a strong public-private partnership.",""]],"170":[[1,"54","1","Strengthening of the National Social Security Strategy and Social Protection Transfers","Regarding the social security system, the implementation of the NSSS will have to be strengthened with greater funding for social protection-related income transfers to the poor and vulnerable.",""],[1,"54","6","Social Protection-Based Income Transfers","A broad-based strategy of inclusiveness with a view to empowering every citizen to participate fully and benefit from the development process and helping the poor and vulnerable with social protection- based income transfers;",""],[1,"55","1","Expanded Social Protection Transfers for Poor and Vulnerable Groups","The social protection programmes will be strengthened to provide higher income transfers to the poor and vulnerable.",""],[1,"55","2","Accelerated Implementation of the NSSS and Poverty-Focused Social Protection Financing","The social protection delivery will be strengthened through a more rapid implementation of the NSSS and increase in funding for poverty-focused social protection programmes",""],[1,"58","2","Social Protection System Development","The main focus of the ADP will be to sharply improve and strengthen health infrastructure, to build the social protection system, alleviate infrastructure constraints to private investment and GDP growth by fast tracking nationally important projects, and implement the BDP2100.",""],[1,"58","3","National Social Security Strategy Fast-Tracking","Implementation of the National Social Security Strategy (NSSS) will be fast-tracked to provide comprehensive social protection to all poor and vulnerable citizens based on a modern Life Cycle based approach.",""],[1,"60","1","Job Creation and Transfer Payments for Poverty Recovery","The 8FYP will put top priority to reverse this income loss through job creation and transfer payments with a view to restoring the momentum of poverty reduction to the path envisaged in PP2041, whereby the target is to eliminate extreme poverty by FY2031.",""],[1,"60","1","Expanded Social Protection System","and expanded social protection system will form the core elements of the poverty strategy.",""],[1,"60","2","Fast-Track National Social Protection System Implementation","the implementation of a much stronger social protection system nationwide based on the fast-track implementation of the NSSS and higher spending on social protection programmes for the urban and rural poor and vulnerable population",""],[1,"60","2","Expanded Social Protection Budget Allocation","The 8FYP will expand the budget allocation for social protection for the poor (excluding civil service pensions which is not targeted to the poor) from 1.2% of GDP in FY2019 to 2% of GDP by FY2025",""],[1,"60","3","Strengthened Social Inclusion Strategy","Along with poverty reduction, social inclusion strategy will be strengthened during the 8FYP.",""],[1,"84","1","Current Safety Net Programme for Persons with Disabilities","In the meanwhile, implementation of the current safety net programme for PWD has continued.",""],[1,"84","2","Social Inclusion Strategy for Marginalized Groups","the 7FYP social inclusion strategy for marginalized groups such as the Dalits and Sex Workers was to eliminate all discrimination, protect them from social abusive practices and offer special programmes through the NSSS",""],[1,"84","3","National Social Security Strategy Implementation Action Plan","Subsequently, with the assistance of development partners, a formal NSSS Implementation Action Plan was adopted in 2018.",""],[1,"84","4","Strengthening Social Protection Programmes and Funding","The 8FYP will make this a top priority both as an important instrument to address the effects of COVID-19 on poverty and vulnurability and to increase the growth elasticity of poverty reduction.",""],[1,"96","3","Expansion of Social Safety Net Programmes","Expansion of social safety net programmes to meet the basic needs of people living below poverty line, day labourers and for workers in the informal sector.",""],[1,"99","2","Social Protection Income Transfer Expansion","Regarding the social security system, the slow progress in implementing the NSSS and the inability to increase funding for social protection-related income transfers to the poor and vulnerable will need to be addressed speedily both as a response to offset the negative effects of COVID-19 but also to increase the growth elasticity of poverty as well as economic recovery.",""],[1,"102","7","Social Protection-Based Income Transfers","A broad-based strategy of inclusiveness with a view to empowering every citizen to participate in full and benefit from the development process, and helping the poor and vulnerable with social protection- based income transfers.",""],[1,"109","5","Cash Transfers to Poor Families","Cash transfers to poor families",""],[1,"111","6","Stimulus and Relief Package Implementation","strong effort will be made to fully implement the stimulus and relief package announced in April-June 2020",""],[1,"111","6","National Social Protection Strategy Implementation Acceleration","The social protection delivery will be strengthened through a more rapid implementation of the NSSS and increase in funding for poverty-focused social protection programmes",""],[1,"118","2","Safety Net and Social Protection Programmes","Strategies in relation to reducing income inequality include safety nets, social funds, microcredit, and targeted cash and in-kind programmes, especially in health and education.",""],[1,"147","1","Healthcare and Social Protection Resource Allocation","The 8FYP will put topmost priority in allocating adequate resources to healthcare and social protection and to address the related planning and program implementation constraints.",""],[1,"147","1","Strengthening of the National Social Security Strategy Implementation","Renewed efforts will be made to strengthen implementation of the NSSS.",""],[1,"155","2","Expanded Safety Net Transfers and Food Distribution","the government has responded by increasing safety net transfers including free and subsidized food distribution during the lockdown",""],[1,"163","10","Improved Social Protection Transfer System","Instituting a better system of transferring social protection spending to the poor in order to increase its poverty reduction impact is a major challenge that will need to be addressed in the 8FYP.",""],[1,"168","9","National Social Security Strategy Implementation","In 2015, the Government adopted the National Social Security Strategy (NSSS) to improve the efficiency and effectiveness of the social protection system in Bangladesh.",""],[1,"168","9","Conversion of In-Kind Social Protection to Cash Transfers","Steps are also being taken to convert in-kind programmes to cash transfers to reduce leakages.",""],[1,"168","12","Income Strengthening and Social Protection Expansion","The resilience and stability of income need to be strengthened through efforts to increase the real incomes of both the wage-employed workforce and the self-employed workforce, and through a stronger system of income transfers to the poor and vulnerable based on a vastly strengthened social protection system.",""],[1,"168","13","Expanded Social Protection Spending","social protection spending will need to be increased to offset the short-term increase in poverty",""],[1,"169","8","COVID-19 Poverty Recovery Support Package","The poverty reduction support package will include sharply improving COVID-19 prevention and COVID-19 related healthcare spending to ensure the health safety of all workers and families to allow a return to normalcy; accelerating income transfers through the social protection programme to those who remain affected by COVID-19, loss of income and/ or face COVID-19 related health care spending shocks, providing jobs to those who became unemployed from COVID-19 by accelerating efforts to revive the Cottage, Micro, Small and Medium Enterprises (CMSMEs) through low- cost credit schemes, protecting jobs in the formal sector through the speedy implementation of the various",""],[1,"172","4","Fast-Tracked National Social Security Strategy Implementation","For the 8FYP, two major initiatives will be taken. First, the implementation of the NSSS will be fast-tracked.",""],[1,"172","4","Consolidation of Social Protection Schemes into Life-Cycle Risk-Based Programmes","All efforts will be made to consolidate the multiple schemes into the core Life-Cycle risk-based programmes suggested in the NSSS, move away from in-kind to cash-based transfers on-line transfers, establish Single Registry MIS of beneficiaries based on eligibility criteria identified in the NSSS, and establish an on-line Grievance Redressal System.",""],[1,"172","4","Reformed Social Protection Financing Framework","Second, the financing of a reformed social protection system will be given a high priority.",""],[1,"173","1","Replication of Targeted Livelihood Programmes for Extreme Poverty Reduction","The aim should now be to replicate on a wider scale - and suitably modified where applicable - these programmes to cover most extreme poor groups in the country to reduce extreme poverty significantly in the 8FYP.",""],[1,"177","3","Expanded Social Protection Coverage for Lagging Districts","Giving higher priority and greater beneficiary coverage of social protection programmes to the lagging districts.",""],[1,"180","4","Increase Social Protection Spending","Increase spending on social protection (excluding civil service pension)",""],[1,"181","1","Reallocation of SOE Subsidies to Priority Social Spending","These subsidies will, therefore, be drastically reduced and re-channelled to priority social spending as noted above.",""],[1,"184","1","National Social Security Strategy Fast-Tracking","Implementation of the National Social Security Strategy (NSSS) will be fast-tracked to provide comprehensive social protection to all poor and vulnerable citizens based on a modern Life Cycle based approach.",""],[1,"187","9","Expanded Social Protection Spending","Spending on social protection also needs to go up to provide income support to the large number of near-poor who tripped over to the poverty group owing to income loses from COVID- 19.",""],[1,"187","9","Life Cycle Risk Mitigation Social Protection Reform","More generally, social protection will move to the NSSS recommended Life Cycle risk mitigation approach along with progress towards employment-based social insurance and Universal Health Care.",""],[1,"194","5","External Financing for COVID-19 Health and Social Protection Expenditures","Some of the increase is to enable external financing of essential COVID-19 related expenditures in health and social protection in FY21 and FY22, followed by MLT financing of key infrastructure in transport, energy and power and BDP2100 investments.",""]],"171":[[1,"278","1","Trade Facilitation and Customs Administration Modernization","in addition to completing the unfinished trade reform agenda with emphasis on the trade facilitation component of customs administration modernization.",""],[1,"280","7","Special Bonded-Warehouse Scheme","The special bonded-warehouse (SBW) scheme used largely by the RMG sector and occasionally by others","Customs department | NBR"],[1,"280","7","Duty Exemption and Drawback Scheme","The Duty Exemption and Drawback (DEDO) scheme, both managed by the Customs department","Customs department | NBR"],[1,"287","2","Customs Administration Efficiency and Transparency Reform","Going forward, other aspects of efficiency and transparency will have to be added to customs administration",""],[1,"287","2","Temporary Tariff Peak and Exception Management","Still, protection of specific products through the application of tariff peaks (a high tariff rate) might emerge from time and time and exceptions to the uniform tariff rule would then have to be made as temporary measures.",""],[1,"287","2","Modern Trade Regime for High-Tech Industry","Our trade regime must be so formulated as to enable a modern high-tech industrial sector of the future to function with seamless movement of goods and services across borders or via online with least transaction costs.",""],[1,"287","6","Duty-Free Imported Inputs for Export Production","Access to world-price (duty-free) inputs must be ensured to all exports:",""],[1,"290","1","Chittagong Port Operational Efficiency Enhancement","Operational efficiency at the port must be radically enhanced to ensure lower turnaround time for vessels in order to benchmark good productivity and performance in this port.",""],[1,"290","1","Import Clearance Improvement at Ports","High efficiency in import clearance at ports is critical for export competitiveness.",""],[1,"294","5","Trade Facilitation through Customs Infrastructure and Administration Improvement","trade facilitation with improved customs infrastructure and administration will remain effective mechanisms to promote exports while being consistent with multilateral rules.",""]],"172":[[1,"622","12","Sustainable Land-Use Planning and Innovative Land Management Measures","The government will take appropriate measures to promote sustainable land-use planning and innovative land management practices with particular focus on:",""],[1,"622","13","Land Information System Development","Developing land information system to support planning and decision-making by local authorities, private sector investments and infrastructure development decisions by the government.",""],[1,"622","14","Land Use Planning Tools for Desired Settlement Patterns","Using appropriate planning tools (structure/strategic planning, urban/detailed area planning, action planning) for promoting land use patterns in the desired direction.",""],[1,"622","15","Participatory Land Development Programme","Applying participatory approaches to land development to promote efficient and sustainable land development through techniques such as Land Pooling / Readjustment and Guided Land Development",""],[1,"622","16","Urban Land Pooling and Readjustment Framework","Policy instruments such as land pooling and land readjustment will be used in innovative public- private-community partnerships to manage and coordinate urban expansion.",""],[1,"622","16","Land Law Review and Amendment for Urban Development","Existing laws regulating transaction, development and access to land will be reviewed and modified to support innovative land development and management practices that facilitate land pooling, land readjustment, guided land development, development of the informal sector and poor's access to land.",""],[1,"623","3","Land Market Modernization and Digitized Land Records System","Helping the land market to work efficiently by modernizing the legal and regulatory framework, computerizing the land record system and improving the efficiency of the recording, registration, and mapping of house ownership and transactions.",""],[1,"627","3","Detailed Area Plan, Master Plan, and Structural Plan Modernization and Implementation","Formulate/modernize and implement Detailed Area Plan, Master Plan and Structural Plan",""],[1,"627","5","Area Planning and Structural Planning for Non-RAJUK Areas","Formulate detailed area plan, master plan and structural plan for areas outside Rajuk, CDA, KDA, and RDA",""]],"173":[[1,"119","7","Productivity Enhancement through Training and Appropriate Technology","Enhancing productivity (TFP) through training and proper technology as the basis for the creation of increased opportunities for employment with special emphasis on the agriculture sector.",""],[1,"119","8","Employment Generation and Self-Employment Support","Providing increased incentives, opportunities and capabilities for employment generation and self- employment.",""],[1,"120","6","Labor Market Flexibility and Worker Protection Measures","Bringing about careful flexibility in labour markets with adequate income, working conditions, job training and safety safeguards.",""],[1,"168","13","Short-Term Job Creation Programme","a large number of jobs will need to be created in the first year of the 8FYP to absorb the many domestic unemployed in the informal sector and those who are returning from overseas from loss of jobs owing to COVID-19",""],[1,"171","3","Education and Training Strengthening for the Poor","The 8FYP will focus strongly on the development of education and training, with emphasis on secondary and tertiary enrolments, emphasis on quality, and special attention to improve the access of the poor to education and training.",""],[1,"177","8","Expanded Labour Training Access for Lagging Districts","Provide greater access to labour training to lagging districts.",""]],"174":[[1,"341","5","Time-Bound Zoning Law Compliance Implementation","This matter needs urgent attention and resolution through a time-bound implementation.",""],[1,"345","2","Urban Land Management Reform","Better land management including digitized property records and low-cost land sales and registration procedures are essential reforms to boost housing supply.",""],[1,"345","2","Urban Zoning, Permitting, and Safety Regulation Simplification","The regulatory regime also needs to be simplified and properly enforced in regards to zoning restrictions, building permits and safety standards.",""],[1,"345","2","Housing Materials Trade Tax Reduction","Trade tax reduction on housing materials will also help to lower the cost of housing.",""],[1,"348","14","Zoning Law and Parking Regulation Enforcement","Enforcement of proper zoning laws for all commercial enterprises and strict implementation of parking regulations for all vehicles.",""]],"175":[[1,"346","1","Primary and Secondary Education Quality Improvement","Enhance the quality of education in both primary and secondary education thorough upgrading of both physical facilities and teaching materials.",""],[1,"346","2","Tertiary Education Access Expansion for Women","Expand the reach of tertiary education with a special focus on women to eliminate the gender gap in tertiary education.",""],[1,"346","3","Science and Technology Education Capacity Strengthening","Strengthen the education system capacities in Science and Technology.",""],[1,"346","5","Teacher Training Investment","Invest in teacher training.",""],[1,"346","6","Madrasa Quality Upgrade","Upgrade the quality of madrasas.",""],[1,"346","7","Vocational Training Institution Quality Improvement","Improve quality of vocational training institutions.",""],[1,"347","3","Education and Training Quality Upgrade","The highest priority is to adopt appropriate policies and investments to upgrade education and training quality, including emphasis on expanding tertiary education and science and technology.",""],[1,"347","3","Private Sector Partnership in Education","The on-going policy of partnering with the private sector is sound and should continue.",""],[1,"347","3","Education Quality Standards Oversight Reform","There is, however, a need to improve the government's oversight on quality standards for both public and private educational institutions.",""],[1,"347","7","Expansion of Science and Technology Education","First is the need for expanding the breadth and depth of science and technology education in Bangladesh.",""],[1,"348","5","Education Accreditation Policy","Accreditation policies to ensure minimum quality standards in education.",""]],"176":[[1,"347","3","Advanced Research Grant Program","The Government should also adopt a grant program to facilitate advanced research in all high- priority fields, but especially in science and technology.",""],[1,"347","3","Publicly Supported Overseas Science and Technology Scholarship Programme","Bangladesh can learn from this experience and initiate a similar focused program for high-level skills that are especially scarce.",""],[1,"347","4","Public Research and Development Funding Expansion","Another major policy is to substantially enhance the public spending on Research and Development (R&D).",""],[1,"347","4","Research Grants to Top Universities","Research grants to top universities on specific areas of development interest can be a great facilitator of innovation.",""],[1,"347","4","Link Research with Agricultural and Industrial Sectors","Linking this research to the agricultural and industrial sectors can also leverage public resources with private funding.",""],[1,"348","1","Science and Technology Grants and PPP Initiative","excellence in science and technology through grants and PPP initiative.",""],[1,"348","1","Increased Public R&D Spending","Higher government spending on R&D will also support the growth of scientific education and research.",""],[1,"348","1","IT Graduate Expansion Plan","a long-term plan should be undertaken so that current supply of 5,000 yearly IT graduates can be doubled in next 2-3 years.",""],[1,"348","1","National University IT Education Expansion","colleges under national universities should be required to start IT education.",""],[1,"348","1","IT Education Loan and Scholarship Scheme","special education loan policy and scholarship programmes should be designed to encourage students for IT education enrolment.",""],[1,"348","1","Industry-Academia Collaboration in Academic Programmes","More industry involvement will be ensured during academic programmes.",""],[1,"713","3","Industry-Academia Linkage and Placement Programme","The 8FYP will facilitate this collaboration.",""],[1,"713","4","Skill-Driven Courses in Postgraduate Colleges","With a view to enhancing skills, different skill driven courses will be introduced in post graduate colleges under National University.",""],[1,"713","5","Strengthening the University Grants Commission","Accordingly, the 8FYP will strengthen the UGC to take a leadership role in strengthening university education and advanced academic research.",""],[1,"713","5","Unified Teachers Recruitment Framework for Public Universities","A unified teachers 'recruitment framework will be introduced for all public universities to bring the uniformity and transparency in this area.",""]],"177":[[1,"642","18","National Tuberculosis Control Services","The National TB Program (NTP) of Bangladesh along with its partners has been maintaining basic TB control services with reasonable case detection and excellent treatment outcomes.",""],[1,"643","2","Neglected Tropical Diseases Reduction Interventions","By 2030 it needs to be reduced to 35.0 million and efforts are on through various interventions such as integrated vector management; promotion of clinical management; and active engagement of the communities; etc. for reducing NTDs.",""],[1,"643","5","Expanded Program on Immunization","Bangladesh has developed an effective national immunization program starting from 1979 with the implementation of the Expanded Program on Immunization (EPI).",""],[1,"657","9","Immunization Coverage Expansion and Vaccine Introduction","efforts will be strengthened to maintain and increase coverage of the immunization program, incorporating vaccines for greater number of diseases with especial focus on low performing areas.",""],[1,"657","13","Routine Immunization and Disease Surveillance Strengthening","Strengthening and sustaining of routine immunization and disease surveillance along with Supplementary Immunization Activities, NID, Measles/ MNT Campaigns etc.",""],[1,"658","9","Tuberculosis Control Programme","TB control is an active public health program which will be maintained to reduce all forms of TB prevalence and incidence rates by emphasizing DOTS implementation with effective referral.",""],[1,"658","9","Malaria Diagnostic and Staff Training Strengthening","For this, further strengthening of diagnostic procedures, RDT and emphasized training of staff will be made during the 8FYP.",""],[1,"658","9","National AIDS/STD Programme Roll-over","For this, the national AIDS/STD program (NASP) will be rolled over to the 8FYP as well with the objective to minimize the impact of the HIV/AIDS epidemic.",""],[1,"658","9","District-Level Leprosy Elimination Programme","Leprosy elimination target is to be achieved for every district during the 8FYP through training of health care staff, raising awareness among the population, active detection and patient management in pockets of high leprosy prevalence.",""],[1,"658","10","Multi-sectoral Hepatitis Prevention and Control Programme","Government interventions including establishment of a multi-sectoral approach for activities related to prevention and control; introduction of vaccine to high risk group and establishment of surveillance system for Hepatitis virus infected cases are continuing.",""],[1,"659","1","Strengthening Hepatitis B and C Control Activities","Hepatitis B & C related activities will be strengthened and intensified.",""],[1,"659","1","Neglected Tropical Disease Control and Elimination Strategy Update","Strategies for controlling and eliminating the NTDs will be revisited and updated in collaboration with relevant private sector and NGO actors.",""],[1,"659","1","Infection Prevention and Control Unit Establishment","For this, as per the global standard Infection, Prevention and Control Unit (IPCU) is needed to be established.",""]],"178":[[1,"735","13","Strengthening the Digital Financial Services and Mobile Financial Services System","the 8FYP will make the DFS/MFS system more effective in achieving financial inclusion of the poor and marginalized groups.",""],[1,"736","1","Gender-Inclusive Digital Financial Services Expansion","Although there are efforts to improve the situation through the digitization of G2P in largest transfer schemes that target rural, poor, marginal, and vulnerable women, there exist significant room for making the overall DFS architecture more gender inclusive.",""],[1,"736","1","Expansion of Financial Products for Women DFS Users","This includes, amongst others, expanding the existing product space of female DFS users.",""],[1,"740","5","Digital Payment Incentive Scheme","Incentives could be given for digital payment as opposed to making cash payment.",""],[1,"742","4","Financial Inclusion Interoperability Promotion","a) promote interoperability to speed up financial inclusion by 10 times by 2021;",""],[1,"742","4","Direct Incentives for Financial Service Uptake","b) offer direct incentives for availing financial services till mid-2021;",""],[1,"748","20","Digital Financial Inclusion Policy","Digital Financial Inclusion Policy to incentivise digital financial transactions across the population",""],[1,"749","14","Digital Financial Services Expansion","Breakthrough in access to comprehensive digital financial services [payment, savings, credit, insurance] for 80 million citizens and 40 million businesses",""]],"179":[[1,"744","2","Employment Generation Schemes","d) establish employment generation schemes;","ICT Division"],[1,"744","2","Short-Term Unemployment Benefits","e) initiate short-term unemployment benefits.","ICT Division"]],"180":[[1,"831","2","Women's Nutrition and Lifelong Health Care","nutrition and lifelong health care;",""],[1,"834","3","Communicable and Non-communicable Disease Control and School Health Behaviour Change Programme","Improved health was expected to be achieved through 1) controlling communicable and non-communicable diseases as well as increasing behavioral change communications in schools about health and healthy practices;",""],[1,"834","3","Child Nutrition Improvement Programme","2) increasing food and nutrition intakes of children;",""],[1,"834","3","Child Safe Water and Sanitation Access Initiative","3) ensuring access to safe water and sanitation to reduce environmental health hazards for children.",""],[1,"834","3","National Child Participation Platform","1) creating a national platform for allowing children to express opinions on their needs;",""],[1,"834","3","Universal Birth Registration Mobilization","3) mobilizing municipal corporations to register all births;",""],[1,"839","5","Safe Childbirth and Child Health Improvement Programme","The programme areas include arrangements for safe child birth, eradication of polio, elimination of measles and neonatal tetanus, improvement of nutrition and strengthening the school health programme.",""],[1,"839","5","Adolescent Health Strategy Development","Activities will be undertaken to develop an adolescent health strategy including counselling, building awareness for adolescents on hygienic practices, nutrition, puberty, RTI/STD and HIV/AIDS.",""],[1,"839","5","Regional Diarrhoea Awareness and ORT Promotion","Regional variations will be taken into consideration for awareness building in using ORT for treating diarrhoea.",""],[1,"839","5","Immunization Coverage Equity Initiative","Minimizing regional disparities in immunization coverage will be addressed to reduce disparities in vaccination coverage through effective programmatic interventions.",""],[1,"839","6","Nutrition-Sensitive Social Security Expansion","Nutrition related programme coverage will be expanded, including a nutrition- sensitive approach of the social security system and priority inclusion of poor households with children in social security programmes.",""],[1,"839","6","Child Nutrition Improvement for Infants Under 24 Months","Special attention will be given to improve the nutritional status of children aged 24 months and below.",""],[1,"839","6","Maternal Nutritional Supplement Provision","Provision of nutritional supplement for pregnant and lactating mother will be uncompromisingly implemented.",""],[1,"840","1","Vitamin A Supplementation for At-Risk Children and Postpartum Women","vitamin A supplements will be distributed to children with vitamin A deficiency, measles, persistent diarrhoea or severe malnutrition and to postpartum women within 6 weeks of delivery.",""],[1,"840","1","Universal Salt Iodization for Iodine Deficiency Control","On-going efforts to control iodine deficiency disorders through universal salt iodization will continue.",""],[1,"840","1","Anaemia Control Strategy","Strategies to control anaemia will include iron-foliate supplementation, anathematic treatment, fortification and BCC to increase the consumption of iron-rich foods and promoters of iron absorption.",""],[1,"840","1","Health Care Strategy for Children with Physical and Mental Disabilities","A strategy will be developed to address the health care needs of children with physical and mental disabilities.",""],[1,"840","3","Arsenic Mitigation and Alternative Drinking Water Systems","The specific objectives are to mitigate arsenic problem in drinking water by providing alternative systems",""],[1,"840","3","Expansion of Sanitary Latrine Access","increase rural and urban slum access to sanitary latrines",""],[1,"840","3","Water and Sanitation Service Expansion to Underserved Pourashava Areas","expand water and sanitation services to cover currently underserved Pourashava areas",""],[1,"840","3","Improved Water Supply for Underserved and Hard-to-Reach Areas","provide improved water supply to underserved, un-served and difficult to reach areas",""],[1,"840","3","School Sanitation and Safe Drinking Water Provision","Primary schools will be ensured access to sanitation and safe drinking water.",""]],"181":[[1,"845","6","Preferential Access to Social Security for Dalit Households","Dalit households will be given preferential access to social security programmes.",""],[1,"846","8","Full Implementation of Disability Benefit Schemes","The Government will ensure full implementation of the Disability Benefit schemes proposed in NSSS during the Eighth Plan.",""],[1,"846","8","Child Disability Benefit Cash Transfer","The Government will ensure that every child certified as having a severe disability will be provided with a regular transfer, known as the Child Disability Benefit.",""],[1,"846","8","Severe Childhood Disability Identification Mechanism","The Government will develop a mechanism to identify severe disability among children, which will not only include children with physical disability but also other disabilities like autism, cognitive, mental, sensory impairment, etc.",""],[1,"846","8","Conditionality and Enforcement Against Child Begging","Mechanisms will also be established to remove children with disabilities from the street, making the Child Disability Benefit conditional on children not involved in begging.",""],[1,"846","8","Penalties for Employing Child Beggars","A system of penalties will be introduced for those who employ children as beggars.",""],[1,"846","9","Disability Grant Reform into Regular Transfer Scheme","The current disability grant managed by the Ministry of Social Welfare will be reformed into a scheme that provides a regular transfer to all poor and vulnerable citizens of Bangladesh with a severe disability.","Ministry of Social Welfare"],[1,"847","1","Disability Identification and Appeals Mechanism","identifying severe disability and will establish an appeals mechanism for those who feel that they have been unfairly excluded.",""],[1,"847","2","Reformed Disability Benefit","The introduction of a reformed Disability Benefit will mark a significant change in the lives of the disabled citizens who are poor.",""],[1,"847","2","Vocational Education and Small Business Support for Disability Benefit Recipients","The Ministry of Social Welfare will complement the Disability Benefit by providing additional support to recipients by ensuring access to vocational education and small business schemes and eliminating discrimination in the labour market.","Ministry of Social Welfare"]],"182":[[1,"685","3","Robust and Holistic Education Strategy with Regulatory Framework","the 8FYP will articulate the strategies and policies to address the challenges in the education sector.",""],[1,"707","3","Decentralization of Primary and Secondary Education Governance","Education resource mobilization, budget making, management and service delivery will be strengthened by decentralization involving Upazila and district based-planning and management of primary and secondary school education.",""],[1,"707","3","National Education Commission Oversight Mechanism","A permanent statutory National Education Commission, anticipated in Education Policy 2010, will be used as a mechanism for guiding, exercising oversight and assessing progress and impact of education reforms.",""],[1,"707","4","Education and Skills Data and Survey System","BBS will regularly conduct separate surveys on skills and create a separate database.",""],[1,"707","4","Education and Training Quality Indicator Development","Also, new indicators to be developed that measures the quality-aspect of education and training.",""]],"183":[[1,"584","1","Safe and Sustainable Transport Access Expansion","By 2030, provide access to safe, affordable, accessible and sustainable transport systems for all, improving road safety, notably by expanding public transport, with special attention to the needs of those in vulnerable situations",""],[1,"584","5","Universal Access to Safe and Inclusive Public Spaces","By 2030, provide universal access to safe, inclusive and accessible, green and public spaces, particularly for women and children, older persons and persons with disabilities",""],[1,"584","6","Strengthen National and Regional Development Planning","Support positive economic, social and environmental links between urban, peri-urban and rural areas by strengthening national and regional development planning",""],[1,"584","7","Integrated Urban Policy and Planning Adoption Programme","By 2020 increase the number of cities and human settlements adopting and implementing integrated policies and plans towards inclusion, resource efficiency, mitigation and adaptation to climate change, resilience to disasters.",""],[1,"584","11","Environmentally Sustainable and Resilient Urban Development","Environmentally sustainable and resilient urban development by promoting clean energy and sustainable use of land and resources in urban development, by protecting ecosystems and biodiversity, by building urban resilience, by reducing disaster risks and by mitigating and adapting to climate change.",""],[1,"602","6","Wetland Filling for Urban Expansion","Continuous filling of wetlands for expansion of the city both by the public sector and private organizations;",""],[1,"606","9","Urban Governance Decentralization Reform","Some high-level policy decisions relating to urban governance, especially decentralization is critical to move forward with the urban agenda.",""],[1,"606","9","Urban Governance Strategy Development","The 8FYP will draw on this in defining the urban governance strategy.",""],[1,"607","1","Affordable Housing Projects Under Implementation","Currently 15 flat & 16 plot projects (7286 flats & 2558 plots) are running to minimize acute housing problem & provide affordable housing for all.",""],[1,"607","1","Government Officials Housing Construction Projects","Construction of another 9734 flats under 17 projects is going on in Dhaka, Narayanganj, Chittagong and Noakhali.",""],[1,"607","3","E-Management System for Government Employee Services","Through e-management system, all kinds of information and services for government employees have been simplified including allotment of houses in Dhaka.",""],[1,"611","7","Urban Infrastructure Development and Municipal Capacity-Building Programme","LGED through its intervention since 1990s has tried to address planned intervention in infrastructure development, maintenance and rehabilitation needs and to develop the capacity of the municipalities, especially to raise income, improve financial management capacity and design municipal services in a planned way.",""],[1,"611","7","Urban Water Supply, Drainage, Sanitation, Roads, and Market Infrastructure Projects","Various development projects have been implemented related to a range of urban infrastructure services including water supply, drainage, sanitation, urban roads, and urban market places.",""],[1,"611","7","Urban Local Government Institution Capacity Development Programme","Additionally, projects and programmes have been implemented to develop the capacities of urban LGIs.",""],[1,"612","1","Municipal Governance Support Project for Inclusive Urban Infrastructure","Under the 7FYP, a World Bank-supported Municipal Governance Support Project (MGSP) has shown good-practice examples of inclusive infrastructures in 26 municipalities.",""],[1,"612","3","Drainage System Construction","Construction of drainage system according to drainage master plan and considering a whole network from starting to outfall.",""],[1,"612","5","Case-by-Case Coastal Drainage Planning","In the coastal districts, drainage plans must include ebbs and tides.",""],[1,"612","8","Waterfront Park Construction","Waterfront parks that can be constructed in synergy with other development projects such as river, canal dredging of BWDB, BIWTA or LGED.",""],[1,"612","9","Waterfront Park Development in Bridge Construction Projects","In the bridge construction projects, LGED has been utilizing the river banks (the space acquired as approach of bridge or being used as ground level of viaduct) as waterfront parks.",""],[1,"613","1","Riverfront Public Space Restoration","The national river conservation commission and BIWTA have been active to restore the riverfront public spaces.",""],[1,"613","1","LGED-Led Riverfront Space Development","LGED can also take the lead for restoration of riverfront spaces and development with help from the district administration.","LGED | district administration"],[1,"613","4","Urban Governance Improvement Projects in Municipalities","Since 1990s, through its different developing partner assisted projects, LGED has been working for improving urban governance in the municipalities.",""],[1,"613","4","Mainstream Urban Governance in Urban Local Government Institutions","Therefore, a good strategy is to be developed to mainstream urban governance in urban LGIs.",""],[1,"614","1","ICT-Based Municipal Office Management and Decision-Making","Under the 8FYP, ICT-based office management and decision making will be a priority.",""],[1,"614","2","Municipal Staff Training Programme","LGED is entrusted with providing training to most of the staff of the municipalities.",""],[1,"614","2","Urban Management Unit Capacity Expansion","To provide training in a comprehensive way, the urban management unit of LGED requires more staff and capacity building.",""],[1,"614","3","Municipal Development Planning Programme","Local Government Division and Local Government Engineering Department have so far developed development plans for 256 municipalities.","Local Government Division | Local Government Engineering Department"],[1,"614","3","Municipal Development Plan Preparation by RAJUK and Development Authorities","Six development plans of different municipalities were developed by RAJUK and other development authorities.",""],[1,"614","6","Urban and Rural Local Government Institutional Reform","To move towards that goal, the PP2041 envisages major institutional reforms for urban and rural LGIs.",""],[1,"615","1","Democratically Elected and Accountable City Governance Reform","Cities will be characterized by a governance system that entails democratically elected, strong and accountable city governments.",""],[1,"615","2","Legal Clarification of City Government Responsibilities","City governments will have well-defined responsibilities that are enshrined in the legal framework.",""],[1,"615","3","Coordination Mechanisms for Shared Area Management","The coordination mechanisms with higher levels of government in the management of common areas will be well defined within the principle that matters that involve exclusively the interest of the city are primarily the responsibility of the city.",""],[1,"615","4","Municipal Financial Autonomy Framework","Financial autonomy of cities will be ensured through a legally defined financial framework that involves sharing of taxes, national grants and market borrowing.",""],[1,"615","7","National Grant System for Co-financing and Incentive Payments","the national grant system will be used for co-financing or as incentive payments.",""],[1,"615","8","Participatory Urban Planning Consultation Process","At the city level, the planning process will be participatory with a well-defined and structured consultation process with the residents.",""],[1,"615","9","Urban Local Government Reform Implementation Plan","Under the 8FYP, the LGD will take the lead to develop the first phase of a time-bound actionable implementation plan for the periods FY2021-FY2025 in consultation with the LGIs, other ministries and national research institutions.","LGD | LGIs | other ministries"],[1,"615","10","Strengthening Urban Institutions and Service Agencies","the functioning of the existing urban institutions and service agencies will be strengthened to improve the delivery of basic urban services.",""],[1,"616","2","Secondary Cities Development Measures","the government would take measures for the development of infrastructure, services, innovation, human capital, good government and strong enabling environments.",""],[1,"616","8","Urbanization Strategy for Balanced Urban and Regional Development","The government will also adopt an urbanization strategy that will guide investment decisions around the country for balanced urban and regional development.",""],[1,"616","9","Urban Development Planning Preparation","Preparation of urban development plans for all the urban areas/centres consisting of Structure Plans, Detailed Area Plans and Action Plans",""],[1,"616","10","Urban Building Control Legal Formalization","Enact appropriate laws to formalize the current building control practices in the urban areas around the country.",""],[1,"616","12","District and Upazila Planning Preparation","Preparation of District level regional plans and Upazila level sub-regional plans.",""],[1,"616","13","National Drainage and Sewerage Infrastructure Planning","Preparations of infrastructure plan (road, drain, natural water course) that can help prioritize investment in drainage planning and sewerage infrastructure throughout the country.",""],[1,"616","14","Pilot Land Management Tools in Urban Fringe Areas","On a pilot basis, carry out one or more tools in land management such as guided land development (GLD), land readjustment, or land pooling in the fringe areas of some urban areas of the country.",""],[1,"616","15","Land Use Regulation for Areas Outside Statutory Urban Plans","Land use regulation for areas outside the jurisdiction of the statutory urban plans will be developed and enforced in view of the fact that many areas will become urban soon.",""],[1,"616","16","Urban Conservation and Renewal Projects","Undertake urban conservation and renewal projects for old, traditional and culturally rich areas.",""],[1,"617","1","National Building Code Adoption","Adopt building codes for the entire country.",""],[1,"617","2","Building Code Enforcement for Hazard-Resistant Construction","Enable concerned agencies in enforcing building codes to protect buildings against hazards such as fire.",""],[1,"617","3","Emerging Hazards Preparedness Planning","Prepare plans to deal with emerging hazards that will have implication for land development and urban expansion.",""],[1,"617","4","Economic Development Corridor Development","The 8FYP will give special emphasis on the development of hard and soft infrastructure (i.e., roads, rail, air services and political, social, and business networks) for facilitating the flows of materials, people, trade, goods, services, and information among the cities of the development corridor.",""]],"184":[[1,"548","2","Climate Fiscal Framework for Public Financial Management","In 2014, the government adopted a Climate Fiscal Framework to mainstream climate finance in the countries Public Financial Management (PFM) systems and processes encompassing strategic planning, budget formulation, budget execution, and parliamentary oversight.","Finance Division | Office of the Auditor General"],[1,"551","2","Environmental Fiscal Reform Initiative","The government is also committed to initiate Environmental Fiscal Reforms (EFR), which can reduce the pricing distortions presently undermining sound environmental management.",""],[1,"551","2","Green Growth Fiscal Incentive Adjustments","an assessment needs to be done on fiscal incentives and necessary adjustments can be brought to incentivise green growth.",""],[1,"551","2","Environmental Management Financing Increase","However, all these reforms must end up in financing environmental management sufficiently.","MoEFCC"],[1,"557","17","Environmental Fiscal Reform Package","The Government will undertake a wide array of environmental fiscal reforms for improving environmental performance to attain sustainable development and green growth.",""],[1,"557","18","Green Public Financial Management Integration","The Government will prioritize the integration of environmental conservation in budgetary management by increasingly undertaking green Public Financial Management (PFM), which will depend on green accounting, procurement and auditing.","Ministries of Finance | Planning | concerned line ministries"],[1,"557","18","Environmental Cost Accounting for Investment Project Selection","Project selection will require full accounting of environmental costs for all investment projects.",""],[1,"557","18","Green PFM Agenda Implementation under the 8FYP","The incorporation of the \"Green PFM\" agenda will happen under the 8FYP and institutional capacities in the Ministries of Finance, Planning and concerned line ministries will be improved and strengthened to achieve this objective.","Ministries of Finance | Planning | concerned line ministries"],[1,"558","5","Reduction of Fossil Fuel Subsidies","The Government will increasingly reduce its subsidies on fossil fuels to support its policies and goals on climate change.",""],[1,"558","5","Green Tax on Fossil Fuel Consumption","The Government will also introduce a green tax on the consumption of fossil fuels as it discourages the emission of CO2 from fossil fuels but also provides a useful avenue for generation of revenue that will be used for supporting clean energy and other environmental programmes.",""],[1,"559","5","Mainstreaming Environmental Fiscal Reforms within the Ministry of Finance","the Government will pursue such partnerships to mainstream EFR within the MoF.","Ministry of Finance (MoF)"],[1,"564","2","Green Accounting and Green Budgeting Initiative","The Government will undertake initiatives to improve the state of green accounting at the both macro and micro levels.","Bangladesh Bureau of Statistics (BBS)"],[1,"564","3","Comprehensive Emissions Accounting System","The Government is committed to develop a comprehensive data on the emissions from all major sources of economic activities.",""],[1,"564","4","Natural Resource Accounting System","The BBS will generate physical statistics about the stock of natural resources and their changes over time.",""],[1,"564","5","Green GDP Computation","The Government will compute Green GDP by factoring in the environmental consequences of growth - after accounting for the depletion of resources, degradation of the environment and restorative environmental initiatives.",""],[1,"564","6","Green Budgeting and Environmental Tax Reform","Government shall endeavour to greening the overall budget and integrate environmental considerations including budgetary provisions for offsetting or minimizing the adverse impacts of development interventions in all development sectors.",""],[1,"578","7","Delta Plan 2100 Environmental Management Integration","The Government aims to support the management of the environment in the long-run by adopting the broad strategies of the Delta Plan 2100, and also integrate Environmental Fiscal Reforms (EFR) into economic planning.",""],[1,"578","7","Environmental Fiscal Reforms Integration","The Government aims to support the management of the environment in the long-run by adopting the broad strategies of the Delta Plan 2100, and also integrate Environmental Fiscal Reforms (EFR) into economic planning.",""],[1,"579","2","Environmental Fiscal Reforms","under the Eighth Plan, initiating Environmental Fiscal Reforms (EFR) will become one of the central agendas in planning for the environment - as the Government is committed to introduce both \"beneficiary pays\" and \"polluter pays\" principles in managing the concerns about the environment.",""],[1,"579","2","Increased Environmental Development Programme Allocations","the Eighth Plan highlights a substantial increase in the allocations in the Annual Development Programmes (ADP) dealing with sustainable development programmes for sustainable development (Table 8.6)",""]],"185":[[1,"59","3","District-Level Decentralization of Primary and Secondary Education","Primary and secondary education will be decentralized to district level, teacher training will be expanded, private provision of education and training will be promoted, and the education budget will grow from 2.0% of GDP in FY2019 to 3.0% of GDP by FY2025.",""],[1,"90","4","Education for All Strategy","the main highlight of the 7FYP strategy is to achieve Education for All (EFA) by FY2020.",""],[1,"91","1","Non-Formal Education Coverage Expansion","Progress with increasing the coverage of NFE continued under the 7FYP",""],[1,"787","4","Primary Education Stipend Scheme","This programme is designed to provide cash assistance through a stipend programme to all the eligible primary school students.",""],[1,"788","1","Primary Education Stipend Project","The Primary Education Stipend Project (PESP) is being implemented by the Ministry of Primary and Mass Education.","Ministry of Primary and Mass Education"],[1,"788","4","Primary School Stipend Increase","it is proposed to implement the NSSS recommendation during the 8FYP.",""],[1,"789","3","Girls' Stipend and Support Transfer Design","One possible approach is to set the transfer (or enhanced stipend) amount equal to the child benefit amount (BDT 900 per month) but separated into three components - BDT 300 as stipend; BDT 300 for purchasing of hygiene products; and BDT 300 for health-related expenses.",""],[1,"789","3","School Security and Safe Space Access Measures","Moreover, merit type interventions such as improved security at the schools, local and community levels as well as access to safe space groups are of public good types with equal access to all girls aged 10 to 19.",""],[1,"789","9","Education Investment Increase and Pilot Scale-Up","Investment for education intervention should be provided by the Ministry of Primary and Mass Education (as part of the proposed increased allocation of 3.0 per cent of GDP in 8FYP in place of current 2 per cent of allocation), while investment for other interventions should be covered from the social protection budget as well as from MoWCA budget.","Ministry of Primary and Mass Education | MoWCA"],[1,"789","9","National Pilot Project for Intervention Scale-Up","However, government should first undertake a pilot project before scaling it up for the entire nation.",""],[1,"817","4","Universal Quality Formal Education Expansion","Universal access to quality education at all levels with enhanced completion for girls and boys has to be ensured.",""],[1,"817","4","Transition Non-formal Education to Formal Education","gradual transition of all non-formal education to formal education should be planned and acted upon.",""],[1,"817","4","Teacher Quality and Curriculum Improvement Reform","Quality education for teachers, curriculum improvement (promote equality and inclusiveness), introduction of extra-curricular activities to build confidence and to overcome the limitations in learning outcomes should be ensured.",""],[1,"817","4","Poverty-Focused Education Support Package","Support for transition from primary and completion of secondary education for both boys and girls should be ensured through poverty focused stipends, free education, books, campaigns and so on.",""],[1,"817","4","Scholarships and Girls' College Access Support","Scholarships, special quota provisions, proximity of colleges, infrastructure including accommodation, transport, water/sanitation for girls and such support for continuation at the college and tertiary levels need to be ensured.",""],[1,"817","4","Women Teachers and Safe School Environment Initiative","Increased proportion of trained women teachers, teachers trained on inclusive education and making the education environment safe for girls are essential.",""],[1,"817","4","Private Higher Education Registration and Licensing Standards","The registration and licensing process for private universities and colleges should have criteria on facilities and quota for girls.",""],[1,"817","4","Language and Teaching Staff Curriculum Preparation","Learning language should be emphasized and curriculum and teaching staff should be prepared.",""]],"186":[[1,"507","3","Water, Flood Control and Irrigation Projects","notably, the implementation of the Tribal Health, Nutrition and Population Plan (THNPP), National Education Policy of 2010, the Third Primary Education Development Program (PEDP 3) and various water, flood control and irrigation projects",""],[1,"533","12","Community Forest Expansion and Biodiversity Protection Measures","Community forest will be encouraged and expanded to conserve biodiversity and the watersheds, and measures will be taken to protect wildlife and biodiversity.",""],[1,"533","13","Integrated Watershed Management for Water Flow Preservation","Special initiatives will be undertaken to ensure the flow of water in creeks, water bodies and waterfalls by preserving the natural sources and integrated watershed management.",""],[1,"844","1","Village and Mouza Community Forest Development","Village/mouza community forest will be created and expanded in the CHT to conserve biodiversity and the watersheds and ensure that people have access to water.",""],[1,"844","1","Community-Based Afforestation Initiative","Efforts will be undertaken involving the local communities for afforestation over the region.",""],[1,"844","1","Wildlife and Biodiversity Protection Measures","Measures will be taken to protect wildlife and biodiversity.",""],[1,"844","1","Integrated Watershed and Water Flow Management","Special initiatives will be undertaken to ensure the flow of water in creeks, water bodies and waterfalls by preserving the natural sources and integrated watershed management.",""]],"187":[[1,"501","5","Rural Transformation and Service Improvement Programme","The State shall adopt effective measures to bring about a radical transformation in the rural areas through the promotion of an agricultural revolution, the provision of rural electrification, the development of cottage and other industries, and the improvement of education, communications and public health, in those areas",""],[1,"506","5","Nationwide Participatory Rural Development Promotion","This practice of participatory development should be promoted nationwide.",""],[1,"516","1","Rural Development Planning and Implementation Reform","In light with the government's priority program \"My Village-My Town\", a philosophical change in planning, promoting and implementing rural development program and projects to be visioned during 8FYP.",""],[1,"525","12","Balanced District Development Focus on Poor Regions","Ensure balanced development across districts, with a particular focus on the poor region;",""],[1,"525","15","Rural Development Coordination Mechanism","RDCD has been assigned for coordination of the rural development and relevant activities both at policy and implementation level.",""],[1,"532","1","Lagging Rural Areas Development Support","Special efforts will be made to reduce some of the gaps during the 8FYP by improving infrastructure, giving priority to the needs of these lagging areas in allocating public spending on agriculture and water management, and improving the flow of credit to these areas to boost non-farm enterprises.",""],[1,"532","1","Rural Support Institutions Programme Prioritization","The activities of the various rural support institutions will prioritize these lagging regions in designing their programmes for the 8FYP.",""],[1,"533","1","Integrated Social and Economic Development Support","ensure development in education, healthcare, food and nutrition, employment and protection of land-right, resources, and farm and nonfarm activities.",""]],"188":[[1,"288","6","Trade Agreements with Regional Communities","Bangladesh would be well advised to reach trading arrangements with these groupings.",""],[1,"300","8","Tariff Structure Rationalization for FTA Readiness","Thus, rationalizing Bangladesh's tariff structure then becomes a national imperative if the country seeks FTAs with any country or region in the future.",""],[1,"300","9","Post-LDC Graduation Trade and Commerce Action Plan","The Ministry of Commerce will therefore prepare and implement an action plan for overcoming the potential challenges of trade and commerce after graduation.","Ministry of Commerce"],[1,"301","1","Free Trade Agreement and Preferential Trade Agreement Negotiation","The Ministry is now negotiating with a number trading partners for signing bilateral Free Trade Agreements (FTAs) or Preferential Trade Agreements (PTAs).","Ministry of Commerce"],[1,"301","1","Expansion of Preferential and Free Trade Agreements","The Ministry of Commerce aims to accord as many as PTAs, FTAs and continue efforts joining CEPA during the 8th Five Year Plan.","Ministry of Commerce"],[1,"301","1","Free Trade Agreement Policy Guideline Revision","The Ministry plans to revise the Free Trade Agreement policy guideline during the 8th Five Year Plan to make it more pragmatic.","Ministry"],[1,"301","2","FTA/PTA Impact Study for Lebanon","It has undertaken another study for examining the impact of signing FTA/PTA with Lebanon.","Ministry of Commerce"],[1,"301","2","Joint CEPA Study with India","The Ministry has also taken program for conducting the joint study on Comprehensive Economic Partnership Agreement (CEPA) with India.","Ministry of Commerce"],[1,"301","3","Free Trade Agreement Negotiation Initiative","initiative will be taken for signing FTA with European Union (EU), Association of Southeast Asian Nations (ASEAN), Eurasian Economic Union (EAEU) & MERCOSUR Countries.",""],[1,"301","3","Trade Negotiations Capacity Building","The Ministry is currently engaged in building trade negotiations capacity among officials in the Ministry and relevant agencies.","The Ministry"]],"189":[[1,"259","5","Prisoner Welfare and Rehabilitation Improvement Programme","As a result, under the 8FYP, the Government aims to ensure better facilities for prisoners, by allowing them to have access to professional training and counselling services, develop advanced infrastructure to reduce prisoner burden - and provide special care for female and under-aged prisoners.",""]],"190":[[1,"528","3","Rural SME Support and Patronage Programme","With directions of RDCD, BRDB has been providing many supports like funds, training, technology, raw materials etc. to make the rural SMEs sustainable though several projects uplifting the rural socio-economic conditions.","RDCD | BRDB"],[1,"528","4","Rural Energy Access Development Initiative","During the upcoming 8th five- year period, BRDB will undertake necessary development initiatives to provide low cost energy facilities in a feasible way to the less-facilitated communities of those remote areas.",""],[1,"529","1","Agricultural Mechanization Services through KSS","Mechanization services will provide to the farmers through Krishok Samobay Samitee (KSS).",""],[1,"529","1","Farmer Sensitization on Agricultural Technology Use","Alongside this endeavour will be made to sensitize the rural farmers to use this technology and also training will be imparted for the utilization and repair of the machineries.",""],[1,"531","7","Public Investment in Farm Technology and Productivity","Supportive policies include the implementation of BDP2100, public investment in farm technology and productivity, support policies for strengthening fishing activities including the harnessing of the potentials of the Blue Economy, public investment in rural infrastructure, and credit policies to promote non-farm economic activities.",""],[1,"531","7","Fishing Sector and Blue Economy Support Policies","Supportive policies include the implementation of BDP2100, public investment in farm technology and productivity, support policies for strengthening fishing activities including the harnessing of the potentials of the Blue Economy, public investment in rural infrastructure, and credit policies to promote non-farm economic activities.",""],[1,"532","2","Strengthening of Non-Formal Education Strategy","The implementation of the Non-Formal Education strategy will be strengthened to eliminate rural adult illiteracy for both males and females, increase rural education coverage and quality, and provide skills training through the various rural support institutions.",""],[1,"532","2","Rural Skills Development Training for Disadvantaged Groups","The training will provide skills development training to the rural poor, particularly disadvantaged women and socially excluded groups, to generate self-employment in non-farm sectors.",""],[1,"532","2","On-Farm Research and Extension Training Services","The on-farm research and extension services will impart training to farmers to enable farm productivity increases.",""]],"191":[[1,"670","10","Rights Protection and Non-Discrimination Framework","Protect, promote and monitor rights and non-discrimination: right to adequate food and to be able to feed oneself in dignity; and all other - related rights (employment, children's rights, women's rights, focus on marginalized groups, poor households and women)",""],[1,"670","10","Refugee and Humanitarian Law Compliance","Uphold refugee and humanitarian law in protracted crises",""]],"192":[[1,"679","7","Child Marriage Law Enforcement and Awareness Campaign","Strengthen the implementation of the law against child marriage with support from local government agencies, education staff, NGO-based health and social workers and the community leaders.",""]],"193":[[1,"756","2","Bengali Language and Literature Development Programme","Programmes for development of Bengali language and literature and reference books for higher education were continued with greater emphasis.",""],[1,"756","2","Fine Arts Education Expansion in Schools","To enhance appreciation of fine arts, various fine art subjects were introduced in primary and secondary schools as per education policy.",""],[1,"756","3","Shilpakala Academy and District Library Expansion","The activities of the establishment, expansion and development of Shilpakala Academy and library at district and upazila level were continued under the Bangladesh Shilpakala Academy and the Department of Public Library respectively.",""],[1,"756","3","Free Education Materials for Disadvantaged Students","Students and people from impoverished backgrounds were provided free education materials from both public and private libraries.",""],[1,"756","3","Secondary School Cultural Trainer Recruitment","for the purpose of conducting cultural activities in the secondary schools in district and upazila levels, the recruitment of various trainers has played an important role in reducing poverty through generating jobs.",""],[1,"756","4","Public Library Infrastructure Construction and Development","Construction and development of infrastructure of libraries by Directorate of Public Libraries have continued at the district and upazila levels to provide and expand reading services for the population.","Directorate of Public Libraries"],[1,"756","5","Expansion of Shilpakala Academies and Folk Arts and Crafts Development","The activities of bodies established under the MoCA in the form of establishment and expansion of Shilpakala Academies at the district and upazila levels, and the preservation, expansion and development of folk art and culture through Bangladesh Folk Arts and Crafts Foundation have widened the scope for a significant number of women to learn more on the art and culture.","MoCA"],[1,"757","5","Bangladesh Shilpakala Academy Curriculum Materials and Teacher Training Support","Bangladesh Shilpakala Academy needs to be equipped to produce a large number of subject oriented texts and train teachers for matching with national education policy requirements.",""],[1,"758","3","Bengali Language and Literature Development and Medium of Instruction Facilities","Develop Bengali language and literature and create facilities to develop Bengali as the medium of instruction.",""],[1,"758","6","Book Production and Affordable Publication Support","Help and promote production and publication of quality books and make them available to the masses at reasonable prices.",""],[1,"758","7","National Book Policy Implementation Programmes","Undertake programmes for implementation of the national book policy.",""],[1,"758","10","National-to-Rural Library Network Development","Establish and develop a library network system from the national to the rural level and introduce modern technology through the entire network.",""],[1,"758","12","Fine and Performing Arts Infrastructure Development","Develop infrastructural facilities for fine and performing arts including drama and theatre and explore private and voluntary involvement in this area.",""],[1,"759","3","Library Network Development Programme","Programmes will be undertaken to develop the library network, infrastructural facilities and services from national to the rural levels in order to meet the education, recreational, cultural and information need of people from all walks of life.",""],[1,"759","5","Fine Arts Introduction in Primary and Secondary Education","Fine arts like music, painting, arts & crafts, recitation, acting; dancing, theatrical performances would be introduced at primary & secondary level as per education policy.",""],[1,"759","7","Bengali Language, Literature, and Reference Books Development Programme","Programmes for development of Bengali language and literature and reference books for higher education will be continued with greater emphasis;",""],[1,"759","8","Book Development and Reading Habits Programme","Programmes will be undertaken for book development and development of reading habits;",""]],"194":[[1,"821","5","Women's Access to Productive Resources Expansion","Women's access to productive resources should be increased.",""],[1,"821","5","Women's Inheritance Rights Enforcement and Family Code Review","Community orientation and legal enactment on the Prime Minister's directive to give women due share of their inherited property should be initiated and enforced.",""],[1,"821","5","Joint Khas Land Distribution and Forestry Co-management","The current practice of distribution of khas land in the name of both spouses of poor families and women's access to forestry resources through co-management groups should continue and expand.",""],[1,"821","5","Disaster-Induced Migration Housing and Land Support","In case of disaster induced migration, women should be considered as a special group for housing or land support.",""],[1,"821","5","CEDAW-Based Inheritance Law Review","The spirit of CEDAW and its application in case of inheritance in other countries with Muslim majority should be assessed and considered for a uniform family code.",""],[1,"822","1","Women's Participation in Community Resource Governance","Women's participation in accessing and taking decisions regarding community resources should be ensured by provisions of women's participation under the Social Forestry Rules, Water Management Policy, Forestry Sector Policy, WATSAN Policy and such others.",""],[1,"822","1","Women's Access to Community Resources in Markets and Khas Lands","All sectors should consider access of women to community resources such as shop distribution in markets, or agriculture in khas lands.",""],[1,"822","1","Women's Participation Monitoring in Resource Associations","Women's participation in water, forestry or such other associations and groups should be ensured to reach a critical mass and monitored to benefit them.",""],[1,"822","1","Training and Information Support for Women's Participation","Provision of imparting training and providing information should be incorporated to prepare women to participate effectively in these groups.",""],[1,"823","5","Women’s Inclusion in Sectoral Committees and Associations","Memberships in different sectoral committees and associations including business associations should enforce measures to include more women.",""],[1,"823","5","Gender-Responsive Representation in Water and Resource Management Bodies","The water management associations, sanitation committees, water supply committees, disaster management committee, forest management committees and such others formed as per the policies/rules of the sectoral ministries should include women with clear TORs.",""],[1,"823","5","Orientation on Women’s Roles and Equal Decision-Making Participation","Women should be oriented on their roles and responsibilities and their male counterparts should be oriented on equal participation and roles in decision making.",""]],"195":[[1,"830","2","Positive Portrayal of Women in Media Initiative","Portrayal of women's positive image will be promoted.",""],[1,"830","3","Men's Engagement Programme for Gender Equality","More programmes would include active engagement of men in all spheres to promote women's advancement and curb men's participation or support of harmful practices.",""],[1,"830","3","Men as Advocates for Social Norm Change","It is also important to develop groups of men as advocate to change social behaviour, prevent VAW, share household responsibility, promote gender equality and hold other men accountable for discriminatory behaviour.",""],[1,"831","3","Joint Gender Equality Advocacy Initiatives","Development and advocacy initiatives on gender equality issues and to form public opinion against harmful practices would be pursued jointly and they should be partners in better delivery of services, especially in rural and remote areas.",""]],"196":[[1,"844","7","Dalit Education Inclusion Quota and Access Measures","a special quota for Dalit and other excluded students will be created in government schools and colleges, and access of Dalit adolescents and youth to all government owned skill training institutions will be ensured.",""],[1,"844","8","Dalit Outreach and Participation Support","Local Government Institutions, i.e. Upazila and Union Parishads, along with NGOs will be involved to locate disadvantaged Dalit people and help enable them to participate in development activities.",""],[1,"844","8","Dalit Representation in Political Party Committees","Dalit representation in all committees of political parties at national and local level will be ensured.",""],[1,"845","1","Anti-Discrimination Awareness Campaign for Dalits and Excluded Communities","Massive awareness raising to stop all kinds of discrimination and untouchability against Dalits and excluded communities will be undertaken.",""],[1,"845","2","Special Commission on Dalits","The Government will form a special commission on Dalits to evaluate current environment and level of discrimination and provide key recommendations on improving the socio-economic conditions of Dalit communities in Bangladesh.",""],[1,"845","3","Review of Colony Allotment Policy for Dalit Service Access","The Government will review the allotment policy of colonies under every City Corporation and municipality and ensure that marginalized groups of Dalits are allotted harassment free access to electricity, gas and water supply services.",""],[1,"845","4","Preferential Municipal Cleaning Job Access for Dalits","Dalits will be given preferential access to cleaning jobs in municipalities, including lease of public toilets of City Corporations to Dalit sweepers.",""],[1,"845","7","Public Education Against Discrimination and Equity-Inclusion Campaign","Massive public education against discrimination and towards equity-inclusion will be promoted, building greater transparency through social audits and public hearings.",""]],"197":[[1,"844","9","Khas Land Allotment for Dalit Settlement","The Ministry of Land will give priority to allotting khas land to people of Dalit communities for settlement under the Asrayan type housing project.","Ministry of Land"],[1,"844","9","Estate Land Earmarking for Tea Garden Workers Housing","For tea garden workers, planters/owners will be encouraged to earmark land within the estates so that they can build their own dwelling.",""],[1,"844","9","Sweeper Colony Construction Programme","Special programmes like construction of sweeper colonies will be implemented.",""],[1,"845","5","Dalit Family Resettlement Support","Proper resettlement will be provided for evicted Dalit families.",""]],"198":[[1,"5","5","Padma Bridge Construction Project","Despite the withdrawal of committed funding by a development partner, this largest bridge of Bangladesh currently under construction by the national finance will connect southwestern parts of Bangladesh to the rest of the country.",""],[1,"5","5","Dhaka Metro Rail and Elevated Expressway Construction","Construction of metro rail and elevated expressway in the capital with a view to ease the traffic congestion is moving faster.",""],[1,"5","5","Payra and Matarbari Deep-Sea Port Construction","To put the impetus on export trade construction of two deep-sea ports at Payra and Matarbari is approaching towards completion at a faster pace.",""],[1,"61","3","Integrated Transport System Development Strategy","The transport sector strategy in the 8FYP will follow the strategy initiated in the 7FYP with an emphasis in areas where performance gaps exist.",""],[1,"61","3","Modern Transport Technology Introduction","Special emphasis will be placed on the introduction of modern technology for increasing capacity and improving quality and productivity of the system",""],[1,"61","3","Seaport Development and Dhaka Transport Linkage","Special emphasis will be placed on ... development of the two seaports with smooth transport links to Dhaka",""],[1,"61","3","Transport Mode Integration Initiative","Special emphasis will be placed on ... integration of road, rail and inland water transport",""],[1,"61","3","Regional Transport Connectivity Participation","Special emphasis will be placed on ... participation in global and regional transport connectivity initiatives that help develop the land route links between South Asia and East Asia through Bangladesh.",""],[1,"61","3","Transformational Transport Infrastructure Completion","On the investment side, the strategy would continue to prioritize timely completion of all transformational transport infrastructure projects consisting of inter-city bridges, highways, tunnels, and sea ports",""],[1,"61","3","Transport Project Supervision and Delay Control","These transformational projects are highly capital intensive, are multi-year in nature, and require strong supervision to avoid cost over-runs and delays.",""],[1,"61","3","Mass Urban Transit Expansion","The 8FYP will maintain the priority given to mass urban transit facilities",""],[1,"61","3","MRT Line-6 Completion Acceleration","The 8FYP will maintain the priority given to mass urban transit facilities and will speed up the completion of MRT Line-6 (the first elevated Metro Rail of Bangladesh) by December 2021.",""],[1,"62","1","Inter-Modal Transport Balance Improvement","The 8FYP would put special emphasis to improve the inter-modal transport balance, where progress was limited during the 7FYP, with greater emphasis on inland waterways that are low-cost in nature and are environment friendly.",""],[1,"62","1","Inter-District Airline Connectivity and New International Transport Construction","The importance of transport, especially air transport, for tourism would be emphasized with a focus on strengthening inter-district airline connectivity and the construction of a new international transport.",""],[1,"62","1","Transport User Charges and Fee Reform","Greater efforts will be made to improve resource mobilization through the introduction of user charges and fees for a range of public transport services including road user charges, air and sea port fees, inland water and rail fares.",""],[1,"88","3","Transport System Improvement Programme","Special emphasis was placed on the introduction of modern technology for increasing capacity and improving quality and productivity of the system, development of the two seaports with smooth transport links to Dhaka, establishment of effective railway linkages between the east and west zones of the country, integration of road, rail and inland water transport, and participation in global and regional transport connectivity initiatives that help develop the land route links between South Asia and East Asia through Bangladesh.",""],[1,"88","4","Transformational Transport Infrastructure Investment","On the investment side, a conscious decision was taken to prioritize transformational transport infrastructure projects that helps modernize the Bangladesh transport network so as to improve the mobility of goods and services across the nation, facilitate international trade, reduce cost and improve competitiveness.",""],[1,"88","4","Dhaka Mass Transit and MRT Line 6 Completion","Recognizing the special challenge posed by growing urbanization and urban traffic congestion, the 7FYP sought to introduce mass transit starting with the capital city Dhaka, with a targeted completion of MRT Line-6 (the first elevated Metro Rail of Bangladesh) in December 2021.",""],[1,"88","4","Public-Private Partnership Transport Financing Strategy","Mindful of the resource constraints and high investment costs, the 7FYP strategy was to combine ADP allocations with a strong public-private-partnership (PPP) effort.",""],[1,"88","4","Rail and Inland Waterway Transport Rebalancing","The plan also intended to improve the inter-modal transport balance with greater emphasis on rail and inland waterways that are low-cost in nature and are environmentally friendly.",""],[1,"88","4","Inter-District Air Connectivity Improvement","The importance of transport, especially air transport, for tourism was recognized with a focus on improving inter-district airline connectivity.",""],[1,"88","4","Transport User Charges and Fee Reform","Efforts were also to be made to improve resource mobilization through the introduction of user charges and fees for a range of public transport services including road user charges, port fees, inland water and rail fares.",""],[1,"125","1","Major Infrastructure Investment Programme","much of the public sector investment will need to be directed to major infrastructure projects in power, energy and transport.",""],[1,"127","3","Annual Development Program Expansion","Despite the revenue constraints, the 7FYP continued to provide increasingly greater allocation to the Annual Development Program (ADP) to boost the public investment program (Figure 3.3).",""],[1,"127","3","Large Transformational Infrastructure Project Completion","Although revenue shortage required some cutbacks, ADP programmes continued to increase as share of GDP.",""],[1,"127","3","Mega Projects Implementation","Thus, infrastructure development including implementation of mega projects took up more than 50% of the total ADP during the 7FYP.",""],[1,"127","3","Transport Infrastructure Investment","Most allocation was concentrated on transport with a significant number of transformational projects including the Padma Bridge.",""],[1,"128","4","PPP Funding Mobilization for Power and Transport","much stronger effort will be needed to channel PPP-type funding into power and transport.",""],[1,"128","4","Completion of Ongoing Transport Infrastructure Projects","The main emphasis will be the timely completion of all ongoing transformational transport infrastructure projects.",""],[1,"184","1","Major Highway and Bridge Expansion","major initiatives will be taken to broaden and accelerate the implementation of other major highways and bridges, power sector projects, and providing access to serviced land to foreign and domestic investors in the context of the Special Economic Zones (SEZ) initiative.",""],[1,"187","12","Completion of Ongoing Transformational Infrastructure Projects","The top priority will be to complete all ongoing transformational project.",""],[1,"187","12","Additional Power, Energy, and Transport Projects for Growth Acceleration","Other power, energy and transport projects needed to support growth acceleration will be pursued.",""]],"199":[[1,"10","1","Environmental Management and Pollution Reduction Efforts","Bangladesh has also continued its efforts in managing its environment in a sustainable way, which focused on reduction in air and water pollution, increasing forest coverage and improving preservation of biodiversity.",""],[1,"52","4","Environmental Management and Pollution Reduction","Bangladesh has continued the move forward with its environmental management focused on reduction in air and water pollution, increasing forest cover and improving preservation of biodiversity.",""],[1,"63","5","Environmental Protection and Climate Change Adaptation and Mitigation Measures","Many laws and regulations have been enacted over the years to protect the environment and programmes and policies are in place to adapt and mitigate the adverse effects of climate change.",""],[1,"64","1","Biodiversity Improvement and Climate Change Adaptation Pilot Programmes","were also taken to improve biodiversity and implement climate change adaptation pilot programmes through the BCCTF resources.",""],[1,"64","2","PP2041 Environmental Management Strategy Implementation","the main focus of the 8FYP sustainable development strategy is to initiate the first phase implementation of PP2041 environmental management strategy.",""],[1,"64","2","Environmental Cost Integration into Macroeconomic Framework","Integrating environmental costs into the Macroeconomic Framework;",""],[1,"64","2","Air and Water Pollution Reduction Measures","Reduce air and water pollution;",""],[1,"64","2","Fuel Subsidy Removal","Removal of fuel subsidies;",""],[1,"64","2","Green Tax on Fossil Fuel Consumption","Adoption of green tax on fossil fuel consumption;",""],[1,"64","2","Industrial Emissions Taxation","Taxation of emission from industrial units;",""],[1,"64","2","Surface Water Pollution Prevention","Prevention of surface water pollution.",""],[1,"64","3","Air and Water Pollution Reduction Efforts","the 8FYP will prioritize the ongoing efforts to reduce air and water pollution",""],[1,"64","3","Forestry Management Strengthening","the 8FYP will prioritize the ongoing efforts to ... strengthen forestry management",""],[1,"64","3","Environmental Fiscal Reform Capacity and Regulatory Development","Efforts will be made to build up institutional capabilities, policies and regulations for the implementation of environmental fiscal reforms (EFR) and the development of the green growth strategy",""],[1,"64","3","Green Growth Strategy Development","Efforts will be made to build up institutional capabilities, policies and regulations for the implementation of environmental fiscal reforms (EFR) and the development of the green growth strategy",""],[1,"64","3","Global Climate Change Programme Coordination and Resource Mobilization","Proper coordination with global climate change programmes will be maintained along with stronger efforts to mobilize global climate change resources",""],[1,"93","1","Environmental Law and Climate Adaptation and Mitigation Framework","Many laws and regulations have been enacted over the years to protect the environment and programmes and policies are in place to adapt and mitigate the adverse effects of climate change.",""],[1,"93","1","Air and Water Pollution Control Measures","This progress continued under the 7FYP, with special emphasis on air and water pollution control.",""],[1,"93","1","Brick Kiln Air Pollution Management","the focus on implementation was strengthened with significant progress in managing the air pollution from brick kilns",""],[1,"93","1","Leather Industry Water Pollution Reduction","reducing water pollution from the leather industry.",""],[1,"93","1","Biodiversity Improvement Measures","Important steps were also taken to improve biodiversity.",""],[1,"93","3","Low-Carbon Mitigation Action in Power, Transport, and Industry","Bangladesh has expressed her intention in the NDC (Nationally Determined Contributions) to take action on mitigation in order to reduce GHGs emissions by following a low carbon development pathway.",""],[1,"93","4","National Adaptation Plan Formulation and Integration","Bangladesh has prepared a NAP Roadmap towards formulating a comprehensive National Adaptation Plan (NAP) with a view to reducing vulnerability to the impacts of climate change by building adaptive capacity and resilience.",""],[1,"93","4","Bangladesh Climate Change Strategy and Action Plan Update","Bangladesh is also under the process of updating the BCCSAP.",""]],"200":[[1,"10","1","Human Development, Women's Empowerment and Social Inclusion Efforts","Bangladesh also continued to push ahead with human development, women empowerment and social inclusion as key elements in realizing the dream of the Father of the Nation Bangabandhu Sheikh Mujibur Rahman for achieving a just society with no discrimination on the basis of gender, religion, race or caste.",""],[1,"52","3","Female Labor Force Participation and Gender Equality Enforcement Measures","The 8FYP will make stronger efforts to enhance female labor participation rate and implement all legal provisions to eliminate gender discrimination and violence against women.",""],[1,"60","2","Gender Gap Elimination in Financial Inclusion","eliminating gender disparity in financial inclusion",""],[1,"60","3","Women's Economic Empowerment and Labor Force Participation Measures","On the gender front, the 8FYP will focus on increasing economic empowerment and better implementation of the 2011 NWDP.",""],[1,"60","3","Women's Labor Force Participation Support Measures","Women's labor force participation will be increased through closing the gap between male and female enrollments in tertiary education, especially in TVET, better access to training programmes, improving child care availability, improving safety of women's movements and in the work place, and increasing access to basic facilities like toilet and sanitary napkins in the work place.",""],[1,"60","3","Child Protection Law Implementation and Child Benefits Reform","The strategy for the children's advancement during the 8FYP will emphasize full implementation of all child protection laws and reduction in child poverty through strengthened social protection benefits based on a reformulated Child Benefits Program as envisaged in the NSSS.",""],[1,"61","1","Administrative Capacity Strengthening for Social Inclusion","The strategy for the 8FYP will place special emphasis on improving administrative capacity at both the ministerial and local government levels and strengthening partnerships with civil society organizations.",""],[1,"82","3","Implementation of the National Women Development Policy 2011","The implementation of the National Women Development Policy (NWDP) 2011 has continued during the 7FYP.",""],[1,"83","2","Children Act 2013 Implementation and Enforcement Strengthening","The implementation of the Children Act of 2013 is ongoing, need a costed action plan and allocation of resources accordingly.",""],[1,"83","2","Child Focused Budget Implementation","The concept of Child Focused Budget has been introduced and is being implemented.",""],[1,"83","2","Child Nutrition Improvement Efforts","However, progress in the area of children nutrition requires additional effort.",""],[1,"83","2","Consolidated Child Benefits Program Acceleration","the implementation of the consolidated Child Benefits Program recommended by the NSSS needs to be fast-tracked.",""],[1,"83","2","Children Act Enforcement Capacity and Dedicated Social Workforce","Implementation capacity for enforcement of the Children Act 2013 also needs strengthening and need deployment of dedicated social service workforce for children including children with disabilities.",""],[1,"83","2","Child Data Systems for Street and Institutionalized Children","Data on children living on street and living in orphanages or institutional care facilities are lacking in the country.",""],[1,"83","2","Child Deinstitutionalization and Foster Care Reintegration Mechanism","Deinstitutionalization of children living in institutions or orphanages and family or community based reintegration through developing a foster care mechanism with cash grant will be effective to protect more children in terms of increasing capacity for social integration and cognitive development.",""],[1,"83","2","Support for Organizations of Persons with Disabilities","Community Based Organizations of Persons with Disabilities and network of persons with disabilities need more support to create opportunity for them to speak about the issues affecting their life.",""],[1,"84","1","Disability Skill Development Programmes","There are some programmes for skill development.",""],[1,"86","5","Child-Focused Public Investment and Budgeting Evidence Generation","Following strategic actions will be undertaken: (a) evidences are generated to advocate for greater and better public investments for children by way of analysing child focused budgeting including preparation of budget brief, pursuing fiscal space analysis including institutional investment plans for children, pursuing public expenditure review for children, pursuing cost benefit analysis of selected interventions for children,",""],[1,"86","5","Capacity Building for Child-Focused Budgeting","(b) ccapacity of duty bearers enhanced in child focused budgeting process,",""],[1,"86","5","Citizen Participation in Budgeting Process","(c) involvement of citizen (including children) to empower them to participate in budgeting process to improve transparency and accountability.",""],[1,"119","6","Gender Equality and Equal Access Initiative","Ensuring gender equality by providing women and girls with equal access to education, health care, employment and representation in political and economic decision-making process.",""],[1,"164","6","Women Empowerment Programme","Women Empowerment Programme aims to eliminate discrimination against women in all forms, increase women's participation in social and family decision-making, ensure participation in education and work, and prevent violence.",""],[1,"164","6","Legal and Regulatory Measures for Women Empowerment","various initiatives have been taken including enactment of various laws and regulations",""],[1,"164","6","Rural Maternal Health Center Expansion","establishment of 12,956 rural maternal health centers",""],[1,"164","6","Maternity Leave Extension","extension of maternity leave from 4 months to 6 months",""],[1,"174","1","Targeted Social Services for Deprived Groups","be used to develop interventions for specific areas or sub-groups to ensure they receive adequate and appropriate social services to reduce their deprivations.",""],[1,"772","8","Women Empowerment Strategy Implementation","Implement the government's women empowerment strategy and policies as articulated in chapter 14 to eliminate all bias against female youth and enable her to fully participate in all relevant human activities.",""],[1,"774","6","Strengthen Enforcement of Child Marriage and Violence Against Women Laws","the tougher implementation of the child marriage law and laws to prevent violence against women",""],[1,"774","6","Eliminate Gender Gap in Tertiary and Vocational Education Access","the elimination of gender gap in access to tertiary and vocational education",""],[1,"774","6","Implement Twelve Years of Compulsory Education","the implementation of the 12 years compulsory education will help reduce the NEET population substantively",""],[1,"811","10","Child Marriage Prevention and Adolescent Health Programmes","The Government has undertaken some programmes through the Ministry of Women and Children Affairs (MoWCA) which are aimed at preventing child marriage and promoting adolescent health, creating awareness among not only children but also their parents and community leaders regarding the harmful effects of child marriage, dowry and eve teasing.","Ministry of Women and Children Affairs (MoWCA)"],[1,"811","11","Girls' STEM Education Promotion","Girls' education in Science, Technology, Engineering and Mathematics (STEM) is being promoted.",""],[1,"811","11","Gender-Balanced Curriculum Review","The contents of education are being reviewed to reduce gender bias and to incorporate sexual and reproductive health issues.",""],[1,"811","11","Gender Mainstreaming in Teacher Training","Teachers' training contents now include gender issues.",""],[1,"812","2","National Action Plan to Prevent Violence Against Women and Children","Furthermore, the National Action Plan to Prevent Violence against Women and Children (2018-2030) and the National Action Plan to Prevent Child Marriage are being implemented by the Government and civil society organizations.",""],[1,"812","2","National Action Plan to Prevent Child Marriage","Furthermore, the National Action Plan to Prevent Violence against Women and Children (2018-2030) and the National Action Plan to Prevent Child Marriage are being implemented by the Government and civil society organizations.",""],[1,"812","2","Sexual Harassment Prevention Measures","The government is working to curtail sexual harassment in public places, educational institutions and in social media.",""],[1,"815","2","Gender Equality and Women's Empowerment Measures","The mission is to ensure women's advancement as self-reliant human beings and reduce discriminatory barriers by taking both developmental and institutional measures.",""],[1,"815","2","Women's Capability and Access Expansion","Gender equality and women's empowerment agenda for the 8FYP is based on pursuing strategies and actions that not only enhance women's capabilities and access to resources and opportunities but also address the barriers in structures and institutions and aim at changing social norms and protecting their rights are critical to integrate within the plan.",""],[1,"815","2","Gender Equality Monitoring and Accountability Mechanisms","Establishing monitoring, oversight and accountability mechanisms is equally important.",""],[1,"815","9","Women's Human Capabilities Improvement Programme","Improve women's human capabilities: This deals with women's and girls' access to health care, life expectancy, nutrition, reproductive health, education, information, training, and other services that enable women to achieve better health and educational outcomes.",""],[1,"816","2","Women's Advancement Enabling Environment","Create an enabling environment for women's advancement:",""],[1,"816","3","Adolescent Social Clubs and Recreation Centres","This also includes establishing and operating social clubs and recreation centres for the development of the participating adolescents and for ending child marriages.",""],[1,"816","8","Legal and Regulatory Environment for Gender Equality","Establish conducive legal and regulatory environment for gender equality",""],[1,"816","10","Institutional Capacity, Accountability and Oversight Improvement","Improve institutional capacity, accountability and oversight",""],[1,"818","4","Strict Enforcement of Minimum Marriage Age","The existing age at marriage for girls and boys would be strictly enforced.",""],[1,"818","4","Universal Birth Registration Enforcement","Compulsory registration after birth of a child will be ensured.",""],[1,"818","4","Child Marriage Restraint Act Revision","The revised Child Marriage Restraint Act 2013 would include penal provisions for both guardians and registers.",""],[1,"818","4","Civil Society Mobilization Against Child Marriage","Civil society movements against child marriage would be strengthened, community orientation improved and support for continuation of education at secondary levels will be ensured to eliminate child marriage.",""],[1,"819","1","Expanded Social Protection for Women with Disabilities","Based on the new National Social Security Strategy (NSSS), appropriate social protection measures would be further extended and expanded to cover more such persons, especially women.",""]],"201":[[1,"55","9","ICT-Based Entrepreneurship Promotion","Promote ICT-based entrepreneurship embracing 4th Industrial Revolution (4IR);",""],[1,"62","4","ICT Services Export Promotion Incentives","Export of ICT services including software development will be promoted through fiscal incentives",""],[1,"62","4","Technology Parks and ICT Research Investment","Emphasis will be placed on development of ICT soft wares for exports through investments in Technology Parks and public investment in ICT research and development",""],[1,"113","2","ICT-Based Entrepreneurship Promotion","encourage ICT-based entrepreneurship",""],[1,"114","7","ICT-Based Entrepreneurship Promotion","Promote ICT-based entrepreneurship",""],[1,"339","1","ICT Export Promotion Strategy","An important target for the services exports for the Eighth Plan will be to boost the penetration of Bangladesh into the global ICT market through a well thought out ICT strategy that looks at both domestic market and also the global market.",""],[1,"340","3","ICT Industry Problem-Solving and Export Promotion Initiative","the Government in concert with the Bangladesh Computer Council is proactively engaged in resolving the problem issues on a priority basis, activities that will be intensified during the 8FYP.","Government | Bangladesh Computer Council"],[1,"340","3","ICT Start-up Incubation and Support Programme","Bangladesh Hi-Tech Park Authority (BHTPA) is nursing and promoting IT Start-ups/IT Entrepreneurs to establish giant IT Company like Google/Apple / Microsoft/Amazon/Alibaba.","Bangladesh Hi-Tech Park Authority (BHTPA)"],[1,"340","3","Free Utility and Workspace Support for ICT Start-ups","BHTPA has allotted space, internet and electricity free of cost to 100+ selected local IT Start-ups/IT Entrepreneurs; some of them are transformed into registered BPO/KPO/IT Company.","Bangladesh Hi-Tech Park Authority (BHTPA)"],[1,"340","3","International Standards Certification Support for ICT Firms","BHTPA is promoting local BPO/KPO/IT Companies for getting international standards like CMMIL-5, CMMIL-3, ISO- 9001 and ISO- 27001 etc.","Bangladesh Hi-Tech Park Authority (BHTPA)"]],"202":[[1,"55","2","Implementation of Economic Stimulus Packages","strong effort will be made to fully implement the stimulus packages announced in April-May 2020",""],[1,"55","2","Low-Cost Loan Support for Cottage, Micro and Small Enterprises","This will be done immediately through the provision of low-cost loans through the banking sector",""],[1,"55","2","Regulatory and Institutional Barrier Removal for CMSE Outreach","All institutional or regulatory barriers will be removed to reach out these enterprises pro-actively",""],[1,"56","3","Conversion of SME Foundation into Small Business Agency","The institutional and financial support to CMSMEs will be vastly enhanced through the conversion of the SME Foundation into Small Business Agency (SBA) as in the USA that will serve as a one-stop shop to promote CMSMEs, working closely with the Bangladesh Bank on the financing side.",""],[1,"57","1","Overseas Employment and Remittance Expansion Programme","The 8FYP will make a comprehensive push to expand overseas employment and remittance earnings through G2G negotiations, by lowering the cost of migration through low-cost loans from the Bangladesh Probashi Bank, by increasing training and other services to potential migrants, and by stronger support in the work place against exploitation and abuse in host countries through the local Bangladesh Embassies and High Commissions.",""],[1,"57","2","Remittance Inflow Acceleration Initiative","Emphasis on accelerating remittance inflows through new employment and improved skill base will be strengthened.",""],[1,"60","2","Digital Financial Inclusion Enhancement","the 8FYP will make the digital/ mobile financial services (DFS/MFS) system more effective in achieving financial inclusion of the poor and marginalized groups",""],[1,"60","2","National Identification Database Strengthening","strengthening the national identification database",""],[1,"60","2","Digital Payments Infrastructure Improvement","improving the payments infrastructure including the establishment of the interoperability amongst digital financial service providers",""],[1,"60","2","DFS Innovation Support for Small Businesses","promoting innovations to make DFS services more supportive of growth of small business holders",""],[1,"81","5","Microcredit Expansion and Financial Access Support","These programmes have continued to improve access and services during the Seventh Plan.","Bangladesh Bank | Microcredit Regulatory Authority (MRA)"],[1,"81","5","ICT-Based Mobile Banking for Financial Inclusion","New financial instruments based on ICT (mobile banking) are slowly changing the landscape of financial service access to the poor in both rural and urban areas.",""],[1,"82","1","Pro-Poor Growth and Inclusion Measures","pro-poor growth through increase in employment, labour productivity and wages, the development of human capital with better access to poor, the expansion of micro-credits and loans to improve the access of the poor to growth, reform of taxes with emphasis on progressive personal income taxation and improved access of the poor to social protection programmes.",""],[1,"96","8","Working Capital Loan Support for Affected Industries and Services","Working Capital loans to affected industries and service sector",""],[1,"96","20","Refinance Scheme for Professionals, Farmers, and Small Traders","Refinance scheme for professionals, farmers, and small traders",""],[1,"97","5","Working Capital Loan Interest Subsidy for Affected Industries and Services","Working Capital loans for the affected industries and service sector (Interest Subsidy from fiscal resource)",""],[1,"97","6","Working Capital Loan Interest Subsidy for SMEs","Working Capital loans for the SMEs including the cottage industries (Interest Subsidy from fiscal resource)",""],[1,"97","18","Refinance Scheme for Professional Farmers and Small Traders","Refinance scheme for professional farmer and small traders",""],[1,"97","22","Cash Transfer Program for Export-Oriented Industry Workers","Social Protection (Cash Transfer) program for the export oriented industry workers",""],[1,"111","6","Micro and Small Enterprise Job Protection and Credit Support","Topmost attention will be given to protect the jobs and enhance new jobs in the micro and small enterprise sector that presently employ an estimated 28 million people",""],[1,"111","6","Low-Cost Loan Facility for Micro and Small Enterprises","This will be done immediately through the provision of low-cost loans through the banking sector",""],[1,"111","6","Flexible SME Lending Coordination by Bangladesh Bank","The Bangladesh Bank will work with commercial banks and the non-bank financial institutions how this can be done in a flexible and low-cost manner","Bangladesh Bank"],[1,"111","6","Removal of Institutional and Regulatory Barriers for Enterprise Outreach","All institutional or regulatory barriers will be removed to reach out these enterprises pro-actively",""],[1,"113","2","CMSME Dynamism Enhancement","infuse dynamism in CMSMEs",""],[1,"113","2","Modern Services Sector Strengthening","strengthen the modern services sector",""],[1,"114","11","CMSE Regulatory Simplification and Support Expansion","The 8FYP will place strong emphasis in dynamising these CMSEs by making a concerted effort to remove these constraints.",""],[1,"114","11","SME Institutional and Financial Support Enhancement","In particular, the regulatory barriers will be simplified and the institutional and financial support to CMSEs will be vastly enhanced through the conversion of the SME",""],[1,"115","1","Small Business Agency One-Stop Shop for CMSE Promotion","Foundation into Small Business Agency (SBA) as in the USA that will serve as a one-stop shop to promote CMSEs, working closely with the Bangladesh Bank on the financing side.",""],[1,"115","1","ICT-Enabled SME Credit Access Solutions","Innovative financial solutions involving ICT will be used to improve access to commercial bank credit through low-cost approaches to loan applications, approvals and supervision.",""],[1,"115","1","Credit Guarantee Scheme Development","Credit Guarantee Schemes will be developed to reduce credit risks and to provide startup capital.",""],[1,"115","5","Support for Women Entrepreneurs","Providing support to organisations that promote women entrepreneurs in informal and formal economy, giving access to finance schemes such as micro-credit, receiving better education and getting more support from men and other family members are essential factors for a woman to freely indulge themselves in the labour market.",""],[1,"163","1","Microcredit Access Expansion Programme","The government's programme to expand access to microcredits is another factor that has helped reduce poverty.",""],[1,"163","1","Microcredit Cost Reduction Measures","efforts are needed to lower the cost.",""],[1,"163","1","Microcredit Market Competition and Public Funding Support","Interest costs can be lowered by improving competition in the supply of microcredit, providing more funding to suppliers from public sources, and increasing the saving of the rural community that are members of the microcredit suppliers.",""],[1,"163","1","Digital Microcredit Delivery Improvement","Already, the use of ICT through smartphones is improving market information and lowering transaction costs.",""],[1,"163","1","Microcredit Borrower Training and Technology Transfer","On the demand side, the productivity of the use of microcredit can be enhanced through better training, knowledge, and technology transfer to the borrowers.",""],[1,"163","1","8FYP Microcredit Support Strengthening","These solutions will be further strengthened in the 8FYP.",""],[1,"164","2","Amar Bari Amar Khamar Rural Livelihood and Savings Project","Amar Bari Amar Khamar project has been taken to accelerate poverty alleviation and sustainable development by increasing agricultural production and livelihoods by forming and investing its own capital in the rural economy.",""],[1,"167","5","Microcredit Access Expansion and Regulation","The 7FYP poverty reduction strategy continued to expand access to microcredits.","Microcredit Regulatory Authority (MRA)"],[1,"171","1","CMSE Sector Support and Financing Expansion","A major strategic shift in the 8FYP employment strategy is to boost the CMSE sector through better access to bank financing and through one-stop support for technology, training, marketing, and regulatory improvements based on converting the SME Foundation into an institution like the Small Business Association (SBA) of the USA.",""],[1,"171","1","Credit Guarantee Scheme for CMSE Financing","Adoption of a Credit Guarantee Scheme (CGS) can be very helpful to address this constraint.",""],[1,"172","2","Microcredit Service Expansion and Cost Reduction","This progress will be strengthened in the 8FYP.",""],[1,"177","7","Support Programme for Non-Farm Rural Enterprises in Lagging Districts","Supporting the growth of non-farm rural enterprises in the lagging districts through focussed support programmes including credit, technology, and marketing services.",""],[1,"180","13","Rural Formal Credit Expansion","The 8FYP will take steps to improve this.",""]],"203":[[1,"7","4","Policy and Institutional Reform for Inclusive Development","The plan has emphasised on appropriate policies and institutions, and devised suitable development strategies for promoting prosperity, fostering inclusiveness, reducing poverty, and inequality.",""],[1,"54","2","Institutional Strengthening Programme","Emphasis will be placed on institutions like the local government, the urban institutions, land administration, strengthening of the National Board of Revenue, the Bangladesh Bank, and the Public-Private Partnership.",""],[1,"54","2","Judiciary, Election Commission, and Democratic Institutions Strengthening","The strengthening of the judiciary, the Election Commission and other democratic institutions will continue",""],[1,"54","2","Public Agency Implementation Capacity Upgrade","implementation capacity in public agencies and ministries will be upgraded to ensure timely implementation of major public investment programmes and public policies in transport and social sectors.",""],[1,"64","8","Judicial Financial and Legal Support Programme","Financial and legal support to the judiciary to strengthen its capacity to ensure faster disposal of civil and criminal cases.",""],[1,"65","2","Zero-Tolerance Anti-Corruption Enforcement and Public Disclosure","The government's policy of zero tolerance of corruption will be enforced strictly with information on actions shared publicly.",""],[1,"65","3","Anti-Corruption Commission Strengthening","Strengthening the Anti-Corruption Commission in securing better quality investigations and fair resolutions.",""],[1,"94","3","Institutional Strengthening and Good Governance Programme","The Plan continued the effort initiated in the 6FYP to strengthen institutions and encourage the practice of good governance throughout the entire public system.",""],[1,"94","3","Judiciary Strengthening","The Plan emphasized strengthening of judiciary, law enforcing agencies, democratic institutions, economic policy making institutions, decentralization and reform of public administration.",""],[1,"94","3","Law Enforcement Capacity Strengthening","The Plan emphasized strengthening of judiciary, law enforcing agencies, democratic institutions, economic policy making institutions, decentralization and reform of public administration.",""],[1,"94","3","Democratic Institutions Strengthening","The Plan emphasized strengthening of judiciary, law enforcing agencies, democratic institutions, economic policy making institutions, decentralization and reform of public administration.",""],[1,"94","3","Public Administration Reform and Decentralization","The Plan emphasized strengthening of judiciary, law enforcing agencies, democratic institutions, economic policy making institutions, decentralization and reform of public administration.",""],[1,"94","3","Parliamentary Oversight Strengthening","The Parliamentary Standing Committees have been strengthened to provide checks and balance on the government through stronger parliamentary oversight.",""],[1,"94","3","Judiciary Resource Augmentation","The judiciary was beefed up through allocation of higher resources.",""],[1,"94","5","National Integrity Strategy","The Government has adopted a policy of zero tolerance to corruption.",""],[1,"95","1","Annual Performance Agreements Accountability System","the system of Annual Performance Agreements (APA) to enhance the state of accountability in line Ministries and make them more accountable to the Cabinet.",""],[1,"99","3","Institutional Strengthening and Governance Reform","the Eighth Plan would need to probe deeper and take a more focused and comprehensive approach than was possible in the Seventh Plan.",""],[1,"99","3","Public Agency Implementation Capacity Strengthening","implementation capacity in public agencies and ministries remain limited that adversely affected the implementation of major public investment programmes and public policies in transport and social sectors.",""],[1,"102","9","Critical Institutions Development and Improvement Initiative","Development and improvement of critical institutions necessary to lead the economy to UMIC status by FY2031.",""],[1,"118","2","State Capacity Strengthening for Pro-Poor Implementation","emphasis on strengthening state capacity and on expanding its role in selected aspects of the economy should be considered.",""],[1,"118","2","Governance Improvement through Democratic Accountability and Transparency","Further effort in improving governance by strengthening democratic accountability and transparency needs to be put in place by developing nations who are in dire need to eradicate poverty.",""],[1,"119","4","Coordination of Growth Strategy Implementing Institutions","Ensuring that the ministries/divisions/institutions responsible for implementing growth strategies (ministries of finance, commerce, planning, NBR and the BB) are organized well, work in coordination and are focused on maintaining macroeconomic stability","ministries of finance | commerce | planning | NBR | the BB"],[1,"119","5","Anti-Corruption Administrative Simplification and Digital Public Services Reform","Eliminating corruption and rent seeking behavior through regulatory simplifications, e- procurement, online tax collections and online payments for all government transactions, setting service standards and transparent fee structure for public services and by establishing an online public grievance redressal system with specified response timelines",""],[1,"146","2","Public Investment Quality and Procurement Transparency Measures","Transparency in tendering process and ensuring quality at different phases of project implementation, and making contractors responsible even after the delivery of projects will be key to ensuring quality of project implementation.",""],[1,"184","2","Prudent Public Spending and Public Service Delivery Improvement","Prudent spending of public sector resources for better public service delivery and incentive, subsidy and transfer programmes, and improved efficiency of public sector enterprises will be important for public sector resource efficiency and productivity.",""]],"204":[[1,"248","4","Tax Base Broadening Measures","the Government of Bangladesh has undertaken numerous measures to broaden the tax base in Bangladesh.",""],[1,"248","4","Taxpayer Enrollment and Compliance Events","The National Board of Revenue (NBR) also organizes regular events to enrol new taxpayers and encourage the existing taxpayers to pay their due share accordingly.","National Board of Revenue (NBR)"],[1,"248","4","Fiscal Reform and NBR Capacity Investment","Consequently, the Government will prioritize fiscal reforms and adequate investments in the NBR capacity.","National Board of Revenue (NBR)"],[1,"283","3","Tariff Regime Rationalization and Modernization","One required priority action is the further rationalization and modernization of the tariff regime.",""],[1,"283","3","Tax Regime Shift Toward Direct Taxation","It is also necessary to adjust the tax regime to shift the focus from indirect tax to direct tax for revenue collection sources.",""]],"205":[[1,"343","1","ICT Support for COVID-19 Response","The Government mandates the ICT Division to undertake necessary actions to support other ministries to integrate ICT for COVID 19 response, impact mitigation and growth.","ICT Division"],[1,"727","17","ICT Support for COVID-19 Response","ICT will also be a key driver for the line ministries for mitigating COVID 19 impact.","line ministries"],[1,"744","3","Inter-Ministerial Support for Business Continuity","c) support other line ministries and industries for successful operation shift;","ICT Division"],[1,"745","3","Health and Safety Support for ISP Workers","d) provide proper safety gears and necessary health support;","ICT Division"]],"206":[[1,"507","4","Hilly Region Food and Nutrition Security and Livelihood Projects","The MoCHTA has been working to ensure 'food and nutrition' security of the people in the hilly region, and implemented several projects to increase households' income opportunities.","MoCHTA"],[1,"507","4","Horticulture, Bamboo, and Spice Value Chain Support","These projects supported with the cultivation of varieties of fruits, bamboo and spices, as well as storing, processing and marketing of products.",""],[1,"533","7","Hilly Region Livelihood Diversification and Small Enterprise Expansion","The ministry will expand small and cottage industries, trading, poultry and livestock rearing, beekeeping and mushroom cultivation, cultivation of fruits and medicinal plants and non-farm activities, which will increase employment and income opportunities in the hilly region.",""],[1,"533","8","Market Access Infrastructure Development","Infrastructures will be developed to eliminate barriers in marketing the local products into national and international markets.",""],[1,"533","9","Post-Harvest Value Chain Development Program","A special program will be developed to strengthen post-harvest storage, value-chain development, processing, packaging, and marketing.",""],[1,"533","9","Private Investment Promotion for Local Product Processing and Marketing","Private investment in processing, packaging, and marketing the local products and services will be encouraged.",""],[1,"533","10","Skills Development Training Expansion for Overseas Labour Markets in the CHT Region","Existing skills development training will be extended in the CHT region, targeting the overseas labour markets.",""],[1,"533","11","Ecotourism and Community-Based Tourism Promotion","Ecotourism and community-based tourism abiding by the legislations narrated in the HDCs Acts, CHTRC Act and Allocation of Business of MoCHTA will be encouraged as a means of income generation.",""],[1,"533","11","Local Investment for Sustainable Tourist Sites and Facilities","Local investment will be encouraged to develop sustainable tourist spots and facilities in Rangamati, Bandarban and Khagrachari.",""],[1,"534","2","Chittagong Hill Tracts Poverty Reduction Support Measures","Special attention will be given to lower the large incidence of poverty in CHT by giving priority to the allocation of resource transfers from LGD, selection of rural infrastructure projects relating to irrigation, drainage, roads, bridges and culverts, imparting training and research to CHT, and improving access to credit from the micro-credit institutions","LGD"],[1,"841","2","Livelihoods Support for Extreme Poor Households","Extreme poor households, where the occurrence of child labour is highest, will be covered by livelihoods interventions for adult earners.",""],[1,"843","2","Income Generating Activities Expansion","Income generating activities through small and cottage industries, trading, poultry and livestock rearing, beekeeping, mushroom cultivation, and others will be expanded.",""],[1,"843","2","Social Forestry and Diversified Livelihood Support","The income of poor people will be enhanced through social forestry in hill areas, cultivation of fruits and medicinal plants, and expanding non-farm employment opportunities.",""],[1,"843","2","Youth Employment Expansion Through Farm and Non-farm Sectors","Equal emphasis will be given to the farm and non-farm sectors including internal and external labour mobility to expand employment opportunities for the youth.",""],[1,"843","3","Marketing Infrastructure Development and Market Access Programme","Proper market infrastructure and rural road and market facilities will be developed so that farmers/producers can achieve a better price from selling their products.",""],[1,"843","3","Agricultural and Local Product Market Access Reform","Measures will be taken to eliminate barriers so that agricultural and other local products have easy access to national and international markets.",""],[1,"843","3","Postharvest Management and Value Chain Development Programme","A special programme will be developed to strengthen postharvest management, value chain development, processing, packaging, and market access, and to engage private sector market linkages.",""],[1,"843","3","Private Investment Promotion for CHT Processing and Marketing","Private investment in processing, packaging, and marketing CHT products and services will be encouraged.",""],[1,"843","5","Eco-Tourism and Community-Based Tourism Promotion","Tourism, especially ecotourism and community-based tourism will be encouraged as a means of income generation for the local people.",""],[1,"843","5","Private Investment for Sustainable Tourist Facilities","Private local investment will be encouraged to develop sustainable tourist spots and facilities in Rangamati, Bandarban and Khagrachari by engaging tribal people.",""],[1,"843","7","Microcredit Expansion and Technical Training for the Poor","Measures should be taken for the expansion of micro credit distribution activities and technical training among the poor.",""]],"207":[[1,"51","4","Education Quality and Skills Upgrading Programme","the Fourth Industrial Revolution is requiring rapid changes in skills that needs fast tracking of education quality and skills upgrading program",""],[1,"58","3","Education Sector Investment and Human Capital Development Programme","Budgetary allocations to the education sector will be increased to create better human capital through universal general education, skill development programmes, and training and greater access to ICT solutions.",""],[1,"59","3","Adult Literacy and Education Quality Improvement Programme","The 8FYP seek to achieve 100% adult literacy rate and will consolidate past gains in primary and secondary education to accelerate progress in tertiary education.",""],[1,"59","3","Workplace-Relevant Education Quality Reform","Most focus will be placed on education quality with emphasis on learning and acquiring skills that are relevant to the work place.",""],[1,"59","3","Science, Mathematics, ICT, and Problem-Solving Education Strengthening","Education quality will emphasize science, maths and ICT and developing problem solving skills.",""],[1,"59","3","Technical Education Expansion through TVET System","Technical education will be promoted through expansion of the TVET system.",""],[1,"59","3","Expanded Training Programmes through Partnerships","Training programmes will be vastly expanded through public-private partnerships, through on the job training, and through partnership with NGOs and development partners.",""],[1,"59","3","District-Level Decentralization of Primary and Secondary Education","Primary and secondary education will be decentralized to district level, teacher training will be expanded, private provision of education and training will be promoted, and the education budget will grow from 2.0% of GDP in FY2019 to 3.0% of GDP by FY2025.",""],[1,"90","4","Education for All Strategy","the main highlight of the 7FYP strategy is to achieve Education for All (EFA) by FY2020.",""],[1,"90","4","Secondary and Tertiary Enrolment Expansion","Related to this, the two specific targets were: (1) achieve 100% adult (15 plus) literacy; (2) achieve 100% net primary enrolment rate.",""],[1,"90","4","Education Quality and Equity Improvement","Other objectives included increasing enrolments in secondary and tertiary education; improving education quality at all levels; improving the equity of education; improving labour force training and skills through a concerted skills development strategy; and increasing the spread of science and technology education.",""],[1,"90","4","Concerted Skills Development Strategy","improving labour force training and skills through a concerted skills development strategy; and increasing the spread of science and technology education.",""],[1,"91","1","Non-Formal Education Coverage Expansion","Progress with increasing the coverage of NFE continued under the 7FYP",""],[1,"91","2","Strategic Plan for Higher Education Expansion","To further accelerate the expansion of tertiary education, the government in 2017 adopted the Strategic Plan for Higher Education in Bangladesh: 2017-2031.",""],[1,"91","4","TVET System Improvement through Education and Skills Policies","The Government expressed its commitment to improving the TVET system through the implementation of the National Education policy-2010 and the National Skills Development Policy-2011.",""],[1,"91","4","National Technical and Vocational Qualifications Framework","National Technical and Vocational Qualifications Framework (NTVQF) has been designed to improve the quality and consistency of nationally recognized qualifications.",""],[1,"91","4","Skills for Employment Investment Program","Another significant initiative is the Skills for Employment Investment Program (SEIP) under the Ministry of Finance (funded by ADB and the government) which has partnered with a number of industry associations such as BASIS, BTMA, BGMEA, AEOSIB and others to impart vocational training with globally recognized skills certifications where appropriate.","Ministry of Finance"],[1,"91","4","Integrated TVET Development Action Plan for Madrassa Students","The Technical and Madrassa Education Division (TMED) has developed an integrated TVET development action plan to promote and strengthen TVET activities for the madrassa students.","Technical and Madrassa Education Division (TMED)"]],"208":[[1,"59","1","Nutrition Improvement and School Mid-Day Meals Expansion","Regarding nutrition, the 8FYP will accelerate the progress made in improving child and mother nutrition with a combination of augmented supply of nutritious food in general and through school mid-day meals, through education campaigns, through nutrition counselling in local health clinics, and through expansion of related social security programmes.",""],[1,"59","2","Population Management and Reproductive Health Inclusion Strategy","The focus in the 8FYP will shift more onwards converting population as an asset as a part of the inclusion agenda whereby the emphasis will shift to managing an ageing population, reducing maternal mortality through greater access to birth attended by skilled staff, reduction in early age female pregnancies, enhanced access to reproductive health education and health care, increase in female labor force participation and better use of the youth population in the development process.",""]],"209":[[1,"114","10","Agricultural Export Promotion Initiative","Agriculture exports will be promoted to increase farm income and employment in non-crop activities especially fisheries, fruits and vegetables and dairy products",""],[1,"120","5","Global Value Chain Participation Support Measures","Encouraging and promoting participation in global value chains (GVCs) with supportive policies for improved infrastructure, strengthening human capital (education and training are relevant in this regard) and incentivise research and development as knowledge and technology spill over can enhance growth benefits of trade;",""]],"210":[[1,"119","9","Equality of Opportunity and Market Access Reform","Enforcing equality of opportunity in terms of access to markets, resources, finance and unbiased regulatory environment for businesses and individuals.",""],[1,"155","2","Strengthening Poverty Reduction Strategy Elements","some elements of the poverty reduction strategy relating to health care, social protection, reduction of vulnerability to climate change and natural disasters, and non-farm job creation may need to be further strengthened",""],[1,"179","9","Redistributive Fiscal Policy Reform","The 8FYP will initiate the first phase implementation of this fiscal policy.",""]],"211":[[1,"137","3","Prudent Monetary Policy Management","This policy of prudent monetary management has been implemented successfully through a bi-annual monetary policy statement (MPS).",""],[1,"138","13","Interest Rate Reduction Support","The government has supported the reduction of interest rates to 9% on loans to boost economic activity, especially in the face of COVID-19 downturn.",""],[1,"138","13","Evidence-Based Interest Rate Management Review","For the medium-term, the government will look careful at interest rate management based on research and evidence.",""],[1,"139","1","Interest Rate Management and Banking Sector Constraint Reform","Two inter-connected issues will guide interest rate management in the 8FYP.",""],[1,"140","2","Maintain Positive Real Deposit Interest Rates","banks will continue to offer at least marginally positive real interest rates to the depositors",""],[1,"140","2","Inflation Reduction Efforts","Bangladesh bank will continue its efforts to reduce inflation further to ensure a sustained lowering of the structure of deposit and lending rates","Bangladesh Bank"],[1,"140","4","Market-Driven Interest Rate Policy Reform","Bangladesh will adopt a proper market-driven interest rate policy.",""],[1,"140","4","Treasury Bill Supply as Monetary Policy Instrument","The BB can then influence interest rates more effectivelythrough the supply of T-bills as a key monetary policy instrument.",""],[1,"201","2","Monetary-Fiscal Coordination for Domestic Financing","it will require better coordination between monetary and fiscal policy in order to avoid any potential scope for crowding out of private sector credit.",""]],"212":[[1,"145","5","Insurance Actuarial Department Establishment and Student Support Fund","All the insurers will open actuarial department in their companies and to give financial assistance to the actuarial students.",""],[1,"145","6","Unified Messaging Platform for Insurance Policy Data","IDRA will develop a framework to store all the policy related data in a digital policy repository called Unified Messaging Platform.",""],[1,"145","6","Digital Insurance Compliance and Anti-Fraud Services","Thus it will help to reduce money laundering and fraudulent activity by fake insurance agents.",""],[1,"145","10","Insurance Regulatory Capacity Strengthening","Measures will be taken to strengthen capacity of IDRA and other insurance related institutions.",""],[1,"187","10","Insurance Product Diversification and Distribution Expansion","For increasing penetration of insurance in our economy, insurance sector is planning to diversify insurance products both in life and non-life sub-sectors like Bhaban Bima, Bangabandhu School Bima, Insurance for all Passengers, Neuro-developmental Insurance, Agriculture Enterprise Insurance etc.",""]],"213":[[1,"164","5","Education Assistance and Stipend Support Programme","Education Assistance Trust aims to ensure 100% enrollment of the school going children, distribute free books up to secondary level, provide stipends including free education to girls.",""],[1,"177","10","ICT Access Expansion through Education and Special Training Programmes","Enhance access to ICT services through the education system and special training programmes to the lagging districts.",""],[1,"184","1","Education Financing and Skills Development Expansion","Budgetary allocations to the education sector will be increased to create better human capital through universal general education, skill development programmes, and training and greater access to ICT solutions.",""],[1,"187","11","Education and Training Programme Strengthening","Human capital buildup will require strengthening of education and training programmes along with the spread of ICT education.",""],[1,"187","11","Expansion of ICT Education","Human capital buildup will require strengthening of education and training programmes along with the spread of ICT education.",""],[1,"187","11","Increase Education Spending","Therefore, spending on education will grow from 2.0% of GDP in FY19 to 3.0% by FY25.",""]],"214":[[1,"164","1","Prime Minister's Special Initiatives","The Hon'ble Prime Minister has designed 10 special initiatives with effort to building a middle income country free of poverty and hunger by 2021 and a developed country by 2041.",""]],"215":[[1,"237","3","E-Procurement Expansion","The Government has introduced online procurement systems to reduce corruption and increase competitiveness in government contracts, as it will enhance both more participation and transparency in the tender process guiding public procurement.",""]],"216":[[1,"233","1","Legal Aid Access Expansion","The Government of Bangladesh is committed to improve access to justice for the poor and marginalized people.",""],[1,"233","1","Village Court Operations","The village courts are currently operational in 27 districts and their case disposal rate is high.",""],[1,"233","1","National Legal Aid Service Delivery","The National Legal Aid Services Organisation (NLASO) is providing services in 64 districts through the District Legal Aid Offices along with a national hotline.",""],[1,"233","1","Judicial Capacity Building for ADR","The Government has also prioritized improving the capacity of judicial institutions to undertake Alternate Dispute Resolution (ADR) along with enhancing public awareness of such mechanism.",""],[1,"243","3","Judicial Services Accessibility and Affordability Investment","Thus, to improve the state of the rule of law in Bangladesh, the following activities are prioritized under the 8FYP:",""],[1,"244","4","Local Justice Services Capacity Enhancement","Increasing the capacity of local justice services to resolve disputes at low cost, fairly and quickly - so producing better outcomes for people.",""],[1,"244","8","Informal Justice Sector Strengthening","Consequently, to improve the effectiveness of the informal justice sector, the following activities will be undertaken under the 8FYP:",""],[1,"245","2","Village Courts Scale-Up and Universal Union Coverage","The Government will scale up village courts and ensure their 100% coverage of all Unions under the 8FYP.",""],[1,"245","4","Village Court Awareness Campaign","The Government will encourage the local agencies to increase the awareness amongst citizens in rural communities for them to use the village court mechanism to resolve disputes without resorting to formal judicial institutions, so that the problem of case backlogs in the formal Judiciary is reduced over time.",""],[1,"245","5","Legal Aid Expansion for Victims","To improve the access to justice, the Government will offer legal aid to approximately 200,000 victims annually by 2025.",""],[1,"245","6","National Legal Aid Services Organization Capacity Investment","The Government will invest in the National Legal Aid Services Organization's (NLASO) capacity so that it can effectively reach the poor and marginalized communities, and improve their access to legal redressal.",""],[1,"245","7","Partnerships with NGOs and Non-State Actors for Legal Aid Access","The NLASO will also formulate greater partnerships with the NGOs and other non-state actors to facilitate the access to justice.",""],[1,"245","8","Diagnostic Assessments for Legal Aid Instrument Design","The NLASO will commission diagnostic assessments so that better instruments are designed to deliver legal aid.",""],[1,"245","8","Legal Aid Eligibility and Vulnerability Profiling Assessment","It will also assess and document the proportion of the vulnerable population who qualify for legal aid, and their key profiles in order to understand the combination of factors that shape who has access to justice and when.",""],[1,"245","9","Institutionalization of Paralegalism","The Government will institutionalize Para-legalism as an instrument to complement the objectives of the NLASO.",""]],"217":[[1,"234","4","District Case Coordination Committees","The introduction of Case Coordination Committees (CCC) at district level has succeeded in bringing together key justice system actors on a regular basis to address local problems related to prison overcrowding and case congestion.",""],[1,"234","4","Justice System Coordination and Information-Sharing Mechanism","Along with Police and Magistrates, the CCCs play an important role in joining up the justice system to ensure each service provider talks to the others and avoid operating in siloes.",""],[1,"243","4","Judiciary Recruitment Acceleration","the Government under the 8FYP, will continue expediting the recruitment to the Judiciary to increase the judge-to-people ratio.",""],[1,"244","1","Special Support Measures for Pipeline District Courts","Additional measures will be undertaken for such \"pipe-line\" districts to ensure that Districts Courts in such administrative Districts have the necessary resources to dispose cases efficiently in a time-bound manner.",""],[1,"244","2","Continuation of Supreme Court Strategic Plan Implementation","the Government under the 8FYP will remain committed to all the goals, strategies and activities that were formulated by the Supreme Court of Bangladesh, which remain incomplete or unrealized.",""],[1,"244","3","District Court Case Filtering and Judicial Capacity Strengthening","Reducing pressure on the district level courts and institutions by filtering out simple, minor or vexatious cases, while better equipping the actors in the judicial process to manage the serious and complex ones in need of legal representation and adjudication.",""],[1,"244","5","Court Case Backlog Review and Filtering Mechanism","The Government will take a two-pronged approach based upon the findings of the Justice Audit.",""],[1,"244","6","Inter-Ministerial Coordination Mechanism for Case Management Feedback","During Eighth Plan an Inter-Ministerial coordination mechanism will be established to complete the policy-evidence feedback loop from district (CCCs) to national level.",""],[1,"246","2","E-Judiciary Digitization Project","Law and Justice Division has planned to undertake a development project valuing Tk. 2690 crore to develop ICT infrastructure, supply hardware and install connectivity with the help of Bangladesh Computer Council.","Law and Justice Division | Bangladesh Computer Council"],[1,"246","3","Independent Prosecution Service Establishment","Government plans to institute a permanent attorney service to provide adequate, prompt and expert service.",""],[1,"246","4","Judicial Academy Establishment","Judicial Academy will conduct research and studies in the areas of interest, develop standard curriculum, design planning and standard training, maintain international collaboration and deal other issues for both subordinate and higher judiciaries.",""],[1,"246","5","Judicial In-Service Training and Professional Development Programme","The Government of Bangladesh acknowledges that Judges need continuous in-service training.",""],[1,"247","1","Specialized Judicial Training and Thematic Working Groups","Government will undertake specialised projects and activities to train Judges on all such dimensions - and will form specialised groups to address the key issues that carry key economic importance.",""]],"218":[[1,"233","2","Law Access and Translation Portal","all updated laws are provided in the website (laws of Bangladesh) of the Legislative and Parliamentary Affairs Division.","Legislative and Parliamentary Affairs Division"],[1,"239","4","Legislative Officials Training Programme","Therefore, expertise should be increased through providing national and international training.",""],[1,"239","5","Translation of English Laws into Bengali","Therefore, all English laws should be translated in Bengali.",""],[1,"239","5","Expansion of Translation Officer Capacity","In Bangladesh, there is also shortage of translation officer which should be increased.",""],[1,"246","1","Legislative Process Improvement Programme","For that purpose the following activities will be undertaken during the 8FYP to improve the existing law making process: (i) local and overseas training of legislative officials and various diploma and higher studies courses relating to legislative drafting for preparing skilled manpower in conformity with international standard, (ii) set up of legislative research cell and legislative editing unit, (iii) translation of all act from English to Bengali and vice versa on the basis of priority and importance, (iv) set up of legislative library with electronic cataloguing system, an archive and record room for conservation and preservation of historical and important documents in the field of law, (v) set up of law public awareness cell and resource documentation centre, and (vi) codification and update of subordinate legislation.",""]],"219":[[1,"234","2","Multi-Sectoral Program on Violence Against Women","The Multi-Sectoral Program on Violence Against Women (MSP- VAW) under the Ministry of Women and Children Affairs (MoWCA) runs eight One-stop Crisis Centres (OCCs) at the division levels and 60 One-stop Crisis Cells (OCCs) to provide information and referral services to the victims of VAW.","Ministry of Women and Children Affairs (MoWCA)"],[1,"244","7","Study on Barriers to Justice for Women and Children","The Government will invest in better understanding the barriers to justice for women and children.",""],[1,"244","7","Review of Nari O Shishu Court Operations","A root and branch study of the workings of the Nari O Shishu courts will be conducted so that services can be adjusted accordingly.",""]],"220":[[1,"265","1","Economic Recovery Program","the 8FYP will have to start off with an economic recovery program that can then morph into the medium-term development agenda for rapid pro-poor and inclusive growth as envisioned in PP2041.",""],[1,"265","3","COVID-19 Economic Recovery Stimulus Package","In the first phase of policy response, the Government has launched a $12 billion (over Tk.1 trillion) stimulus (or relief) package to cushion the economy from the immediate health-cum-economic shock.",""],[1,"265","3","Economic Recovery Package for FY2021","The FY2021 Budget should comprise the economic recovery package that will launch the 8FYP to fuel economic recovery and resume the growth trajectory that was laid during the past 10 years.",""]],"221":[[1,"265","2","Trade and Industrial Policy Revamp","That calls for trade and industrial policy to be revamped during the 8FYP to cope with the impending challenges.",""],[1,"265","2","Manufacturing and Export Base Diversification","A particularly important task is to diversify the manufacturing production and export base to insulate the economy from adverse developments associated with dependence on one single product group.",""],[1,"265","2","Manufacturing Sector Restructuring for Job Creation","The other task is to restructure manufacturing sector in a way that it creates more jobs as it grows, notwithstanding the ramifications of technology change and growing capital intensity of production associated with the on-going Fourth Industrial Revolution (4IR).",""],[1,"266","2","Coordinated Industrial and Trade Policy Alignment","In articulating trade and industrial policies during the period of the 8FYP these two approaches will be kept in perspective.",""],[1,"266","3","Industrial Structural Transformation Strategy","Thus, the principal focus of our industrial policy during the 8FYP will be to achieve structural transformation where industry's share in GDP would reach 40-45% of GDP by 2030 thereby absorbing the bulk of the labour force that was hitherto under-employed in agriculture and informal services.",""],[1,"266","3","Infant Industry Support Scheme","Furthermore, to develop a globally competitive manufacturing sector the strategy would be to provide support to infant industries with time-bound and performance-based criteria.",""],[1,"266","3","State-Business Industrial Policy Coordination","Strategic coordination between the state and businesses in formulation and implementation of industrial policy is the accepted practice in Bangladesh.",""],[1,"266","5","Trade Policy Support for Industrialization Strategy","The concurrent trade policy will have to be supportive of the industrialization strategy focusing on developing a globally competitive manufacturing sector with strong and sustainable export performance.",""],[1,"295","4","WTO-Consistent Industrial Policy for Export-Oriented Industrialization","Given the changing global and domestic landscape, our industrial policy will have to encompass government efforts to promote industrialization that generates export-led and productivity-based rapid growth.",""],[1,"295","4","Industrial Growth Promotion for Employment and Regional Balance","In practice, industrial policy may include such goals as employment generation, increased output, removing regional disparity in incomes or investment, and enhancing technological capacity.",""],[1,"296","1","Human Capital and Technological Capability Enhancement Measures","services, and policies to enhance human capital and technological capability, such as research and development, education, and creation of industrial clusters.",""],[1,"297","4","WTO-Consistent Industrial Policy Reform","Bangladesh industrial policy to be WTO-consistent will have to be comprehensive rather than target specific sectors; that is, there should be a concerted effort to shift toward more generic policies for promoting industrial development.",""],[1,"297","4","Industrial Infrastructure, Human Capital, Innovation, and Technology Diffusion Support","Policies related to infrastructure, human capital formation, innovation through more R&D, and diffusion of technology is now critical for export competitiveness.",""]],"222":[[1,"298","1","Bangladesh Regional Connectivity Project","Other projects under MoC i.e., 1) Bangladesh Regional Connectivity Project 2) Export Diversification and Competitiveness Development Project (Tier-2), 3) E- banijjo korbo, nijer babsa gorbo project will certainly contribute to establish digital Bangladesh as envisaged under the \"Vision-2021\" and the Perspective Plan 2021.","MoC"],[1,"301","2","Expansion of Border Haats","16 more border Haats are expected to be opened during the 8FYP period.",""],[1,"301","4","Trade Policy Mainstreaming in Development Planning","it is time to mainstream trade policy.",""]],"223":[[1,"291","2","Inland Waterway Development Strategy Implementation","Implementation of the inland waterway development strategy articulated in the Delta Plan will be of high priority.",""],[1,"291","2","Inter-modal Transport Balance Improvement","Additionally, much more attention needs to be given to the issue of inter-modal transport balance based on cost and efficiency.",""]],"224":[[1,"252","4","Election Commission Strengthening and Electoral Transparency Support","Consequently, under the 8FYP, the following activities will be pursued to enhance the performance of the EC: (i) The Government will offer all necessary support to EC to expand the use of electronic voting machines to improve transparency in the electoral process; (ii) EC will execute its operations independently and effectively; and (iii) More measures will be taken to improve EC's capacity to monitor election expenditure by candidates and control campaign contribution during local and national elections.",""],[1,"252","5","Parliamentary Process Transparency and Participation Measures","To that end, the following activities will be undertaken during the 8th Plan to improve the role of the Parliament as a reservoir of people's trust and aspirations: (i) The Government will remain committed to increasing the number of hearings open to the public, particularly of important budgetary committees such as the Public Accounts Committee; (ii) Efforts will be undertaken to reduce the time that is lost due to lack of quorum;",""],[1,"253","1","Public Accounts Committee Functioning Improvement","improvements in the functioning of Public Accounts Committee",""],[1,"253","1","Women’s Parliamentary Representation Increase","The Govt. will try to ensure that percentage of seats held by women in the national parliament is at least 33% by 2025.",""],[1,"253","2","Ombudsman Appointment","The government will ensure the appointment of an Ombudsman which was committed under the 7th Plan.",""]],"225":[[1,"255","3","Public Order and Citizen Security Enforcement","The Government of Bangladesh remains committed to maintain public order and safeguard the assets and lives of its citizens under the 8FYP period.","Ministry of Home Affairs (MoHA)"],[1,"255","3","Law Enforcement and Internal Security Operations","Guaranteeing the enforcement of the law, protecting the citizens from internal and external threats, maintaining security in the border, battling narcotics, terrorism and other social vices and rehabilitation of prisoners remain the key objectives of the Ministry of Home Affairs (MoHA).","Ministry of Home Affairs (MoHA)"],[1,"255","3","Inter-Agency Public Safety Coordination","As a result, the MoHA will ensure the cooperation of all the agencies under its jurisdiction to offer the necessary safety and security.","Ministry of Home Affairs (MoHA)"],[1,"255","4","Police Effectiveness and Accountability Improvement","under the 8FYP, the following activities will be prioritized:",""],[1,"255","5","Strategic Directions and Organizational Reforms for Bangladesh Police","The Government will formulate strategic directions and organizational reforms to support planning and budgeting, enhanced accountability and oversight, as well as a modernized legislative framework.",""],[1,"255","6","Police Personnel Capacity Building and Modern Training Centres","Proper initiatives will be undertaken to increase skills and competency of police personnel by means of arranging training, workshops and seminars in the country.",""],[1,"256","1","Upgrade Bangladesh Police In-Service Training Centres","to improve the infra-structure, equipment, transport and ICT facilities for furnishing a total of 30 In- Service Training Centres of Bangladesh Police.",""],[1,"256","1","Capacity Building for Training Centre Facilitators and Instructors","The facilitators and instructors of In-Service Training Centres will be trained at home and abroad through some capacity building projects.",""],[1,"256","1","Women-Friendly Police Training Centre Upgrading","The existing training centres would be made women-friendly with respect to quality of training, infrastructures and allied services",""],[1,"256","4","Police Investigation, Operations and Prosecution Improvement","The Government will increase efforts to improve police operations, investigation and prosecution to enhance fair and equitable justice.",""],[1,"256","4","Police Grievance Redressal System","Grievance Redressal Systems (GRS) will be introduced into police administration more effectively to ensure fair treatment of both police officials and citizens.",""],[1,"256","4","IGP Complaint Cell Strengthening","IGP's Complaint Cell will be more effective as a Grievance Redressal System to ensure fair treatment to both police officials and citizens.",""],[1,"257","1","Digitalization of All Police Stations","different steps will be taken to digitize all police stations of Bangladesh Police for making them fully accessible to the citizens from all walks of life.",""],[1,"257","4","Model Police Stations Service Improvement","Moreover, under the 8FYP, the Bangladesh Police will continue to provide services from \"Model Police Stations\" to improve the facilities for delivery of services.",""],[1,"260","2","National Tele-Communication Monitoring Centre Strengthening","The objective of NTMC for 8th Plan are as follows: (i) Support the procurement of state-of-the-art technological devices that can protect citizens from terrorist organizations; (ii) Increase parliamentary audits of its expenditure to ensure more public scrutiny of its expenditure; (iii) More investments in training, infrastructural facilities to accommodate all major components of NTMC like data centre, monitoring station and physical security measures; (iv) Deploy necessary IT experts to deal with emerging threats from telecommunication sectors; (v) Ensure annual hearings of NTMC officials with the Honourable Prime :selected: Minister and Defence Advisors to ensure that basic privacy of citizens are not violated.",""]],"226":[[1,"256","2","Anti-Terrorism Unit Infrastructure and Capacity Development","Required initiatives will be undertaken to develop infra-structure for ATU in Dhaka and all over the country to curb terrorism and religious militancy.",""],[1,"256","2","Procurement of Modern Counter-Terrorism Equipment","Besides, modern equipment will be procured and forensic labs will be set up in this purpose.",""],[1,"256","2","Counter-Terrorism Policy Formulation","In addition, Counter-Terrorism policy will be formulated incorporating other stakeholders in the initiative of ATU.",""],[1,"256","3","Establishment of Six Divisional Forensic Laboratories","For this reason, six more forensic labs will be established to make Bangladesh Police an effective investigating agency, which will be prioritized under the 8FYP.",""],[1,"257","3","Cybercrime Prevention Capacity Building and Technology Investment","The Government remains committed to reducing cybercrime and will undertake the necessary capacity building measures and investments in technology that will allow the prevention of cybercrime in the society.",""],[1,"257","3","Social Media Misuse and Fake News Reduction Measures","Especially, measures will be taken to reduce the misuse of social media networks to disrupt communal harmony through the spreading of \"fake news\" that hurt religious sentiments of any community.",""]],"227":[[1,"256","5","Crime Prevention and Community Policing Measures","Measures will be taken to improve the trust and interaction between the community and the Police resulting in improved access to justice, human rights and reduced fear of crime.",""],[1,"256","5","Bit Policing Technique Rollout","Bangladesh Police is applying Bit Policing technique countrywide as an implementation tool of community policing.",""],[1,"256","6","Community Policing Strengthening Initiative","Under the 8FYP, these efforts will be further strengthened to enhance better policing services for the citizens.",""],[1,"256","6","Community Policing for Crime Reduction","In particular, efforts of finding durable solutions to reduce crime through community policing would be continued.",""],[1,"256","6","Functional Community Policing Measures","The Community policing would be made functional through practical initiatives like: (a) Community Policing Forums; (b) Sector-wise community involvement; (c) Open house day; (d) Bit meetings; (e) Youth and Student involvements; (f) School/College based awareness programmes; (g) Mass meeting/ Rallies; (h) Anticrime meetings; (i) Victim Re-contract; (j) Door to door/ home to home visits.",""],[1,"257","2","Strengthening and Capacity Building of the 999 National Emergency Service","So, investments in the necessary infrastructure of the 999 centre and developing a pool of trained human resource will receive priority under the 8th Plan.",""],[1,"257","5","Enhanced CCTV and Surveillance Coverage","Under the 8th Plan, the Government will ensure that selected metropolitan police jurisdictions and selected portions of highways would be brought under the surveillance of CCTVs to increase the state of safety on national highways and key cities.",""]],"228":[[1,"256","7","Gender-Sensitive Policing and Victim Support","The government is committed to ensure the rights of women and children at all levels by ensuring equitable and sensitive policing and support services for the victims.",""],[1,"256","7","Woman Policing Strategy","it will develop a Woman Policing Strategy (WPS) through the Bangladesh Police to mitigate gender discrimination in policing services.",""]],"229":[[1,"257","6","National Human Trafficking Prevention and Suppression Action Plan Implementation","In 2018, PSD has adopted the National Plan of Action to Prevent and Suppress of Human Trafficking (NPA-PSHT) 2018-2022.","Public Security Division (PSD) of MoHA"],[1,"257","6","National Authority Capacity Strengthening for Anti-Trafficking Coordination","Under the 8FYP, PSD aims to strengthen the capacity of the National Authority to better implement the NPA.","Public Security Division (PSD) of MoHA"],[1,"257","6","Anti-Trafficking Coordination and Lead Agency Development","During the implementation of the 8FYP, this Authority can grow into the lead agency to coordinate all out efforts against the traffickers.",""],[1,"257","6","Legal Enforcement for Safer Migration and Mobility","As a priority, PSD plays a critical role in enforcement of legal provisions (Migrants Act 2013 and PSHT Act 2012) to make mobility of people, migration and migrants safer.","Public Security Division (PSD) of MoHA"],[1,"257","6","Law Enforcement and Border Control Capacity Development","The 8FYP will focus in investing in capacity development for law enforcement and border control to combat trafficking and smuggling in persons.",""],[1,"257","6","Counter-Trafficking Committee Strengthening and Activation","The 8FYP can provide resources and capacity building assistance to strengthen and activate these CTCs.",""],[1,"257","6","Strengthening the Role of the Public Security Division in Anti-Trafficking","Hence during the 8FYP, the government will set priority on strengthening the role of PSD in meeting the objectives set in the NPA to prevent and suppress human trafficking.","Public Security Division (PSD)"],[1,"258","10","Human Trafficking Reduction Operations","Increasing operation to reduce human trafficking mainly women and children in neighbouring countries;",""]],"230":[[1,"258","2","BGB Goal 2041 Implementation Priorities","the 8FYP will prioritize the achievement of the targets within BGB Goal 2041",""],[1,"258","3","Border Guard Personnel Expansion","Increasing the number of personnel working for the BGB to meet the international standards;",""],[1,"258","4","Logistics Investment for BGB Operations","Increasing investments in logistics that facilitate the effective functioning of the BGB;",""],[1,"258","5","Quick Response Force Strengthening within BGB","Supporting formation and strengthening of a \"Quick Response Force\" within the BGB which will work to supply modern arms and ammunition to the border points swiftly in case of any emergency;",""],[1,"258","6","Permanent Station on St Martin's Island","Establishing a permanent station on the St Martin's island to protect the territorial integrity of Bangladesh;",""],[1,"258","7","Mechanized Border Inspection System Installation","Installing mechanized inspection system in Benapole and other land borders;",""],[1,"258","8","Border Security Infrastructure Expansion","Enhancing the security of the international boundary between Bangladesh, India and Myanmar through increasing the number Border Out Posts (BOP) and the construction of border ring roads and barbed wire fencings;",""],[1,"258","9","Comprehensive Anti-Smuggling Strategy","Developing a comprehensive strategy with all stakeholders to reduce smuggling;",""],[1,"258","11","Myanmar Border Supervision for Camp Security","Increasing supervision of the Myanmar border to maintain peace at the Rohingya camps.",""]],"231":[[1,"258","1","Rohingya Repatriation and Rehabilitation Effort","The Bangladesh government has been making diplomatic efforts in persuading Myanmar to repatriate the refugees.",""],[1,"258","1","Bhasan Char Rohingya Relocation Site Development","the government of Bangladesh has been developing a relocation site in 'Bhasan Char' island to rehabilate the Rohingya refugees.",""]],"232":[[1,"258","12","Coast Guard Modernization and Capacity Expansion","During the 7FYP period, the Government has also articulated the - Coast Guard Goal 2030 - which is a strategic document to modernize the Bangladesh Coast Guard.",""],[1,"259","1","Coast Guard Modernization and Surveillance Upgrade","under the 8FYP period, the Government will prioritize implementing the targets as noted in the \"Coast Guard Goal 2030\".",""],[1,"259","1","Coastal Surveillance Technology Enhancement","helicopters, Unmanned Aerial Vehicles (UAV), maritime patrol aircrafts and adding new generation surveillance technologies.",""],[1,"259","1","Marine Resource Protection for Blue Economy","It will also ensure that the strategic objectives of the \"Blue Economy\" agenda are protected by ensuring the safety of our marine resources.",""]],"233":[[1,"259","2","Strengthening the Bangladesh Ansar and Village Defence Party","under the 8FYP period, the following initiatives will be taken to strengthen the role of the Ansar and Village Defence Party (VDP):","Ministry of Home Affairs"],[1,"259","3","Public Welfare Delivery Capacity Enhancement","The Government will enhance its capacity to effectively dispensing public welfare activities as per the instruction of the Government effectively;",""],[1,"259","4","Logistical Support for National Emergency Response","It will receive logistical support to ensure that it can effectively support the Bangladesh Armed Forces in any national emergency.",""]],"234":[[1,"259","6","Fire Service and Civil Defence Capacity Strengthening","under the 8FYP, the Government will strengthen the capacity of the Fire Service and Civil Defence department to ensure public safety by investing in training of key emergency personals, importing necessary technologies and fire-fighting instruments to effectively carryout rescue operation during any man-made or natural disasters.",""],[1,"259","6","Fire Safety Surveillance and Enforcement Team","The Government will also develop a surveillance team under the Fire Service Department to monitor hazardous economic activities, so that fire safety regulations are effectively enforced across the key \"fire-hotspots\" of the country.",""]],"235":[[1,"303","3","Women-Focused Skills Development and TVET Investment","That calls for a more forceful skill-development policy directed towards women with adequate investment in TVET and other training options.",""],[1,"320","10","Upazila Training Facility Expansion","Each Upazila should have a training facility in coordination with BTEB.",""],[1,"321","7","International Labour Market Skills Development","Attach highest importance to developing skills responsive to the needs in international labour market.",""]],"236":[[1,"321","11","Overseas Employment Diplomacy Declaration","A declaration of decade of \"overseas employment diplomacy\" may be a cornerstone of the paradigm shift.",""],[1,"322","2","Ethical Recruitment and Empathy Training Reform","'Ethical recruitment' and 'empathy' will be two key parameters for this mind-set shift agenda.",""],[1,"322","3","Institutional Reform for Skilled Overseas Employment","The paradigm shift will include an agenda of institutional reform, which can cater to the need of potential employees of all sections of the society.",""],[1,"322","6","Upgrade BMET to a Full-Fledged Department","BMET will have to be raised to a Full-fledged department.",""],[1,"322","7","Institutional Mapping and Migration Coordination Mechanism","One of the major action points for the Ministry during the period of 8FYP will be mapping the activities of these two key institutions reducing overlap in mandate and activities and ensuring appropriate integration of activities in the migration continuum.",""],[1,"322","7","Integrated Digital Service Management for Migration Coordination","The responsibility of coordination will be with the Ministry with an integrated digital service management.",""],[1,"322","8","Centre for Research on Labour Migration","a new Centre for Research on Labour Migration will be established linked with the Research Wing of the Ministry with a similar status in BIDS or BIISS.","Ministry"],[1,"322","8","Labour Market Research Unit","The Ministry will also establish a Labour Market Research Unit (LMRU) inside BMET.","The Ministry"],[1,"322","9","Overseas Employment Diplomacy Capacity and Coordination Enhancement","Without reducing focus on trade diplomacy, Bangladesh will be able to reap the benefit of foreign employment market through 'overseas employment diplomacy'.","Ministry of Expatriates' Welfare and Overseas Employment | Ministry of Foreign Affairs"],[1,"323","6","Overseas Employment Market Expansion Roadmap","the Ministry will launch an 'Overseas employment market expansion road- map' by a new 'Market Expansion Task-force', combining all relevant Ministries and agencies.","Ministry"],[1,"323","7","National Action Plan for Skills Development and Migration Management","a National Action Plan for Skills Development and Migration Management has been developed.",""],[1,"323","8","Skills Development Collaboration Initiative","The Ministry will take initiative during this period to work with National Skills Development Authority (NSDA) and Bangladesh Technical Education Board and Future of Work Lab.","Ministry"],[1,"323","11","Skills Classification Policy for Migration","The Ministry will develop a 'Policy for Skills Classification for Migration' to replace the traditional 4 level category (Less-Skilled, Semi-Skilled, Skilled and Professional) to new competency-based grading system (NTVQF).","The Ministry"],[1,"323","11","BMET Occupational Database Upgrade","The Ministry will also upgrade BMET occupational database by re-classifying migrants in terms of the new classification system.","The Ministry"],[1,"323","11","Annual Wage Rate Review Mechanism","Annual review will be conducted in COD to establish realistic wage rates and differentials for skilled workers.",""],[1,"324","5","Migration Information Communication Strategy","The Ministry will develop a communication strategy on skills training & NTVQF qualification and better-quality information on safe migration for aspiring migrants.","The Ministry"],[1,"324","6","Public-Private Partnership for Migrant Worker Services","The Ministry will initiate private-public partnership in the areas of access to services for migrant workers at home and abroad with a provision of quality control and engaging expatriate Bangladeshi professionals.","The Ministry"],[1,"324","7","Mainstreaming of Service Delivery Programs through Public-Private Partnership","The Ministry will mainstream services under those programmes/projects through public-private partnership, engaging Office of the Public-Private Partnership at Prime Minister's Office.","The Ministry | Office of the Public-Private Partnership at Prime Minister's Office"],[1,"325","1","Institutional Capacity Strengthening for Migrant Worker Protection","During the 8FYP, Ministry will allocate resources for strengthening institutional capacity for ensuring protection, rights and well-being of migrant workers, especially women migrants.",""],[1,"325","4","Introduction of the International Recruitment Integrity System","The Ministry will explore the scope of introduction of International Recruitment Integrity System (IRIS) for encouraging private sector recruiting agencies at home and destination countries practicing fair recruitment to reduce excessive cost of migration as well as protection of rights of migrants.","The Ministry"],[1,"325","5","Skilled Migration Market Expansion and Protection Criteria Policy","While Bangladesh's strategy will be to explore new markets and facilitating migration with higher skills, Bangladesh will take a stance of 'no migration', unless a minimum set of criteria is fulfilled in terms of wage, rights and protection, in line with international conventions.",""],[1,"325","6","Migration Service Mapping and Digitization Initiative","The Ministry will initiate mapping of all existing services and assess the effectiveness and adequacy.","The Ministry"],[1,"325","7","Labour Migration Data Strategy","The Ministry will develop a labour migration data strategy, which will facilitate all relevant Ministries, Agencies at home and abroad to share data to better strategize and provide services to migrant workers as well as better protection.","The Ministry"],[1,"326","1","Migration Process Streamlining Project","The Ministry will undertake project for further streamlining the process of migration with optimization of engagement of intermediaries, by launching an accountability framework for intermediary.","Ministry"],[1,"326","2","Technical Committee for Migration Action Plan Coordination","the Ministry will form a technical committee for coordination of implementation of action plan so that activities, programmes and projects complement in terms capacity and specialization, rather than compete with each other.","Ministry"],[1,"326","3","Private Sector Engagement for Safe and Gainful Migration","The Ministry will lead and take effective initiative and programmes to include the private sector in promoting migration of skilled workers, protection rights and ensure gainful migration.","The Ministry"],[1,"326","4","Ethical Recruitment System Development and Monitoring","The Ministry will develop \"ethical recruitment\" system and monitor BAIRA for implementation.","Ministry"],[1,"326","5","Zero Recruitment Cost Migration Strategy","The Ministry will take leadership in mobilizing governments and stakeholders of sending countries and international stakeholders for developing a strategy of 'zero recruitment cost migration' (employers pay model) and 'every citizen's right matter' policy for safety and rights of migrant workers.","The Ministry"],[1,"326","6","Low Recruitment Cost Migration Programme","The Ministry will undertake a five-year programmes targeting 'low recruitment cost migration' through negotiation with employers, recruiting agencies and service providers.","The Ministry"],[1,"326","7","BOESL Market Access and Capacity Expansion","The Ministry will also increase capacity of BOESL for accessing new market and expanding existing market, which will reduce cost of migration and increase competition, through market- based incentives for reducing cost.","The Ministry"],[1,"336","3","Migrant Worker Support and Remittance Facilitation Services","This is a welcome development and benefitted from a range of government support services including remittance facilitation, government level dialogue with host countries to protect the interests of the migrant workers, tax exemption and cash incentives, and information sharing.",""],[1,"336","3","Legal Overseas Employment Promotion and Migrant Welfare Protection","There is a dedicated Ministry, The Ministry of Expatriate's Welfare and Overseas Employment, that is dedicated to the promotion of legal overseas employment, promoting migrant well-being, and protecting promotes the interests of the migrant workers abroad and at home.","The Ministry of Expatriate's Welfare and Overseas Employment"],[1,"336","3","Improvement of Migrant Employment Support Services","Further efforts are underway to improve these services.",""]],"237":[[1,"323","2","Expansion of District Employment and Manpower Offices","the Ministry will establish DEMOs in all uncovered districts, and increase capacity of the offices at migration-prone districts","Ministry"],[1,"323","2","Decentralization of Pre-departure Migration Processes","a number of pre- departure processes were decentralized",""],[1,"323","2","Registration and Smart Card Distribution Facilities Development","the facilities of registration and smart card distribution will be developed in all 64 districts",""],[1,"323","2","Definition of DEMO Scope of Work","Scope of work for the DEMOs need to be outlined to ensure effective migration, employment and reintegration facilitation",""],[1,"324","3","One-Stop Service for Potential Migrants","The 8FYP will introduce seamless one-stop-service for the potential migrants by integration of physical and digital infrastructure.",""],[1,"324","4","Grievance Management System Expansion and Integration","The 8FYP will expand the capacity of the grievance management system integrating with national grievance management.",""]],"238":[[1,"321","10","Migrant Return and Reintegration Support","Make sure that return of the migrants is ensured through sustainable social and economic reintegration.",""],[1,"322","4","Sustainable Reintegration of Migrant Workers Policy","The Ministry will initiate adoption of a 'Sustainable Reintegration of Migrant Workers Policy'.","The Ministry"],[1,"322","4","Rules for Wage Earner's Welfare Board Act 2018 Adoption","The Ministry will expedite adoption of a 'Rules for Wage Earner's Welfare Board Act 2018', so that benefits of provisions for migrant workers reach them.","The Ministry"],[1,"325","3","Support Package for Returning Migrant Workers","The Ministry will explore scope of introduction of a package of support for returning migrant workers (including entrepreneurial skills training, job placement and skills assessment) to assist their reintegration into the domestic labour market.","The Ministry"],[1,"326","8","Sustainable Reintegration of Migrant Workers Policy","The Ministry will initiate adoption of a 'Sustainable Reintegration of Migrant Workers Policy'.","The Ministry"],[1,"326","8","Rules for Wage Earner's Welfare Board Act 2018 Adoption","The Ministry will expedite adoption of a 'Rules for Wage Earner's Welfare Board Act 2018', so that benefits of provisions for migrant workers reach them.","The Ministry"],[1,"326","8","Returnee Migrant Reintegration SOP","The Ministry will adopt a Standard Operating Procedure (SOP) for returnee migrant reintegration, especially for female migrants.","The Ministry"],[1,"326","9","Returnee Migrant Reintegration Referral Mechanism and Support Package","The Ministry will establish an inter-ministerial and inter-agency/department \"referral mechanism\" for the sustainable reintegration of the returnee and will develop and implement a package of support for returning migrant workers, including social and psychosocial reintegration, entrepreneurial skills training, job placement and skills assessment to assist their reintegration into the domestic labour market.","The Ministry"],[1,"327","1","Reintegration Services Capacity Building for Returnee Migrants","Capacity building of the DEMOs and WEWB to deliver reintegration services to the returnee migrants including referral for medical, psychosocial support, skills development, economic rehabilitation and financial inclusion.",""]],"239":[[1,"324","8","PKB Branch Network Expansion and Digital Banking Services","The Ministry will work closely with the PKB to remove all bottlenecks, including expanding the branch network including agent banking outlets in each Upazila.","Ministry"],[1,"324","9","Cash Incentive for Remittance through Regular Channels","The government has also introduced a very progressive system of 2% cash incentive to the migrant workers for sending their remittance through regular channel.",""],[1,"324","9","Migrant Worker and Family Insurance Service Expansion","The government has introduced insurance service for migrant workers and their family members.",""],[1,"324","10","Financial Literacy and Remittance Management Training for Migrants","The Ministry will take comprehensive plan to promote financial literacy and remittance management training for migrants at the pre-departure stage.","The Ministry"],[1,"324","10","Remittance Utilization Awareness for Migrant Families","The Ministry will lead activities to ensure migrant's families are well aware about the gainful utilization of remittance.","The Ministry"],[1,"326","10","Mandatory Deposit Scheme for Migrant Workers","During 8FYP, initiatives will be taken to introduce new mechanism, including the introduction of mandatory deposit schemes for migrant workers, which can be deducted by the remittance receiving banks and accumulate in the account of migrant workers.",""],[1,"342","5","Remittance Productive Use and Migrant Worker Support Programme","Develop effective programmes for the productive use of remittance inflows and improve facilities for migrant workers to legally exploit job opportunities abroad and send remittances home.",""]],"240":[[1,"337","1","Public Investment in Transport and Logistics Infrastructure","demand for these services from trading and passenger traffic presents a substantial investment opportunity for local investors that needs to be cashed in through proper public investments in related assets and infrastructure (sea ports and airports, operation of private and public shipping and airlines, and container terminals) and with facilitating regulatory policies.",""],[1,"337","1","Facilitating Regulatory Policies for Transport Services","and with facilitating regulatory policies.",""],[1,"338","20","Civil Aviation Authority Head Office Construction","Construction of Civil Aviation Authority's Head Office",""],[1,"338","22","Airport Infrastructure Development and New International Airport Construction","Infrastructural development of the existing airports and construction of a new international airport.",""],[1,"345","4","Inter-District Road Upgrading to Four-Lane Standard","Convert all inter-district roads to 4-way lanes.",""],[1,"345","5","Asian Highway Road and Bridge Link Completion","Complete the road/bridge links to make the Asian Highway functional.",""],[1,"345","6","Padma Bridge Completion","Complete the Padma Bridge.",""],[1,"345","7","Completion of Ongoing Urban Flyover Projects","Complete all on-going flyovers in major urban centres, especially Dhaka and Chittagong.",""],[1,"345","8","Dhaka Circular Road Completion","Complete the Dhaka circular road.",""],[1,"345","9","Urban Mass Transit Project Implementation","Implement all urban mass transit projects as scheduled",""],[1,"345","10","Karnaphuli Tunnel Completion","Complete the Karnaphuli tunnel.",""],[1,"345","11","Railway Capacity Expansion","Expand the railway capacity.",""],[1,"345","12","Matarbari Dedicated Port Development","Build the Matarbari dedicated port.",""],[1,"345","13","Mongla Port Capacity and Effectiveness Upgrade","Upgrade the effectiveness and capacity of the Mongla Port.",""],[1,"345","14","Hazrat Shahjalal International Airport Upgrade","Upgrade Hazrat Shahjalal International Airport.",""],[1,"345","15","Cox's Bazar Airport Upgrade","Upgrade the Cox's Bazar Airport.",""],[1,"345","16","New International Airport Development","Initiate work on the new international airport.",""]],"241":[[1,"338","28","Tourism Training Courses and Centres Expansion","Maintaining tourism related training courses and establishing 4 more tourist training centres",""],[1,"344","5","Tourism Workforce Supply and Quality Measures","Introduce measures to address issues pertaining to the supply and quality of workforce in the tourism industry.",""]],"242":[[1,"342","4","Skills Development for Service and Industrial Sectors","Develop capabilities that strengthen the skills base for the service industry and the industrial sector.",""],[1,"342","9","Skills Development for Employment and Entrepreneurship","Support skills development for employment and entrepreneurship",""],[1,"342","10","Facilitation of Technical Skills Import","Import of technical skills in the area of aviation, international shipping, ICT and tourism should be facilitated.",""],[1,"350","1","Skills Retraining and Workforce Inclusion Measures","This will entail skills retraining for lifelong learning, job redesign, establishment of inclusion and diversity in the workforce and government support in matching education with employment policies.",""],[1,"350","2","Systems Approach for Entrepreneurship and Employment","Support a systems approach for entrepreneurship and employment: Ensure whole of society approach that benefits the most marginalized and vulnerable and ensures a sustainable, meaningful, evidence-driven approach to transforming employment and self-employment.",""],[1,"350","5","Public-Private Cooperation for Innovation and ESG Investment","Create space for public-private cooperation on financing, support to the innovation ecosystem, demand-creation (for both national and international markets) and ESG (environmental social governance) investment:",""]],"243":[[1,"348","6","Health Practitioner and Private Facility Licensing","Licensing of health practitioners and private hospitals/clinics/labs to ensure health safety and acceptable standards.",""],[1,"348","7","Healthcare Grievance Unit","Ensure accountability of healthcare professionals by establishing a grievance unit under the Ministry of Health and Family Welfare that looks at public complaints for poor services.","Ministry of Health and Family Welfare"],[1,"348","8","Food Vendor Licensing for Sanitation and Health Safety","Licensing of food vendors in hotels, restaurants and other commercial food vendors to ensure sanitation and health safety standards.",""],[1,"348","13","Mandatory Liability Insurance Requirement","Require purchase of liability insurance for all healthcare providers and enterprises engaged in the transport industry.",""]],"244":[[1,"342","6","Prudential Regulation Enforcement Strengthening","Strengthen implementation of prudential regulations to boost service quality, increase public safety, improve compliance and ensure accountability of service providers.",""],[1,"348","9","Driver Licensing and Driving Record Monitoring","Strict monitoring of licensing and driving records of truck and bus drivers.",""],[1,"348","10","Road Damage Monitoring Based on Vehicle Weight and Loading Norms","Monitoring of road damage based on vehicle weight and loading norms.",""],[1,"348","11","Commercial Vehicle Safety Features Enforcement","Strict implementation of safety features of commercial vehicles",""],[1,"348","15","Public Education and Enforcement of Regulations","The implementation of these regulations will require proper education through mass media as well as cooperation with the private enterprises.",""],[1,"348","15","Administrative Penalty and License Revocation Mechanism","To minimize the administrative burden on public institutions, a system of financial penalty and revoking of licensing where deemed necessary will be instituted",""],[1,"349","1","Online Licensing Administration and Complaint Registry","all licensing requirements will be administered online with established timelines for responses.",""],[1,"349","1","Online Enterprise Grievance Redress Mechanism","An online complaint registry will be established to redressal enterprise grievances.",""],[1,"349","1","Regulatory Staff Capacity Building and Ethics Enforcement","Staff of public regulatory agencies will be enhanced as necessary and will be given necessary training.",""],[1,"349","1","Disciplinary Enforcement for Public Service Ethics Violations","Strict disciplinary actions will be enforced for public service agents that are found in violation of ethical and service standards.",""]],"245":[[1,"362","2","Climate Resilience Fund","To meet the excess maintenance and repairing cost as well as construction of infrastructure to protect livelihood will require maintaining a resilience fund.",""],[1,"362","2","Climate-Affected Population Habitation Support","Also, it will require significant amount of money for habitation of the people affected by the impacts of climate change.",""]],"246":[[1,"365","4","Agricultural Supply Chain Restoration and Development","Restore and develop the agricultural supply chain aftermath of COVID-19 crisis; minimise the impact of COVID-19 for smooth agriculture growth and ensure food security after the crisis.",""],[1,"368","5","Agricultural COVID-19 Stimulus Package","the government, in the backdrop of the Covid- 19 fallout, announced a stimulus package of BDT 5,000 crore for farmers to boost agricultural production.",""],[1,"368","5","Fertilizer Subsidy Allocation","an additional BDT 9,500 crore was allocated for fertilizer subsidies (as in the budget for FY2021) as part of the government's strategy to minimise the impact.",""],[1,"368","5","Seed Distribution Support for Affected Farmers","Seeds worth BDT 150 crore will be distributed among affected farmers so that agricultural production would be continued.",""],[1,"369","1","Expansion of Cash and Food Transfer Programmes","The existing cash and food transfer programme including VGD, VGF, and EGPP will also be expanded and other new employment generating programmes will be initiated.",""],[1,"369","1","New Employment-Generating Programmes","The existing cash and food transfer programme including VGD, VGF, and EGPP will also be expanded and other new employment generating programmes will be initiated.",""],[1,"369","2","Stimulus Loan Disbursement Monitoring Body","A monitoring body will be established for the disbursement of loan from the stimulus and for monitoring its effective implementation.",""],[1,"369","2","Agricultural Crisis Management Fund","Besides, a long-term Crisis Management Fund should be established for the agriculture sector so that production and supply chains are not disturbed from any crisis.",""],[1,"369","2","Price Stabilization Policy Measures","Besides, price stabilization policies should be adopted and implemented.",""]],"247":[[1,"369","4","Seed Production Capacity and Distribution Channel Improvement","The Bangladesh Agricultural Development Corporation (BADC), Department of Agricultural Extension (DAE) and other government agencies need to enhance their capability for producing more seeds.",""],[1,"369","4","Farmer Extension Programme for Balanced Fertilizer Use","Extension programmes will be designed to encourage farmers to use recommended/balanced doses of chemical fertilizers.",""],[1,"369","4","Fertilizer Subsidy Rebalancing Policy","The government has already adopted the policy of rebalancing fertilizer subsidy policy in favour of non-urea fertilizers.",""],[1,"369","4","Organic and Bio-Fertilizer Production and Use Strategy","Furthermore, strategies for extensive production and use of organic/bio fertilizers, and proper utilization of soil guide and soil testing facilities will be developed and implemented.",""]],"248":[[1,"366","12","Low-Interest Agricultural Credit Facility","To extend credit facilities to farmers through banks and other financial institutions at a low rate of 2 per cent.",""],[1,"370","2","Tenant Protection and Pre-emption in Land Transfer","strategies are needed to safeguard of the tenants against eviction and granting them the right of pre-emption in land transfer.",""],[1,"370","2","Distribution of Government Khas Land to Landless and Marginal Farmers","The government khas land needs to be distributed among the landless and the marginal farmers.",""],[1,"373","4","Agricultural Credit Facilitation for Small Farmers and Intermediaries","Easing agricultural credit facilities for small farmers and intermediaries",""]],"249":[[1,"370","5","Precision Agriculture Promotion","the 8FYP will give more focus on Precision Agriculture (PA), which will ensure optimization of inputs use and maximization of returns while preserving resources and reducing environmental risks.",""],[1,"370","6","Good Agricultural Practices Protocol Development and Certification","Certification and accreditation will continue to be the main focus for safe food production and marketing at local and export markets.",""]],"250":[[1,"374","3","Livestock Research and Technology Development","The Bangladesh Livestock Research Institute (BLRI) is responsible to identify the livestock and poultry production constraints at the national and farm level, seek solutions to those problems through multi and inter-disciplinary and inter-institutional research and to develop technologies to help food and nutrition security, contributing to poverty alleviation, employment and income generation, and reduced environment pollution.",""],[1,"378","1","Adaptive Livestock Research and Technology Transfer Programme","To generate need-based technology and improve livelihood of livestock farmers through adaptive research and to transfer developed technologies to users through training of extension workers, planners, livestock farmers and other stakeholders",""],[1,"378","2","Climate-Resilient and Low-Cost Feed and Fodder Production","To develop climate resilient and low-cost feeds and fodders production",""],[1,"378","12","Livestock Research and Development Capacity Enhancement","Productivity will be enhanced through extensive research and development activities.",""],[1,"378","12","Safe Animal Products and Livestock Input Development","Research capacities of BLRI and other universities/institutes undertaking the relevant research activities will be enhanced to address the national priority and harness the untapped potential of regional livestock resources, and to ensure safe production of animal products and by-products, animal protein supplement, feed additives, premixes, probiotics and mineral and vitamin supplements as inputs for poultry and livestock development.",""],[1,"378","12","Private and NGO Livestock Research Support Initiative","Initiatives will be taken to encourage and support private agencies and NGOs to undertake livestock research.",""],[1,"378","13","Livestock Breed Improvement and Artificial Insemination Programme","Breed development through crossbreeding local variety with suitable exotic variety should be of upmost priority.",""]],"251":[[1,"379","3","Collateral-Free Concessional Loan Facility for Poultry and Livestock Farmers","Short-to-medium term collateral-free loan facilities at subsidized interest rates, amongst others, should be introduced for poultry and livestock farmers.",""]],"252":[[1,"379","5","Livestock Management Practice Improvement","Better management practices such as quality assurance of feed stuff including water, disease and pest control, hygienic processing of products and environmentally safe disposal of wastes are important strategies.",""],[1,"379","5","Livestock Human Capital Training and Extension Support","The DLS has a role in developing human capital through training on appropriate feed mixture, vaccination and adherence to bio-security guidelines.",""],[1,"379","5","Livestock Insurance Scheme Introduction","Introduction of insurance schemes, at least for large commercial farms, will also be an important consideration.",""],[1,"379","5","Veterinary and Extension Services Strengthening","Veterinary and extension services are critical for livestock farming, although the DLS offices do not exist beyond the upazila level.",""],[1,"379","5","Lead Farmer Approach Expansion","The lead farmer approach will be continued with more training and incentives for the farmers.",""]],"253":[[1,"390","2","Inland River Port Development and Operations","The Bangladesh Inland Water Transport Authority (BIWTA) is another organization engaged in river conservation and developing, maintaining and operating inland river ports.",""],[1,"398","2","Implementation of NRC River, Water, Environment and Biodiversity Recommendations","The specific recommendations will be implemented with the participation of and collaboration with all actors, organisations, departments and authorities at the local and national level.",""],[1,"398","2","3R Waste Technology for Urban and Rural Waste Disposal","One notable suggestion is the implementation of 3R (Reduce, Reuse, and Recycle) technology to dispose of all kinds of urban as well as rural domestic and industrial wastes to protect river and water bodies.",""],[1,"398","2","Regional River and Water Body Master Plans","Under the close supervision of NRC Commission, ten committees have been formed to prepare master plans of ten regions of the country to free the rivers, canals, water bodies, haor-baor, and coastal areas from illegal grabbers; prevent river water pollution; conserve the environment, ecology and biodiversity of rivers; improve navigability; prevent river erosion; undertake flood control and river development multipurpose usages.",""],[1,"398","6","Multi-layered Water Negotiation Dialogue Mechanism","Incorporation of multi-layered dialogues that will enable participating countries to initiate negotiations from new entry points and also link water related negotiations with other river interests and regional cooperation issues.",""],[1,"399","2","Multi-Track Water Diplomacy and River Basin Management","multi-track water diplomacy has to be applied to prevent or peacefully resolve conflicts related to water availability, its allocation or use between and within states for better understanding of trans boundary issues and to ensure effective formulation and implementation of common river basin management schemes related to joint usage and equitable allocation of water resources that are centred on the concept of benefit sharing.",""],[1,"399","3","Environmental Flow Maintenance and River Monitoring Initiative","It is imperative that environmental flow is maintained in the rivers and as such, necessary initiatives have to be taken both on a bi- and multi-lateral basis and enacted accordingly.",""],[1,"399","4","Simultaneous Multiple-Treaty Negotiation Approach","Simultaneous negotiation of multiple treaties has to be done to ensure that the benefits given up on one treaty could be used as leverage for another more significant treaty.",""],[1,"399","5","Transboundary River Water Sharing Agreements","Prioritization of rivers has to be done in implementing devised schemes regarding water sharing.",""],[1,"399","6","Demand-Based Common River Basin Management Schemes","Demand based common river basin management schemes has to be initiated where the involved countries will weigh in their views regarding mutually beneficial river management and solve common issues both bi- and multi-laterally through construction of necessary infrastructure on optimal hydrological and ecological locations within the river basins.",""],[1,"399","7","International Mediation and Third-Party Engagement Mechanism","International approach can be implemented that will involve active participation of a third party, either an international organisation or a country.",""],[1,"399","8","Benefit-Sharing Mutual Gains Negotiation Framework","Benefit-sharing \"mutual gains\" model has to be implemented that discourages unilateral actions and further encourages coordination between riparian countries.",""],[1,"399","8","Joint River Basin Organization Establishment","The framework agreement has opened the opportunity for conducting negotiations through establishment of joint body river basin organizations in pursuing common river basin management.",""],[1,"399","8","Sub-Regional Cooperation for Power, Navigability, and Connectivity","Involving various sub-regional cooperation issues such as in power sector or navigability and physical connectivity can greatly enhance the mutual gains basket.",""],[1,"400","4","Bangladesh Delta Plan Investment Plan","The Bangladesh Delta Plan Investment Plan (BDP2100IP) consists of a total of 80 projects: 65 are physical projects, and 15 are institutional and knowledge development projects.",""]],"254":[[1,"402","2","Delta Policy Framework and Institutional Reform Agenda","The other two aspects relate to Delta policy framework and reforms of Delta institutions.",""],[1,"402","5","Fiscal Framework Implementation for the 8FYP","The government will dutifully implement the fiscal framework for the 8FYP, which builds on the approved fiscal framework of the PP2041.",""],[1,"402","5","Critical Tax Reform Programme","The most important policy assumption is that the government will undertake critical tax reforms to enable tax revenue to grow from 8.9% of GDP in FY2020 to 14% of GDP in FY2025.",""],[1,"402","5","8FYP Public Investment Programme Implementation","Without this critical reform the ability to implement the 8FYP PIP for BDP2100 will not happen.",""],[1,"402","6","Cost Recovery Policy for Urban Water Supply and Irrigation and Flood Control","The government will institute cost recovery policies in urban water supply and in irrigation and flood control measures to allow revenues from cost recovery policies in these Delta programmes from 0.1% of GDP now to about 0.3% of GDP by FY2025.",""],[1,"402","6","Institutional Reform of City Corporations and Municipalities for Urban Water Cost Recovery","This calls for major reforms in City Corporations and Municipalities for cost recovery in urban water supply",""],[1,"402","6","Establishment of Water User Associations","for the establishment of effective Water User Associations (WUAs) in rural areas.",""],[1,"402","7","Private Participation in Delta Investments","The government will facilitate private participation in Delta investments.",""],[1,"403","1","Delta Wing and Delta Fund Institutional Reform","These include the initiation of the process for establishing the Delta Wing in General Economics Division (GED) of the Planning Commission and the process for establishing the Delta Fund led by GED.","General Economics Division (GED) of the Planning Commission"],[1,"403","1","Delta Operations and Maintenance Capacity Strengthening","the 8FYP must focus on improving the O&M and project implementation capacities of all Delta line ministries and agencies",""],[1,"403","1","Decentralized Water Management Framework","lay the foundations for decentralized water management that is critical for long-term sustainability of the BDP2100 program",""],[1,"403","1","Delta Knowledge Creation and Dissemination Channel","initiate Delta-related knowledge creation and dissemination channel",""],[1,"403","1","Results-Based Monitoring and Evaluation System","lay the foundations for a comprehensive results-based Monitoring and Evaluation (M&E) System",""],[1,"403","3","Quick Review of Existing O&M Practices","To determine the current O & M practice and their adequacy, a quick review on existing O&M practices in relevant Delta Ministries / Departments can be done.",""],[1,"403","4","Operations and Maintenance Good Practice Framework","Based on that review, establish good O&M practices in terms of sources of funding, institutional accountability, and monitoring and evaluation.",""],[1,"403","6","Strengthening Core Delta Institutions","it is imperative to strengthen the core delta institutions.",""],[1,"403","7","Strengthening of BWDB and WARPO","Both institutions need considerable strengthening in new technology, innovation, integrated planning, research, economic management and consultative processes.",""],[1,"403","7","Support for Local Water Body Establishment and Coordination","They will also need to help out with the establishment of the local water bodies and learn to work with them collegially as a complementary institution rather than as a competing institution.",""],[1,"403","7","Support for Decentralized Water Management","WARPO and the BWDB can make this process smoother and less costly through proper support and coordination.",""],[1,"403","8","BWDB Capacity Strengthening and Expert Staffing","These gaps will have to be addressed with proper staffing of experts in the missing areas.",""],[1,"403","8","Innovative Water Management Solutions Development","BWDB must be encouraged to find innovative engineering solutions to water management problems in the same spirit as the Dutch Delta Works.",""],[1,"403","8","University and International Training for Water Engineers","Considerable interaction with water engineers in the universities and international training from countries like the Netherlands that have excelled in designing innovative technical solutions to coastal belt management, river management, flood control and irrigation.",""],[1,"403","8","No-Regrets Flood and Irrigation Engineering Solutions","Attention should be given to designing and adopting \"no regrets\" engineering solutions to flood and irrigation management projects.",""],[1,"404","1","Municipal Water and Sanitation Institutional Reform","emphasis should be placed on converting these institutions into autonomous bodies with considerable scope for cost recovery from users based on service provided.",""],[1,"404","1","Performance-Based Block Grant Funding for Municipalities","This can also support innovative ways of encouraging good performance of municipalities by linking budget funding (block grants) with performance.",""],[1,"404","3","Creation of Participatory Local Water Bodies","Moving forward, what are needed are some bold and radical efforts to create truly participatory local water bodies in the same spirit as the Dutch water bodies.",""],[1,"404","4","Beneficiary Stakeholder Representation Reform in Water Management","Establishment of this missing link in water management is an essential reform for successful management of the Delta Plan.",""],[1,"404","5","Water User Institution Establishment","The water bodies should be established based on: 1) a careful review of good practices and international experiences including the Dutch experience; 2) analysis",""],[1,"405","2","Local Water Management Bodies Formation","The foundations for a more decentralized approach to water management must be initiated during the 8FYPicluding formation of local water management bodies as indicated in BDP 2100.",""],[1,"405","3","Delta Knowledge Unit Establishment","The institutional requirement is to create a knowledge unit with three main responsibilities:",""],[1,"405","4","Digitized Delta Knowledge Library","collate all relevant delta related knowledge globally and nationally into a digitized knowledge library;",""],[1,"405","5","Delta Data Bank Establishment","establish a delta data bank;",""],[1,"405","6","Delta Knowledge and Data Updating Initiative","develop and implement a comprehensive delta knowledge and data updating effort.",""],[1,"405","7","Delta Knowledge Bank Implementation Process","To initiate the implementation process for the Delta Knowledge Bank during the 8FYP, as a first step, the Delta Wing should undertake a quick stock taking of existing Delta-related research and data.",""],[1,"405","7","Delta Knowledge and Data Upgrading Agenda","This report should be shared with other delta-related public agencies and with private research institutions to develop a knowledge and data upgrading agenda.",""],[1,"405","7","Delta Monitoring and Evaluation Work Programme","The Delta Wing should review this agenda to check for consistency and relevance with the needs of the delta management, especially in the context of doing a sound monitoring and evaluation of the Delta Plan, and develop a 3-5 years data and research work programme with annual targets.",""],[1,"405","8","Knowledge Work Programme Implementation","Following approval, the knowledge work programme and budget, implementation may proceed.",""],[1,"405","8","Data Work Implementation with Statistics Bureau and Delta Ministries","Data work can be implemented in conjunction with the Bangladesh Bureau of Statistics and other delta ministries.","Bangladesh Bureau of Statistics | other delta ministries"],[1,"405","8","Research Outsourcing to Universities and Local Research Institutions","Research can be out-sourced to universities and local research institutions.",""],[1,"405","8","Delta Wing Coordination and Oversight","The Delta Wing should be responsible for coordination and oversight.",""],[1,"405","11","Sectoral Policy and Programme Monitoring and Evaluation Arrangement","M&E of sectoral policies and programmes should rest with the concerned sectoral ministry and IMED.","concerned sectoral ministry | IMED"],[1,"406","1","Delta Plan Level Monitoring and Evaluation System","The implementation of the Delta Plan level M&E should also commence during the 8FYP.",""],[1,"409","2","Perspective Plan 2041","Bangladesh has now embarked on achieving a visionary goal of becoming a developed economy by 2041 and for which it has adopted the Perspective Plan (PP) 2041.",""]],"255":[[1,"434","2","Environmental Compliance for Power Generation","The government is very much aware of it taking measures to ensure environment rules and regulations are followed in case of power generation.",""],[1,"434","2","Ultra-Super-Critical Coal Power Technology Upgrade","coal-fired power plants will be using latest ultra-super critical technology.",""]],"256":[[1,"454","2","International Cargo Shipping Capacity Expansion","Bangladesh presently has a huge deficit on the NFS account that could be lowered substantially through the expansion of international cargo shipping capabilities.",""],[1,"455","2","Procurement of New Vessels","Procurement of 6 new vessels (3 new Product Oil Tankers and 3 new Bulk Carriers of about 39,000 DWT each).",""],[1,"455","5","Cellular Container Vessel Procurement","Procurement of 4 Nos. cellular Container vessel of about 900-1200 TEUs each.",""],[1,"455","6","Acquisition of Cellular Container Vessels","4 Nos. cellular Container vessel of about 1200- 1500 TEUs each is likely to be acquired from G to G through Danish loan assistant.",""],[1,"455","8","Bangladesh Shipping Corporation Automation and Computerization Programme","Automation programmes to computerization of the overall activities of Bangladesh Shipping Corporation (BSC).",""],[1,"472","8","Bangladesh Shipping Corporation Modernization and Fleet Expansion","To achieve this target, the BSC has to be modernized with an expanded fleet, competent management and quality staff.",""],[1,"472","8","Shipping Fleet Purchase and Lease Expansion","A combination of purchase and lease operations will be used to expand fleet capacity.",""],[1,"472","8","Merchant Navy Employment Incentive for BSC Fleets","The 8FYP will strive to encourage these qualified personnel to seek employment in BSC fleets at internationally competitive salaries.",""],[1,"472","8","Bangladesh Shipping Corporation Management Upgrade and Staff Training","BSC management will be upgraded with technical competent and business-oriented professionals to be able to handle international shipping consignments efficient and effectively.",""],[1,"472","8","Private Sector Participation in International Shipping","In international shipping private sector may also be encouraged to participate.",""]],"257":[[1,"461","4","Road User Charges for Cost Recovery","the idea of introducing cost recovery from road users through the institution of a well-designed road user charges still remains to be made effective.",""],[1,"462","12","3R Intermodal Connectivity for Port Hinterland Access","3R (Rail, Road and Riverine) intermodal connectivity to support the hinterland connectivity of all ports of Bangladesh.",""],[1,"465","3","Road User Charge Reform","A proper road user charge will be developed that also accounts for congestion, risk of traffic accidents and environmental pollution and implemented in a phased manner.",""],[1,"465","3","Road Maintenance Financing","These resources will be used to improve the maintenance of roads, bridges and highways.",""],[1,"465","3","Transport Network Environmental Mainstreaming","Environmental considerations will be given emphasis in developing transport network including roads.",""],[1,"465","3","Carbon Pricing and Efficient Fossil Fuel Pricing","Fossil fuel will be priced efficiently and consideration will be given to the introduction of a carbon tax.",""],[1,"465","3","Clean Energy Transport Promotion","Clean energy transport options such as electric inter-city trains, electric elevated Mass Rapid Transit (MRT)/Metro Rail and Underground MRT/Metro Rail, electric buses, electric cars etc. will be promoted.",""],[1,"465","3","Port and Rail Service Standards Improvement","Service standards will be set for port clearings and rail services in terms of timeliness, online user-friendly ticketing and clearance documentation options, and in-transit services.",""],[1,"467","2","Sustainable and Innovative Road Technology Adoption","For longevity of road infrastructures, sustainable as well as innovative technologies will be adopted.",""],[1,"468","3","Road User Charges and Toll Financing for Road Maintenance","The development and implementation of a well-designed road user charges will be instrumental in providing resources for road network upgrading and maintenance.",""],[1,"468","3","Modern Road Maintenance Technology and Innovation Introduction","For maintenance of different road network components like highways, bridges, culverts and other road furniture, modern technologies and innovative approaches need to be introduced in order to ensure best value for money.",""],[1,"468","3","Focused Studies on Road and Toll User Charges","The 8FYP will place emphasis on implementing both these policies through focused studies to determine the proper road and toll user charges based on economic principles as well as affordability concerns.",""],[1,"475","4","Electric and Pollution-Free City Bus Fleet Expansion","Provision of large electric bus/pollution free bus operated by BRTC phasing out other small buses from the cities for rapid movement in all divisional cities.",""],[1,"475","5","Pedestrian and Cyclist Special Lanes","Creating special lanes for pedestrians and cyclists.",""],[1,"475","6","Promotion of High-Efficiency and Alternative Fuel Vehicles","Promoting high efficiency and alternative fuel vehicles.",""],[1,"475","7","Intelligent Transportation Systems Rollout","Introduce Intelligent Transportation Systems (ITS) initially in Dhaka and then extend to other metropolises.",""],[1,"475","9","Commercial Parking Facilities Development","Commercial parking facilities will be encouraged through private investment.",""],[1,"475","9","Parking Regulation Enforcement","All parking regulations will be strictly enforced with penalties for non-compliance.",""],[1,"475","10","Peak-Hour Road Access Management","Time of day use restrictions will be introduced in heavily congested roads.",""],[1,"475","11","Pedestrian Road Introduction in Dhaka and Other Metropolises","The emphasis would be given on the introduction of pedestrian roads in Dhaka City and then extend to other Metropolises.",""]],"258":[[1,"480","2","Mobile Number Portability Service Licensing","Mobile Number Portability Services (MNPS) license has been issued in favour of an operator in 2018 to provide the facility to avail the services of any other mobile operator while keeping the mobile number unchanged.",""],[1,"480","2","Tower Sharing Licensing Framework","tower sharing license has been issued in favour of 4 (four) operators in order to ensure proper utilization of tower resources, reducing demand for electricity connection and cultivable lands and to ensure health and environmental protection.",""],[1,"480","2","Telecommunication Value Added Services Regulatory Guidelines","Regulatory Guidelines for Issuance of Registration Certificate for Providing Telecommunication Value Added Services (TVAS) have been issued in 2017 to provide safe, useful, efficient, universal and affordable Telecom Value Added Services to the general public.",""],[1,"480","3","Mobile Handset Ecosystem Regulation and IMEI Database System","NOC Automation and IMEI Database have been set up in BTRC in 2019 for the protection of government revenue and facilitation of legal mobile handset imports and preparation and preservation of IMEI database.","BTRC"],[1,"480","5","Telecommunications Quality of Service Enforcement","QoS guideline has been formulated and being enforced in order to improve the quality of telecommunication services.",""],[1,"484","5","Digital Transformation Strategy","A comprehensive Digital Transformation Strategy (DTS) is very much essential for Bangladesh containing strategic vision for the country's digital transformation, clear priorities and objectives, measurable targets, sufficient budget and thorough monitoring and evaluation criteria.",""],[1,"484","5","Phase-by-Phase Digital Transformation Implementation Roadmap","A phase by phase implementation roadmap also needs to be prepared in this regard.",""],[1,"485","5","Telecommunication Industry Network Transformation","it will be necessary to prepare the telecommunication industry to fuel other sectors in harnessing the potential of 4IR.",""],[1,"485","5","Telecom Business Model and Organizational Reform","New business models will be required in telecommunication industry in order to leverage emerging disruptive technologies and for that network transformation will be necessary.",""],[1,"485","5","Digital Age Telecom Governance Reform","Above all, reforms in existing policy and regulatory models will be required for the digitization of the country's industrial sectors.",""],[1,"489","2","Personal Data Privacy Legal and Regulatory Framework","New laws, regulations and codes of practice must be there aiming to balance the interests of individuals who have a right to privacy.",""],[1,"490","3","IoT Legal and Technical Standards Framework","To enable a 4IR compliant digital connectivity ecosystem, proper guiding documents must be formulated within a very short time span.",""],[1,"492","3","Digital Transformation Strategy Formulation","Formulation of a comprehensive Digital Transformation Strategy (DTS) for Bangladesh by 2021.",""],[1,"492","4","Digital Transformation Strategy Implementation Roadmap","Preparing a phase by phase implementation roadmap for the Digital Transformation Strategy (DTS) by 2021.",""],[1,"492","5","Network Remodelling for Digital Transformation","Assessing the needs for remodelling the network including addition and/or removal of network segments to support the National Digital Transformation Strategy.",""],[1,"492","9","Licensing and Regulatory Regime Reform","Reforming the licensing and regulatory regime for faster network and organizational transformation of the service providers.",""],[1,"493","8","International Long-Distance Telecommunication Service Policy Reform","Reformulating the International Long-Distance Telecommunication Service Policy, 2010 to make it compliant with the requirements of future networks.",""]],"259":[[1,"493","1","5G Network Assessment and Migration Planning","Performing complete assessment of the present network and services and determine the migration requirements in order to smooth deployment of 5G and enabled services by June, 2021.",""],[1,"493","2","Spectrum Allocation Roadmap for 5G Networks","Preparing spectrum allocation roadmap up-to 2030 for 5G networks.",""],[1,"493","3","5G Service Introduction","Introducing 5G services in the country by June 2021.",""],[1,"493","4","5G Use Case Pilot Programme","Piloting 5G use cases in significant sectors such as agriculture, transportation, health, energy and manufacturing industries.",""],[1,"493","5","5G Coverage Action Plans","Preparing action plans to bring all the districts and metropolitan cities, industrial areas, economic zones, export processing zones and universities under the coverage of 5G by 2025.",""],[1,"493","6","5G Regulatory Review and Formulation","Review prevailing directives/guidelines/regulations/rules/Acts and/or formulate new one for smooth deployment of 5G and associated services.",""]],"260":[[1,"496","8","Affordable Digital Device Access Initiative","Making available affordable and easy to use digital devices to all of the citizens.",""],[1,"496","12","Curriculum Upgrade Coordination","Coordinating with the concerned authorities to upgrade the curriculum for the new generation.",""],[1,"496","13","Adult Digital Literacy Training Programme","Provide training to the adult population for basic literacy on the usage of digital technologies.",""],[1,"496","14","Digital Rights and Safe Access to Digital Technologies Initiative","Strengthening the civic rights of the citizens such as right to information, freedom of expression in lawful ways, participation in the policymaking and user privacy will be strengthened through non-discriminatory, affordable, easy to use and safe access to digital technologies for all citizens of Bangladesh.",""],[1,"496","15","Digital Divide Monitoring Framework","Developing a framework including relevant indicators for the government to regularly assess progress and performance towards bridging the digital divide.",""],[1,"496","17","Skills-Relevant Education and Training Provision","Placing stronger focus by the education and training providers on skills development opportunities that are relevant to the needs of learners, society and the economy.",""]],"261":[[1,"498","1","Transport Infrastructure PPP Investment Mobilization","The 8FYP financing strategy for transport infrastructures call for greater mobilisation of PPP investments in toll roads, bridges, aviation and international shipping.",""],[1,"498","1","Transport Cost Recovery Policy Strengthening","Cost recovery policies will be strengthened learning from the good practice example of the Chittagong Port Authority that earns substantial profits.",""],[1,"498","1","Transport Operations and Investment Self-Financing Mechanism","Cost recovery from airports, inland water transport, road user charges, and railway services can play a major role in O&M as well as self-financing of investments.",""]],"262":[[1,"502","5","Digital Transformation of Union Centres","Digital transformation of Union Centres;",""],[1,"502","10","Local Government PFM Reform Initiatives","The Local Government Division has undertaken several initiatives to improve the governance and financial accountability of the local government institutions (LGIs).","Local Government Division"],[1,"502","11","Annual Financial Audit and Performance Assessment System for Union Parishads","Strengthening annual financial audits and performance assessment systems for UPs.",""],[1,"502","13","Union Parishad Audit Quality Strengthening","Strengthening the quality of UP audits.",""],[1,"502","14","Union Parishad and LGD MIS Establishment","Establishing a fully functional MIS system within UPs and LGD",""],[1,"502","15","Union Parishad Service Delivery Improvement","Improving service delivery by UPs.",""],[1,"524","14","Use Union Parishad Premises for Digital and Community Learning Centres","The UPs premises will be used for Union Digital Centres, as well as for community learning centres.",""],[1,"525","7","Union Parishad Complex Construction and Upazila Complex Expansion","Construction of all remaining Union Parishad Complexes (1166 Nos.) Extension of Upazila Complexes (400 Nos)",""]],"263":[[1,"507","2","GIS-Based Digital Rural Development Database","A reliable GIS based Digital database has to be established to ensure efficient and effective implementation of the programmes for an inclusive and vibrant rural economy, and also to ensure the implementation of the \"no one is left behind\" government initiative in sustainable rural development.","RDCD"],[1,"526","5","Rural Livelihood Mapping and Open Source Database","Under the 8FYP endeavour will be made by BRDB to accomplish Rural Livelihood Mapping and publish the 'Livelihoodpedia of Bangladesh.","BRDB"],[1,"526","8","Rural Development Central Beneficiary Database System","A central beneficiary database system should be developed for rural development activities which will be administered by RDCD.",""],[1,"532","3","GIS-Based Rural Economy Database System","A GIS based database system will be established at RDCD to providing reliable information on rural economy and its develoment status.",""]],"264":[[1,"516","14","Expansion of Social Safety Net Coverage","Extend social safety nets coverage",""],[1,"516","15","Primary Health Care and Nutrition Services Promotion","Promote primary health care and nutrition services",""],[1,"527","4","Expansion of Social Safety Net Programmes","RDCD projected to extend its social safety net programmes under 8FYP with abovementioned dimension.",""],[1,"532","5","Strengthening Rural Social Protection Programme Implementation","Strengthen the implementation of social protection programmes: The government is acutely aware of the need to strengthen the implementation of the various rural social protection programmes to maximise the poverty reduction impact.",""]],"265":[[1,"524","2","Rural Community Waste Management Participation and Awareness Campaign","The rural community will be involved in waste management.",""],[1,"524","3","Waste Management Business Model Development","Two business models of waste management - degradable and recyclable - will be developed, involving the UPs in 100 UPZs at the beginning;",""],[1,"524","4","Waste Management Business Model Development","A business model will be developed for waste management at 500 GCs, initially.",""],[1,"529","3","Participatory Rural Waste Management Initiative","Initiative will also be taken to waste management in rural area in a participatory manner.",""]],"266":[[1,"524","6","National Physical Plan Development","Relevant ministries/agencies will develop National Physical Plan by 2022;",""],[1,"524","7","Upazila Master Plan Preparation","The UPZ Master Plan will target the long-term strategic plan, mid-term sectoral plan and short- term detailed area plan by 2025 for 250 UPZs (by 2030 for all).",""],[1,"524","8","Upazila Planning Staffing and Master Plan Enforcement","UPZs will be adequately staffed with the posts of 'Senior Planner' and associates to enforce the master plan;",""],[1,"524","10","Upazila Plan for Youth and Cultural Facilities","UPZ plan will incorporate spaces for Mini Stadium, Multimedia centre, Mini-theatre, Youth sports centre as per 2018 election manifesto;",""],[1,"524","11","Open Educational Institution Fields and Playgrounds to the Community","A policy will be taken to open up the fields and playgrounds of educational institutions community people;",""],[1,"524","12","Bridge Vicinity Recreational Space Development","The vicinity of bridges will be developed as recreational space under bridge development, and walkway and park on the banks of rivers/canals;",""],[1,"524","13","Community Spaces in Public Housing Provision","LGD will develop provision for community spaces in public housing, implemented by LGED and UPZs;","LGD"],[1,"524","16","Upazila Capacity Building for Master Plan Enforcement","Capacity building of UPZs for enforcement of Master Plan;",""],[1,"527","6","Local Land Use Planning and Zoning Initiative","initiative will be taken jointly with local people, BRDB, DAE and other agencies to develop land use plan under the UP.",""]],"267":[[1,"526","3","Rural Community Capacity Development","Capacity development for rural community: To enhance community capacity, focus will be given to develop Human Resources, Networking among all relevant Stakeholders in rural area, leadership development and institutional capacity development.",""],[1,"527","2","Women Empowerment Development Activities","BRDB and other agencies under RDCD will introduce different types of development activities under the 8FYP for women empowerment and bring them in the mainstream of the rural society.","BRDB | RDCD"],[1,"527","2","Women Empowerment Training and Post-Training Support","The focus area for women empowerment activities will be training, post training support, market linkage, leadership development, income generating activities etc.",""],[1,"527","2","Coordinated Action Against Dowry and Child Marriage","There will be coordinated effort with concern stakeholders for reducing dowry, child marriage, evils of eve-teasing for women empowerment and gender parity in the rural area.",""],[1,"527","5","Promotion of Indigenous Local Culture and Sports","To this end indigenous local culture and sports will be promoted and a congenial atmosphere will be created for those events.",""],[1,"527","5","RDCD Support for Socio-Cultural Activities","RDCD, through its agencies, will take initiative and patronize the socio cultural activities.","RDCD"],[1,"527","5","Rural Development Society Sports and Cultural Events","Initiative will be taken to arrange sports competition among the rural development societies, hosting the joint cultural event by the societies and UPs and promote the social capital in rural area.",""],[1,"530","14","Capacity Building for Rural People through Union Parishad and Village-Based Organizations","Capacity Building of Rural People Through Union Parishad and Village Based Organization after Corona Pandemic",""]],"268":[[1,"527","7","Low-Cost Rural Housing Initiative","Government of Bangladesh has already taken a number of initiatives to provide low cost rural housing facilities to the rural poor.",""],[1,"527","7","Multi-Storey Rural Housing Construction","Rural housing is a new concept by which multi-storied buildings will be constructed on a comparatively small piece of land at a convenient rural area so that many more rural people",""],[1,"528","1","Rural Housing Programme Implementation","BRDB has also a plan to implement the program during this 8th 5-year period.","Bangladesh Rural Development Board (BRDB)"],[1,"528","2","Rural Micro-Infrastructure Development Schemes","BRDB has been implementing micro-infrastructure development schemes at rural areas by Participatory Rural Development system since 2000.",""],[1,"528","2","Mainstreaming of Rural Micro-Infrastructure Construction","it has been decided to mainstreaming the construction of rural micro infrastructure through Participatory Rural Development system in the 45th board meeting in 2012.","LGRD&C Minister"],[1,"528","2","Micro-Infrastructure Code Creation for BRDB","BRDB has already approached the Finance Division through RDCD, to create a micro infrastructure code in favour of BRDB under revenue budget head, so that BRDB could implement the rural micro-infrastructure program on a regular basis.","Finance Division | RDCD"],[1,"531","7","Public Investment in Rural Infrastructure","Supportive policies include the implementation of BDP2100, public investment in farm technology and productivity, support policies for strengthening fishing activities including the harnessing of the potentials of the Blue Economy, public investment in rural infrastructure, and credit policies to promote non-farm economic activities.",""]],"269":[[1,"529","2","Rural Climate Change Mitigation and Adaptation Measures","For the mitigation and adaptation of the climate change consequences necessary measures will be taken in the rural area.",""],[1,"529","3","Rural Environmental Resource Management Measures","Environment friendly utilization of land and natural resources of development of rural environment will be ensured.",""],[1,"529","3","Environmental Regulatory Enforcement and National Environment Law Support","With a view to preserve ecological balance and prevent indiscriminate damage of soil, forests, water ways and animals, regulatory measures will be taken and proper application of the National Environment law will be assisted.",""],[1,"529","3","Reduction of Chemical Fertilizers and Insecticides and Promotion of Organic Manure","Necessary measures will be taken to scale down the use of chemical fertilizers and insecticides and increase the use of organic manure in agriculture.",""],[1,"529","3","Rural Environmental Awareness and Social Mobilization Campaign","Social movement for motivating rural people to actively contribute to environmental sustainability, live healthy lives and prevent pollution of soil, water and air will be strengthened.",""],[1,"529","5","My Village-My Town Initiative","Implementation of My Village-My Town - Establishment of Bangabandhu Model Village;",""]],"270":[[1,"530","8","Institutional Development for Infrastructure and Governance","Institutional development will be ensured both in terms of infrastructure and governance to accomplish the aforesaid activities.",""],[1,"530","9","BARD Applied and Action Research Programme","In the 8th plan period, BARD will conduct action research on:",""],[1,"530","15","Regional Academy Establishment for Coastal and Haor Livelihoods","BARD will establish regional academy in Barisal, Chittagong (excluding CHT) and Shylhet division to promote the livelihood for the people of coastal, haor and char land area.",""],[1,"530","16","Jashore Rural Development Academy Establishment","A new Academy will be established in Jashore to disseminate the RDA developed model for poverty reduction in Southern Part of Bangladesh and attaining the Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs).",""],[1,"531","1","Rural Development Action Research Programme","During 8th plan period, the RDAs and BAPARD will undertake action research on Sustainable Livelihood Development; Socio-economic Development of Rural Farmers through development and dissemination of cost saving and sustainable agricultural technologies; Safe Food Production; Development of marketing channels for ensuring better prices of rural produces, Adaptation of rural livelihoods with Climate Changes, Impact Covid-19 pandemic on rural economies and the way out, reducing poverty and inequality in rural economy, inclusive rural development, combating adverse impact of disaster in rural areas, development of sustainable rural development models and on other crucial areas of rural development.",""],[1,"532","3","Capacity Building for RDCD and Rural Support Institutions","The BRDB, the BARD, the RDA, the BAPARD will be strengthened to conduct action and adaptive research, disseminate appropriate knowledge, training and technology in the rural areas.",""],[1,"532","3","Foreign and Local Higher Education and Training for Rural Development Officers","Foreign and local higher education and training will be undertaken for the officers of RDCD, Rural Development Academies, BRDB and other rural agencies of RDCD in the fields of sustainable rural development, monitoring and evaluation of development programmes.",""]],"271":[[1,"541","7","Environmental Governance Incentives and Regulatory Policy Framework","Environmental governance is such whereby there is a sound mix of incentives and regulatory policies including the application of the polluter pays principle and a decentralized implementation of environmental policies and programmes.",""],[1,"542","3","National Environment Policy 2018","The Government has promulgated the National Environment Policy 2018 as refinement of the Environment Policy 1992 in order to ensure sustainable development and bring the environment into the mainstream of national development by reflecting the issues of protection and improvement of environment and biodiversity.",""],[1,"542","4","Ecologically Critical Areas Management Rules","Bangladesh government has promulgated Ecologically Critical Areas Management Rules 2016, for its proper management and improvement of the ecosystem.",""],[1,"542","5","Implementation of the Updated National Biodiversity Strategy and Action Plan","To ensure our rich biodiversity be conserved and used sustainably, we need to follow the updated NBSAP formulated in 2016.",""],[1,"543","1","National Biodiversity Strategy and Action Plan Update","Department of Environment will update or revise the NBSAP with the upcoming Global Biodiversity Framework to be adopted for the duration of 2021-2030.","Department of Environment"],[1,"543","2","Implementation of the Bangladesh Biological Diversity Act","Towards full implementation of the Act on Biodiversity, strengthened institutional structure under the Department of Environment will be required.","Department of Environment"],[1,"543","3","National Biosafety Framework Implementation Project","a development project on implementation of the National Biosafety Framework (NBF) has been taken to enhance the capacity on biosafety at various levels",""],[1,"543","3","Biosafety Public Awareness Support","supporting efforts to ensure public awareness on biosafety",""],[1,"543","4","National Oil and Chemical Spill Contingency Plan","National Oil and Chemical Spill Contingency Plan (NOSCOP) is being formulated both in Bangla and in English to combat water pollution both in the inland water and in the coastal and marine water.",""]],"272":[[1,"546","3","National Action Programme for Combating Desertification, Land Degradation and Drought","Bangladesh National Action Program (NAP) for combating Desertification, Land Degradation and Drought (DLDD), 2015-2024 has been formulated to support and enhances the implementation of UNCCD strategy 2008-2018.",""],[1,"546","5","Land Degradation Reduction and Sustainable Land Management Projects","DoE is implementing a number of projects to reduce land degradation and to mainstream sustainable Land Management (SLM) best practices.",""],[1,"552","5","Groundwater Valuation and Water Pricing Reform","8th five-year plan will focus on the valuation (water pricing and water auditing) of the water to limit its unsustainable use.",""],[1,"558","6","Pricing Policy Reform for Water, Sanitation and Solid Waste Services","Consequently, under the 8FYP, the Government will develop appropriate pricing policies to encourage private piped water supply, hygienic and environmentally safe household sanitation and sound management of solid waste.",""],[1,"559","2","Private Financing for Environmental Services","There are three main instruments for boosting private financing for the environment.",""],[1,"561","3","Raised-Platform Drinking Water and Sanitation Infrastructure","Drinking water and sanitation infrastructure need to be constructed on raised platforms.",""],[1,"561","3","Community Water Desalination and Rainwater Harvesting Solutions","For community water supply, constructing desalination plants and rainwater harvesting systems will be considered as feasible solutions.",""],[1,"561","3","Small-Scale Water Treatment Technologies","For smaller scale use, tube wells with appropriate treatment units for arsenic and iron, and pond sand filters to treat water from pond surface will be used as recommended technologies.",""],[1,"561","4","Raised Platform WASH and Housing Infrastructure","housing and WASH structures will be constructed on raised platforms.",""],[1,"561","4","Rainwater Harvesting for Char Areas","Appropriate technologies including rainwater harvesting and community level arsenic/iron removal units for groundwater will be employed.",""],[1,"561","4","Community-Level Arsenic and Iron Removal Units","Appropriate technologies including rainwater harvesting and community level arsenic/iron removal units for groundwater will be employed.",""],[1,"561","5","Rainwater Harvesting Systems for Hill Tracts Drinking Water","To meet drinking water needs, individual or community rainwater harvesting systems with adequate storage will be developed to mitigate the problems.",""],[1,"561","6","Community Water Points and Sanitation Blocks for Urban Slums","community water points and sanitation blocks to be maintained by community- based organizations will be employed as appropriate solutions.",""],[1,"570","6","Water Quality Improvement Measures","under the 8FYP, the Government will implement effective measures to improve the state of water quality in Bangladesh.",""],[1,"570","7","Routine Tube Well Water Quality Monitoring and Remedial Action","Increased monitoring of the quality of water from tube wells in arsenic -prone areas on a routine basis and the implementation of remedial actions.",""],[1,"570","8","Basin-Wide Pollution Source Management","Basin-wide management to check all sources of pollution.",""],[1,"571","1","Surface Water Resource Protection and River Cleaning in Greater Dhaka","Increased protection of the resource base of surface water in greater Dhaka (Dhaka, Tongi, Gazipur, and Narayangonj) by taking appropriate actions for cleaning the rivers, especially: Buriganga, Balu, Turag and Sitalakhya.",""],[1,"571","2","Public Water Body Protection and Recovery","Protection and recovery of public water bodies from encroachment.",""],[1,"571","3","Rainwater Harvesting Options Exploration","Exploration of options for harvesting rainwater.",""],[1,"571","7","Managed Aquifer Recharge Strategy","Developing strategy for managed aquifer recharge and introducing natural and artificial aquifer recharge systems using rainwater harvesting for groundwater recharge.",""],[1,"571","9","Reduction of Harmful Agricultural Chemicals","Reduction of the use of harmful chemicals in agriculture",""],[1,"571","9","Water Filtration and Cleaning System Expansion","increase in the distribution of proper filtration and cleaning systems, either on a large scale or household-based, where water is already contaminated, to improve the access to clean water",""],[1,"597","1","Groundwater Monitoring and Surface Water Management","groundwater monitoring and improved management of surface water is urgently needed.",""]],"273":[[1,"560","2","Expansion of Local Government Institutions in Environmental Management","During the 8FYP, the Government will prioritize the implementation of the beneficiary pays principle by increasing the role of Local Government Institutions (LGI) in environmental management.","Ministry of Local Government, Rural Development and Cooperatives"],[1,"560","2","Establishment of Divisional City Water Supply and Sewerage Authorities","First, the Government will establish WASAs in all 7 Divisional cities by 2025.",""],[1,"560","2","Urban LGI Financial Accounting and Reporting Standards","Second, it will introduce adequate financial accounting and reporting standards that allow a good estimate of the unit cost of the services provided - including capital costs.",""],[1,"560","2","Computerized Management Information System for Urban LGIs","Third, a computerized MIS system will be developed for each urban LGI that provides basic information on the number of customers, amount of water produced and supplied number of hours of water available, the age and quality of water and sanitation infrastructure, amount of revenues collected, missing water in terms of revenues, etc.",""],[1,"560","2","Capacity Strengthening for Local Government Oversight","Fourth, the capabilities of the Ministry of Local Government, Rural Development and Cooperatives that provides oversight to LGIs will be strengthened to provide better guidance, supervision and monitoring of LGIs.","Ministry of Local Government, Rural Development and Cooperatives"],[1,"560","3","Establishment of the Water and Sanitation Regulatory Agency","During the 8FYP, the Government will support the establishment of the Water and Sanitation Regulatory Agency (WASRA) that will be charged with regulating the public and private utilities engaged with supply water and sanitation services and setting prices.",""],[1,"561","2","Environmental Management Decentralization and Coordination Mechanism","To facilitate implementation, a formal coordinating mechanism between the national and local government environmental agencies will be established.",""],[1,"561","2","Citizen Participation in Local Environmental Management","The LGIs will have to be participatory in their approach and adopt proper mechanisms for allowing citizens' participation in all local issues including environmental management.",""],[1,"561","2","Local Government Oversight of Environmental Management","A policy initiative will be formally taken to engage local government authorities down to the Upazila level to involve them in the oversight of environmental management, linking them to development activities.",""],[1,"595","5","WASH Guideline for Community Clinics","GoB has developed a WASH Guideline for Community Clinics in 2019 to ensure better operation and maintenance.",""],[1,"595","5","WASH Strategy for Healthcare Facilities","The Directorate General of Health Services (DGHS) is also preparing a WASH Strategy for healthcare facilities.","Directorate General of Health Services (DGHS)"]],"274":[[1,"569","6","Local Government Climate Change Adaptation Capacity Enhancement","A key mechanism for the Government to enhance the national capacity to improve the measures for adaption to climate change is through an increased understanding of how climate change is likely to affect the livelihood of local communities within the local government administration.",""],[1,"570","1","Partnerships with NGOs and Civil Society for Climate Adaptation","Measures for adaptation to climate change require community wide cooperation, which emerge from partnerships with different stakeholders such as NGOs and relevant actors from the civil society.",""],[1,"570","2","Gender-Inclusive Climate Change Response Framework","the Government will take measures to increase women's knowledge of environmental management and conservation, and investments will be made in education, capacity building training, technology transfer, and environmental projects focusing on women.",""],[1,"570","3","Climate Migration Urban Integration and Housing Support","under the 8FYP, the Government will remain committed to design cities that make them more accommodative by installing efficient systems for facilitating migrant integration into the city, adequate housing for new populations, and job opportunities for those who are looking to work.",""],[1,"570","3","Urban Planning Coordination for Climate Migrants","The Government will closely work with the urban planners to ensure that the needs of the community are being met and that all who seek to migrate from the regions vulnerable to the impacts of climate change are able to do so.",""],[1,"570","4","Gender-Transformative Climate Action in Coastal Districts","The government has undertaken a gender transformative climate action in coastal district to support 700 thousand coastal populations with more climate resilient drinking water, livelihoods and early warning system.",""],[1,"570","4","Review and Update of the Climate Change and Gender Action Plan","Recently an initiative has been taken to review and update the Climate Change and Gender Action Plan under MoEFCC.","MoEFCC"],[1,"570","5","Climate Finance Governance Capacity Enhancement","The capacity and role of parliament, IMED, and OAG are will be enhanced in improving governance mechanism for climate finance.",""],[1,"570","5","Climate Budget Reporting Integration into MP Budget Tracking System","Climate budget report can be also mainstreamed into MP budget tracking system to those areas, which are climate hotspots.",""]],"275":[[1,"619","10","Energy-Efficient Street and Community Lighting","Use energy efficient and low maintenance street and community lighting systems",""],[1,"621","9","Vehicle Taxation and Public Transport Incentive Policy","Controlling car population by introducing appropriate taxation mechanism and incentivizing public transport user.",""],[1,"621","10","Vehicle Emissions Control through Maintenance and Fuel Standards","Controlling emission by enforcing maintenance standard, fuel standard etc.",""],[1,"622","1","Fiscal Incentives for Hybrid and Electric Vehicles","The Government will provide fiscal incentives for hybrid technologies, electric vehicles and imposing strict penalties for the violation of environmental codes by polluters in the transportation sector.",""]],"276":[[1,"627","31","Inter-Ministerial Infrastructure Construction, Repair, and Maintenance","Construct, repair and maintain infrastructures for various departments under different ministries",""],[1,"627","32","Government Building and Infrastructure Design Preparation","Prepare architecture for new buildings and infrastructure for ministries/divisions/departments",""]],"277":[[1,"626","6","Municipal-Community Partnership for Local Service Improvement","Develop Municipal-Community Partnership (MCP) to improve, basic utilities, social services and neighbourhood environment.",""],[1,"628","16","Small-Scale Water Resource Infrastructure Development and Management","Develop, maintain and manage small-scale water resource infrastructures within the Timeline determined by the government",""],[1,"629","15","Birth and Death Information Collection and Management System","Collection and management of information about birth and death",""],[1,"629","22","Urban Graveyard and Lake Development Programme","Construction of graveyards and development of lakes in city areas",""],[1,"629","22","Urban Wholesale and Retail Market Construction Programme","Construction of wholesale and retail markets in city areas",""]],"278":[[1,"624","13","Environmental Improvement and Green Building Initiatives","Introducing and promoting different environmental improvement initiatives and green initiatives e.g. green building, energy efficient building, zero emission building, green city, etc.",""],[1,"625","10","Integrated Environmentally Sound Urban Planning and Management","Prepare and implement integrated, environmentally-sound urban planning and management incorporating environmental and disaster related information and reflecting environmental and disaster management policies and standards.",""],[1,"627","11","Multi-storied Car Parking and Multipurpose Complexes","Construct multi-storied car parking and multipurpose complexes",""],[1,"627","12","Building Identification and Removal of Unapproved and Vulnerable Buildings","Identify, preserve and remove unapproved and vulnerable buildings",""]],"279":[[1,"625","5","Urban Climate Change Adaptation and Disaster Risk Reduction Measures","Keeping in view the above-mentioned problems, the government will take following steps during the 8FYP period:",""],[1,"625","6","Strengthening of City Disaster Management Committees","Strengthen City Disaster Management Committee (CDMC) involving other stakeholders such as the private sector, research institutes, national agencies and utility companies.",""],[1,"625","7","Monitoring and Evaluation Strengthening for Compliance and Enforcement","Strengthen monitoring and evaluation of the existing mechanisms for compliance and enforcement of laws, regulations etc. through conducting regular capacity building workshops of city personnel.",""],[1,"625","7","Climate Change and Disaster Risk Reduction Legal Sensitization","Sensitize legislations, regulations and codes in relation to Climate Change (CC) and Disaster Risk Reduction (DRR).",""],[1,"625","8","Disaster and Environmental Management Coordination Mechanism","Promote close coordination and cooperation among national disaster management and environmental management agencies (i.e. Department of Environment (DoE), department of Disaster Management (DoDM)) urban local bodies (City Corporations and Paurashavas), non- governmental and private sector organizations;","Department of Environment (DoE) | department of Disaster Management (DoDM)"],[1,"625","9","Integration of City Climate Change and Disaster Risk Reduction Policies into National Preparedness and Response System","Integrate city CC-DRR policies and plans in national preparedness and response system.",""],[1,"625","9","Partnerships for Technical Assistance and Techno-Environmental Projects","Strengthen partnerships with relevant organizations for technical assistance, researches and techno- environment projects.",""],[1,"626","1","Cross-Sector Climate Change and Disaster Risk Reduction Integration Workshops","Integrate CC-DRR in all key sectors through multi-stakeholder and participatory workshops.",""],[1,"626","2","Disaster Risk Information System for Urban Planning","Establishment of a comprehensive information system that identifies and assesses the risks involved in disaster-prone areas and integrate it into urban planning and design.",""],[1,"626","3","Community-Based Disaster Preparedness and Response Planning","Preparing community-based disaster preparedness and response plans putting emphasis on early warning system that reaches everyone, measures to protect houses, identification of safe evacuation sites and provisions to help those less able to move quickly.",""],[1,"626","4","Disaster Preparedness and Response Capacity Enhancement","Enhance disaster preparedness and response capabilities through the contributions of the volunteers, local community groups and non-governmental organizations.",""],[1,"626","5","Disaster Preparedness and Response Coordination Mechanism","Facilitate the operation of the disaster preparedness and response mechanisms in a much more coordinated but flexible manner through partnership arrangements with the private sector and in close coordination with all community groups",""]],"280":[[1,"640","3","Health Sector-Wide Approach","Bangladesh has been following a Sector-Wide Approach (SWAp) in the HPN sector since 1998.",""],[1,"640","3","Strengthening Health Sector Coordination and Functional Relationships","the MoHFW has been continuously trying to strengthen its coordination and functional relationship with other stakeholders/Ministries/Agencies involved in providing health services.","MoHFW"],[1,"640","4","Fourth Health, Population and Nutrition Sector Program","The Fourth Health, Population and Nutrition and Sector Program (4th HPNSP) covering the period from January 2017 to June 2022 has taken a holistic approach, which is unique in terms of its focus on (a) strengthening MoHFW's governance and stewardship roles in the HPN sector; (b) strengthening systems/ institutions for efficient service delivery; and (c) expanding HPN services and emphasizing service quality both in public and private sectors.","MoHFW"],[1,"641","1","Health Sector SWAp Continuation","As the Government continued the SWAp in the 7th Five Year Plan period, the same modality will be followed during the 8th Five Year Plan for the HPN sector development.",""],[1,"641","2","Health System Governance and Human Resources Strengthening","The second component focuses on strengthening health systems such as governance and human resources.",""],[1,"642","1","Results-Based Monitoring and Evaluation Mechanism for the HPN Sector","monitoring and evaluation mechanism of the HPN sector has been developed based on results.",""],[1,"642","16","SDG Health Action Plan Implementation","MoHFW has been pursuing to achieve the SDG targets through implementation of an approved SDG Action Plan.","MoHFW"],[1,"642","16","Divisional SDG Stakeholder Workshops","MoHFW conducted Divisional level workshops focusing on SDG related activities for enhancing knowledge and understanding of the stakeholders with key concepts and principles along with targets and indicators of the health-related SDGs, matching those with field level program activities.","MoHFW"],[1,"644","2","Fourth Health, Population and Nutrition Sector Programme","The Government approved the 4th Health, Population and Nutrition Sector Programme (4th HPNSP) in March 2017 for implementation during January 2017 - June 2022 with an estimated cost of USD 14.7 billion, 84% of which will be financed from Government's own resources.",""],[1,"644","3","Health Service Expansion and Health System Strengthening under the 4th HPNSP","The 4th HPNSP has been continuing to expand services and improve health systems through implementation of the strategies like capacity building, stronger governance for better quality services; greater functional coordination of services at the field level; partnerships with the private sector and the community; improvement in quality of care; comprehensive health workforce strategy and action plan; increased investment in prevention and primary care of public health; the rising burden of NCDs through cross-sector interventions on public health awareness and healthy lifestyles and healthy environment; tackling established and new communicable diseases; strengthening surveillance, data quality and information systems; and increasing investment in health.",""],[1,"644","4","Results-Based Financing for the 4th HPNSP","The financing of the 4th HPNSP by the World Bank (WB) is under a new results-based financing modality known as Investment Project Financing (IPF) with Disbursement- Linked Indicators (DLIs).",""],[1,"644","4","Disbursement-Linked Results Verification Mechanism","Disbursement of US$ 588.45 million by the WB and other DPs is to be made upon annual achievement of specifically defined Disbursement-Linked Results (DLRs) with targets covering a total of 16 DLIs.",""],[1,"644","4","Independent Verification Agency Arrangement","The Implementation Monitoring and Evaluation Division (IMED) of the Government has been engaged as the Independent Verification Agency (IVA) for verification of the DLRs.","Implementation Monitoring and Evaluation Division (IMED)"],[1,"645","1","DLI Monitoring and Verification Mechanism","The MoHFW formed a DLI Monitoring Committee in order to monitor progress towards achievement of DLIs, support the line directors (LDs) in implementation and produce reports to be submitted for verification by the IMED.","MoHFW | IMED"],[1,"653","7","Health, Population and Nutrition System Strengthening","Continue to strengthen HPN system that may require reorganizing various systems and institutions based on needs of the day.",""],[1,"653","11","Life-Cycle Health Sector Investment for Human Capital Development","Promote development of human capital through investment in health sector throughout the life cycle.",""],[1,"654","1","Universal Health Coverage Improvement Initiative","MoHFW has been pursuing focused improvements in increasing access to quality health services and improving equity along with financial protection in order to achieve universal health coverage (UHC) by 2030.","MoHFW"],[1,"654","9","Governance, Equity, and Inclusiveness Policy Reform","Establishment of laws, rules and formulation of new policies, updating existing policies, etc. for improved governance, equity and inclusiveness.",""],[1,"654","10","Health System Strengthening and Service Efficiency Reform","The 8FYP will need to lay emphasis on the continuation of efforts to strengthen core systems to support overall improvement in service efficiency, e.g., the reorganization of the financial management, restructuring of CMSD as the major procurement unit and other agencies/institutes.",""],[1,"654","10","Health Sector Program Financing and Technical Support","The health sector Program under the 8FYP period will therefore need adequate financial and technical support to implement, monitor and manage the multifarious challenges posed by the ambitious health goals within the dynamic development process of Bangladesh.",""]],"281":[[1,"643","3","NCD Prevention Awareness Programmes","Awareness programmes on helpful behavioral patterns, changing dietary habits, lifestyle change, etc. are being implemented for preventing NCDs",""],[1,"643","3","NCD Facility Readiness and Doctor Training","facility readiness including training of doctors are going on for better treatment of NCD patients",""],[1,"643","4","Anti-Tobacco Programme","HSD is implementing anti-tobacco program based on WHO- FCTC and Tobacco Control Law of Bangladesh.",""],[1,"643","4","Tobacco Use Awareness-Raising Activities","Awareness raising activities against tobacco use are being implemented continuously.",""],[1,"657","14","Childhood Injury Prevention Strategy","Developing and implementing strategies to prevent childhood injuries including drowning, accidental poisoning and other injuries.",""],[1,"659","2","Integrated Non-Communicable Disease Prevention, Control, and Treatment Services","The government, in partnership with local government bodies and the private sector, will create greater awareness with the assistance of Bureau of Health Education and provide services for the control of unhealthy diet and lifestyle related major NCDs such as cardio-vascular diseases, cancer and diabetes.",""],[1,"659","2","Strengthening and Expansion of NCD Preventive and Curative Measures","Existing preventive and curative measures for the NCDs will be further strengthened and expanded to increase access through providing effective number of personnel, training, logistics and funding.",""],[1,"659","2","Establishment of NCD Corners in UHFWCs","Moreover, NCD corners will be established in each UHFWC in phases during the 8FYP period.",""],[1,"659","4","Mental Health Awareness Partnerships","partnerships with the media and NGOs will be developed to raise public awareness about appropriate attitude and behavior towards mental patients.",""],[1,"659","4","Mental Health and Substance Abuse Training for Frontline Workers","Public sector, NGO/ CBO workers and school and religious teachers, will be trained to identify and counsel substance abuse and mental and emotional cases, provide and follow up simple treatment as feasible, life skill training and refer serious cases to public facility, where treatment facilities will also be expanded.",""]],"282":[[1,"644","1","Modern Family Planning Coverage Expansion","MEFWD is working hard to increase to 100% within 2030.","MEFWD"],[1,"644","1","Adolescent Birth Rate Reduction Initiative","MEFWD also has taken huge activities to reduce it to 50 per 1000 adolescents within 2030.","MEFWD"],[1,"644","1","SDG-Related Stakeholder Workshop Programme","MEFWD conducted divisional level workshops focusing on SDG related activities for enhancing knowledge and understanding of the stakeholders with key concepts and principles along with targets and indicators of the health related SDGs, matching those with field level program activities.","MEFWD"],[1,"649","7","Uniform Family Planning Services in City Corporations","Bringing in uniformity in FP services in the city corporation areas.",""],[1,"649","18","Urban Family Planning Outreach for Slum Areas","To address slum & urban areas for family planning activities and to reduce dropout rate & unmet need for family planning",""],[1,"658","3","Reproductive and Adolescent Health Improvement Activities","Based on these strategies, the reproductive and adolescent health improvement related activities will include:",""],[1,"658","4","Reproductive Health and HIV/AIDS Awareness Activities","Improving knowledge of women, men and particularly the adolescents, on reproductive health (RTI/ STI, abortion, infertility, etc.) including HIV/AIDS, relevant legal and gender equity issues through the activities of DGHS, DGFP, MoWCA, MoY&S, MoE and NGOs.","DGHS | DGFP | MoWCA | MoY&S | MoE"],[1,"658","5","Reproductive and Adolescent-Friendly Health Services Expansion","Increasing access to reproductive and adolescent friendly health services through the frontline health personnel and appropriate NGO workers at individual level, school-based programmes, CCs, strong social/community mobilization and opening up adolescent corners.",""],[1,"658","6","Adolescent Reproductive Health Behavior Change Initiative","Creating positive change in the behavior and attitude of the protectors of adolescents (parents, guardians, teachers, religious leaders, Peers, etc.) towards adolescent RH issues.",""]],"283":[[1,"645","3","Pilot Social Health Protection Scheme","HSD is implementing a pilot social health protection scheme in three upazilas known as \"Shasthyo Shuroksha Karmasuchi (SSK) under which free hospital services are being provided to the poor- below poverty level (BPL) card holders, which are contributing to reducing inequity in health.",""],[1,"645","3","Maternal Health Voucher Scheme","The Maternal Health Voucher Scheme (MHVS) in operation in 55 upazilas is another health protection scheme, the beneficiaries of which are poor and vulnerable pregnant women.",""],[1,"652","1","Universal Health Coverage Strengthening and Health Insurance Scheme Development","It incorporates appropriate strategies and activities for focused improvements in health service delivery for increasing access to, and quality of care and improving equity along with financial protection in order to meaningfully realize the objectives of universal health coverage (UHC) by 2030.",""],[1,"654","7","Expansion of Health Protection Schemes","Expansion of health protection schemes (e.g., SSK, MHVS) for wider coverage of the poor.",""],[1,"655","4","Social Health Protection Scheme Expansion","The social health protection scheme in the name of \"Shasthyo Shuroksha Karmasuchi (SSK) is providing free hospital services to the poor and vulnerable people.",""],[1,"655","4","Maternal Health Voucher Scheme Expansion","The Maternal Health Voucher Scheme (MHVS), in operation in 55 upazilas, is another health protection scheme for ensuring safe delivery of poor pregnant mothers.",""],[1,"655","4","Health Insurance Scheme Exploration","Besides, new areas of health protection will be explored including taking up health insurance schemes for different income groups.",""]],"284":[[1,"645","5","Expansion of Service Coverage in Hard-to-Reach Areas","Gradual expansion of service coverage in the hard-to-reach (HTR) areas ... will be continued during the 8FYP as well.",""],[1,"645","5","Ethnic Minority Health Plan Implementation","effective implementation of ethnic minority health plan ... activities programmed under the 4th HPNSP for addressing inequity issues, will be continued during the 8FYP as well.",""],[1,"645","5","Health Workforce Management for Equity","health workforce management ... activities programmed under the 4th HPNSP for addressing inequity issues, will be continued during the 8FYP as well.",""],[1,"653","3","Innovative Service Delivery Approaches for Hard-to-Reach Areas","Exploring various innovative approaches (e.g., purchasing service to offset inadequate service provision to disadvantaged groups) for improving service delivery particularly for hard-to-reach areas.",""],[1,"653","10","Gender Equality Mainstreaming in Operational Plans","Incorporating activities in relevant OPs on women's right and voice and conducting orientation training, workshops, focus group discussions, etc. for ensuring gender equality.",""],[1,"653","12","Targeted Health Support for Vulnerable Populations","Provide targeted health support to the most socially and economically disadvantaged and vulnerable populations, including those affected by climate change and natural disasters; and help to strengthen their resilience to social, economic and environmental shocks.",""],[1,"653","15","Older Persons Support Technology and Care Infrastructure Development","Develop appropriate technologies, care services and infrastructure to accommodate the needs of older persons, commensurate to the stage of economic development and societal norms, structures, etc.",""],[1,"655","3","District-Specific Health Service Development in the Chittagong Hill Tracts","Assistance will be provided in the Hill District Councils (HDCs) in the Chittagong Hill Tracts (CHT) to develop district-specific health service in co-operation with MoCHTA and with interested DPs.","MoCHTA"],[1,"655","3","Improved Health Services for Geriatric and Ethnic Minority Populations","Steps will be taken for providing improved health services to the geriatric populations, the ethnic minorities and the other categories.",""],[1,"655","3","Disability and Mental Health Service Expansion","Disability issues (autism, mental health, etc.) will also be properly addressed in collaboration with various actors (public, private, NGOs) through preventive and curative services including expansion of services to cater the need of those who are physically or mentally challenged with a view to bringing in more people under universal coverage and reducing individual out-of-pocket expenditure (OOPE).",""]],"285":[[1,"659","3","Integration of Eye Care Activities into Primary Health Care","To facilitate prevention, case identification, referral, management, treatment and rehabilitation, the relevant activities need to be integrated with primary health care (PHC) especially through the services of the community clinics.",""],[1,"659","3","School Sight Testing in Primary Schools","School Sight testing will be included in primary schools",""],[1,"659","3","Vitamin A Administration Programme","the past emphasis on successful vitamin A administration will be continued",""],[1,"659","3","Postnatal Vitamin A Administration through Community Clinics","More attention will be given to postnatal vitamin A administration through CC staff, in collaboration with school teachers and senior students as relevant.",""],[1,"659","3","National Eye Care Plan Upgrade and Implementation","The National Eye Care Plan will be upgraded and implemented in the 8FYP.",""]],"286":[[1,"634","3","Private Sector Participation in Infrastructure Financing","There is now an explicit role of private sector participation in infrastructure financing in Government investment policy and its poverty reduction strategy.",""],[1,"634","3","Government Support for Urban Infrastructure Projects","A large part of the infrastructure projects for urban development would still require government interventions.",""],[1,"634","3","Public Investment in Low-Return Urban Infrastructure","These include in particular those which have high social return but less attractive to private investments.",""],[1,"634","8","Public-Private Partnership Mechanisms for Private Infrastructure Investment","Government has now formulated mechanisms and incentives for greater participation of private infrastructure projects through the public private partnership modality.",""],[1,"634","8","Guidelines for Private Sector Investment in Infrastructure","Additionally, Government has recently established clear guidelines on private sector investment in infrastructure projects.",""],[1,"635","1","Supportive Legal Framework for Private Sector Participation in Urban Development","For involving private sector in urban development and management activities supportive legal framework should be developed and institutional setting should be ensured.",""],[1,"635","4","PPP Project Capacity Building","there needs to be capacity building to undertake PPP projects.",""]],"287":[[1,"660","3","Oral Health Mass Education and Awareness Campaign","Preventive approach through mass education and raising awareness will be prioritized.",""],[1,"660","3","Oral Hygiene Behaviour Change and Restriction Measures","Adoption of proper cleaning procedure of the oral cavity and bringing strict restrictions in bad habits (such as smoking, chewing paan, eating excessive sugary food) can reduce most of the common and complicated oral diseases.",""],[1,"660","3","School-Based Oral Health Education Integration","Oral health awareness should start early in life and this best done both through parent counselling and care and through integration in the school curriculum.",""],[1,"660","3","Mass Media Oral Health Public Campaigns","Mass media public campaigns are also useful tool for improving public knowledge and awareness.",""]],"288":[[1,"660","4","Road Safety Policy and Regulation Dialogue","Dialogue with the Ministry of Road Transport and Bridgesfor safety policies and regulation, enhance skills of DGHS service providers to handle injury patients, build up awareness of the people on pedestrian safety measures will be emphasized by HSD during 8FYP.","Ministry of Road Transport and Bridges | DGHS | HSD"],[1,"660","4","Injury Patient Care Skills Enhancement","Dialogue with the Ministry of Road Transport and Bridgesfor safety policies and regulation, enhance skills of DGHS service providers to handle injury patients, build up awareness of the people on pedestrian safety measures will be emphasized by HSD during 8FYP.","DGHS | HSD"],[1,"660","4","Pedestrian Safety Awareness Campaign","Dialogue with the Ministry of Road Transport and Bridgesfor safety policies and regulation, enhance skills of DGHS service providers to handle injury patients, build up awareness of the people on pedestrian safety measures will be emphasized by HSD during 8FYP.","HSD"],[1,"660","4","Walkway Clearance Community Mobilization","Community mobilization will be done in collaboration with urban NGOs and city corporation authorities to keep walkway free of any hindrance which discourage people from using walkways.",""]],"289":[[1,"660","5","Expansion and Strengthening of One Stop Crisis Centers","HSD will carry out expansion and strengthening of the one stop crisis centers to serve the affected women.","Ministry of Women and Children Affairs (MoWCA) | Ministry of Social Welfare (MoSW)"],[1,"660","5","Sensitization of Health Care Providers on Violence Against Women Survivors","Besides, all health care providers will be sensitized through relevant programmes to pay special attention and prioritize women violence survivors in all public health facilities.",""],[1,"679","8","Comprehensive Study and Policy Framework on Gender-Based Violence","Undertake a comprehensive study on estimating the economic cost of Gender based Violence (GBV) focusing on direct, indirect and induced economic costs for both public and private sectors.",""]],"290":[[1,"662","2","Integrated Disease Surveillance Programme","To this end, an integrated disease surveillance programme will be developed during the 8FYP period to provide timely, complete, regular and high-quality information; early detect and predict epidemics (early warning systems); assess interventions during epidemics; and monitor intervention programmes efficiently.",""],[1,"662","2","IEDCR Strengthening for Epidemiological Surveillance","During 8FYP, IEDCR will be strengthened to turn it into an apex institute for epidemiological surveillance in the country for carrying out epidemiological surveillance of communicable and non-communicable diseases with laboratory support.",""],[1,"662","2","Central Surveillance Unit Establishment","A Central Surveillance Unit will be established for strengthening/maintaining decentralized laboratory-based IT and responding to outbreaks in early rising phase through trained Rapid Response Team (RRTs).",""],[1,"662","2","National Referral Laboratory Network","A country- based referral laboratory network will be established by utilizing the existing functional labs in the identified medical colleges and other major centers in the country and linking them with adjoining districts and upazillas for providing diagnostic services for epidemic prone diseases during outbreaks.",""],[1,"662","2","National NCD Surveillance Coordination","DGHS will coordinate all activities currently carried out by relevant institutes/ agencies to establish an effective NCD surveillance system.","DGHS"],[1,"662","2","Hospital Capacity Strengthening for Disease Surveillance","Capacity of all hospitals will be strengthened to assist in disease surveillance and diagnosis.",""],[1,"662","2","Community Disease Recognition Training","Teachers of primary schools, NGO workers and community volunteers will be trained to identify the clinical features of the most common endemic diseases.",""],[1,"662","2","Private Provider Surveillance Partnership","Partnering with private health care providers for better surveillance, reporting, referral and case management will be established.",""],[1,"662","2","District and Upazila Disease Mapping","Mapping of all major diseases, on the basis of their incidence and prevalence, will be constructed for each district and upazila.",""],[1,"664","1","National Clinical and Antibiotic Use Guidelines","During the 8FYP period, national clinical guidelines as well as antibiotic use guidelines will be prepared and made available to the health care professionals.",""],[1,"664","1","Public Awareness Campaign on Rational Drug Use","Mass awareness will be created about rational use of drugs and the adverse effect of irrational use of antibiotics.",""]],"291":[[1,"667","3","Unified Platform for Postgraduate Medical Education","Bringing in all post-graduate degrees of medical education under one platform and coordinate the activities for quality education.",""],[1,"667","4","Medical Accreditation Council Establishment","Establishment of medical accreditation council.",""],[1,"667","5","Examination Process Modernization and Curriculum Update","Modernization of examination process and inclusion of new/specialized subjects in the medical/dental/nursing/paramedical education curricula in accordance with international standards.",""],[1,"667","5","Super-Specialty Medical Education Expansion","Expansion of super-specialty medical education will be promoted.",""],[1,"667","6","Nursing and Paramedical Education Board Establishment","Establishment of nursing/paramedical education board.",""],[1,"667","9","Medical University and District Medical College Expansion","Implementation of Government's commitment for establishing medical university at every Division for promoting post-graduate medical education and medical college at each district of the country.",""],[1,"667","11","Medical and Nursing Education Research Strengthening","Strengthening medical and nursing education research activities for improving quality in teaching and services.",""],[1,"667","12","Medical, Nursing, and Paramedical Education and Services Policy Reform","Establishment of laws, rules, procedures, and formulation of new policies, updating existing policies, etc. for promoting quality medical, nursing and paramedical education and services.",""],[1,"667","13","Physical Facilities Establishment, Upgradation, and Maintenance","Establishment of new physical facilities & upgradation of existing ones and repair and maintenance of the facilities.",""],[1,"667","14","Private Sector Medical and Nursing Education Quality Assurance","Ensure the standard of medical and nursing education in private sector.",""],[1,"667","15","Basic Subject Specialization in Medical Science","Encourage specialization of basic subject in medical science.",""],[1,"667","18","Nursing Education Accreditation Guidelines","Improve and control the standard of nursing education through the Accreditation Guidelines.",""],[1,"667","22","Nursing Teachers' Training College Establishment","Establishment of a Nursing Teachers' Training College for producing quality nurses.",""],[1,"668","7","NIPORT Head Office Building Construction and Facility Renovation","Construct new multipurpose (Office/Academic/Hostel) building for NIPORT Head Office and renovate existing facilities with modern equipment.",""]],"292":[[1,"669","6","Hand-Washing and Hygiene Promotion","Contribute to increased levels of hand-washing and hygiene",""],[1,"669","6","Safe Drinking Water Provision","Ensure availability of safe drinking water",""],[1,"669","6","Sanitary Facilities Expansion","Improve availability of sanitary facilities in different settings",""],[1,"669","6","Water Access for Women in Agriculture and Fishing","Prioritise the availability of water to women for agriculture and fishing",""],[1,"670","8","Integrated Water Resource Management and Shock Mitigation","Pro-poor, efficient and integrated management of water resources including control for negative impacts, such as water-borne diseases · Risk mitigation and management of water-related shocks (e.g. droughts, floods, water insecurity) through adequate infrastructure, storage and flood control, supporting adaptation to the effects of climate change",""]],"293":[[1,"669","11","Diversified Food Production Improvement","Improve production of diversified food (source of animal protein)",""],[1,"669","11","Women’s Access to Agriculture Extension Services","Empower women to access agriculture extension services, resources",""],[1,"669","11","Nutrition Integration in Agriculture Extension Training","Incorporate basic nutrition into agriculture extension training and tasks",""],[1,"669","11","Nutrition-Sensitive Agriculture Extension and Input Supply System","Build agriculture extension and agriculture input supply system to ensure nutrition is considered in planning and implementation",""],[1,"670","5","Fortified Staples Availability Expansion","Increase availability of fortified staples e.g. salt and oil",""]],"294":[[1,"670","3","Women’s Empowerment for Household Decision-Making","Emphasis on empowerment of women to make decisions about their own and their children's wellbeing",""],[1,"670","3","Six-Month Fully Paid Maternity Leave Implementation","Ensure 6-month fully paid maternity leave is implemented in all sectors",""],[1,"670","5","Responsible Advertising and Marketing Standards for Children","Adhere to high standards in advertising/marketing, focus on children",""]],"295":[[1,"679","9","Real Exchange Rate and Infrastructure Cost Reduction for RMG Growth","Important policies include spurring the growth of RMG by reversing the sharp appreciation of the real exchange rate and reducing the cost and improving the quality of infrastructure and trade logistic services;",""],[1,"679","9","Trade Protection Reduction and Export Diversification Policy","sharply lowering trade protection to reduce the anti- export bias of trade policies and promote export diversification;",""],[1,"679","9","CMSME Credit Access and Support Measures","promote the growth of a dynamic cottage, micro, small and medium enterprises (CMSMEs) sector through improved access to institutional credit and other supportive measures.",""]],"296":[[1,"681","9","Increase Health Investment to 2 Percent of GDP","Bangladesh must at least investt 2 per cent of GDP on Health from existing level of less than 1 per cent of GDP within the 8FYP period.",""],[1,"681","9","Increase Social Protection Investment to 2 Percent of GDP","investment in Social protection should be increased to 2 per cent of GDP by the end of 8FYP from the current 1.2 per cent of GDP (excluding civil service pensions).",""],[1,"681","9","Expand Child-Focused Social Protection Programmes","A large part of the additional allocation (i.e. 0.8 per cent of GDP) should go to Child focused social protection programmes.",""],[1,"682","5","Increased Health Sector Budget and ADP Allocations","The rapid response to COVID-19 and the need to sharply enhance the health sector capacity of Bangladesh calls for substantial increase in budget and ADP allocations.",""]],"297":[[1,"710","3","Introduction of Pre-VOC and VOC Courses in Secondary Education","Pre-VOC and VOC courses in different trade will be introduced in secondary level education so that students would complete their secondary level education with some vocational skills.",""],[1,"710","4","Early TVET Courses and Apprenticeship Linkage Programme","The first step would be to introduce TVET courses at a very early age, from the primary level.",""],[1,"711","1","Industry-Academia Collaboration Incentive Framework","Fiscal incentives for industries, stipends for students, and recognition for TVET institutions for placing their students in industries will be adopted to overcome this.",""],[1,"711","1","Apprenticeship Incentives for Industry Compliance","To make this law effective, the 8FYP will provide incentives to the industry.",""],[1,"711","1","Local-Level Technical and Vocational Training Expansion","A similar support for the TVET institutions will be provided to help them expand technical and vocational training to the local level.",""],[1,"711","1","Subsidized Youth Skills Training and Employment Counselling","The government will also provide subsidized training program with employment counselling to attract youths in skill training program.",""],[1,"712","2","STEM Subject Retention and Promotion Programme","The 8FYP will encourage larger number of students (and parents) to persist with STEM subjects through scholarships, career counselling and information sharing through mass media.",""],[1,"712","2","STEM Teacher Training and Education Support","greater resources will also be mobilized in training and educating teachers at the STEM fields.",""]],"298":[[1,"714","18","Lifelong Learning Education Reform","The overall approach to education in Bangladesh will be adapted to stimulate the curiosity, creativity, and inquisitiveness of students so that they become lifelong learners - open and able to adapt to new environment and experiences in the workspace - at all levels, including pre-primary, TVET, and the madrasa stream.",""],[1,"715","1","ICT Skills Anticipation and Programme Adaptation","education and training systems of ICT need to better assess and anticipate changing skills needs in order to adapt programmes and initiatives offered and guide students/workers towards choices that lead to good outcomes.",""],[1,"715","2","Digital Bangladesh Initiative ICT Policy and Access to Information Programme","Under the digital Bangladesh Initiative (DBI) of the Government several Acts and policies have been undertaken: The ICT Policy 2009, the 'Strategies Priorities for Digital Bangladesh 2011', and ICT Policy 2015.","Government | Prime Minister's office"],[1,"715","2","ICT Skills Expansion and Digital Infrastructure Support","The 8FYP will build on this progress and place greater emphasis on this sector by resolving the issue of high taxation and allocation of more funds, particularly in the public academic institutions, to fast track the spread of the ICT revolution in all academic institutions.",""],[1,"715","2","Advanced ICT and Professional Skills Development","Furthermore, there will be increased focus on technical and professional skills including ICT specialist skills for workers who can initiate innovation and to support digital infrastructure and the true functioning of the digital eco-system.",""],[1,"715","4","STEM Promotion and Scholarship Support Programme","The 8FYP will seek to sharply increase the focus on STEM through scholarships, job counselling and advocacy using mass media.",""],[1,"715","4","School-Level STEM Awareness Through Parent-Teacher Conferences","Parent-teacher conferences at school level will also be used to create awareness among parents to guide their children towards STEM subjects.",""],[1,"738","5","Digital Centre of Excellence for Online Teaching and Learning","A digital centre of excellence for teaching and learning through online media can be a centre of education in coming days.",""],[1,"738","6","Virtual University Establishment","Steps should be taken to establish a Virtual University.",""],[1,"748","22","Digital Education Policy Alignment and IPR Policy Upgradation","Digital Education Policy [in alignment with 8th Five-Year Plan] Up gradation of Intellectual Property Rights [IPR] Policy to ensure appropriate encryption and to protect the providers of online education",""],[1,"748","24","Digital Literacy Curriculum Guideline Development","Development of digital literacy curriculum guideline for each segment of learners by public and private agencies",""],[1,"748","24","Open Digital Literacy Content Licensing","Making curriculum and content for digital literacy open [creative commons licensing]",""],[1,"749","32","4IR-Adjusted Blended Learning Transformation","Transformation of education to 4IR adjusted blended learning approach for all citizens",""],[1,"752","10","Virtual and Multimedia University Establishment","Establish Virtual University, Multimedia University",""]],"299":[[1,"715","3","Skills for Employment and Investment Program","The Skill for Employment and Investment (SEIP): A major initiative to develop skill is the SEIP program taken by the government and supported by the Asian Development Bank.",""],[1,"715","5","Market-Oriented Curriculum and Training Upgrading","The government can obviously step-in and provide training, up-skilling, and re-skilling facilities that are frequently upgraded",""],[1,"716","2","TVET Curriculum Revision and Modernization","a revision of the TVET curriculum is crucial for this.",""],[1,"716","2","TVET Upskilling, Reskilling, and Digital Infrastructure Development","importance would be given to up- skilling and re-skilling workers and creation inclusive digital infrastructure",""],[1,"716","3","Human Capital Development Strategy","The education, training and skills strategy discussed in this chapter seeks to respond effectively to that need.",""],[1,"716","3","Science, Technology, and ICT Investment Expansion","Additionally, investments in science and technology and ICT services discussed in chapter 12 will play a complementary role in upgrading the skill base of Bangladesh required to move towards HIC status.",""],[1,"716","3","Inter-Ministerial Coordination for Education and Training Delivery","Given limited resources, the 8FYP will focus strongly on good governance, sound program implementation and inter-ministerial coordination of all relevant ministries/ agencies that contribute to the development of education and training.",""],[1,"738","10","Student Soft Skills and Innate Capabilities Enhancement Measures","At the school level, measures should be taken to enhance innate capabilities and soft skills of students.",""],[1,"738","10","Labour Force Soft Skills Training Programme","Moreover, existing labour force should also be given training to enhance innate capabilities, along with soft skills.",""],[1,"738","12","Fourth Industrial Revolution Skills Training for the Labour Force","Both existing and new labour force should be given training in performing those tasks in producing 4IR technology-based features.",""],[1,"739","9","Lifelong Learning and Online Learning Skills Development","Lifelong learning attitude and skill should be developed in both existing labour force and future job seekers.",""],[1,"739","9","Online Resource Learning Skills Development","Developing skill of learning from on- line resources is an example of building lifelong learning skill.",""],[1,"744","2","National Training and Skills Curriculum Revamp Strategy","b) develop national strategy to revamp all training and skill development curricula;","ICT Division"],[1,"749","27","Targeted Skills Development Programs","Targeted skills development programs for balancing domestic and overseas employment, and wage and self-employment",""]],"300":[[1,"741","2","Start-Up and Venture Capital Financing Support","The strategy of attracting increasing foreign VC funds in Bangladesh's start-ups should include packaging start-ups led innovation opportunities and promoting them, supporting R&D and encouraging start-ups to develop intellectual property strategy, and easing the operation of VCs in Bangladesh.",""],[1,"742","4","Digital Credit Score Collaboration for SMEs","c) collaborate with MFIs and mobile operators to offer digital credit score for SMEs to promote 4 times growth;",""],[1,"742","4","Regulatory Sandbox for Financial Innovation","e) develop regulatory sandbox by the Bangladesh Bank to allow pilot testing before approval of a policy from the end of 2020.","Bangladesh Bank"],[1,"744","2","Online Small-Scale Loan Platform for CMSMEs","c) introduce online platform for small-scale loans for the CMSMEs;","ICT Division"],[1,"748","12","CMSME Credit Rating Law and Credit Bureau Database","Enactment of a law for CMSME credit rating system with emphasis on credit bureau database under Bangladesh Bank Order, 1972","Bangladesh Bank"],[1,"749","4","Alternative Credit Rating System for CMSMEs and Vulnerable Citizens","Alternative credit rating system for CMSMEs and vulnerable citizens",""]],"301":[[1,"733","3","4IR Technology Labs and Collaborative Platforms","Establish labs focusing on 4IR technologies and collaborative platforms, especially Public-Private",""],[1,"738","4","Task-Level Occupational Analysis and 4IR Impact Projection","In target industries, task level analysis of occupations should be performed, and projection should be made about the task content transformation based on likely implications of each of the technologies underpinning 4IR.",""],[1,"738","14","Technology Assessment and Forecasting for Skills Planning","Technology assessment and forecasting should be taken into consideration to predict task content production transformation for assessing the up- skilling training need.",""],[1,"739","5","Innovation Forecasting and Task Facilitation","Innovation prediction should be made and facilitation should be provided, consequentially increasing the task supply.",""],[1,"739","5","Skills Development Training for New Tasks","Skill development training should be provided for performing those newly introduced tasks.",""],[1,"739","7","Follow-up Task-Level Investigation for Automation","Exiting studies should be complemented with follow up detailed tasks level investigation spelling out the automation of tasks, change of interface of remaining tasks, introduction of new tasks for adopting automation, and also introduction of new tasks due to addition of product features.",""],[1,"739","10","Fourth Industrial Revolution Monitoring and Response Measures","In order to cope up the threat and leverage opportunities, underlying technologies need to be monitored, implications should be assessed, HR development needs to be determined, innovation opportunities need to be identified, and appropriate interventions must be taken.",""]],"302":[[1,"746","3","Cross-Border Freelancer Payment Resolution","The ICT Division is proposing the following interventions in the immediate short-term: a) address cross border payment issues;","ICT Division"],[1,"746","3","Freelancer Market Analysis Promotion","The ICT Division is proposing the following interventions in the immediate short-term: b) promote global/local market analysis;","ICT Division"],[1,"746","3","Professional Development Programmes for Freelancers","The ICT Division is proposing the following interventions in the immediate short-term: c) launch profession development programmes;","ICT Division"],[1,"746","3","Bangladesh ICT Skills Destination Branding Initiative","The ICT Division is proposing the following interventions in the immediate short-term: d) brand Bangladesh as an ICT skill destination;","ICT Division"]],"303":[[1,"746","4","Emerging Technology R&D Ecosystem Development","The ICT Division proposes the following immediate short-term interventions: a) create an ecosystem for encouraging emerging technology R&D;",""],[1,"746","4","Emerging Technology Start-Up Promotion","b) promote emerging technology start-ups;",""],[1,"746","4","Emerging Technology Solutions Funding Support","c) promote and fund emerging technology solutions;",""],[1,"746","4","Emerging Technology Integration in Education","d) promote emerging technologies in the education sector;",""],[1,"746","4","Implementation of Emerging Technology Policies and Strategies","e) ensure implementation of policies and strategies supporting emerging/frontier technology solutions.","ICT Division"]],"304":[[1,"737","9","Technology-Specific SDG Investigation and Intervention Design Support","support is needed to conduct technology specific investigation, to locate realizable potential and designing intervention to turn it into results towards attaining SDGs.",""],[1,"737","11","Line Ministry Digital SDG Responsibility Mapping","Develop line ministry centric responsibility map and programmes for leveraging digital technologies in meeting SDGs.",""]],"305":[[1,"756","3","Cultural Infrastructure Development and Employment Support","Construction, renovation and development of infrastructure to facilitate the pursuit of art and culture have created employment opportunities for the poor.",""],[1,"756","3","Social Safety Net Support for Distressed Cultural Workers","Efforts were made to reduce their poverty by providing financial support to the distressed cultural workers through a social safety net program that has been in operation for a significant number of years.",""],[1,"757","4","Cash Incentives for Vulnerable Artists Affected by COVID-19","the government has taken steps to support vulnerable artists that have been hit by COVID-19 through cash incentives.",""],[1,"757","4","Social Protection Expansion for Vulnerable Artists","The government also intends to extend social protection benefits to them as well.",""],[1,"759","13","Private Sector and Local Government Cultural Development Contribution","Private sector as well as the local government bodies will be encouraged to contribute their resources and efforts for cultural development;",""]],"306":[[1,"758","8","National Research on Great Men and Women","Carry out research on the lives and works of great men and women of our nation.",""],[1,"759","2","Copyright and Related Legal Reform for Cultural Sector Growth","Amend the Copyright Act and other relevant acts to support smooth growth of cultural arena.",""],[1,"759","9","Research Programmes on Lives and Works of Great People","Research programmes on lives and works of great people will be undertaken and memorial libraries and institutions will be established in respective areas;",""],[1,"759","16","New Cultural Policy Formulation and Implementation","To formulate and implement a New Cultural Policy in line with the vision 2041.",""]],"307":[[1,"760","2","Bangladesh Radio Mid-Wave Transmitter Digitization and Modernization","Digitization and modernization of mid-wave transmitter of Bangladesh Radio.",""],[1,"760","3","Bangladesh Television Headquarters Construction","Construction of Head Quarter of Bangladesh Television",""],[1,"760","4","Bangladesh Television Chittagong Centre Modernization and Extension","3. Modernization and extension of Bangladesh Television Chittagong Centre",""],[1,"760","5","Bangladesh Film Archive Building Construction","Construction of Bangladesh Film Archive Building",""],[1,"760","6","BFDC Digitalization and Modernization Expansion","Introduction of digital technology in BFDC and modernization and extension of BFDC",""],[1,"760","7","Bangabandhu Sheikh Mujib Film City Phase I Establishment","6. Establishment of Bangabandhu Sheikh Mujib Film City (Phase I)",""],[1,"760","9","Establishment of Two 10-Kilowatt Radio Stations","8. Establishment of two complete 10-kilowatt radio station at Maymansingh and Gopalgan",""],[1,"760","10","Human Resource Capacity Development for Programme Preparation in Bangladesh Television","Capacity development of human resources for programme preparation in Bangladesh television",""],[1,"760","11","Information Building Construction and Machinery Establishment for the Directorate of Film and Publication","Construction of information building and establishment of machineries in directorate of film and publication",""]],"308":[[1,"762","2","Bangabandhu Film City Development","By 2025, Bangabandhu Film City will be set up with modern facilities for overall development of the film industry.",""],[1,"762","3","BFDC Complex Construction","BFDC Complex will be constructed by 2022.",""],[1,"762","4","BFDC Infrastructure Development and Digital Technology Expansion","By 2023, BFDC Infrastructure Development and Digital Technology will be expanded.",""],[1,"762","5","National Digital Film Display System","Digital film display system will be introduced throughout the country by 2030.",""],[1,"762","6","Bangladesh Film Archive Capacity Enhancement for FIAF Conference","The capacity of Bangladesh Film Archive will be increased for organizing the Federation of International Film Archives (FIAF) conference in 2021at Dhaka.",""],[1,"762","7","Liberation War Audio-Visual Archiving Initiative","Audio visual documents of the Liberation War will be collected and archived in archive from domestic and foreign sources by 2025.",""],[1,"762","8","Digital Modernization of the Department of Film and Publications","Digital technology will be set up by 2020 to modernize the activities of the Department of Film and Publications.",""]],"309":[[1,"760","14","Immediate Appointment of Project Directors","Project directors are being appointed immediate after the approval of development project.",""],[1,"762","13","National Institute of Mass Media Infrastructure Development","Between 2025, infrastructure will be established for the National Institute of Mass Media to provide various facilities.",""],[1,"763","1","National Institute of Mass Communications Training Programme","By 2025, various training programmes will be taken to improve the competence and professional skills of the National Institute of Mass Communications.",""],[1,"763","2","Bangla Film and Television Institute Campus Development","By the year 2025, the new Bangla Film and Television Institute will create their own campus facilities.",""],[1,"763","4","Project Director Panel Preparation and Training","Preparation of panel of potential project directors from all attached departments under Ministry of Information and provides necessary training to selected officials.","Ministry of Information"],[1,"763","5","Department-Level Human Resources for Development Project Formulation and Implementation","Efficient human resources should be created in department level for formulation and implementation of development projects.",""],[1,"763","6","Human Resource Development Training","Appropriate training should be provided for development of efficient human resources.",""],[1,"765","2","Streamlining and Regulation of Development Project Authorization","These matters need to be streamlined and the authorization process needs to be regulated in order to expedite and ensure proper and timely implementation of development projects and also to maximize their efficiency and impact.",""]],"310":[[1,"763","14","Public Awareness Activities for Preventing Religious Militancy and Terrorism","Public Awareness Activities for preventing religious militancy and terrorism.",""],[1,"764","4","Model Mosques and Islamic Cultural Centres Construction Initiative","Under this initiative, 560 model mosques and Islamic Cultural Centres are under construction to create prayer facilities and generate employment for the daily labours and also other socio-religious facilities.",""],[1,"764","5","Islamic Mission Hospital Complex Construction Project","The Shirta, Mymensingh & Kalkini, Madaripur Islamic Mission Hospital Complex is under construction and upon completion will provide free medical services to the poor and disadvantaged people.",""],[1,"764","5","Baitul Mukarram Diagnostic Center Strengthening Project","Baitul Mukarram Diagnostic Center Strengthening Projects:",""],[1,"764","6","Gopalganj Islamic Foundation Complex Establishment Project","The Gopalganj Islamic Foundation complex, which is currently under construction, is aimed at training of religious leaders to enable them to play a more meaningful role in social development as well as be more self-dependent and also knowledge to provide basic/primary medical services to the poor and disadvantaged people of society.",""],[1,"764","6","Collection of Books and Expansion of Reader's Service at National Level and District Libraries of Islamic Foundation Project","Collection of Books and Expansion of Reader's Service at National Level and District Libraries of Islamic Foundation Project: The Central District libraries and Imam Training Academy Libraries were enriched by collecting books under this project on various Islamic topics and socio-development issues as well.",""],[1,"765","4","Primary School Enrollment and Adult Literacy Expansion","Increasing the enrolment of children aged 6 and above to primary school, increase the literacy rate of illiterate adolescent and adults and increase opportunity for learning of the Holy Scriptures with the aim of uplifting morality and upholding religious values.",""],[1,"765","5","Religious Heritage Renovation and Construction Programme","Renovation, repair and construction of historical mosques, temples, pagodas, churches etc. of Bangladesh.",""],[1,"765","6","Religious Book Publication and Nationwide Distribution","Publication of religious books on various subjects and their nationwide distribution to ensure access for all.",""],[1,"765","7","Islamic Foundation Institutional Capacity Strengthening","Strengthening the institutional capacity of Islamic Foundation expanding the organization, human resource training and construction works.",""],[1,"765","8","Vocational and Technical Training for Religious Leaders","Creation of employment and self-employment opportunities of Imams and other religious leaders by providing vocational and technical training.",""],[1,"765","9","Inclusive Representation of Imams and Religious Leaders in Policy Processes","Ensuring effective representation of Imams and religious leaders in policy formulation, planning and decision- making process in various levels.",""],[1,"765","10","Biodiversity Awareness-Raising through Religious Leaders","Awareness-raising activities through the Imams and other religious leaders to preserve bio- diversity and improve the quality of life of the people of the Haors and wetlands and in hard to reach area.",""],[1,"766","1","Pre-Primary and Adult Education Continuation","Continue pre-primary and adult education.",""],[1,"766","1","Darul Akram Madrasah Capacity Expansion and Equipping","Increase the capacity and equip Darul Akram Madrasahs in order to provide opportunities for basic primary education, Islamic education, values and culture.",""],[1,"766","2","Quran Learning Access Initiative for Children","Facilitate and enable access to learn the Holy Quran to 8.76 million school-going students, drop out students and children working in slums.",""],[1,"766","3","Construction of Model Mosques and Islamic Cultural Centres","Construct 560 model Mosques and Islamic Cultural Centres to create prayer facilities for an average of 4 million people.",""],[1,"766","4","Historical Mosque Renovation and Construction Programme","Renovation, repair and construction of 1000 historical mosques of Bangladesh.",""],[1,"766","5","National Mosque Library Expansion Programme","Establish 10,000 mosque libraries across the country to enable lifelong learning facilities on various Islamic subjects and other socio-economic issues.",""],[1,"766","6","Expansion of Islamic Mission Health Promotion Activities","Expanding Islamic Mission activities throughout the country to aid in promoting health care, health education and good lifestyle practices for preventing and managing communicable and non- communicable diseases.",""],[1,"766","7","Publication of Islamic Research Books and Encyclopaedia","Publish religious books on fundamental issues of Islamic research and Islamic encyclopaedia.",""],[1,"766","8","Training for Religious Leaders on Social Issues","Provide training to Imam/ Religious leaders on various social issues such as bio-diversity conservation, primary health care, early marriage hazards, agriculture practices, forestation, dowry, repression of women and terrorism.",""],[1,"766","9","Imam and Muazin Interest-Free Loan and Financial Aid Scheme","The Imam Muazin Welfare Trust will provide interest-free loans and financial aids to Imams and Muazins across the country to enhance their livelihood through business activities support.",""],[1,"766","10","Improve Zakat Collection and Distribution Mechanism","Improve Zakat Collection and Distribution mechanism.",""],[1,"766","11","Financial Support for Temples and Durga Mandaps","Provide financial support to temples and Durga Mandaps.",""],[1,"766","12","Pre-primary and Religious Education Provision","Provide pre-primary and religious education to children.",""],[1,"766","13","Pilgrimage Financial Support Programme","Provide financial support to pilgrimages.",""],[1,"766","14","National Days and Spiritual Occasions Discussion Programmes","Organize discussion programmes on National Days and Spiritual Occasions.",""],[1,"766","16","Enlistment of Hindu Temples and Religious Institutes","Enable enlistment of Hindu Temples and religious institutes.",""],[1,"766","18","Temple-Based Libraries","Establish Temple based libraries.",""],[1,"766","19","Renovation and Development of Hindu Temples and Religious Institutes","Renovation and development of Hindu Temples and Hindu Religious Institutes.",""],[1,"766","20","Pre-primary and Religious Education Expansion","Provide pre-primary education and religious education with a view to increase the enrolment of students at primary level which is also one of the objectives of the new proposed education policy.",""],[1,"766","21","Adult Education and Literacy Programme","Provide adult education with a view to increasing the literacy of adult which is also one of the aims of the proposed education policy.",""],[1,"766","22","Buddhist Religious Education Programme","Provide religious education to increase the proper learning and understanding on holy facts and faith of Buddhism through Tripitakan Education Centre by using religious places like Monastery/Pagoda premises.",""],[1,"767","1","Repair and Renovate Buddhist Religious Institutions","Repair and renovate the Buddhist Religious Institutions to improve and expand the facilities for practicing religious rituals of the Buddhist Community.",""],[1,"767","2","Pagoda-Based Library for Buddhist Community Awareness","Increase awareness and knowledge on Buddhism through pagoda-based library for Buddhist Community.",""],[1,"767","3","Buddhist Family Law Awareness and Knowledge Campaign","Increase awareness and knowledge in the Buddhist Community on Buddhist Family Law.",""],[1,"767","4","Buddhist Monks and Sramanas Skills Training Program","Training program for expanding and improving the skills and knowledge of Buddhist Monks and Sramanas.",""],[1,"767","5","Buddhist Religious Welfare Trust Office Building Construction","Construct own office building and achieve self-sufficiency of the Buddhist Religious Welfare Trust.",""],[1,"767","6","Development of Buddhist Religious Institutions","Ensure and continue the development work of Buddhist Religious Institutions to create opportunities to practice religious culture and rituals of the Buddhist Community.",""],[1,"767","7","Financial Support for Churches","Provide financial support to churches.",""],[1,"767","8","Religious Education for Children","Provide religious education to children.",""],[1,"767","9","National Days and Spiritual Occasions Discussion Programmes","Organize discussion programmes on National Days and Spiritual Occasions.",""],[1,"767","10","Publication of Religious Books","Publication of religious books.",""],[1,"767","11","Church-Based Library Establishment","Establish Church based libraries.",""],[1,"767","12","Renovation and Development of Churches and Religious Institutes","Renovation and development of Churches and Religious Institutes.",""],[1,"778","3","Priority Programmes for Recreation, Culture and Religious Affairs","The 8FYP would support the implementation of all priority programmes for recreation, culture and religious affairs as inputs to the fuller development of the moral and human qualities of the population.",""]],"311":[[1,"770","10","Youth Volunteer Mobilization for Environment and Climate Action","To encourage youth to volunteer in protecting the environment, combating climate change, calamities and nation building",""],[1,"770","11","Youth Participation in Decision-Making Initiative","To involve youth in the decision-making process at local, national and international levels",""],[1,"770","12","Youth Volunteer Mobilization for Environmental Protection and Nation Building","To encourage youth to volunteer in protecting the environment, combating climate change, calamities and nation building",""],[1,"771","1","Youth Policy Coordination Mechanism","Since implementation spreads across various line ministries, a proper coordination mechanism needs to be identified.",""],[1,"771","1","Youth Policy Monitoring and Evaluation System","An M&E system needs to be developed to measure implementation and progress.",""],[1,"778","2","Operationalization of the National Youth Policy","One important policy reform would be to make this policy more operational.",""],[1,"778","2","Results-Based Monitoring Framework for Youth Policy","In that connection, it will be helpful to design a results-based monitoring framework with specific quantitative targets to measure progress with implementation.",""]],"312":[[1,"818","1","STEM Education Promotion for Girls","Science, technology, engineering and mathematics (STEM) education streams with qualified faculty should be promoted in schools, colleges and universities through regulatory measures and increase girls' participation by establishing targets.",""],[1,"818","1","Girls' STEM Outreach and Support Measures","Community awareness and motivation should be strengthened to send girls to STEM at the school and at the tertiary level and technical education.",""],[1,"818","1","Expanded Girls' STEM Support Package","Additional stipends and support for girls, science fair, special training for teachers and science education facility at upazila levels should be expanded for increasing girl students in STEM.",""],[1,"818","1","Girls' ICT Introduction and Higher Education Promotion","Girls should be introduced to ICT and encouraged to undertake higher education in ICT.",""],[1,"818","2","Market-Responsive Technical and Vocational Education Reform","The educational curriculum should be reviewed and updated to cater to the needs of the country and the changing global requirements based on labour market analysis and future projections.",""],[1,"818","2","Girls' Career Guidance and Technical Stream Support","The selection of stream for girls should be backed by career counselling on market needs.",""],[1,"818","2","Technical Education Standardization and International Equivalency","Other areas to focus are standardization and equivalency of technical education and vocational skills with international market, focusing on demand-driven skill development system should be prioritized.",""],[1,"818","2","ICT Proficiency and Trade Skills Modernization Initiative","Measures for proficiency in ICT for all, modernization of trade skills education like driving; learning international languages; hands on training; globally acceptable certification system; and improving teachers' qualification are needed.",""],[1,"818","2","Regular Labour Market Assessment and Curriculum Adjustment","Domestic and international market need assessment and adjustment of curriculum should be undertaken regularly.",""],[1,"818","2","Support Package for Girls in Technical Education","Support for girls like hostel, stipend, sanitation facilities, market information, internship in technical fields and incentives should be ensured.",""]],"313":[[1,"807","6","Climate-Resilient Infrastructure Investment for Vulnerable Communities","Hence, the Government will undertake more investments to increase the safety of such vulnerable communities by building/installing infrastructures that are resilient to the impacts of climate change.",""],[1,"807","7","Early Warning Access and Disaster Service Provider Support Measures","Having access to early warnings remains a challenge and thus, effective institutional measures will be undertaken to overcome this problem.",""],[1,"807","8","Disaster Mitigation Outreach Scale-Up Measures","The Government will develop and implement effective measures to scale up measures to mitigate disasters so that more people are covered.",""],[1,"808","2","Disaster Response Framework Development","the Government will draw lessons from the international community to develop a more effective Disaster Response Framework (DRF).",""],[1,"808","2","Televised Schooling for Service Continuity During Lockdowns","During the Covid-19 pandemic, some innovation has already been used to ensure services like schooling is maintained during the lockdown through televised schooling which can reduce the loss of school days.",""],[1,"808","3","Management Information Systems Investment for Climate and Earthquake Monitoring","The Government will invest in Management Information Systems (MIS) to strengthen the monitoring of climate change and vulnerability to earthquakes, etc.",""],[1,"808","4","Technical Risk Accounting Team for Disaster and Climate Change","Hence, the Government will form a technical team led by Ministry of Planning, to undertake a rigorous risk accounting, and determine the baseline, benchmarks and targets - that will improve Bangladesh's resilience against natural disasters and various manifestations of climate change.","Ministry of Planning"],[1,"808","5","Industry Disaster and Climate Risk Profiling for Private Investment","government will develop disaster and climate change risk profile of industry sector for risk-informed private investment",""],[1,"808","5","Supply Chain Resilience Strategy","developing strategies for supply chain resilience to avoid extreme disaster events",""],[1,"808","5","Private Sector Business Continuity Planning","Business Continuity Planning as a part of disaster recovery in the private sector",""],[1,"808","6","Disaster Loss and Damage Response Measures","Furthermore, in order to address the losses and damages from natural disasters and climate change more effectively, the following steps will be undertaken:",""],[1,"809","1","Bilateral and Multilateral Engagements for Transboundary Water Cooperation","Against that context, the Government will develop more bilateral and multilateral engagements to ensure that the South Asian countries develop a more coherent strategy to address both short, medium- and long-term environmental challenges faced by this region.",""],[1,"809","2","Environmental Management Improvement Measures","the Government will undertake specific activities to ensure that the management of the environment is sufficiently improved under the 8FYP.",""],[1,"809","10","Post-Disaster Social Safety Net Expansion","Increase the number of recipients of social welfare/safety net allocations after any disaster.",""],[1,"809","13","Gender-Sensitive Disaster Risk Reduction and Climate Risk Reduction Investment","Increased investments in gender sensitive DRR and climate risk reduction to reduce the cost for response and recovery.",""],[1,"809","18","Disaster Shelter Management Guidelines Improvement","Improve guidelines for Disaster Shelter Management.",""],[1,"809","19","Disaster Impact and Risk Assessment Guidelines Strengthening","Strengthen Disaster Impact and Risk Assessment Guidelines.",""],[1,"809","20","Emergency Fund Management Guidelines Improvement","Improve Emergency Fund Management Guidelines.",""],[1,"809","21","Early Warning System Technology Adoption","Improve early warning systems through relevant technology adoption.",""],[1,"809","22","Emergency Responder Training Investment","Increase investments in training emergency responders to cope with extreme events.",""],[1,"809","23","Coastal Afforestation Programme","Increase afforestation through a major programme along all coastal areas of the country.",""],[1,"809","24","Indigenous Coping Mechanism Guidebook Strengthening","Strengthen Indigenous Coping Mechanism Guidebook.",""],[1,"809","25","Community Risk Assessment Guidelines Enhancement","Enhance Community Risk Assessment Guidelines.",""],[1,"818","3","Water Conservation Programme for Northern Region and Coastal Belt","Also, water conservation programme for the Northern region and coastal belt is important to ease water stress and protect from salinity.",""]],"314":[[1,"819","3","Equal Wage and Benefits Compliance Monitoring","Monitoring to enforce equal wage and benefits for women and men as per Labour laws should be strengthened.",""],[1,"819","3","Employment-Oriented Safety Net Programmes","Safety net programmes designed to create employment for women and men should support transition to sustainable employment.",""],[1,"819","3","Short-Term Employment Targets in Construction and Development Projects","Target for short-term employment opportunities under construction and development projects for women should be set for women equal wage.",""],[1,"819","4","Public Sector Women's Employment Quota Expansion","The quota of 15% for women staff in public service should be enhanced",""],[1,"819","4","Recruitment of Women into Vacant Public Service Posts","Filling up of the existing vacant positions can absorb a large number of women with right qualifications",""],[1,"819","4","Women-Friendly Outsourced Employment Requirement","for outsourced employment, the supplier should be directed to ensure women's employment",""],[1,"819","4","Improvement of Women's Working Conditions","The working conditions should be improved with recruitment, promotions especially at senior levels; addressing safety and security concerns at field levels; decent work environment, and gender sensitivity among management",""],[1,"819","4","Transparent Recruitment and Performance Evaluation Reform","Transparent recruitment, promotion and annual evaluation should be ensured",""],[1,"819","4","Private Sector Regulation for Women's Employment","The private sector should be regulated to increase women's employment",""],[1,"819","4","Monitoring of Women's Workforce Participation","the situation of women in the workforce should be monitored",""],[1,"821","1","Workplace Safety and Occupational Health Improvement Measures","Improvement of work environment through safety, occupational health and safety and maternity, unemployment benefits.",""],[1,"821","1","Women-Friendly Workplace Support Facilities","Medical, child care and other facilities should be improved to encourage women to join and continue in the labour market.",""],[1,"821","1","Fair Wage and Equal Pay Enforcement","In addition, fair wage for informal employment should be ensured and equality of wage for men and women should be enforced.",""],[1,"821","1","Maternity and Child Care Support Provisions","Provisions of maternity and child care support should be ensured.",""],[1,"821","1","Hazardous Work and Child Labour Elimination Initiative","Elimination hazardous work and child labour and creating decent work, occupational health and safety, unemployment benefits and human development opportunities for working persons should be ensured.",""],[1,"831","2","Gender Wage Gap Reduction Measures","narrowing of wage gap between similarly qualified male and female workers;",""],[1,"831","2","Workplace Anti-Discrimination Enforcement","elimination of all types of biases against female staff at the work place;",""]],"315":[[1,"819","5","Labour Market Analysis for Skills and Employment Planning","Women's skills for access and mobility within the local and international job market through regular labour market analysis should be ensured.",""],[1,"819","5","Information Updating and Trade Skills Modernization Support","Updating of information; support for Balancing, Modernization, Rehabilitation and Expansion (BMRE); modernization of trade skills; product diversification, upgrading of employable education and skills should continue based on market need assessment.",""],[1,"819","5","Curriculum Update Based on Labour Market Needs","Labour market needs should be informed to education sector for updating education system and curriculum.",""],[1,"831","2","Equal Access to Education and Skills for Women","The key areas would be to ensure equal benefit from quality formal education; marketable skills to maximize productivity and potential of women;",""]],"316":[[1,"820","4","Inclusive Financial System for Women","Inclusive financial system to ensure access of women in simple terms at a low and no interest should be established.",""],[1,"820","4","Expansion of the ICVGD Model","The Investment Component of Vulnerable Group Development (ICVGD) model should be expanded for provision of capital and skills for the poor.",""],[1,"820","4","Simplification and Decentralization of Bank Lending Procedures","The banks and financial institutions should simplify the procedures, delegate authorities at the division/district levels up to a certain limit for lending to support women entrepreneurs avail the opportunities provided by Bangladesh Bank for institutional finance.",""],[1,"820","4","G2P Social Allowance and Finance Transfer System","All transfer of social allowance and finance should be through G2P using ICT.",""]],"317":[[1,"821","2","Community Orientation Campaign Against Violence Against Women in Public Places","Creating public opinion against VAW in public places through community orientation and motivation by using communication methods and media will be emphasized.",""],[1,"821","2","Workplace Violence Prevention Compliance Mechanism","The High Court directives on prevention of workplace violence by establishing Committee and complain box should be followed by all ministries, agencies, offices and private sector corporate offices.",""],[1,"821","2","Administrative Guideline for Compliance with Workplace Violence Directives","The Ministry of Public Administration should issue a guideline for all ministries, agencies and private sector to comply with the directives.","Ministry of Public Administration"],[1,"821","2","Sexual Harassment Legislation","Legislation to address sexual harassment as per Supreme Court order will be a priority.",""],[1,"821","2","Rapid Response and Law Enforcement Orientation on Workplace Violence","Fast action on violence committed at public/work places and orientation on the laws for the members of law enforcing agencies in implementation and enforcement of the legal provisions should be ensured.",""],[1,"824","3","Sexual Harassment Law and Compliance Framework","Law needs to be formulated as per the directives from the High Court in 2010 on sexual harassment in public places like educational institutions and work place.",""],[1,"824","4","Legal Harmonization with ILO Violence and Harassment Convention","The domestic laws and policies on labour, migration, occupational health and safety and other relevant laws of Bangladesh should be reviewed and made consistent with the Convention.",""],[1,"830","5","Gender-Based Violence Prevention and Support Services Expansion","The on-going initiatives under the multi-sectoral programme and institutional mechanisms should be expanded.",""],[1,"831","1","Legal and Programmatic Measures on Violence Against Women","The new dimensions of VAW against the elderly women, children and through ICT need addressing though legal and programmatic provisions.",""],[1,"831","1","Workplace and Institutional Anti-Sexual Abuse Guidelines","General guidelines should be issued for all private and public institutions to formulate and enforce policies to protect women from sexual abuse at work places/ educational institutions and other public places.",""],[1,"831","1","Legal Reform to Address Marital Rape","Marital rape should be brought within legal provisions.",""],[1,"831","1","Professional Social Work Mechanism for Violence Against Women Support","Development and institutionalizing a professional social work mechanism should be explored for support in cases of VAW.",""],[1,"831","1","Social Research on Violence Against Women and Girls","Social research should be conducted to identify the root causes of violence against women and girls and actions to be taken for remedies.",""],[1,"831","2","Social Norms and Violence Against Women Reduction Actions","actions that enhances positive social norms and reduces VAW and other harmful practices.",""]],"318":[[1,"823","3","Strengthening Local Government Citizens' Committees and Women's Participation","The ward committees at the union level, the Town and Ward level Coordination Committees under the municipalities, the Upazila Women's Forum and the Standing Committees under the unions should be strengthened ensuring women's leadership and participation as per the laws.",""],[1,"823","3","Gender-Responsive Open Budget and Development Planning Enforcement","The open budget formulation, development planning and project implementation with participation of women and addressing their needs should be enforced and monitored.",""],[1,"823","3","Women's Forum Outreach and Capacity Building Support","Proper communication to bring in women in these forums, support for their capacity building and utilization of the gender budget for local government institutions should be ensured as per the guidelines and monitored.",""]],"319":[[1,"823","6","Expansion and Strengthening of Youth Forums and Adolescent Clubs","Youth forums and the adolescent clubs formed under different ministries including MoWCA should be expanded and strengthened.","MoWCA"],[1,"825","3","Adolescent Awareness and Youth Clubs Programme","The government wants to make the adolescent boys and girls aware on multifarious issues like demerits of child marriage, violence against women and girls, discrimination against the women by organizing clubs all over the country.",""],[1,"825","3","Adolescent Sports and Cultural Activities Support","Initiatives will also be taken to facilitate them for different sports and different cultural activities.",""],[1,"830","4","Child and Adolescent Gender Equality Socialization Programme","Early initiation and continued investment in children and adolescents is critical through education curriculum, sports and culture, social behaviour, media and all other means to promote the culture of equality between girls and boys and their equal human rights is necessary, so that men do not grow up with a discriminatory view towards women.",""],[1,"830","4","Girl-Centred Adolescent Empowerment Programme","Girl-centred programmes equipping adolescent girls with knowledge and skills can build their confidence and contribute to the efforts to end inter-generational poverty, illiteracy, ill health, and gender inequality.",""]],"320":[[1,"824","1","Review and Revision of Discriminatory Laws and Policies for CEDAW Compliance","Remove all discriminatory provisions in laws and policies in consistency with CEDAW: Despite formulation of good laws, some laws and policies are not yet in full conformity with CEDAW.","MoWCA"],[1,"824","2","Strengthening Enforcement of Women's and Girls' Rights Laws","the hindrances to their enforcement should be removed through establishing effective mechanisms, accountability and training for law enforcing agencies.",""],[1,"824","2","Implementation of Disability Rights and Protection Act for Female PWDs","All laws related to the rights of disadvantaged groups like the persons with disabilities (PWDs)' Rights and the Protection Act 2013 should be implemented with care for assisting female PWD's development in all areas.",""],[1,"824","2","Expansion of Legal Aid and Faster Justice for Gender-Based Violence Cases","The Legal Aid Fund should be increased and the legal system should be simplified and faster in case of rape and sexual harassment.",""],[1,"824","2","Gender-Sensitive Justice Support Measures","Practice of gender sensitive procedures, retention of legal practitioners to support women, more tribunals to deal with repression of women and girls and human trafficking, security of justice seekers should be ensured.",""],[1,"824","5","Girl Child Rights Mainstreaming in Laws and Policies","Girl children as a distinct group should be recognized as girls are also vulnerable to violence and exploitation.","MoWCA"],[1,"825","1","Gender Review of Sectoral Laws and Policies","All laws and policies should be reviewed before their approval and enactment by MoWCA and gender experts.","MoWCA"],[1,"825","2","Strengthening Law Enforcer Accountability and Responsiveness","To achieve this objective, the law enforcing agencies are to be more effective and activated.",""],[1,"825","2","999 Emergency Response App","The present 999 apps in really a good initiative to receive the most urgent cry for help but it depends upon the sincerity of them.",""],[1,"825","2","Training and Accountability for Law Enforcers","The law enforcers might be given training and motivation and their accountability might be ensured.",""],[1,"825","4","Gender-Responsive Human Resource Policy Reform","Government should direct all public and private institutions to ensure women's participation and benefits through incorporating provisions in human resource policies (recruitment, training, promotion) and removing all provisions that hinder women's advancement.",""],[1,"825","4","Institutional Women's Development Target Setting","Each agency should be motivated to have specific target or measures for women's development.",""],[1,"825","4","Mandatory Gender Progress Reporting Requirement","A mandatory reporting from large institutions above a minimum turn over should be brought under reporting on progress.",""],[1,"831","2","Gender Equality Law Enforcement and Monitoring","Enforcement of laws and policies and effective monitoring should be ensured for good administration and governance.",""]],"321":[[1,"825","5","Climate-Resilient Infrastructure Development","In the natural calamity prone areas, all infrastructure (transport, energy, water, sanitation, market, service centres) design and construction should consider the climate change affects and be resilient to climatic shocks.",""],[1,"825","5","Gender-Responsive Water, Sanitation, and Early Warning Infrastructure","Hygienic water and sanitation services, communication infrastructure for early warning about calamities, all weather transportation should be established and maintained.",""],[1,"825","5","Inclusive and Safe Shelter Upgrading","Shelters should include water, sanitation, privacy, to address women's needs and support child care, disability, child birth and address women's safety and security concerns.",""],[1,"825","6","Gender-Responsive and Accessible Infrastructure Design Standards","All infrastructure including building, transport (bus, train and water ways) should be convenient for women, children and PWDs.",""],[1,"826","2","Remote Area Infrastructure Connectivity Improvement","Infrastructure development should be aim at connectivity with remote areas.",""],[1,"831","2","Gender-Responsive Infrastructure for Mobility and Economic Gains","infrastructure that facilitates women's human development, mobility and economic gains;",""]],"322":[[1,"826","3","Private Sector Supportive Workplace Infrastructure Provision","Infrastructure for workplace safety and security concerns, child care, housing and toilet facilities, etc. should be ensured by the private sector as well.",""],[1,"826","3","Regulatory Incentives for Low-Cost Worker Amenities","Motivation and regulatory provisions for private sectors should be established to develop low cost housing, child care facilities and transportation services with water and sanitation facilities for employees.",""],[1,"826","3","Monitoring of Breastfeeding Facilities Directives","High court directives on breast feeding facilities in public places should be strictly monitored.",""],[1,"826","3","Industrial Dispersal for Improved Worker Living Conditions","Dispersal of industries to improve the living conditions of workers of with adequate infrastructure is essential.",""],[1,"826","3","Expansion of Women's Access to Rural Market Infrastructure","Women's access to rural market corners and such infrastructure should be expanded in collaboration with the local government institutions (e.g. municipalities, city corporations) in both urban and rural areas.",""]],"323":[[1,"829","2","Environmental Awareness, Capacity Building, and Livelihood Support","Awareness raising, capacity building and livelihood support activities in environmental protection and bio-diversity conservation should be undertaken and expanded involving women.",""],[1,"829","2","Youth Environmental Engagement Initiative","Children and youth should also be engaged in these activities to protect environment.",""],[1,"829","2","Pollution Control and Hygienic Practice Improvement","Pollution control, improvement of hygienic practice, economic use of natural resources would facilitate protection of environment and depletion of resources.",""],[1,"829","2","Environmental Orientation on Forest Conservation and Renewable Energy","Women and men should be oriented on forest conservation, renewable energy, land use planning, environmental protection to minimize exposure to hazards.",""]],"324":[[1,"829","5","Involuntary Resettlement Compensation and Resettlement Plans","Therefore, women's loss should be estimated and they should be given due compensation for the loss of livelihoods and assets for involuntary resettlement during land acquisition and construction of infrastructure through resettlement plans.",""]],"325":[[1,"831","2","Gender Equality Priority Action Package","Priority areas would be chosen on the basis of contribution towards both economic growth and women's empowerment and actions that can facilitate results in more than one area.",""],[1,"831","2","Targeted Resource Allocation for Lagging Areas","An assessment of geographic areas that lag behind national average as measured by different gender equality indicators would be prioritized for resource allocation and closing the gender gap in the identified areas.",""],[1,"831","3","Gender Mainstreaming in Macro-Economic and Sectoral Policies","Mainstreaming of gender would continue and all macro-economic and sectoral policies would integrate gender as a crosscutting theme.",""],[1,"831","3","Gender Equality Action Planning","Action plans should be drawn with a view to reduce inequality and promote an equal relationship between sexes.",""]],"326":[[1,"834","1","Social Exclusion Elimination and Inclusion Strategy","Through the Constitution, the Government is committed to eliminating all kind of social exclusion.",""],[1,"836","4","National Social Security Strategy for Marginalized Groups","The new National Social Security (NSSS) puts considerable emphasis to bring these marginalized groups under the umbrella of social protection.",""],[1,"839","1","Constitutional Equality and Inclusion Implementation","The Eighth Plan strategy for inclusion is based on implementation of the Constitution that provides equal rights and opportunities to all citizens irrespective of race, religion, caste, creed or profession.",""]],"327":[[1,"839","3","Child Rights Policy and Service Delivery Package","ensuring children's rights and advancement through the implementation of government policies and legislations; (ii) providing health services the children need; (iii) ensuring access to food and nutrition they need; (iv) providing access to girls to education, training and development opportunities; (v) ensuring access to urban poor children to early childhood development, education, sports and cultural activities providing knowledge and life skill; (vi) protecting children from all forms of abuse, exploitation and violence; (vii) providing access to children particularly in urban and remote settings to clean water and sanitation, and a healthy environment",""],[1,"839","3","Caregiver and Public Support for Child Development","ensuring support of duty bearer, parents and other care givers on whom children have to depend; and (x) :selected: ensuring widespread public support for survival and development of children",""]],"328":[[1,"836","3","Dalit Inclusion and Rights Protection Strategy","A key strategy will to cooperate with local bodies and NGOs to identify the disadvantaged people and enable them to participate in development activities.",""],[1,"836","3","Inclusive Education Measures for Dalit Children","The Government will uphold the right to education for children from Dalit communities with the expectation to ensure schools becomes non-discriminatory and inclusive spaces for all children.",""],[1,"836","3","Special Quota for Dalit and Excluded Students","a special quota for Dalit and other excluded students will be created in government schools and colleges",""],[1,"836","3","Access to Government Skill Training Institutions","access of Dalit adolescents and youth to all government owned skill training institutions will be ensured.",""],[1,"836","3","Priority Khas Land Allocation for Disadvantaged Communities","Then priority will be given to the disadvantaged communities in khas land allocation.",""],[1,"836","3","Land Allocation Encouragement for Tea Garden Workers","Tea Garden owners will also be encouraged to assign some land within the estate to their extreme poor workers as a mean for them to build their own garden.",""],[1,"836","3","Interagency Coordination for Dalit Inclusion Governance","all government functionaries will need to coordinate their activities at all levels to ensure the effective governance of this issue.",""]],"329":[[1,"841","5","Ethnic Communities Socio-Economic Rights and Social Protection Programme","The government is committed to ensuring socio-economic and political rights, fundamental human rights, and social security, while enabling ethnic people to retain their social, cultural, and traditional identities.",""],[1,"841","5","CHT Access to Services and Livelihoods Support Programme","The ethnic communities of the CHT will be ensured access to education, health care, food and nutrition, employment, and overseas employment, and protection of rights to land and other resources.",""],[1,"841","5","Priority Financing for CHT Development Projects","Additional finance will be allocated as a priority for the implementation of projects that contribute to the development of the people of the CHT and to bridging the development gap between the hills and the plains.",""],[1,"841","5","CHT Cultural Identity Preservation Measures","Special measures will be taken to preserve the characteristics of the CHT and the cultural identity of the ethnic groups.",""],[1,"842","1","Ethnic Communities Rights and Social Security Support","The government is committed to ensuring socio-economic and political rights, fundamental human rights, and social security, while enabling tribal people to retain their social, cultural and traditional identities.",""],[1,"842","1","CHT Access to Basic Services and Livelihoods Programme","The ethnic communities of the CHT will be insured access to education, health care, food and nutrition, employment, and overseas employment, and protection of rights to land and other resources.",""],[1,"842","1","Priority Financing for CHT Development Projects","Additional finance will be allocated as a priority for the implementation of projects that contribute to the development of the people of the CHT and to bridging the development gap between the hills and the plains.",""],[1,"842","3","Implementation of the UN Declaration on the Rights of Indigenous Peoples","The Government will consider implementing the UN Declaration on the Rights of Indigenous Peoples 2007 and ratifying the ILO Convention 169.",""],[1,"842","3","Ratification of ILO Convention 169","The Government will consider implementing the UN Declaration on the Rights of Indigenous Peoples 2007 and ratifying the ILO Convention 169.",""]],"330":[[1,"841","5","Separate Land Commission for Ethnic Minorities","the government will take measures to establish a separate land commission for ethnic minorities in the plain land.",""],[1,"842","5","Chittagong Hill Tracts Land Dispute Resolution","The Land Commission will resolve the land disputes in CHT following the amended Land Commission Dispute Resolution Act 2001 to ensure the rights to land.",""],[1,"842","5","Chittagong Hill Tracts Land Disputes Resolution Rules","Rules of the CHT Land Disputes Resolutions will be enacted soon so that CHT Land Disputes Resolution Commission can function",""],[1,"842","5","Chittagong Hill Tracts Land Survey","A land survey will be carried out in consultation with the key stakeholders as per the provisions of the CHT Peace Accord.",""],[1,"842","5","Ethnic Land Dispute Policy Formulation","An appropriate land policy will be formulated which can deal with land disputes involving ethnic groups.",""],[1,"842","5","Secure Land Tenure System","A secure land tenure system will be introduced.",""]],"331":[[1,"842","6","Community Participation in Development and Natural Resource Management","The Government will ensure participation of local people in development activities and management of natural resources and will recognize the traditional customs and knowledge of the various ethnic peoples.",""],[1,"842","6","Community-Based Technology Adoption Support","The Government will ensure community involvement in the adoption of technologies in line with the traditional food production system.",""],[1,"842","6","Vocational Skills Training and Support","The Government will provide appropriate training and support to people for development of their vocational skills and knowledge.",""],[1,"843","4","Ethnic Community Human Resource Development Programme","Existing human resource development programmes will be augmented to address the special needs of ethnic people and strengthen their vocational and social skills.",""],[1,"843","4","Youth Training and Support Programme","Necessary training and support will be provided to the youth.",""],[1,"843","4","Strengthened Service Delivery Monitoring for Ethnic Communities","Monitoring and supervision will be strengthened so that education, health and maternal child health services, social safety nets, and nutrition and housing facilities reach the ethnic people.",""],[1,"843","4","Ethnic Community Labour Market Preparation Measures","Special arrangements targeting ethnic communities to prepare them to take up the opportunities provided by national and global labour markets, including overseas employment, and thus enable them to increase their income.",""],[1,"843","4","Youth Skills Development Support for CHT","Appropriate skill development training and support will be delivered to the youth of CHT, to provide vocational and social skills.",""]],"332":[[1,"846","3","Multi-Sector HIV/AIDS Coordination and Management Strengthening","Coordination mechanisms and management capacity at different levels will be strengthened to ensure an effective multi-sector HIV/AIDS response.",""],[1,"846","3","HIV/AIDS Strategic Information and Research Strengthening","Also, strategic information systems and research for an evidence-based response will be strengthened.",""],[1,"846","4","HIV Response Legal and Policy Facilitation","The Government will make laws and policies that facilitate the HIV response and work with uniformed services and health care workers to increase knowledge and tolerance.",""]],"333":[[1,"847","6","Specialized Support and Workplace Accommodation for Persons with Disabilities","Some persons with disabilities require specialised support services, assistive devices and job modifications",""],[1,"847","6","Recognition of the Right to Decent Work for Persons with Disabilities","more importantly, the right to decent work needs to be recognised.",""]]}});